"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">&quot;Iminir desh kar&quot;: Also shortened to &quot;Desh Kar&quot; \u2014 literally translates as &quot;just us&quot;; a saying used between Storm Lords, similar to &quot;been there, done that&quot;; can also be used as an expression of sympathy or frustration at the burdens of being Iminir</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">&quot;Sehe nu lu'u thim.&quot; &quot;Do not pollute yourself with the works of man&quot; or &quot;honour/honor nothing of human craft&quot;, the Tribal vow of the Predator Kings</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">&quot;Su a sar-hith sa&quot;: &quot;Pay each spirit in kind&quot;, the Tribal vow of the Bone Shadows</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>- Non-Canon -</u></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">&quot;Ina aske bur kikuru har hae su thakh, ma ur garum kal ku garum.&quot;: On the ragged edge of the world I'll roam, and the home of the wolf shall be my home. (Robert Service, </span></span></span><i>The Nostomaniac</i><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">&quot;Kuth iduthanna namthuf&quot;: &quot;To cut the silver writing/markings/inscriptions&quot; \u2014 refers to the act of the Pure removing your auspice, specifically the act of removing your silver brands, but pretty much a catch-all for Pure initiation</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">&quot;Nu lul kal usala nuth.&quot;: &quot;&quot;Let no false 