ts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T19:35:42-07:00","id":127931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=127901#post127901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And follow it up with an oldie but a good: <b>Son of a bitch</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Noted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=127892#post127892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's start with one of my favorite words: <b>Motherfucker.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>What context are you looking for the swear to be in? The f-word has many uses (and so do its derivatives); I can kill two birds with one stone by making multiple translations if you have ideas on what definitions of that word you want translated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T22:18:20-07:00","id":142085,"title":"","content":"First hey how are ya, it's been a while.<br /> Second I have a couple for ya bud: Fang-Shapers, for the custom Pure tribe I have built (Actually will redesign it for Idigam Chronicles <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) and Knights of Saint Adrian","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T00:03:13-07:00","id":142131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=142085#post142085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First hey how are ya, it's been a while.<br /> Second I have a couple for ya bud: Fang-Shapers, for the custom Pure tribe I have built (Actually will redesign it for Idigam Chronicles <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) and Knights of Saint Adrian</div> </div> </div> </div>'Sup Koro? Hoped your guys have been enjoying the dictionary. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Let's see....<br /> <br /> <b>Mother****er: </b>If you are Pure, it's <b>Uzuhamukask</b>, which is a particularly foul insult as it implies you're equivalent to one of Luna's steaming piles of poop left on the doorstep \u2014 Predator Kings throw it around frequently, Silver Fangs absolutely lose their heads if you use it in their presence, and the Fire-Touched just sigh and add it to the list of your sins. Rarely heard around Forsaken, but when it is, it's quite blasphemous and even worse that a certain, female-oriented c-word in English. A milder (but still very inappropriate) version used is <b>Amukask</b>, which doesn't carry the Lunar connontations.<br /> <br /> <b>Son of a B****: </b>Again, if you're among the Pure, the equivalent is <b>Uzuhdur</b>, which is fairly harsh. The term &quot;bitch&quot; by itself doesn't carry many negative connotations, for obvious reasons \u2014 that being said, one term is <b>kliatamadur</b>, which means roughly &quot;son of the lowly mother&quot;. <b>Kliatama</b> is a not-so-nice word for a female that will sleep around to gain favours, rank and status, referring to the fact she became/will become a mother because she has to use her body in order to keep her place in the pack. Females that haven't had children from these affairs yet are known as <b>kliat murruf</b>, which roughly means &quot;lowly reproductive organs&quot;. A cruder term for this is <b>murrusuuf nidu</b>, or just <b>murrusuuf</b>, the latter of which can refer to both males and females who engage in these activities.<br /> <br /> <b>Knights of Saint Adrian: </b>This would translate to <b>Angzermedlu</b>, which is very close in etymology to <b>Angzermusim</b>, the name for Angels of the God-Machine (<b>Angii-Thilikh</b>).<br /> <br /> <b>Fang-Shapers: </b>For these, I created <b>Kukthidum</b>, which means &quot;fang-shaping pack&quot; or &quot;fang-creating pack&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T14:01:40-07:00","id":142663,"title":"","content":"How about these?<br /> <br /> 1. Soulless (either the adjective(aka heartless) or the actual condition)<br /> <br /> 2. To fight honorably <b>or</b> to fight dishonorably<br /> <br /> 3. Heroic(or Hero) <b>or</b> Villainous(or Villain)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T14:14:20-07:00","id":142670,"title":"","content":"Oh wow! Welcome back to translation land!<br /> <br /> I personally would like to request some sort of first tongue translation of &quot;one day we shall meet again&quot; either in friendly connotation such as between parting pack or packmates, or in a connotation insinuating next time there shall be blood and/or death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T17:18:19-07:00","id":142802,"title":"","content":"Who were you on the old forums, Dessembrae? Your avvie seems familiar....<br /> <br /> Ooh, some good requests here! Let's see:<br /> <br /> <b>Soulless: </b>A soulless person, i.e. one who seems to have no sense of morality or conscience, may be called a <b>viruhursakh </b>(which is particularly harsh or strong to use, as it implies you're heartless because of Soulless Wolf, a.k.a. Viruhk-Ur), or more plainly, <b>nuhursakh</b> (&quot;no-heart&quot;). The latter term can also refer to someone who has become soulless in the context of losing their soul; while we already know <b>zi'ir </b>is used for Morality 0 werewolves, a similar term is used for those who have experienced soul loss \u2014 <b>zi'rih</b>, &quot;spirit-eaten&quot;. Though the term often refers to those turned into hollowed shells by hosts and other spirits, it can refer to anyone who has lost their soul. Zi'irs who became zi'irs due to the Soul Loss condition of GMC are sometimes called <b>rih-galer </b><b>zi'ir </b>(or just <b>rih-galer</b>), &quot;Broken Souls damned by being eaten&quot;. Horrifying in its context, as the thought of a wolf losing their minds because their soul was snatched is much like how a spirit is absorbed into another spirit by being eaten \u2014 they lose themselves, sometimes quickly and sometimes slowly.<br /> <br /> <b>To Fight: </b>In the old dictionary, I didn't really give a word for &quot;fight&quot;, but I gave specific terms for different kinds of fighting, reflecting how the Uratha have several words for types of fighting due to their culture. The word for &quot;challenge&quot;, <b>habalthu</b>, was meant to be used in my translations to refer to fighting most of the time, reflecting how most &quot;fights&quot; between wolves are challenges for dominance. Ergo, to fight honourably would likely depend on the tribe you're part of; for example, all wolves would probably use the term <b>Urfarah habalthudu</b>, which means &quot;to fight like Father Wolf himself&quot;, as a major compliment to an honourable fighter. Tribes individually may use the names of their totems to refer to what they consider honourable fighting, i.e. <b>Fenris habalthudu</b> for a skillful Blood Talon warrior, <b>Kamduis </b><b>habalthu </b>for a Bone Shadow who always gives the spirit a fair shot, and so on. On the other hand, dirty fighting might be known to the Forsaken as <b>Anshega habalthudu</b>, which means &quot;you fight like the Pure&quot; \u2014 not very flattering for a werewolf of Luna's. The opposite of this, for the Pure, is obviously <b>Urdaga habalthudu</b>, Some may use <b>gurim habalthudu</b>, meaning &quot;you fight like a sick animal&quot;, the lowercase voiced around Fire-Touched by pronouncing the &quot;gur&quot; as a guttural growl to take a swipe at their totem. Pure instead use <b>Uzuhabalthudu</b>, which is a lot stronger-sounding a term of the Uratha, and is meant to clearly identify them in a conversation as children of the traitorous Bitch Moon. The worst of dirty fighters \u2014 those who give unnecessarily painful deaths or compromise their packs and others \u2014 may get slapped with <b>viruhabalthu</b>, which means &quot;your fighting is inherently corrupted and filthy&quot;. A worse version of this is <b>Maelhabalthu</b>, which not only refers to the dirty fighting tactics of the Bale Hounds, but also those who go to extremely foul lengths to win a fight, to the point of consorting with Wound-spawn and foul hosts.<br /> <br /> <b>Heroic and Villainous: </b>Heroic would be <b>kalekal-zi</b>, &quot;one of a renowned soul&quot;; the greatest of heroes are made distinct in this term by having no hypen between &quot;kalekal&quot; and &quot;zi&quot;, meaning &quot;one who is inherently renown&quot;. Villains are known as <b>zi'ira </b>(original term by Mr. Shopping of <i>Detroit Rock City </i>fame), which means &quot;close to being broken-souled, foul, dishonourable or of low morality&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>One Day We Shall Meet Again: </b>Friendly version? <b>&quot;Kin ah kana kalsufala guth Iduth</b>.&quot; \u2014 &quot;There will be a time to meet when the Moon turns well,&quot; meaning that the parties will meet by the mercy of Mother Moon. Hostile version? <b>&quot;Ku sahfa Suth-Iduth su-ah hiri'us nuku.&quot; \u2014</b> &quot;I promise I find you under a Bloodied Luna,&quot; or, &quot;I swear I will find you under a bloody moon.&quot; Get rid of the &quot;sahfa&quot; part if you're not hell-bent on revenge or otherwise furious.<br /> <br /> Edit: Almost forgot \u2014 if you're Pure, the friendly version is, <b>&quot;Ku nuku kin ina nuduth ah,&quot; </b>which means, &quot;We will meet in moonless times.&quot; This refers to meeting in a place where there is no trace of Luna or her servants, such as the hated Forsaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 05-20-2014, 12:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T18:44:33-07:00","id":142927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=142131#post142131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 'Sup Koro? Hoped your guys have been enjoying the dictionary. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> .<br /> <br /> <b>Knights of Saint Adrian: </b>This would translate to <b>Angzermedlu</b>, which is very close in etymology to <b>Angzermusim</b>, the name for Angels of the God-Machine (<b>Angii-Thilikh</b>).<br /> <br /> <b>Fang-Shapers: </b>For these, I created <b>Kukthidum</b>, which means &quot;fang-shaping pack&quot; or &quot;fang-creating pack&quot;.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> I've been well,I sure do enjoy your dictionary ^^<br /> <br /> I love those translation, they are awesome! I do have two more for you if that is alright<br /> <br /> I have asked for these two before, but due to problems and such I have lost their translations: Chimera and Tie Lin","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T18:53:11-07:00","id":142933,"title":"","content":"What does &quot;Tie Lin&quot; mean, if I might ask? It looks like a Chinese name.<br /> <br /> As for the term <b>chimera:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Suasumthurah:</b> Chimera, the mythical Greek beast, and also referring to the patron of the Stargazers.<br /> <br /> <b>sharsusar:</b> Chimera, unnatural hybrid; animera and humera (as described in Skinchangers) are called <b>hidumamu-sharsusar </b>and <b>lu'u-sharsusar</b>, respectively. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Something interesting to note here is the mashup nature of the term <b>hidumamu </b>itself \u2014 we have <b>hidumam</b>, a rare word in First Tongue in that it is the distinct plural of another word (<b>hidum</b>, meaning &quot;animal&quot;), combined with the <b>-u suffix</b> that often denotes a type of host (<b>az</b>, &quot;spider&quot;, &quot;poisonous vermin&quot; compared to <b>Azlu</b>, &quot;spider host&quot;, for example). Therefore, &quot;an unnatural hybrid host to animals&quot;. And yet, the term for a humera is rather straightforward \u2014 then again, if you pronounced that final u with emphasis, you could also get a word that means &quot;an unnatural hybrid host to a human&quot;, in a case where the suffixed form and the original form are only differentiated by pronunciation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 05-19-2014, 10:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T19:13:50-07:00","id":142950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=142933#post142933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does &quot;Tie Lin&quot; mean, if I might ask? It looks like a Chinese name.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Tie Lin means &quot;Iron Scales&quot; in Chinese ^^<br /> <br /> Also, this is the last one for me for the time being my friend: thousand faces","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T21:22:35-07:00","id":143012,"title":"","content":"You probably don't need this, but in case you're interested, here's a Sumerian Dictionary with the Reversed Grimms Law pre applied: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/19YdC-2Phr8b2JndCZniCbw9l3SCnhHjcEkfi-rspTyE\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets...HjcEkfi-rspTyE</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T21:38:46-07:00","id":143040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=143012#post143012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You probably don't need this, but in case you're interested, here's a Sumerian Dictionary with the Reversed Grimms Law pre applied: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/19YdC-2Phr8b2JndCZniCbw9l3SCnhHjcEkfi-rspTyE\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets...HjcEkfi-rspTyE</a></div> </div> </div> </div>This?<br /> <br /> This is amazing.<br /> <br /> I HEARBY MAKE YOUR USERNAME INTO AN HONOURARY WORD!<br /> <br /> <b>nikink</b>: A librarian, a scholar, a professor or teacher of a lost or exclusive art (such as a type of ritual); powerful spirits that attend to libraries, as well as those that attend to places of lost knowledge and sacred power, are known as Nikinkhim.<br /> <br /> Edit: Almost forgot the translations.<br /> <br /> <b>Tie Lin (Iron Scales): </b>Three versions depending on what the name is supposed to mean or imply. <b>Ansarmusinhirigus</b> if he literally has a body of iron scales, <b>Ansar-Musinhirigus </b>if an iron-scaled form is part of what he is, and <b>Ansar Musinhirigus </b>if he has some sort of iron scale or something representing iron scales, such as scale armour.<br /> <br /> <b>Thousand Faces: </b>Similar thing here. <b>Li'imikhi </b>if a fundamental part of him is to literally have a thousand faces; <b>Li'im-Ikhi </b>if a thousand faces are a feature of his; <b>Li'im Ikhi </b>if the thousand faces are more &quot;a thousand guises&quot;, or if he's known to be called that because he has a thousand faces he can change into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 05-20-2014, 01:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T23:05:34-07:00","id":143131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=143040#post143040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I HEARBY MAKE YOUR USERNAME INTO AN HONOURARY WORD!<br /> <br /> <b>nikink</b>: A librarian, a scholar, a professor or teacher of a lost or exclusive art (such as a type of ritual); powerful spirits that attend to libraries, as well as those that attend to places of lost knowledge and sacred power, are known as Nikinkhim.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Bwahahah! Awesome, thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T23:16:47-07:00","id":143133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=143131#post143131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bwahahah! Awesome, thanks! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I even have an etymology behind it:<br /> <br /> <b>nikkik: </b>Forbidden knowledge, lost arts, dark magics and dangerous gifts or powers; often used to refer to things so dangerous they must be kept away, or anything associated with severe Wounds and the realm of the Maeljin.<br /> <br /> <b>kinkh: </b>To work with; to coax, to be skilled at, to manipulate.<br /> <br /> Ergo, the word and name of the Nikinkhim would refer, in the oldest texts, to spirits that guarded wellsprings of forbidden and unknown knowledge, though today it's more of a catch-all term for any spirit that guards a hoard of arcane knowledge or power. The Nikinkhim don't seem to mind the broadened term.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T02:22:00-07:00","id":143211,"title":"","content":"I'm working on something and could really use a word which cognates to the Greek <i>Furies</i> and <i>Nemesis</i>, the emphasis - in the usual confusing way of ancient languages - is on a person who is both a hunter for retribution and the relationship to that which they hunt. In essence the hunter is both the nemesis and his enemy is his nemesis, the Furies come in conceptually with the idea that these two combatants will mutually destroy each other in their respective quests for retaliation. This should also describe a hate that runs deeper than tribe or oath, but not the out of control fury of death rage, more akin to an obsessive suicidal ambition. It should be as close as the People come to 'suicide by cop'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/15.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div><br /> That guy you've never heard of.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3069-runeknight3","name":"RuneKnight3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3069_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T04:38:55-07:00","id":143308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RuneKnight3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=143211#post143211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm working on something and could really use a word which cognates to the Greek <i>Furies</i> and <i>Nemesis</i>, the emphasis - in the usual confusing way of ancient languages - is on a person who is both a hunter for retribution and the relationship to that which they hunt. In essence the hunter is both the nemesis and his enemy is his nemesis, the Furies come in conceptually with the idea that these two combatants will mutually destroy each other in their respective quests for retaliation. This should also describe a hate that runs deeper than tribe or oath, but not the out of control fury of death rage, more akin to an obsessive suicidal ambition. It should be as close as the People come to 'suicide by cop'.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Suicide By Cop: </b>That's actually a pretty easy one, I think, as I had a concept bouncing around in my head before my hiatus on my translation work. If you're Pure, the term is <b>&quot;tagayaskir Taga Dan&quot;</b>, a term originally coined by the Fire-Touched; it means &quot;to make a hunting cry for Taga Dan&quot;, Taga Dan being the canonical Eden the Fire-Touched preach that is free of lies and a hunter's paradise. The hunting cry part means you are actively pursuing it, i.e. chasing down your own way into the paradise. That being said, Predator Kings have their own version: <b>&quot;Huzurutag&quot;</b>, or &quot;Huzuruth's hunt&quot;. If you're Forsaken, it's <b>tag kunamus</b>, &quot;the death hunt&quot; or &quot;hunting one's own demise&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 05-20-2014, 07:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T07:53:48-07:00","id":143451,"title":"","content":"Translation for Ephsy's character's name into First Tongue: <b>Ursufgutha Serthahagaranzhudur</b>, or &quot;Scourge, Child (Member) of the Lodge of Wrath&quot;. &quot;Scourge&quot; in FT is translated as <b>usangurim</b>, meaning to be a terrible troublemaker, vermin or problem, but that has many negative connontations; <b>ursufgutha</b> refers to a beast or monster, especially a monstrous werewolf, and can also refer to a werewolf considered a scourge. It may or may not be negative, depending on the context in how it's used; for example, a ferocious Blood Talon might be called an ursufgutha in a complimentary way as if to say, &quot;Dude, you took on that Azlu nest like a BEAST!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T07:58:40-07:00","id":143458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=143451#post143451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Translation for Ephsy's character's name into First Tongue: <b>Ursufgutha Serthahagaranzhudur</b>, or &quot;Scourge, Child (Member) of the Lodge of Wrath&quot;. &quot;Scourge&quot; in FT is translated as <b>usangurim</b>, meaning to be a terrible troublemaker, vermin or problem, but that has many negative connontations; <b>ursufgutha</b> refers to a beast or monster, especially a monstrous werewolf, and can also refer to a werewolf considered a scourge. It may or may not be negative, depending on the context in how it's used; for example, a ferocious Blood Talon might be called an ursufgutha in a complimentary way as if to say, &quot;Dude, you took on that Azlu nest like a BEAST!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>More literally, since Serthaha means &quot;Those who Punish&quot;, or Punisher singularly, it could be &quot;Child of the Punisher&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T07:59:23-07:00","id":143460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=143458#post143458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More literally, since Serthaha means &quot;Those who Punish&quot;, or Punisher singularly, it could be &quot;Child of the Punisher&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That too! Thank you for pointing that out as well. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T00:39:09-07:00","id":149200,"title":"","content":"I've been curious about a thing for quite a while now. It sprang from the talk of translating some of the names into Swedish. I realised that I was only translating a translation, so I wonder: What are the literal translations of the first tongue tribe names (into English, Swedish would be great, but I doubt you know it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )? The Ivory Claws would be the most needed ones, but alas, I don't remember their first tongue name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T00:55:56-07:00","id":149204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=149200#post149200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been curious about a thing for quite a while now. It sprang from the talk of translating some of the names into Swedish. I realised that I was only translating a translation, so I wonder: What are the literal translations of the first tongue tribe names (into English, Swedish would be great, but I doubt you know it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )? The Ivory Claws would be the most needed ones, but alas, I don't remember their first tongue name.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will try to remember my best of what they literally mean, as I actually did this a while ago, but never posted it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Suthar Anzuth: </b>&quot;Bloodied eagle's talons&quot; or &quot;bloody eagles&quot;. Also could be translated as &quot;blood-drenched talons of the eagle&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Hirfarthra Hissu: </b>Literally &quot;ghosts of the bones&quot; or &quot;shades of the bones&quot;. <b>Hissu </b>is a term for a human or humanoid ghost.<br /> <br /> <b>Iminir</b><b>: </b>&quot;Lords of the rain&quot;, &quot;lords of the storm&quot; or &quot;rulers of the storm&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Izidakh: </b>&quot;Fire's touch&quot; or &quot;touched by fire&quot;. Pretty straightforward there.<br /> <br /> <b>Tzuumfin: </b>&quot;Claws of white&quot; or &quot;white claws&quot;. The <b>tzuum </b>part appears to be derived from Sumerian &quot;hum&quot;, which possibly means white, but in First Tongue, it appears to refer to ivory the material or a shimmering, polished white.<br /> <br /> <b>Ninna Farakh</b>: Very interesting etymologies for this! It appears that it can either mean &quot;the hunters/predators that spread out&quot;, &quot;the hunters (that are a part) of the body&quot;, or &quot;the hunters/predators who rule over all&quot;. There's also &quot;the seat of the predators&quot;, meaning that the Predator Kings claim the throne of all hunting beasts of the world.<br /> <br /> <b>Farsil Luhal: </b>&quot;Masters of canal-splitting&quot; or &quot;masters of digging irrigation ditches&quot;. Irrigation was an essential development in the practice of agriculture \u2014 could this be a hint that the Iron Masters helped humanity rise to power by teaching them certain technological advances?<br /> <br /> <b>Meninna: </b>&quot;The crowned hunters&quot;. Another boastful name to compete with the Predator Kings.<br /> <br /> <b>Thirhirtha Numea: </b>&quot;Natives of the forests of nowhere&quot;. This took me entirely too long to figure out. @_@<br /> <br /> Edit: Almost forgot:<br /> <br /> <b>Anshega: </b>&quot;The geas (sworn sacred oath) of heaven&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Urdaga: </b>&quot;The wolves of the sacred hunt&quot;. Note the similarities between <b>daga</b> and <b>dah</b>, which refers to a sacred hunt in the context of the <b>Siskur-Dah </b>from the Idigam Chronicles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 06-19-2014, 09:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T07:45:58-07:00","id":149397,"title":"","content":"One piece of text I would love translated is the phrase &quot;This is the way the world ends.&quot;<br /> <br /> In Tribes of the Moon, it is said this phrase was found painted on the wall in a cave and serves as a warning for those who are part of the Lodge of the Final Winter. I have no idea if it will affect your translation, but the phrase has served as the foundation for a lodge who believe that the Pure will bring about the Apocalypse, Luna herself will fall from orbit, and shards of her stone flesh will rain upon the world like atom bombs.<br /> <br /> Always has been one of my favorite lodges especially since I am running a game which will eventually utilize the W:TA Apocalypse book where this can indeed happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T09:21:53-07:00","id":149442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=149204#post149204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right