; border-radius: 10px;\">affag (yes, this is really how it's translated, it's one of those &quot;unfortunate words&quot;)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Seawall/Groyne:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">niksuhumsagarfath</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Devourers:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> agrih (agrihim if a spirit and plural, agrim if singular and a spirit)</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Fire-Possesed:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">izilu (if a Ridden)<br /> iziduhu (if they are creatures that inherently have fire as a trait of theirs)<br /> izag (if they use or own some sort of fire or flame)</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Jewel In the Crown:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">ninzukhinaha<br /> ninzukh-ina-aha<br /> ninzukh ina aha</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I will go into detail as to what these mean later. As for why I have given three versions of certain words, it's a trait I noticed in First Tongue that was lost in Sumerian \u2014 hyphens, spaces and affixes/suffixes all determine a word's relation to the nature of something. For eexample, i'ilth makaf means &quot;a sea in the wild&quot;, i'ilth-makaf means &quot;a sea that is untamed (but that's not necessarily it's whole nature)&quot;, and i'ilthakaf means &quot;a sea that is inherently wild and feral&quot;.<br /> <br /> And, straight from the devs as translations for &quot;Protectorate&quot;:<br /> <br /> Gi-Uru: A place under protection; another name for a Protectorate.<br /> Zahhiri: Also a name for a Protectorate, but carries a symbolic, more militaristic connontation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T00:35:24-08:00","id":338809,"title":"","content":"And before I forget:<br /> <br /> nuharul: Thing of no place (lit. &quot;something inherently not of any world or place of existence&quot;) \u2014 a strong insult somewhere between &quot;bastard&quot; and &quot;piece of shit&quot; in terms of severity, but HIGHLY insulting to use on something high-ranking like a spirit; a harsher, more impolite term for a Magath.<br /> <br /> muthrahabalthu: Spirit fight \u2014 usually meaning a worthless fight between spirits. It literally means &quot;mote challenge&quot;, and like urdurhabalthu and wolf cubs, it refers to a senseles feud that's more reserved for motes trying to pick each other off.<br /> <br /> &quot;Lal ku nukuk!&quot;: &quot;Show me your teeth!&quot; \u2014 werewolf version of, &quot;Come at me, bro!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Duzag lal nuku!&quot;: &quot;Show yourself to me!&quot; \u2014 werewolf version of, &quot;Come at me, bro!&quot; when dealing with spirits","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T07:26:25-08:00","id":339035,"title":"","content":"You're a scholar and a gentleman, Sikla. Thank you so very much. By tha way, Nuharul sounds familiar. Maybe it was one of the insults that appeared in &quot;Three Shades of Night&quot;? Anyway,i really like the meaning,aswell as the traduction. If you still take requests, i'll have more... on time, with these you've made i'll have fun for a while. By the way, i've always wanted to ask you: is sikla sumerian? If it is so,what does it mean?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T07:36:18-08:00","id":339040,"title":"","content":"Big Cheers, Mister Sikla Alkis <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Keep up the good work!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">Malkavian Madness Forum</a> - Your pbp fix. Be it nWoD, cWoD, CoC, D&amp;D or something else entirely, come over here and get your game on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/348-infernalgoose","name":"InfernalGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T07:41:16-08:00","id":339043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=339035#post339035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're a scholar and a gentleman, Sikla. Thank you so very much. By tha way, Nuharul sounds familiar. Maybe it was one of the insults that appeared in &quot;Three Shades of Night&quot;? Anyway,i really like the meaning,aswell as the traduction. If you still take requests, i'll have more... on time, with these you've made i'll have fun for a while. By the way, i've always wanted to ask you: is sikla sumerian? If it is so,what does it mean?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just put your translations here and I'll get to them as soon as I can. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And yes, &quot;nuharul&quot; is from Three Shades of Night!<br /> <br /> Re: Sikla \u2014 no, but is IS from a conlang. In David Clement Davies's &quot;The Sight&quot; (which is a Bone Shadow book if I've ever freaking seen one), it refers to a wolf of Omega rank. &quot;Sikla Alkis&quot; is a palindrome of that, and is meant to mean something along the lines of &quot;double omega&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>InfernalGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=339040#post339040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Big Cheers, Mister Sikla Alkis <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Keep up the good work!</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://www.abbyofftherecord.com/wp-content/uploads/2012/01/FingerGuns.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T12:31:43-08:00","id":339307,"title":"","content":"In recognition of the removal of unihar from 2e canon, I have decided to take the term and give it a new meaning for use in 2e games. Anyone can feel free to use it, devs included:<br /> <br /> <b>unihar:</b> One of the absolute worst insults ranking up there with &quot;shiniduth&quot;, a unihar is a foul name for an illegitimate, unwanted or otherwise looked-down upon child or pack member. It has a meaning similar to the original meaning of &quot;bastard&quot;, but is far worse \u2014 it comes from an ancient superstition that two Uratha mating would produce a vile, horrible monster that would leave the mother infertile and devour the rest of the pack. Said superstition is believed to originate from the Ivory Claws (who once used it to scare their tribemates away from certain partners), but it has spread throughout both sides and is considered unacceptable in werewolf society. To call someone a unihar is to call them a monster for ever being born, a potential liability and a nuharul all at once, and people will look at you like you're insane if you use it in affectionate terms.<br /> <br /> And if you call a spirit a unihar, run. Just run. It means something truly, truly terrible to those of the Hisil, to the point where you ST is justified in siccing a horde of otherwise-peaceful nature spirits on you if you use it on them. So horrible is the meaning and implication, the spirits have made sure it's lost to time, and hearing the word can send them into a frenzy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T16:49:50-08:00","id":339543,"title":"","content":"I'm imagining somebody say that in the middle of a Loci and have every spirit turn their heads simultaneously and glare at them like lifeless zombies. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> How do you say:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Pack goes to war tonight </b><i>(In both anger and flat connotations)</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>You are beneath my notice.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>You can not stop my vengeance now!</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T17:00:09-08:00","id":339564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=339543#post339543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Pos