a Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T02:14:57-08:00","id":339877,"title":"","content":"Hooray! Thanks, man. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","name":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T07:37:11-08:00","id":339990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=339043#post339043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In David Clement Davies's &quot;The Sight&quot; (which is a Bone Shadow book if I've ever freaking seen one), it refers to a wolf of Omega rank. &quot;Sikla Alkis&quot; is a palindrome of that, and is meant to mean something along the lines of &quot;double omega&quot;.[/img]</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the explanation! I will search that book, the summary seems interesting! How is the writing quality? Good aswell?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T07:57:58-08:00","id":340019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ursufgutha Storm-Born</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=339877#post339877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hooray! Thanks, man. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No problem, boss. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=339990#post339990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you for the explanation! I will search that book, the summary seems interesting! How is the writing quality? Good aswell?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> YMMV, but it might be a bit meandering/purplish at some points, and the female lead might come across as angsty to some. That being said, it's a solid read and it's set in medieval Romania, so you might get some ideas from it for Dark Era chronicles. A good book for the wolf/xenofiction lover. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T15:23:47-08:00","id":341266,"title":"","content":"Since the spirits speak Sumerian, I'm wondering if the Uratha should call Luna by his/her Sumerian name instead, being that the original is Greco-Roman. I saw on an earlier post that the word might be &quot;Idulth&quot;. Should the patron deity of the Uratha be called Idulth for Second Edition then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T15:51:35-08:00","id":341289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=341266#post341266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the spirits speak Sumerian, I'm wondering if the Uratha should call Luna by his/her Sumerian name instead, being that the original is Greco-Roman. I saw on an earlier post that the word might be &quot;Idulth&quot;. Should the patron deity of the Uratha be called Idulth for Second Edition then?</div> </div> </div> </div>To repeat: they speak a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constructed_language\" target=\"_blank\">conlang</a> called &quot;the First Tongue&quot; that was developed largely by taking Ancient Sumerian and running the words through a reversal of the processes of <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grimm%27s_law\" target=\"_blank\">Grimm's law</a>. Mother Luna's First Tongue name has been <i>Amahan Iduth</i> <a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/wtf1ecorep19.png\" target=\"_blank\">since the 1e corebook.</a> To repeat once more: this is not new \u2014 the First Tongue has been this way for the entirety of Werewolf: the Forsaken's printed run so far.<br /> <br /> She is still likely to be referred to with human-language sobriquets like Luna, Tsukuyomi, or the Warden Moon as well for the foreseeable future, because conlangs are tricky business and having a point of common comparison with existing mythology for newcomers to the game, but her First Tongue name is only likely to change in terms of 2e's increased fluidity of gendered-pronoun presentation.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sikla, would you happen to have a First Tongue translation for &quot;Warden&quot; on-hand?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T16:20:54-08:00","id":341318,"title":"","content":"<i>Ennu</i> is the obvious choice for 'Warden' but there may be a more poetic word to use instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T16:50:13-08:00","id":341332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=341289#post341289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sikla, would you happen to have a First Tongue translation for &quot;Warden&quot; on-hand?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe I do. I will search my archives and post when I find it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=341318#post341318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Ennu</i> is the obvious choice for 'Warden' but there may be a more poetic word to use instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>OH MY GOD A DEV POSTED IN MY THREAD \u2014<br /> <br /> *ceases fangirling*<br /> <br /> Ahem. ^^; But yeah, &quot;ennu&quot; works for all purposes, so go with that. I will come up with something more poetic and symbolic for things like packs and fetishes, but in all instances, <b>the word of God trumps mine.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T06:38:43-08:00","id":341847,"title":"","content":"Here's something I've been holding off on requesting, but now that you're back!<br /> <br /> I'd like the deedname Fury-Forged-By-Storm translated into First Tongue, please. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","name":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T10:39:35-08:00","id":342081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ursufgutha Storm-Born</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=341847#post341847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's something I've been holding off on requesting, but now that you're back!<br /> <br /> I'd like the deedname Fury-Forged-By-Storm translated into First Tongue, please. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've got almost all the words for that, so it'll be a quickie. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Just need some clarification: does the title suggest that he is inherently/his nature is mostly like the fury of the storm, or that the fury of the storm is just a major part of him?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T11:58:55-08:00","id":342122,"title":"","content":"Well, he is a Cahalith who Changed gazing into a gibbous moon amidst the eye of a literal storm, but I figure that the name is also metaphorical. The 'fury' is his passionate - and yes, angry - nature which can definitely run away from him once unleashed. The 'storm' is not singular, as it represents the multiple crises in his life by which he has been run ragged only to come out stronger each time, thereby forged.<br /> <br /> I hope that makes sense. XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3702-ursufgutha-storm-born","name":"Ursufgutha Storm-Born","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T12:01:31-08:00","id":342126,"title":"","content":"It does. I just needed to know how to handle the adjectives \u2014 with three different ways to do it, context means everything. xD Oh, the joys of languages!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T18:50:21-08:00","id":345307,"title":"","content":"For Pale_Crusader:<br /> <br /> Kidnap Crew: Luzudu-Ulurdum (&quot;the pack that has a kidnapping strategy as second nature&quot;)<br /> Tooth and Nail: Kukanzuthud (&quot;warriors of tooth and talon&quot;) or Kukumfinhud (&quot;warriors of tooth and claw&quot;); second is better for Pure<br /> Twisted Licks: Sursharsuuf (&quot;the many licks that twist around&quot;)<br /> Torrent-of-the-Forest: Thir-Kasagardagakurum (&quot;great mud river of the forest&quot;)<br /> Fistful of Dollars: Guzenthima-Farakdu (&quot;money brawler&quot;)<br /> Shanty-Hovel: Haf-Thirikag-Garum (&quot;undesirable and falling-down house&quot;)<br /> Ass-Biter: Skedu-Kukagul (&quot;crapmaker-biting one&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T19:01:33-08:00","id":346314,"title":"","content":"How do you say Dirt Scratcher in the first tongue?<br /> <br /> <br /> Going to name my Werechickens after it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T19:11:03-08:00","id":346316,"title":"","content":"Why are they called Dirt Scratchers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T19:22:15-08:00","id":346323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=346316#post346316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are they called Dirt Scratchers?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's what chickens do. Also they're going to have some relation to farming and agriculture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T19:29:09-08:00","id":346331,"title":"","content":"Right, going to add that to my list. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For Storm-Born:<br /> <br /> Shariminbharduthdur: Fury-Forged-By-Storm (lit. &quot;many-storm-forged-made-rage-child&quot;)<br /> <br /> Still working on other translations; in the meantime, have these while I finish the other requests. If these have FT terms anywhere, please let me know:<br /> <br /> hithdum: A fetish; a spirit-touched object<br /> <br /> Hisilthimir dur: &quot;Shadow-forgetting one&quot; \u2014 a wolf that doesn't cross over into the Hisil, is physically unable to, or forgets how; the spirit equivalent is &quot;Hisilthimir hith&quot;, and the non-werewolf equivalent is &quot;Hisilthimir ul&quot;<br /> <br /> Gurihalthimir dur: &quot;Flesh-forgetting one&quot; \u2014 the opposite of the above entry, it is a wolf that cannot or does not leave the Shadow. Spirit equivalent is &quot;Gurihalthimir hith&quot;, and non-werewolf cases are &quot;Gurihalthimir ul&quot;.<br /> <br /> Urhisilinti: &quot;Wolves that walk the Shadow's way&quot; \u2014 a wolf of Primal Urge 5+ or greater that increasingly must stay near locuses or in the Shadow to even exist. Those that have left for the Shadow entirely are called &quot;Uzakal Urhisilinti&quot;.<br /> <br /> Shargus: &quot;Many-skins&quot; \u2014 refers to a werewolf with multiple, non-werewolf forms via a fetish or something like the Anybeast gift, or a shapeshifting entity with multiple forms; a skindancer who uses multiple animal skins to change form<br /> <br /> ur ina hidum gus: &quot;wolf in an animal skin&quot; \u2014 werewolf with the Anybeast power that sticks to one or two forms, or a werewolf currently in its Anybeast form<br /> <br /> Hisiligim: The effect on one's eyes when they use Two-World Eyes or gaze into the Shadow; the death equivalent is &quot;Hissigim&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","us