n-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T06:44:53-08:00","id":346608,"title":"","content":"Sooo... i know i said i would be quiet some time, but the other day some inspiration struck, and well, i got some new words for you, Sikla. <br /> <br /> Last Whisper<br /> The Gates of Silence / The Quiet Gates<br /> Twin Mountains<br /> Red Gulch <br /> <br /> PS. I'll have my &quot;The Sight&quot; copy by the end of next week. I'll tell you how i like it then <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T07:01:54-08:00","id":346640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=346527#post346527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thanks for the reminder! I almost forgot about those. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Those were the war ones, right?<br /> <br /> Also: <a href=\"http://www.fluentin3months.com/roll-your-r/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.fluentin3months.com/roll-your-r/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. ^_^ Near the bottom of the page, last couple of posts, I think.<br /> <br /> <br /> By the way, what method are you using to create the language? Is it completely custom designed, or is there inspiration from RL languages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T08:17:29-08:00","id":346669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=346608#post346608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sooo... i know i said i would be quiet some time, but the other day some inspiration struck, and well, i got some new words for you, Sikla.<br /> <br /> Last Whisper<br /> The Gates of Silence / The Quiet Gates<br /> Twin Mountains<br /> Red Gulch<br /> <br /> PS. I'll have my &quot;The Sight&quot; copy by the end of next week. I'll tell you how i like it then <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh yay! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If you like it, it's part of a loose trilogy by the same author. The first is &quot;Firebringer&quot;, the last is &quot;Fell&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=346640#post346640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep. ^_^ Near the bottom of the page, last couple of posts, I think.<br /> <br /> <br /> By the way, what method are you using to create the language? Is it completely custom designed, or is there inspiration from RL languages?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sumerian run backwards through Grimm's Law, with bits of grammar filched from the books and based on RL Sumerian (thanks An Fhuiesog!). It's not completely perfect Sumerian grammar because a) I didn't get a keep-it-simple-stupid method of going about it, as every source I had was technobabble, and b) I wanted to have the feel of a weirdly poetic proto-language, which is what the devs went for. It's full of metaphors and constructions that disappeared when it evolved into the human-friendly offshoot we all know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T15:23:26-08:00","id":353176,"title":"","content":"Anyway I could get Reap-The-Whirlwind translated?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3777-the-scorpion","name":"The Scorpion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T17:05:24-08:00","id":353269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Scorpion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=353176#post353176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway I could get Reap-The-Whirlwind translated?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've added that to the list of stuff I'm working on. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T19:05:20-08:00","id":353342,"title":"","content":"Can you add something like Victory-over-Aberration translated? It's the name of a spirit of scapegoating I have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T08:01:06-08:00","id":354728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=353342#post353342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you add something like Victory-over-Aberration translated? It's the name of a spirit of scapegoating I have.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That I can do! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T00:28:59-08:00","id":356370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=341289#post341289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To repeat: they speak a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constructed_language\" target=\"_blank\">conlang</a> called &quot;the First Tongue&quot; that was developed largely by taking Ancient Sumerian and running the words through a reversal of the processes of <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grimm%27s_law\" target=\"_blank\">Grimm's law</a>. Mother Luna's First Tongue name has been <i>Amahan Iduth</i> <a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/wtf1ecorep19.png\" target=\"_blank\">since the 1e corebook.</a> To repeat once more: this is not new \u2014 the First Tongue has been this way for the entirety of Werewolf: the Forsaken's printed run so far.<br /> <br /> She is still likely to be referred to with human-language sobriquets like Luna, Tsukuyomi, or the Warden Moon as well for the foreseeable future, because conlangs are tricky business and having a point of common comparison with existing mythology for newcomers to the game, but her First Tongue name is only likely to change in terms of 2e's increased fluidity of gendered-pronoun presentation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, when I read the book, she was only called Luna in the text. This is the first time that I heard the name &quot;Amahan Idulth&quot;. So what you are telling me is that Werewolf's definition of spirits and the spirit definitions of Mages are BOTH correct? If so, then I am relieved. For a moment there, I thought that there would be a spiritual race war due to grammar.<br /> <br /> Also, what the hell is Grimm's Law? That's the first time I heard of that too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T00:31:56-08:00","id":356371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=356370#post356370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh, when I read the book, she was only called Luna in the text. This is the first time that I heard the name &quot;Amahan Idulth&quot;. So what you are telling me is that Werewolf's definition of spirits and the spirit definitions of Mages are BOTH correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>In a nutshell? Yes, in 1e. 2e has yet to show if that remains the same. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If so, then I am relieved. For a moment there, I thought that there would be a spiritual race war due to grammar. </div> </div> </div>Trust me, there are plenty of other things that could cause a spiritual race war. The rights over a powerful loci that borders on mage-wolf territories is one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, what the hell is Grimm's Law? That's the first time I heard of that too. </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://people.uleth.ca/~daniel.odonnell/Tutorials/grimms-law-and-verners-law-notes\" target=\"_blank\">http://people.uleth.ca/~daniel.odonn...ners-law-notes</a> - For your notes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T02:20:15-08:00","id":356470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=356370#post356370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, when I read the book, she was only called Luna in the text. This is the first time that I heard the name &quot;Amahan Idulth&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>See pages 19, 22, 53, 160 in the corebook. That first one is the Lexicon, btw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T02:31:28-08:00","id":356472,"title":"","content":"I just realized something. These new &quot;Sumerian-ish&quot; terms? They were the original language that the werewolves used. Even though I only saw that language when they talked about the Auspices, I assumed that the First Tongue was something original that Onyx Path made for the game. By indicating what the language consists of, it totally brought me out of immersion for the game. It's like having your kid meet Mickey Mouse, and then after the meeting, you tell your kid that Mickey is actually a guy in a costume. <br /> <br /> That's why I was confused. I am so sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T08:04:03-08:00","id":356625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=356472#post356472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just realized something. These new &quot;Sumerian-ish&quot; terms? They were the original language that the werewolves used. Even though I only saw that language when they talked about the Auspices, I assumed that the First Tongue was something original that Onyx Path made for the game. By indicating what the language consists of, it totally brought me out of immersion for the game. It's like having your kid meet Mickey Mouse, and then after the meeting, you tell your kid that Mickey is actually a guy in a costume.<br /> <br /> That's why I was confused. I am so sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's no problem! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> First Tongue IS something that Onyx Path made for the game, however. It's a conlang heavily based on a real-life lang to the point of leaning on it, but it's a conlang nonetheless, even if most of the words are Sumerian with a few sound changes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T00:28:23-08:00","id":358089,"title":"","content":"More translations for the New Year! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Still behind, though \u2014 if it's not here, I'm still working on it.<br /> <br /> Nyrufa:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Four options for &quot;the pack goes to war tonight&quot; if phrased poetically:<br /> <br /> &quot;Tonight we bloody our fangs!&quot;: Khilaske shakurdum kuk suthadu!<br /> &quot;Tonight we tear throat!&quot;: Khilaske shakurdum burdu keli!<br /> &quot;Tonight the Moon turns red!&quot;: Khilaske Iduth suthadu!<br /> &quot;Tonight is a night of rattling howls!&quot;: Khilaske kal kuluskirkhil!<br /> <br /> &quot;The pack goes to war tonight.&quot;: &quot;Urdum ina hafaldu khilase.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You are beneath my notice.&quot;: &quot;Nuku kal igim thirikdu ina ku.&quot; (lit. &quot;You fall beneath my gaze.&quot;)<br /> <br /> &quot;You cannot stop my vengeance now!&quot;: &quot;Nuku nuhalithakase ku nihhina-kakana!&quot; (lit. &quot;You cannot stop now my call for justice!&quot;)<br /> <br /> Dirt Scratchers: Sagardur-Karam (&quot;dirt-child birds&quot;)</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> FallenEco:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Cursed Dance of the Rulers: Azithanir Elum (&quot;the song and dance/the play of the cursed kings&quot;)</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Phersus:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Last Whisper:<br /> Zal Dumuskir<br /> Zal-Dumuskir<br /> Zaldumuskir<br /> <br /> Gates of Silence/The Quiet Gates:<br /> Mekhar Thakkan<br /> Mekhar-Thakkan<br /> Mekhathakkan<br /> <br /> Twin Mountains:<br /> Min Hursakh<br /> Min-Hursakh<br /> Minhursakh<br /> <br /> Red (as in Red-Coloured) Gulch:<br /> Kusk Sagakuth<br /> Kusk-Sagakuth<br /> Kusagakuth<br /> <br /> Red (as in Bloody) Gulch:<br /> Suthar Sagakuth<br /> Suthar-Sagakuth<br /> Suthasagakuth</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 01-04-2015, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T10:28:17-08:00","id":358398,"title":"","content":"That was awesome, Sikla. thank you very, very much, and by the way, Happy New Year to you and all the rest!<br /> <br /> I don't know why, but the First Tongue (*cough*summerian*cough*) is so beautiful phonetically. Sounds primitive, but also poethical in a way. Loving also the sounds of &quot;Cursed Dance of the Rulers&quot; and &quot;Dirt Scratchers&quot;. I'd promise to be quiet for a time, but i think that would be lying... :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T15:27:51-08:00","id":358583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=358398#post358398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was awesome, Sikla. thank you very, very much, and by the way, Happy New Year to you and all the rest!<br /> <br /> I don't know why, but the First Tongue (*cough*summerian*cough*) is so beautiful phonetically. Sounds primitive, but also poethical in a way. Loving also the sounds of &quot;Cursed Dance of the Rulers&quot; and &quot;Dirt Scratchers&quot;. I'd promise to be quiet for a time, but i think that would be lying... :P</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't mind the requests, I really don't. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I get caught up with them eventually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T11:42:45-08:00","id":359347,"title":"","content":"While I'm working on a couple more translations, here are some new words featured in recent translations that I've yet to elaborate on:<br /> <br /> bhar: To forge something, or to fire something in a kiln<br /> bhur: Brightness, glow, spreading light<br /> bhurudh: Deep; to have depth<br /> dumuskir: A whisper or the act of whispering (lit. &quot;breezy-voice&quot;)<br /> gi'endhu: To step; to move<br /> igim: To gaze; to witness; to view<br /> min: Twin, dual, double; sameness or a copy<br /> nihhina-kakana: Revenge, vengeance (lit. &quot;a cry for justice&quot;)<br /> sharingi: A swarm; a horde; an undulating mass<br /> shaku: We (possessive form, &quot;ours&quot;, is &quot;shakag&quot;)<br /> shanuku: They (possessive form, &quot;theirs&quot;, is &quot;shanukag&quot;)<br /> zalag: Shine, brightness, glow; concentrated light, often said of intense light or sunlight \u2014 more universal than and directly related to the more lunar-oriented <i>zalah</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 01-05-2015, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T09:37:45-08:00","id":360246,"title":"","content":"Here are some astrological terms for you guys to flavour your games with. I'm still working on other translations, this is just to work out a few translating muscles that have been stagnating in my brain \u2014 I wanted to poetically challenge myself:<br /> <br /> <b>Aries</b>:<br /> <br /> - The Ram (English Name): <i>Ulkudhughal</i> (lit. &quot;The Sky Ram&quot;)<br /> - The Labourer (Babylonian Name): <i>Ulke-Lukunka</i> (lit. &quot;The Hireling of the Heavens&quot;), or <i>Anagarrath</i> (&quot;The Slave of Heaven&quot;) to the Pure<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Taurus</b><br /> <br /> - The Bull (English and Babylonian Name): <i>Malanabis</i> (lit. &quot;The Bull Made of Stars&quot;)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Gemini</b><br /> <br /> - The Twins (English Name): <i>Mindur-Ina-Malan</i> (lit. &quot;The Twin Children In the Stars&quot;)<br /> - The Great Shepherd and Twins (Babylonian Name): <i>Ur-Ina-Eren</i> (lit. &quot;The Wolf Amongst the Herd&quot;)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Cancer:</b><br /> <br /> - The Crab (English Name): <i>Kashumfin</i> (lit. &quot;The Great Crab&quot;)<br /> - The Tortoise (Babylonian Name): <i>Kanifuna</i> (lit. &quot;The Great Tortoise&quot;)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Leo</b><br /> <br /> - The Lion (English Name): <i>Nirsua</i> (lit. &quot;The Cat-King&quot;)<br /> - The Great Dog (Babylonian Name): <i>Iurhir-Ina-Usala Nuth</i> (lit. &quot;The Sleeping Dog&quot;)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Virgo:</b><br /> <br /> - The Virgin (English Name): <i>Guthirim</i> (lit. &quot;Purest Maiden&quot;)<br /> - The Furrow (Babylonian Name): <i>Amahadum</i> (lit. &quot;Mother's Den&quot;)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Libra:</b><br /> <br /> - The Scales (English and Babylonian Name):<i> Uthanga-Ladul</i> (lit. &quot;Helios's Balancer&quot; [the scales were sacred to the Sumerian sun god Shamash])<br /> - The Claws of the Scorpion (Purely Babylonian Name): <i>Suhu-Lalazagsag-Umfin</i> (lit. &quot;Scorpion's [Pain-Tails'] Claws&quot;)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Scorpio:</b><br /> <br /> - The Scorpion (English and Sumerian Name): <i>Suhu-Lalazagsi</i> (lit. &quot;Pain-Tail&quot;)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sagittarius:</b><br /> <br /> - The Archer (English Name): <i>Sharmalanag-Ti</i> (lit. &quot;Arrow of the Many Stars&quot;)<br /> - The Chief Ancestor/The God Nergal (Sumerian/Babylonian Name): <i>Urfarahag-Kuunag</i> (lit. &quot;The Shadow Cast by Urfarah&quot;)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Capricorn:</b><br /> <br /> - The Goat-Fish (English/Babylonian Name): Isibmas (lit. &quot;The Sacrificial Priest-Goat&quot; [Capricorn was used to mark the beginning of the winter solstice before the stars drifted])<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Aquarius:</b><br /> <br /> - The Water-Bearer (English Name): <i>Kakilludu</i> (lit. &quot;Bringer of Water&quot;)<br /> - The God Ea (Babylonian Name): <i>Namsillu-Nir</i> (lit. &quot;Lord of Watery Deaths&quot; [Aquarius was negatively associated with dangerous flooding, and the FT name is...less flattering than the human one])<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Pisces:</b><br /> <br /> - The Fishes (English Name): <i>Minbu</i> (lit. &quot;The Twin Fish&quot;)<br /> - The Stag/The Great Swallow/The Tails (Babylonian Names [Pisces as we know it was originally part of a bunch of other constellations]: <i>Shul</i> (lit. &quot;The One of Many&quot; [referring to how Pisces has changed so much in its definition; to the werewolves, Pisces appears as a mercurial, almost Magath-like spirit])","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 01-07-2015, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T10:18:10-08:00","id":360277,"title":"","content":"So there are three spirits whose names I'd like to be translated.<br /> <br /> I've got a dissent spirit in my vampire game who's on the way to becoming the lord of the local spiritscape (city of Seattle and surrounding environs). Its name is Cracks-in-the-Wall, it mostly gained power from helping out the vampires of Seattle rebel against power structure and the Traditions.<br /> <br /> A powerful spirit near Mt. Rainier/Cinebar, Washington is a spirit of cinnabar. Basically it's a king or a duke (I admit not knowing how spirit hierarchies are supposed to work, I'm making it up as I go along). Haven't quite figured a name out for it. Maybe Red-Earth-Rot, or Poison-Veined-Stone.<br /> <br /> Finally, there's a spirit of Inspiration (basically a Muse) protecting a nascent RPG publisher in Vancouver, Oregon. Its name is Seeds-The-Fertile-Soil, which I think is appropriately poetic.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance, I appreciate your good work. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T09:39:57-08:00","id":361394,"title":"","content":"Okay, so I had some <i>oooooold</i> translations that never got done, and some stuff that has to be redefined now that spirits have dev-made names. If someone could contact Seraph Kitty on here and tell them their translation is done, that would be grand:<br /> <br /> Redefined:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">athalim: A group of spirits in service to a totem or a group of shapeshifters or mages \u2014 though they may not be the group's patrons, they have some sort of loyalty or ties to the group, and do things for them</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> For Seraph Kitty:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">ram: udhughal (if not castrated)<br /> sheep: ulakhar (for ewes, lambs and castrated sheep)<br /> steadfast, loyal, devoted: zidh<br /> harthakhdul: world-walker, world-walking one; nomad, worldly traveller \u2014 &quot;Gurihathakhdul&quot; refers more to someone who's extensively travelled the physical world<br /> Hisithakhdul: one who has extensively travelled the Shadow, or roams it nomadically<br /> mi'imuth: Biracial, bicultural \u2014 a mix of two different parentages from things such as different ethnicities or clans<br /> Hisimuth: &quot;Shadow-blooded&quot;, i.e. someone with spiritual heritage<br /> uzuhith: A spirit in a physical, flesh-like form, such as a lust spirit taking the form of a handsome bachelor; plural is &quot;uzuhithim&quot;</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> More Elaborated Terms:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">lukanka: hireling, servant, labourer<br /> mas: a goat; a sacrificial animal<br /> suhu-lalazagsi: scorpion (lit. &quot;pain-tail&quot;)<br /> kuunag: a shadow, in reference to a shadow cast by an object or a being; this word inherently carries a definite article's specification of meaning, so something like <i>ur kuunag</i> means &quot;the wolf's shadow&quot;, instead of <i>ur ki'unag</i>, 