is.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">sikedu: web, net<br /> <br /> Webspinners:<br /> &quot;Spins webs&quot;<br /> Kath Sikedu<br /> Kath-Sikedu<br /> Kathsikedu<br /> <br /> &quot;Those that are spinning webs&quot;<br /> Kathdu Sikedu<br /> Kathdu-Sikedu<br /> Kathdusikedu<br /> <br /> Deep Ones:<br /> &quot;Many of the deep&quot;<br /> Shar Bhurudh<br /> Shar-Bhurudh<br /> Sharbhurudh<br /> <br /> &quot;Ones of the deep&quot;<br /> Bhurudh Ul<br /> Bhurudh-Ul<br /> Bhurudhul</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Misc. Reptile and Random Other Words (because I made a cat post):<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">musarana: frog, toad, amphibian<br /> na'iska: trickster, jester, fool<br /> nahag: extremist, barbarian; torturer; one who gives out extreme punishments or follows extreme Darwinism; sometimes used to refer to vicious &quot;secret police&quot;-type groups, such as those found among the Pure<br /> magal: memory, recall<br /> mesith: catch-all term for lizards<br /> aghumesgith: dinosaurs, prehistoric lizards; the name means &quot;dawn lizards&quot;<br /> minezi: reincarnation, past lives; the name means &quot;twice-lived&quot; and it can refer to the Past Lives mechanic of W:tA, the Mokole's Mnesis function, or just reincarnation in general<br /> halpa'egah: alligator<br /> samfasa: crocodiles \u2014 may also apply to crocodilians in general<br /> undegi: venomous lizards, or lizards with heavy bacteria counts in their mouth, like the komodo dragon \u2014 may also be known as &quot;mirska&quot;, though that name refers more to poisonous snakes<br /> sidra: a name for smaller crocodilians like caimans; the offspring of any crocodilian may also be known as sidra</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Wild Eyes:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">&quot;Nuku ina kurdumfathdu?&quot; - &quot;Will you marry me?&quot; (lit. &quot;Will you come and find a den with me?&quot;)<br /> <br /> &quot;Nuku thamnamdu ku?&quot; - &quot;Will you marry me?&quot; (less poetic, more literal translation)</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 01-21-2015, 12:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T12:37:54-08:00","id":372805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href