me":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T14:45:27-08:00","id":419345,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not sure I\u2019d go with the six-pointed star for an indicator of whose holy book it (the Torah) is. Perhaps\u2026 \u201cThe holy book that is a Tree of Life\u201d? Or \u201cThe holy book received at the mountain\u201d? The magen david seems like something irrelevant to the book itself, you know?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":2192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","user":"Heu","date":".  context! 02-25-2015, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T14:55:17-08:00","id":419358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=419345#post419345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not sure I\u2019d go with the six-pointed star for an indicator of whose holy book it (the Torah) is. Perhaps\u2026 \u201cThe holy book that is a Tree of Life\u201d? Or \u201cThe holy book received at the mountain\u201d? The magen david seems like something irrelevant to the book itself, you know?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;The Holy Book Received At the Mountain&quot; makes a lot more sense, actually. I think I'll change it to that, thank you very much for the suggestions! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T17:40:39-08:00","id":419622,"title":"","content":"More kennings. 31/101 translated in total as of this post:<br /> <br /> idutha: &quot;moon-way&quot; = the sky<br /> dumuzal: &quot;wind-end&quot; = calm weather<br /> muth-izi: &quot;fire of blood&quot; = weapons<br /> iduth-tuf: &quot;moon-struck&quot; = a fool<br /> kelidar = &quot;throat-crusher&quot; = &quot;strangler&quot; = a wolf<br /> kafronthir = &quot;sea-pig&quot; = a whale<br /> imin-ayalu = &quot;deer of the storm&quot; = a ship<br /> emetha = &quot;land of the tongue&quot; = speech<br /> thima'na = &quot;thought stone&quot; = &quot;mind-stone&quot; = the heart<br /> shaduksium-uth: &quot;shields' sun&quot; = a sword","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T22:49:08-08:00","id":419862,"title":"","content":"Pretty funny, the word used in Sweden today for wolf, 'varg', is originally a kenning. 'Varg' means pretty much 'reaver'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T06:46:52-08:00","id":420111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=419862#post419862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty funny, the word used in Sweden today for wolf, 'varg', is originally a kenning. 'Varg' means pretty much 'reaver'.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The word for a bear has something similar in several languages. The French name for a fox, &quot;renard&quot;, is also an example of this phenomenon \u2014 it's taken from the name of a talking fable version of the animal. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> More kennings, 41/101 now translated:<br /> <br /> Ur-Rihdu: &quot;feeder of the wolf&quot; = the god Tyr<br /> Uthumamu-Farah: &quot;father of raging beasts&quot; = &quot;father of monsters&quot; = the god Loki<br /> Manamzu-Uhamusenir: &quot;greatly wise raven lord&quot; = &quot;all-wise raven ruler&quot; = the god Odin<br /> Kusk-Zum: &quot;red-beard&quot; = the god Thor<br /> Kaulum-Ul: &quot;the greatly-fruitful one&quot; = &quot;the fruitful&quot; = the god Freyr<br /> Uthanna-Erdu: &quot;crier of gold&quot; = the god Freyja<br /> Ilimmahan-Mu'u'adur: &quot;son of nine mothers&quot; = the god Heimdall<br /> Badu-Ilalum: &quot;founder of songs&quot; = &quot;first maker of poetry&quot; = the god Bragi<br /> Harnir-Nidur: &quot;daughter of the earth&quot; = &quot;daughter of <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Fj\u00f6rgynn&quot; = the goddess Frigg<br /> Skekhesir-Nir: &quot;lady of the snowshoes&quot; = the goddess Skadi</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> And some derived terms from the kennings, plus a few others:<br /> <br /> ilalum: poetry, ballads, songs, hymns; the spoken word<br /> gah: mouth, jaws, gullet<br /> gislak: a clearing; a cleared piece of land<br /> lulafuna: a cloak<br /> nihunua: a thread, a string<br /> umamu: beasts, animals; monsters as a whole may be known as &quot;uthumamu&quot;<br /> anah: a drink<br /> gu'ur: wood, logs<br /> ersu: a bed; a place to sleep<br /> ulum: to be fruitful; to be fertile<br /> unu: hall<br /> Hafaferunu: Valhalla (lit. &quot;hall of the battle-chosen&quot;)<br /> esir: shoe<br /> skekhesir: snowshoe<br /> zum: beard, facial hair<br /> feru: to choose, to pick specifically, to take as part of privilege<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Harnir = the earth deity Fj\u00f6rgynn (feminine form is Haramahan)</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 03-29-2015, 11:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T07:17:23-08:00","id":420135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=420111#post420111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The word for a bear has something similar in several languages. The French name for a fox, &quot;renard&quot;, is also an example of this phenomenon \u2014 it's taken from the name of a talking fable version of the animal. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I know the Russian word for bear is something along with honey-eater.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=420111#post420111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sutharzi-Unu: Valhalla (lit. &quot;hall of reaped souls&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>This kinda gives the wrong impression. Reaping implies that humans are like the straws of wheat in a field, to be taken as a group, Valhalla is literally &quot;the hall of the chosen&quot;, it was a specific privilege to be taken by the valkyries.<br /> <br /> That said, would you mind if I asked for a few specific kennings? For some variation with the gods.<br /> <br /> I'd like to know how to translate &quot;The masked one&quot; and &quot;the gallows-god&quot;, for Odin, and &quot;Lady of the slain&quot; for Freyja, if you please. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T07:19:12-08:00","id":420137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=420135#post420135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, would you mind if I asked for a few specific kennings? For some variation with the gods.<br /> <br /> I'd like to know how to translate &quot;The masked one&quot; and &quot;the gallows-god&quot;, for Odin, and &quot;Lady of the slain&quot; for Freyja, if you please. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I can do that! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And yeah...the name for Valhalla doesn't seem to fit. I read the English translation wrong. Gonna go fix that!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T07:54:54-08:00","id":420171,"title":"","content":"Also! I don't mean to be demanding, but could you do something like &quot;The hall of the Lady&quot;, for Sessrumnir? Freyja's equivalent of Valhall?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T10:10:52-08:00","id":420407,"title":"","content":"Certainly! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You're not being demanding at all! We're getting a new setting, we need terminology!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T16:59:16-08:00","id":422316,"title":"","content":"Kennings for Seidrmadr:<br /> <br /> The Masked One (Odin): Muni-Ina-Ikhi-Gataf (lit. &quot;the man in a mask&quot;)<br /> The Gallows-God (Odin): Namsusdhur-Ulkenir (lit. &quot;the sky-lord of the death-ropes&quot;)<br /> The Lady of the Slain (Freyja): Hafanamsu-Nir (lit. &quot;the lady of the battle-dead&quot;)<br /> Sessrumnir: Kamunu-Shadushgi (lit. &quot;the great, beautiful hall of many sitting-places&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 02-27-2015, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T17:16:25-08:00","id":422330,"title":"","content":"If I may make a few requests...<ul><li>&quot;Throne-Mother of the Gods&quot;</li> <li>&quot;Death-Priests of the South&quot;</li> <li>&quot;Evening Spirit of Blood&quot;</li> <li>&quot;The Never-Caught-Prey&quot;</li> <li>&quot;Lord of Divine Words&quot;</li> <li>&quot;Eaters of the World&quot;, Devourers?; looking for something better than<i> 'Agalu Har'</i> or '<i>Agalu Haresi'</i> . Might need a different phrase...</li> <li>&quot;Kings of Non-Dreams&quot;, undreams? antidreams?</li> <li>&quot;Those who Returned Shared&quot;</li> <li>&quot;the Burning Sands&quot;</li> <li>&quot;Pits of Hungry Death&quot;</li> <li>&quot;Slayer of the Lord of Chaos&quot;</li> </ul><br /> Thank you for your time. Don't worry about not getting to this for a while.<br /> What you've done so far is amazing!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":".  attempting self-help 02-27-2015, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T13:21:51-08:00","id":423364,"title":"","content":"Are there any go-to words for &quot;genius&quot; or &quot;scout&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T17:58:00-08:00","id":425872,"title":"","content":"54/105 kennings now translated (including Seidrmadr's):<br /> <br /> giazu-athal: &quot;secret-sharer&quot; = a friend<br /> hasthaf-namsigir: &quot;holds wise words firmly&quot; = &quot;wielder of counsel&quot; = a wise man<br /> irillu-su: &quot;melting body&quot; = &quot;melting one&quot; = a weak man<br /> matha-nazarul: &quot;land warder&quot; = a king<br /> ur-anah: &quot;drink of the wolf&quot; = blood<br /> garum-nidu: &quot;girl of the houses&quot; = a wife<br /> dagukurum-hirfathra: &quot;river-bone&quot; = a rock<br /> endenag-asde kasinfu: &quot;winter spear&quot; = an icicle<br /> hafadur: &quot;children of battle&quot; = soldiers or warriors<br /> nusuthikhi: &quot;no blood-drenched face&quot; = &quot;un-blooded&quot; = one not yet tested in battle<br /> <br /> And derived words:<br /> <br /> giazu: to share, to divide, to allot<br /> athal: a secret<br /> hasthaf: to hold firmly; to wield; to have at the ready<br /> namsigir: counsel, advice<br /> irillu: to melt, to become a liquid; to lose composure, to break down emotionally (lit. &quot;water-manifest&quot;)<br /> nazaru: a guard, a protector; a warden, a watchman; the act of watching or protection","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T09:13:46-08:00","id":426624,"title":"","content":"I have another translation that I\u2019d like, if you have time: Chaplain. Like the religious leaders for military units. Implication of counselor and warrior as well as priest(ess, in this case). It\u2019s for a Cahalith Blood Talon, if that helps you understand the angle I\u2019m coming from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T12:11:08-08:00","id":426791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=426624#post426624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have another translation that I\u2019d like, if you have time: Chaplain. Like the religious leaders for military units. Implication of counselor and warrior as well as priest(ess, in this case). It\u2019s for a Cahalith Blood Talon, if that helps you understand the angle I\u2019m coming from.</div> </div> </div> </div>The word you're looking for is <b>Isib</b>, which means &quot;priest&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That's the more generic term, though; what you probably want is <b>Hafal-Isib</b>, which literally means &quot;war priest&quot;. Does that work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""