eed some more excitement in their lives. Or Rahu, if you need to peel someone off of them....</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the advice. I'll probably throw this stuff up on Sunday, as it's getting uncomfortably late here, and I'll be busy tomo- well, today and tomorrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T13:47:09-08:00","id":430562,"title":"","content":"Hey, Sikla! I tend to be pretty good at putting your dictionary to good use, but I can't find these and I'd like your opinion:<br /> <br /> &quot;grace&quot; (&quot;aplomb&quot;)<br /> &quot;under&quot; (&quot;below&quot;, &quot;sub&quot;)<br /> &quot;pressure&quot; (&quot;gravity&quot;, &quot;weight&quot;).<br /> <br /> And then the whole phrase as you'd write it: &quot;grace under pressure&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'll probably have a tone more later. I did some back in the day and I'll put them up here for you to plunder. I think I have &quot;nerd rage&quot; somewhere. XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T14:16:40-08:00","id":430600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gebbethine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=430562#post430562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, Sikla! I tend to be pretty good at putting your dictionary to good use, but I can't find these and I'd like your opinion:<br /> <br /> &quot;grace&quot; (&quot;aplomb&quot;)<br /> &quot;under&quot; (&quot;below&quot;, &quot;sub&quot;)<br /> &quot;pressure&quot; (&quot;gravity&quot;, &quot;weight&quot;).<br /> <br /> And then the whole phrase as you'd write it: &quot;grace under pressure&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'll probably have a tone more later. I did some back in the day and I'll put them up here for you to plunder. I think I have &quot;nerd rage&quot; somewhere. XD</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sweet! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Any and all contributions are most appreciated. I'll see what I can do about these.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T15:54:48-08:00","id":430716,"title":"","content":"Does &quot;afuruskum&quot; or &quot;afurusum&quot; mean medicine?<br /> Got a bit behind on my doc. whoops. ;P I switched out the English Translation to a new doc (which is still linked) just so I wouldn't clutter up the other one. Still all WIP.<br /> ... Man, I really need to figure out a good way to format all this information so it's easy to access. xP<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All Things Strive.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4708-litheon","name":"Litheon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T16:56:43-08:00","id":430831,"title":"","content":"These are deed-names, so I fudged and sort of crushed them together, took out vowels or syllables to merge them, etc, buuuuuut--<br /> <br /> Izidumaskh (One-Who-Smokes; Smoker)<br /> Nighzuduruth (Nerd Rage; lit. baby-knowledge fury)<br /> Urhursathra (Sword-Up-Your-Ass, lit. Sword-in-Spine).<br /> Burskirizu (Broken-Voiced Thief).<br /> Kamuzhuhilask (Epic Face-Palm)<br /> Nukanunnhishun (He Who Serves -- as in 'you got served, boooooy!')","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T17:02:06-08:00","id":432006,"title":"","content":"@gebbethine: These don't look half-bad. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I can clean them all up, if you want, to match the grammatical rules I <s>sort of</s> have laid out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> @Litheon: That should be &quot;afurusum&quot;. The one with &quot;sk&quot; is a typo on my part. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> As for formatting \u2014 spreadsheet?<br /> <br /> And...well, I came up with this after I noticed I've started referring to the Werewolf fandom as a whole: <b>Ki'u'nadum</b>. It means &quot;The Onyx Pack&quot;, as <b>ki'u'na</b> means &quot;night-stone&quot;, referring to dark stones like onyx or obsidian. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T18:54:25-08:00","id":432109,"title":"","content":"You can if you want, but as Deed Names, I'm not too worried. I'm much more interested in your take on my request further up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T18:55:14-08:00","id":432110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gebbethine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=432109#post432109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can if you want, but as Deed Names, I'm not too worried. I'm much more interested in your take on my request further up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Duly noted! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T10:18:30-07:00","id":432713,"title":"","content":"Hey! I'd like to drop yet another request here!<br /> How would you translate &quot;Joy-of-fights&quot;, with a brawling emphasis here. It's supposed to be the name of a spirit who feeds off of the mostly good-spirited fighting at a rather run-down bar. (It's really a nice guy, who tends to use it's numina to speed up the healing of anyone who is too badly hurt, after all, if they are badly hurt, they can't keep fighting...)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T12:12:49-07:00","id":432911,"title":"","content":"I don't know if this strictly falls under the purview of First-Tonge translation, but it seems on-point enough that it's worth asking here. Can I get an &quot;in-character&quot; etymology for <i>Gauru</i>? I know the lexicon term is a throwback to the name Werewolves used for themselves in Apocalypse, and I assume Apocalypse derived it from the French <i>Loup-Garou</i>, though I may be mistaken there. But in-game I'm at a loss... All the other forms translate to things like true-human, near-human, near-wolf, and true-wolf, and Gauru seems like a bit of an outlier with those naming conventions, and I'm at a loss for what the literal meaning would be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-08-2015, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T12:28:42-07:00","id":432938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=432911#post432911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if this strictly falls under the purview of First-Tonge translation, but it seems on-point enough that it's worth asking here. Can I get an &quot;in-character&quot; etymology for <i>Gauru</i>? I know the lexicon term is a throwback to the name Werewolves used for themselves in Apocalypse, and I assume Apocalypse derived it from the French <i>Loup-Garou</i>, though I may be mistaken there. But in-game I'm at a loss... All the other forms translate to things like true-human, near-human, near-wolf, and true-wolf, and Gauru seems like a bit of an outlier with those naming conventions, and I'm at a loss for what the literal meaning would be.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Funny thing you mention that, I've got this worked out:<br /> <br /> Ga = gah, meaning &quot;mouth&quot; + Ur = wolf&quot;, U = &quot;gift, present&quot;<br /> <br /> Together, they make <i>Gauru</i>, which I translate as &quot;gift of the wolf's maw&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T12:40:19-07:00","id":432954,"title":"","content":"That is epic! Thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T22:01:12-07:00","id":436716,"title":"","content":"Whew, been awhile since I last visited. Been playing with the new book <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Sikla, I have a request from one of the other players in my game. Her character is playing as a were-spider, we've been using the normal werewolf names for her shapes, I was wondering if you could translate some more spider related ones? Oh! Also, another member of the pack got mutated into a were-owl when he allowed a Strix god thing ride in him to avert a gigantic catastrophe, so owl forms would be great too!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T22:05:30-07:00","id":436720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wild-Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=436716#post436716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whew, been awhile since I last visited. Been playing with the new book <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Sikla, I have a request from one of the other players in my game. Her character is playing as a were-spider, we've been using the normal werewolf names for her shapes, I was wondering if you could translate some more spider related ones? Oh! Also, another member of the pack got mutated into a were-owl when he allowed a Strix god thing ride in him to avert a gigantic catastrophe, so owl forms would be great too!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What kind of terms are you pals looking for? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> A bit of direction helps narrow down the translations into something useful. Sometimes, I literally stare at the screen until something pops into my head. @_@ My eyeballs....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T01:44:47-07:00","id":436827,"title":"","content":"Similar suggestion to Wild-Eyes but more specific. May help him. How about nWoD names for the oWoD Werespider forms? I can't find the &quot;casual&quot; names for them, just the fancy ones so here goes:<br /> <br /> Homid = Human<br /> Lilian = Hybrid Form that varies wildly between different oWoD Werespiders. (Some could be like the <a href=\"http://elderscrolls.wikia.com/wiki/Spider_Daedra_%28Oblivion%29?file=Beast_oblivion_spiderdaedra.png\" target=\"_blank\">Spider Daedra</a> from Oblivion, others have Spider heads and eight limbs but no spider adomen)<br /> Pithus = Giant Spider = (body mass of 500-700 pounds, but size varies depending on Spider form. A long legged small bodied one would have a two story leg span while a wolf-spider would be the size of a small car)<br /> Crawlerling = Swarm of Spiders (100 to 1000 spiders once again depending on species)<br /> <br /> Not sure if you need or want the details, but I figured they wouldn't hurt.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately this wouldn't translate over 100% to Wild-Eyes request since it sounds like his player as 5 forms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T10:23:47-07:00","id":437197,"title":"","content":"If it hasn't been asked, what would be a good term for triggers, like something that causes a werewolf to rage?<br /> <br /> Also what would be a way to say 'red hood' like a hood someone might wear to conceal their identity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T11:37:26-07:00","id":437289,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Afro about has it right, I would like first tongue terms for those shifters equivalent forms. Each of these players has all five forms, they would all use Hishu of course, so I would need terms for near spider/owl, war spider/owl, and the actual spider/owl form. Now that I think of it, the Dalu form shouldn't need a new name since it's already &quot;near man&quot; thus the other animal it's getting closer to shouldn't be a factor. Oh, and yes, the spider's pure spider form is indeed a swarm of spiders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T05:43:56-07:00","id":445650,"title":"","content":"The players in one of the werewolf games that I'm starting up made up their totem last night: a Roadrunner. Turns out those little birds are <i>awesome</i>.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I looked up some wikifacts about the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geococcyx\" target=\"_blank\">Geococcyx</a> to get some good traits, etc..., and I found out that one of their names is &quot;Snake-killer&quot;.<br /> <br /> So for the totem, I thought I'd go with &quot;Snake eater&quot;. I don't need it translated, i just want to make sure I got it translated correctly:<br /> <br /> <b><u>Rih'mirska</u></b>. Should translate to &quot;eater of snakes&quot; if I've got that right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T06:15:30-07:00","id":445699,"title":"","content":"Dumuskirga'a <i>should</i> be Whisper(ing) Fox.<br /> <br /> But, do I need to conjugate Dumuskir?<br /> When will there be online courses for First Tongue grammar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T21:10:13-07:00","id":448806,"title":"","content":"I require a translation sir! For &quot;Wonderful One-Oh-One&quot; (and just &quot;One-Oh-One&quot; as the spirit in question prefers to be called).<br /> <br /> Because we decided that one of our friend's dice collection, numbering one hundred and one dice which he affectively calls the wonderful one-oh-one, has gotten big enough that one of them ate all the other tiny little spirits and now it became a Rank 1 spirit. Symbolically significant number and he gave it a name, therefor it works. It is the collective spirit of his dice collection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T12:41:25-07:00","id":450713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FlailBot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=445699#post445699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dumuskirga'a <i>should</i> be Whisper(ing) Fox.<br /> <br /> But, do I need to conjugate Dumuskir?<br /> When will there be online courses for First Tongue grammar?</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need to conjugate anything. It looks good as it is, thought if you want to indicate whispering as something ongoing or something he continuously does, it would be <b>Dumuskirduga'a</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And to be honest, I've never thought of putting up a course for it before!<br /> <br /> Will be getting to these requests as soon as I can, as well as the other kennings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T17:30:01-07:00","id":451102,"title":"","content":"One more request to pile on you (I'm so sorry!). Deed name for my Iron Master Elodoth, &quot;Honeyed-Lips-Bloodied-Tongue&quot;. I'd also love to know just &quot;Honey-Lips&quot; for more casual circumstances. The idea is that she's sweet and coaxing and can worm her way into anything, but she's not afraid of blackmail or other intimidation tactics, and both are very much a part of who she is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T17:58:43-07:00","id":451117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=450713#post450713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't need to conjugate anything. It looks good as it is, thought if you want to indicate whispering as something ongoing or something he continuously does, it would be <b>Dumuskirduga'a</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And to be honest, I've never thought of putting up a course for it before!<br /> <br /> Will be getting to these requests as soon as I can, as well as the other kennings.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Muchos gracias. I'm trying to capture both sneaking and cowardice, which I think whisper worked well for. It's also a play on <a href=\"http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leisefuchs\" target=\"_blank\">http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leisefuchs</a>, which is like a hand-sign for children to be quiet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T22:31:54-07:00","id":451314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FlailBot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=451117#post451117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Muchos gracias. I'm trying to capture both sneaking and cowardice, which I think whisper worked well for. It's also a play on <a href=\"http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leisefuchs\" target=\"_blank\">http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leisefuchs</a>, which is like a hand-sign for children to be quiet.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really clever! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Heu, your deed name has been added to my list.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T19:58:50-07:00","id":456508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=445650#post445650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The players in one of the werewolf games that I'm starting up made up their totem last night: a Roadrunner. Turns out those little birds are <i>awesome</i>.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I looked up some wikifacts about the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geococcyx\" target=\"_blank\">Geococcyx</a> to get some good traits, etc..., and I found out that one of their names is &quot;Snake-killer&quot;.<br /> <br /> So for the totem, I thought I'd go with &quot;Snake eater&quot;. I don't need it translated, i just want to make sure I got it translated correctly:<br /> <br /> <b><u>Rih'mirska</u></b>. Should translate to &quot;eater of snakes&quot; if I've got that right.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Rih'mirska is indeed right, but &quot;mirska&quot; is a term for poisonous snakes and things like dragons. If it eats any snakes, it's <b>Rih'usum</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T20:21:22-07:00","id":456522,"title":"","content":"*crawls back in*<br /> <br /> Usumgus-Nazaru: Snakeskin Wardens<br /> Dalag-Skir: The Warning Howl<br /> Zaggadul: Twitter the Bird-Spirit (lit. means &quot;The One Who Keeps Tweeting&quot;)<br /> <br /> umalas-gi'endhu: grace (lit. &quot;moves with care&quot;)<br /> aplomb: zikkir (lit. &quot;life-pride&quot;, i.e. &quot;self-confidence&quot;; k'kir is pride in the positive sense, and synonymous with things like good self-esteem, a job well done, etc.)<br /> ki'i: under, below<br /> pressure, weight: already translated as <b>gu'usu</b><br /> hargu'usu: gravity (lit. &quot;world-weight&quot;)<br /> <br /> Habalthag-Namhulif: Joy-of-Fights (lit. &quot;The Fight's Joyfulness&quot;)<br /> <br /> Hishu = Homid = Human<br /> Az'u = Spider-Gifted = Near-Spider Form<br /> Habathaz = Fighting Spider = Lilian<br /> Kazul = The Great Spider = Pithus<br /> Sharaz = Many-Spider = Crawlerling<br /> <br /> Hishu = Homid = Human<br /> Ninnadakh = Predator-Touched = Near-Human Form<br /> Ka-Ninna = Great Predator = War Form<br /> Taginna = Hunting Predator = Near-Owl Form<br /> Fa-Ninnahan = True Owl = Owl Form<br /> <br /> Sahk-Kusklulafuna: Red Hood<br /> sahk-lulafuna: hood (lit. &quot;head-cloak&quot;)<br /> <br /> Rumsar-As-Nas-As: Wonderful One-Oh-One (&quot;As&quot; [&quot;One&quot;] For Short)<br /> <br /> Guthtun-Suthemehir: Honeyed-Lips-Bloodied-Tongue (&quot;Guthtun&quot; for just &quot;Honey-Lips&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T08:30:25-07:00","id":456890,"title":"","content":"Thank you! How would you say, &quot;grace under pressure&quot; as a whole phrase, sticking as closely to its metaphorical meaning as possible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T09:00:16-07:00","id":456916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gebbethine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=456890#post456890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you! How would you say, &quot;grace under pressure&quot; as a whole phrase, sticking as closely to its metaphorical meaning as possible?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that would go something along the lines of <b>&quot;umalas-gi'endhu udhkalki'i gu'usu&quot;</b> \u2014 &quot;grace when you are under pressure&quot;. <b>Kal</b> has been affixed to <b>ki'i</b> to mark a state of being, and <b>udh</b> (which means &quot;when&quot;) marks the nature of that being. (I.e., it is what it is, it is who it is, it is when it is, etc.)<br /> <br /> Edit: Now that I think about it, I should probably put these down here for reference for myself and others later.<br /> <br /> <b>udh:</b> When, as in, &quot;When does this happen?&quot;<br /> <b>eanam:</b> What, as in, &quot;What is this?&quot;<br /> <b>aggil:</b> Where, as in, &quot;Where are we?&quot;<br /> <b>abha:</b> Who, as in, &quot;Who are you?&quot;<br /> <b>anash:</b> Why, as in, &quot;Why would you do that?&quot;<br /> <br /> Affixing these to the verb <b>kal</b> (to be) results in the following constructions:<br /> <br /> <b>udhkal</b>: &quot;When one is.../When they are....&quot;<br /> <b>eanamkal:</b> &quot;When what this is.../When what these are....&quot;<br /> <b>aggilkal:</b> &quot;When where this is.../When where these are....&quot;<br /> <b>abhakal:</b> &quot;When one who is..../When ones who are....&quot;<br /> <b>anaskal:</b> &quot;When why there is..../When why there are....&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 03-25-2015, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T09:14:28-07:00","id":456944,"title":"","content":"Many thanks for your work, Sikla!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-25-2015, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T09:17:01-07:00","id":456946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=456944#post456944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many thanks for your work, Silka!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not done yet. I'm working on a pronoun list because I just realized there's no definitive set of them I've laid out, and pronouns are important to a lot of languages. One sec.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T09:28:44-07:00","id":456962,"title":"","content":"The pronoun in First Tongue is like a spirit name: it is a summation of affixes and a stem that, in a nutshell, provides someone with what they're looking at while they address the subject. Pronouns in FT revolve mostly around &quot;what is me&quot; and &quot;what is not me&quot;, with further descriptors to specify what you are and what you aren't.<br /> <br /> <b>ku:</b> I, me, mine. The base of pretty much every pronoun that follows. Gender-neutral.<br /> <b>nuku:</b> You, yours. Literally means &quot;not-me&quot;. Gender-neutral, and may also be used for the <b>ze/<b>xe/xir/hir</b></b> third-pronoun in English to denote genderless/third-gender individuals.<br /> <b>muninuku:</b> He, him. Literally means &quot;not-me male&quot;.<br /> <b>nidunuku:</b> She, hers. Literally means &quot;not-me female&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>shakunuku:</b> We, us, ours. Literally means &quot;many-me-not-me&quot;. Gender-neutral. Place &quot;muni&quot; after the &quot;sha&quot; part to indicate &quot;we the males&quot;, or &quot;nidu&quot; to indicate &quot;we the females&quot;.<br /> <b>shanuku:</b> They, theirs. Literally means &quot;many-not-me&quot;. Gender-neutral. Place &quot;muni&quot; after the &quot;sha&quot; part to indicate &quot;they the males&quot;, or &quot;nidu&quot; to indicate &quot;they the females&quot;.<br /> <br /> And three corrections:<br /> <br /> With the release of 2e, <b>farah</b> as a term meaning &quot;father&quot; (and it's shortened form, <b>fafa</b>) is only used for very powerful divinities, such as Father Wolf. For spirits lower than Rank 4 and mundane creatures, we use the term <b>aya</b>, and its shortened form <b>a'a</b>. Idigam and totems do not follow this trend. Also, <b>aske</b> (which means &quot;now&quot;) should be spelt <b>ase</b>, but either spelling can do based on your preference. I will be using <b>ase</b> from now on. The word <b>zur</b>, which meant the same as <b>gathra</b> (chiminage) in 1e now refers to religious rites and offerings in general, and not specifically the gifts, offers and favours used in social maneuvering with spirits. Gathra is bribing a fire spirit with a giant forest fire if it joins your side \u2014 zur is leaving money in the collection plate at a Catholic mass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 03-25-2015, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T09:47:15-07:00","id":457003,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Sikla!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T12:22:53-07:00","id":457134,"title":"","content":"And some more useful words:<br /> <br /> <b>u'</b>: but, also, yet<br /> <b>u'nu:</b> nor<br /> <b>annakal:</b> because, for<br /> <b>gushashukaldu:</b> rather, rather than<br /> <b>minsur:</b> both<br /> <b>assur:</b> either<br /> <b>nussur:</b> neither<br /> <br /> And some stuff for FallenEco:<br /> <br /> <b>Dihimag-Huzamahan</b>: Throne-Mother of the Gods<br /> <b>Kanagmehu-Namsib:</b> Death-Priests of the South<br /> <b>Shurah-Muthim</b> or <b>Shurah-Suthim</b>: Evening Spirit of Blood (latter suggests a war-like spirit, or a spirit of spilt blood)<br /> <b>Nuah-Hespar-Nul:</b> The Never-Caught-Prey<br /> <b>Dufukag-Anbes-Nir:</b> Divine Lord of Words<br /> <b>Sharnuvisktha-Nir:</b> Kings of Non-Dreams<br /> <b>Izidu-Saragarul:</b> The Burning Sands<br /> <b>Rih-Namsu-Siduk:</b> Pits of Hungry Death<br /> <b>Thiknir-Usul:</b> Slayer of the Lord of Chaos<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>huza:</b> throne<br /> <b>nuah:</b> never, at no time<br /> <b>ni:</b> prey; food animal<br /> <b>shurah:</b> Sundown, sunset, dusk<br /> <b>setsethah:</b> Sunup, sunrise, dawn<br /> <b>shurin:</b> cricket<br /> <b>anbes:</b> holy, blessed, divine<br /> <b>saragar:</b> sand; dry, loose earth<br /> <b>saragh:</b> to be dry<br /> <b>dhuru:</b> to be wet","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 03-25-2015, 11:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T12:35:37-07:00","id":457182,"title":"","content":"Hey! Sorry if you've got too much on your plate, but I was curiois about something(might be useful if I ever get to play a member of the Lodge of the Redeemed). How would you translate John 3:16? You know, &quot;For God so loved the world that he sent His only begotten son, that whoever believes in him shall not perish, but have eternal life.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T12:51:03-07:00","id":457214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=457182#post457182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey! Sorry if you've got too much on your plate, but I was curiois about something(might be useful if I ever get to play a member of the Lodge of the Redeemed). How would you translate John 3:16? You know, &quot;For God so loved the world that he sent His only begotten son, that whoever believes in him shall not perish, but have eternal life.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sure! This is a quick one:<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Mathufarah su'us Muninukumu'u'adurul annakal kakiliteg Harul \u2014 thuabhakal damdu Muninukumu nu namsu, u' sar-nuku duhudu thurizi.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> And some elaborations:<br /> <br /> <b>thu:</b> All, everyone<br /> <b>Mathufarah:</b> &quot;Great Father of All&quot;, the FT name for the Christian God","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T21:13:00-07:00","id":457721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=457134#post457134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And some stuff for FallenEco:<br /> <br /> <b>Dihimag-Huzamahan</b>: Throne-Mother of the Gods<br /> <b>Kanagmehu-Namsib:</b> Death-Priests of the South<br /> <b>Shurah-Muthim</b> or <b>Shurah-Suthim</b>: Evening Spirit of Blood (latter suggests a war-like spirit, or a spirit of spilt blood)<br /> <b>Nuah-Hespar-Nul:</b> The Never-Caught-Prey<br /> <b>Dufukag-Anbes-Nir:</b> Divine Lord of Words<br /> <b>Sharnuvisktha-Nir:</b> Kings of Non-Dreams<br /> <b>Izidu-Saragarul:</b> The Burning Sands<br /> <b>Rih-Namsu-Siduk:</b> Pits of Hungry Death<br /> <b>Thiknir-Usul:</b> Slayer of the Lord of Chaos</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T12:11:27-07:00","id":458228,"title":"","content":"For Ephsy:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">&quot;Kal neha-hugunbanamm, nukukal, ina minsur nukuhabalthu nukuzi. Neha-hugubanamm nu kal nuzillumun-neha \u2014 neha-hugunbanamm kal gurginabis-neha. Kin sar-thidila nunamlughuth u' nunamnusahk, nukuzi gulumu u' nuthiguth. Nu nithubh-su abhakal neha-zi; nu na'aki-zi abhakal neha-su. Nihhinakal Zisilim.&quot;</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> For FallenEco, because I missed this:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Rihar-Kagagh:</b> Eaters of the World (lit. &quot;Great Jaws that Devour the World&quot; or &quot;Great Appetite that Devours the World&quot;)</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>hugunbanamm:</b> determination, determined, driven (lit. &quot;wholly willing&quot;)<br /> <b>za:</b> movement in general<br /> <b>umun:</b> a puddle; a patch of water<br /> <b>nuza:</b> unmoving, stagnant; unenergetic, lethargic; slowness, torpor<br /> <b>gagh:</b> the jaws or mouth of a predatory animal; a great appetite or hunger<br /> <b>gurgu:</b> a wave; a flood of water<br /> <b>bis:</b> a shore; a riverbank; the edge of a water body<br /> <b>lughuth:</b> tense, tight; drawn tight<br /> <b>nusahk:</b> to be uncaring; to be reckless<br /> <b>gulumu:</b> balanced, steady; to balance to steady oneself<br /> <b>nithubh:</b> relax, stretch out, laze about; to remove tenseness from something","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T15:36:34-07:00","id":458406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=456962#post456962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>shakunuku:</b> We, us, ours. Literally means &quot;many-me-not-me&quot;. Gender-neutral. Place &quot;muni&quot; after the &quot;sha&quot; part to indicate &quot;we the males&quot;, or &quot;nidu&quot; to indicate &quot;we the females&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>why isn't this just shanu?. What's the importance Specifying that we includes me?<br /> <br /> Also thanks for all your hard work!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T15:46:12-07:00","id":458408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FlailBot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=458406#post458406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> why isn't this just shanu?. What's the importance Specifying that we includes me?<br /> <br /> Also thanks for all your hard work!</div> </div> </div> </div>To show you're also part of that group. The power inherent in FT vocab is a lot stronger than any mortal language, so it's kind of like a guy who has all his titles listed off as a symbol of recognition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T19:26:21-07:00","id":458576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=458408#post458408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To show you're also part of that group. The power inherent in FT vocab is a lot stronger than any mortal language, so it's kind of like a guy who has all his titles listed off as a symbol of recognition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume that First Tongue between werewolves is pidgin First Tongue, and peppered with slang from their native languages, but Spirits maintain a&quot;pure&quot; dialect and that's what you've been doing.<br /> <br /> Plus my games feature a lot of language interplay and I like to have an excuse to pepper my werewolf speech with random English, Spanish, and German slang. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T20:04:19-07:00","id":458596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=458576#post458576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume that First Tongue between werewolves is pidgin First Tongue, and peppered with slang from their native languages, but Spirits maintain a&quot;pure&quot; dialect and that's what you've been doing.<br /> <br /> Plus my games feature a lot of language interplay and I like to have an excuse to pepper my werewolf speech with random English, Spanish, and German slang. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That is correct. The FT I'm using is what you'd find in a standard dictionary, and I have created specific werewolfy phrases and terminology before, along with noting where they are and where their usage falls. Pronunciation I don't have a firm grip on, but I know the books have noted it as &quot;rough&quot; and &quot;guttural&quot;, along with comparisons to Dutch and German in pronunciation. Which makes sense, as it's Sumerian run backwards through the process that turned PIE stop-consonants into Proto-Germanic ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T07:30:44-07:00","id":458992,"title":"","content":"<b>Mayeh'ren:</b> Promethean Disquiet<br /> <b>ithud:</b> the moons/satellite planetoids of other worlds; may also be known by the less formal (and more Earth-oriented) term &quot;nuduth&quot;<br /> <b>illusith:</b> boat, ship (lit. &quot;water-rider&quot;)<br /> <b>sith:</b> to ride; the act of riding<br /> <b>Urfarah-pakk:</b> First Tongue translation of the Uratha oath \u201cUrfarah\u2019s breath\u201d, which is roughly equivalent to \u201cgood God\u201d or \u201cdear God\u201d. A slightly more blasphemous version is Urfarag-pakk.<br /> <b>besthimadur:</b> psychics (lit. &quot;blessed thought children&quot;)<br /> <b>gaaliha:</b> a death sentence, an execution; a punishment that will end in the death of the one punished, or is meant to; an individual feared for being an unbeatable opponent<br /> <b>defir:</b> rites, spells or other powers that are meant to break wards, bindings and protective spells \u2014 their opposite is <b>efira</b><br /> <b>skargal:</b> cruelty, sadism; merciless, unforgiving<br /> <b>sasir:</b> a dividing force; a major schism in belief or politics; a problem or issue that splits apart a group, or causes resentment among their members<br /> <b>kekornis:</b> a familiar, such as those used by mages, witches and certain hunters of the Lucifuge group<br /> <b>inada:</b> sabotage; a saboteur<br /> <b>yul:</b> poison, venom, toxins<br /> <b>wasdum:</b> difficulty, adversity, misfortune; hostility<br /> <b>pataaku:</b> artwork; the arts as a whole; things created to be aesthetic<br /> <b>Ghalfros:</b> the Wargaz from 1e's <i>Mirrors</i> sourcebook<br /> <b>Anu:</b> the Atlanteans from 1e's <i>Mirrors</i> sourcebook<br /> <b>Namsuthdur:</b> the dhampyrs from 1e's <i>Mirrors</i> sourcebook and V:tR<br /> <br /> <br /> And before I forget, for BigDamnHero:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Pataaku-Ina-Wasdum</b>: Art-Through-Adversity</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 03-27-2015, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T07:40:05-07:00","id":459000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=458992#post458992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And before I forget, for BigDamnHero:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Pataaku-Ina-Wasdum</b>: Art-Through-Adversity</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, thanks!<br /> <br /> Not to sound greedy, but how would I change that up if I wanted to use it as a platitude or phrase? <b>&quot;Pataaku ina wasdum</b>&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T07:42:47-07:00","id":459001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=459000#post459000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Awesome, thanks!<br /> <br /> Not to sound greedy, but how would I change that up if I wanted to use it as a platitude or phrase? <b>&quot;Pataaku ina wasdum</b>&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>What you posted is exactly what you'd do. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T08:10:37-07:00","id":459013,"title":"","content":"64/105 kennings translated as of this post:<br /> <br /> <b>namatha-ina-gahuzu:</b> rocky islands in the mouth-meat = gum-skerries = teeth<br /> <b>uhamusen-rihdu:</b> one who is feeding ravens = feeder of ravens = a warrior<br /> <b>Makanir-Unudur:</b> Aegir's daughters = the waves<br /> <b>urag-rigsu:</b> the wolf's joint = the wrist<br /> <b>enden-akugum:</b> winter's blanket = snow<br /> <b>duksium-kukdu:</b> one who keeps biting shields = shield-gnawer = berserker<br /> <b>ithakusgidu-nidu:</b> bow-lady = a valkyrie<br /> <b>ansafdum-nihdugu:</b> ring-rich = a generous person<br /> <b>izi-gurgu:</b> burns the waves = igniter of waves = poison, or the bile of Jormungandr<br /> <b>abisdur:</b> cow-children = cattle-kin = people who can't defend themselves (considered derogatory)<br /> <br /> <br /> And derived terms:<br /> <br /> <b>gahuzu:</b> the gums (lit. &quot;mouth-meat&quot;)<br /> <b>Makanir:</b> FT name for Aegir, Norse god of the sea<br /> <b>rigsu:</b> joint, tie, binding; a joint on a skeleton<br /> <b>akugum:</b> blanket, quilt<br /> <b>nihdugu:</b> to be wealthy; to have plenty; to be rich<br /> <b>ansafdum:</b> a ring or earring","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T19:44:53-07:00","id":459609,"title":"","content":"Requesting translations for spirits called &quot;Runt&quot;, &quot;Grey-Mantle&quot;, &quot;Bone-That-Binds&quot;, and &quot;Father-Fortress&quot; please! The latter is the name of our pack Totem.<br /> <br /> Also &quot;We are the hammer!&quot; if you would be so kind, which is an evocative chant used by our pack during the Siskur-Dah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 03-27-2015, 10:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T21:08:56-07:00","id":459661,"title":"","content":"Ye, are you playing a pack of Maccabees?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T21:13:20-07:00","id":459663,"title":"","content":"Has anyone translated the Ithaeur's quote yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T06:35:08-07:00","id":459879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=459663#post459663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone translated the Ithaeur's quote yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to, but circumstances beyond my control mean that I have no known idea when I may be able to get 2e.<br /> <br /> YeofLittleFaith: On it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T07:05:17-07:00","id":459906,"title":"","content":"Translated!<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Shakunuku kal giragul!&quot;:</b> &quot;We are the hammer!&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Firdu-Farah</b> or <b>Dhuunum-Farah</b>: Father Fortress (for a Rank 5+ spirit; the latter doesn't have a strictly military connontation)<br /> <b>Firdu-Aya</b> or <b>Dhuunum-Aya</b>: Father Fortress (for anything below a Rank 5+ spirit; the latter doesn't have a strictly military connontation)<br /> <b>Esthadu-Hirfathra:</b> Bone-that-Binds (lit. &quot;bone that is binding&quot;)<br /> <b>Nafara-Lulafuna:</b> Grey-Mantle (lit. &quot;cloaked/mantled with/in grey&quot;)<br /> <b>skeru:</b> runt, weakling, whelp; the runt of the litter<br /> <b>dhuunum:</b> another name for a fortress, or any sort of large, impenetrable building; doesn't necessarily have to have the military connotation of <b>firdu</b><br /> <br /> And some random Mage words, just because:<br /> <br /> <b>Umfaras:</b> The Primal Wild, home of the <b>Sar Umfisan'na-Anzaghar</b>, or the Watchtower of the Stone Book<br /> <br /> <b>Pulhatas:</b> The Aether, home of the <b>Guzenheshla-Anzaghar</b>, or Watchtower of the Golden Key<br /> <br /> <b>Pilukas:</b> Arcadia, home of the <b>Idugukat-Anzaghar</b>, or the Watchtower of the Lunargent Thorn (and possibly the Fae)<br /> <br /> <b>Mapa'as:</b> Pandemonium, home of the <b>Anfarathi Kuth-Anzaghar</b>, or the Watchtower of the Iron Gauntlet<br /> <br /> <b>Zidigas:</b> Stygia, home of the <b>Anaguthima-Anzaghar</b>, or the Watchtower of the Lead Coin<br /> <br /> The Lone Watchtower is known as the <b>Numunamzu-Anzaghar</b>, which literally translates to &quot;the Watchtower of Nameless Wisdom&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 03-28-2015, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T10:23:54-07:00","id":460163,"title":"","content":"Super cool. Thanks again!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T10:27:22-07:00","id":460165,"title":"","content":"Those are great as aways, Sikla!<br /> <br /> Thanks for the bonus Mage terms, but it seems it will be called the Watchtower of the Singing Stone (rather than stone book) in 2nd edition, how would that be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T10:34:38-07:00","id":460172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=460165#post460165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those are great as aways, Sikla!<br /> <br /> Thanks for the bonus Mage terms, but it seems it will be called the Watchtower of the Singing Stone (rather than stone book) in 2nd edition, how would that be?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be <b>Skir'na-Anzaghar</b>, then. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: more Mage terms! (Changed slightly from the original to avoid repetition.)<br /> <br /> <b>Atumma:</b> Acanthus (lit. &quot;thorn-witches&quot;)<br /> <b>Anfar-Nammsithim:</b> Mastigos (lit. &quot;the iron willworkers&quot;)<br /> <b>Zalihdar:</b> Moros (lit. &quot;the end-sayers&quot;/&quot;the doomsayers&quot;)<br /> <b>Anunnhisib:</b> Obrimos (lit. &quot;priests of power&quot;)<br /> <b>Thufuzidu:</b> Thyrsus (lit. &quot;life-makers/&quot;those who make life sprout into being&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 03-28-2015, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T12:09:40-07:00","id":460268,"title":"","content":"Alright, I've got a bit of a challenge, Silka. My 2e wolf belongs to a cult of solar energy enthusiasts/environmental activist/(at the highest levels) outright sun-worshippers. The cult is called the Solarpunk Revolutionaries, after the solarpunk aesthetic going around. I could use translations for these terms:<br /> <br /> Solarpunk Revolutionaries (and just solarpunk)<br /> Sunhaven<br /> <br /> (Yes, I know how Helions feel about wolves. 1. my wolf joined before her First Change. 2. most members are human)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T13:18:33-07:00","id":460363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=460268#post460268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, I've got a bit of a challenge, Silka. My 2e wolf belongs to a cult of solar energy enthusiasts/environmental activist/(at the highest levels) outright sun-worshippers. The cult is called the Solarpunk Revolutionaries, after the solarpunk aesthetic going around. I could use translations for these terms:<br /> <br /> Solarpunk Revolutionaries (and just solarpunk)<br /> Sunhaven<br /> <br /> (Yes, I know how Helions feel about wolves. 1. my wolf joined before her First Change. 2. most members are human)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a challenge for me! *does a Rosie the Riveter impression*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T19:27:17-07:00","id":460605,"title":"","content":"<b>bhuryaan: </b>mentor, teacher, instructor<br /> <b>koha: </b>smog, smoke, fumes; poisoned air, air that can barely be breathed; the harsh atmosphere of other planets that is poisonous to Earth-creatures<br /> <b>purmaaz</b>: lava, magma, molten rock<br /> <b>purmaazursakh: </b>a volcano, especially an active one<br /> <b>giren: </b>radiation, radioactivity<br /> <b>siggorah: </b>paranoia, suspicion, mistrust; different from <b>ennukhu </b>in that this is destructive paranoia, not the wariness of someone on their guard<br /> <b>hakar: </b>a revolt, a revolution; a revolutionary is known as a <b>haghar</b><br /> <br /> <b>uthannunhia: </b>solarpunk (lit. &quot;sun-power&quot;)<br /> <b>Uthannunhia-Shaghar: </b>Solarpunk Revolutionaries (singular <b>Uthannunhia-Haghar</b>)<br /> <b>Uthumalas</b>: Sunhaven (lit. &quot;safe place of the sun&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T20:07:31-07:00","id":460627,"title":"","content":"I'm curious to see a rendering of <b>He-Who-Has-Seen-Further</b> that accounts for the Newton quote and its mythological allusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T02:25:37-07:00","id":460872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=460627#post460627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious to see a rendering of <b>He-Who-Has-Seen-Further</b> that accounts for the Newton quote and its mythological allusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Newton quote?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T02:27:31-07:00","id":460873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=459879#post459879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I want to, but circumstances beyond my control mean that I have no known idea when I may be able to get 2e.<br /> <br /> YeofLittleFaith: On it!</div> </div> </div> </div>Arcane said xhe would buy you a copy!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T05:58:51-07:00","id":460975,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, I'm not acustomed to ask for favors I don't deserve but...<br /> <br /> Sikla, could you help me with the name of my player's pack Totem? It is a Rank 2 Spirit of Fortune (in the bad/good luck and also what future holds meanining) with a side of cat flavouring. I tentatively refer to it (her?) as Fickle Fortune. Fickle as in mischievous and whimiscal, as cats tend to be.<br /> <br /> How that would be in First Tongue?.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T05:59:04-07:00","id":460976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=460975#post460975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm, I'm not acustomed to ask for favors I don't deserve but...<br /> <br /> Sikla, could you help me with the name of my player's pack Totem? It is a Rank 2 Spirit of Fortune (in the bad/good luck and also what future holds meanining) with a side of cat flavouring. I tentatively refer to it (her?) as Fickle Fortune. Fickle as in mischievous and whimiscal, as cats tend to be.<br /> <br /> How that would be in First Tongue?.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure I can!<br /> <br /> That would probably be <b>Thuahdifala-Nihdugunamm</b>. The term <b>thuahdifala</b> means &quot;always going in a different direction or changing&quot; (i.e., &quot;fickle&quot;), and <b>nihdugunamm</b> means &quot;fortune&quot; or &quot;luck&quot; (lit. &quot;rich of fate&quot;). And it's not a favour you're asking for, the title of this thread is literally &quot;Doing First Tongue Translations&quot;. Why wouldn't I help?<br /> <br /> Still working on the Sees-Further quote. I want to get something fitting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 03-29-2015, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T08:01:51-07:00","id":461042,"title":"","content":"75/105 kennings translated as of this post:<br /> <br /> <b>Namzalagul'u:</b> Balder's gift = mistletoe<br /> <b>hafal-susk:</b> war-garments = armour<br /> <b>abis-thirikdu:</b> one who makes cattle fall = cattle-tripper = a wolf<br /> <b>namsusu-kuthdu:</b> one who is cleaving dead bodies = carrion-cleaver = a raven or eagle<br /> <b>suthargagh:</b> the bloodied-red mouth of a predator = red jowl = another kenning for a wolf<br /> <b>hafaldur:</b> children of battle = soldiers or raiders<br /> <b>sahkthir:</b> head-forest = hair<br /> <b>gafukaskkurag:</b> apple of the chest = apple of the breast = the heart<br /> <b>rih-hirimazinum:</b> bear-shirt = berserker<br /> <b>ramaamudu:</b> one who is roaring = roarer = a bear<br /> <b>afful:</b> old one = another name for an eagle<br /> <br /> And derived terms:<br /> <br /> <b>Namzalagul:</b> the god Balder (lit. &quot;the one of brightness&quot;)<br /> <b>u:</b> a gift, in the material sense; to be blessed with or to be given the qualities of something (may also be written as <b>'u</b>)<br /> <b>susk:</b> clothing, clothes, garments<br /> <b>namsusu:</b> carrion or dead bodies<br /> <b>ukaskkurag:</b> apple fruit<br /> <b>ramaamu:</b> to roar, to bellow; to growl or snarl loudly<br /> <br /> And some canon terms to add:<br /> <br /> <b>Wasu-Im:</b> Soft Rage, literally &quot;the rage meant to terrify&quot;. First stage of <b>Kuruth</b>, the Death Rage.<br /> <b>Basu-Im:</b> Also known as the Death Rage, it means &quot;the rage meant to lay low&quot;, and the sufferer tears mindlessly into anything.<br /> <br /> And some more words:<br /> <br /> <b>isibh:</b> a spiritual warrior like a paladin, a warrior-priest or a warrior-monk; not to be confused with a <b>hafal-isib</b>, which is a military chaplain, though a chaplain could also be an isibh<br /> <b>zaanyah:</b> a presence or aura that inspires fear; to be of a terrifying presence; something that inspires fear in someone by its very existence; compare <b>yeh'ren</b>, which refers to something that frightens by an inherent offness, and <b>uthkuk</b>, which means to intimidate through a display of something or a show of force<br /> <b>kirek:</b> albinism; those who have albinism<br /> <b>hafsu:</b> to be bad-smelling; to have a sickly or stinking body from disease<br /> <b>zif-umamu:</b> meaning &quot;beast's mark&quot;, it refers to the little signs that might betray a shapeshifter's true nature, such as the Bestial Reflection or Blackened Eyes Metis conditions of W:tA, or the eyeshine from someone in Dalu<br /> <b>esthasur:</b> a conjoined twin; a condition in which a twin is absorbed in the womb, and manifests as a tumour or underdeveloped parts in an adult body<br /> <b>sur:</b> a half of something<br /> <b>suzif:</b> a birthmark (lit. &quot;body-mark&quot;)<br /> <b>fuful-umfin:</b> refers to claws that are soft, blunt or fragile; those born with no claws in any form are known as <b>numfin</b><br /> <b>uzakal-muth:</b> hemophilia, one who bleeds easily; lit. means &quot;vanishing blood&quot;<br /> <b>hirisuguf:</b> a hoof<br /> <b>lu'ukhaziha:</b> &quot;the human-face curse&quot;, in which a human face presents itself in all of a shapeshifter's forms; also known as <b>erekhaziha</b> to the werewolves<br /> <b>sunudu:</b> the senses, such as the five senses (taste, smell, hearing, touch)<br /> <b>kasunudu:</b> to be hypersensory, to have enhanced senses; <b>kasunutu</b> is the opposite of the canon <b>naestu</b>, and means &quot;to be able to smell and taste greatly&quot;<br /> <b>salkuk:</b> thin, loose or fragile teeth; those born with no teeth are known as <b>nukuk</b><br /> <b>ithakusgidu-sanimbathra:</b> kyphosis, or a hunchback; lit. means &quot;bow-back&quot;<br /> <b>umamsu:</b> to be monstrously ugly; to be hideous; to be transformed into something hideous<br /> <b>numalu:</b> hairlessness, baldness<br /> <b>naafutu:</b> to be lost<br /> <b>kuluhuziha:</b> seizures, lit. &quot;the shaking curse&quot;; absence seizures are known as <b>naafutigiziha</b> (lit. &quot;the curse of lost eyes&quot;)<br /> <b>thimigi:</b> the third eye; may refer to a third eye physically in the forehead of some creatures<br /> <b>illu uzu:</b> transparent or translucent flesh","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 03-29-2015, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T10:50:37-07:00","id":461226,"title":"","content":"And here is my go at the 2e Ithaeur quote:<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>Nu-ha za e\u2019ne nu hur. Di e\u2019ne ta aha.&quot;:</b> &quot;No one is protected/shielded by their house/their refuge. Chaos/arrows/the bird of prey comes from behind/the rear.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 03-29-2015, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T11:00:42-07:00","id":461235,"title":"","content":"Awesome, thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T11:01:48-07:00","id":461236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FlailBot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=460872#post460872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Newton quote?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://en.wikiquote.org/wiki/Isaac_Newton#Quotes\" target=\"_blank\">Shoulders.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T11:09:07-07:00","id":461245,"title":"","content":"O-KAY!<br /> <br /> Now that I have a chance to look at 2e...I gotta do some clean-up. The devs have a lot of new canon terms, so I have to reshuffle my stand-ins around to mean something better. That being said, <b>SOME WORDS ARE NOW CANON</b>! <b>&quot;Urdur&quot;</b>, which means &quot;puppy&quot;, HAS THE APPROVAL OF THE WRITERS! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Here's the new canon terms so far:<br /> <br /> <b>Abni-Gur:</b> The \u201ccrucible of becoming.\u201d Storm Lord philosophy that by overcoming hardship they might one day become like Urfarah.<br /> <b>mus-rah:</b> \u201cHoly killing ground,\u201d a Hunter term for territory.<br /> <b>Sanghba\u2019zir:</b> An oathbreaker, especially one who violatesthe Oath of the Moon.<br /> <b>Mir:</b> \u201cRage,\u201d the killing fury that overcomes werewolves in Gauru form.<br /> <b>Sugrah:</b> A Storm Lord game of spotting weaknesses in one\u2019s tribemates to show off cunning and strengthen the tribe.<br /> <b>Urghir:</b> \u201cDog,\u201d derogatory term for high-Harmony Uratha. Someone who clings too closely to the world of Flesh.<br /> <b>Uzahal:</b> \u201cFade,\u201d derogatory term for low-Harmony Uratha. Someone who becomes too spirit-like.<br /> <b>hurmas-hi:</b> the Cahalith mindset, lit. &quot;submitting to dreams&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Nu Sum Ghumur Nu Su Ghid&quot;:</b> Offer no surrender you would not accept, the canon Blood Talon oath.<br /> <b>&quot;Nu Mus Halhala&quot;</b>: Let no sacred place in your territory be violated, the canon Hunters In Darkness oath.<br /> <b>&quot;Kul Kisura Udmeda&quot;</b>: Honour your territory in all things, the canon Iron Masters oath.<br /> <b>&quot;Nu Si Gid Namtar&quot;:</b> Allow no one to witness or tend to your weakness, the canon Storm Lords oath.<br /> <br /> <b>gid:</b> to transfer, to pass along; to lay a burden on<br /> <b>si:</b> to remember, to recall, to recount (replaces sakthaf lifir, which now means &quot;to recall, to recount from rote memory; another name for eidetic memory&quot;)<br /> <b>kisura:</b> border, territory; a boundary line<br /> <b>kul: </b>to honour a person, a place or thing; to honour a tradition; to pay respects<br /> <b>udmeda: </b>forever, always (replaces thuri, which now means &quot;immortal, long-lasting, not forgotten&quot; and nusirah, which means &quot;something that inherently cannot be affected by time, or is meant to resist the wear of time, through magic or the means of physics itself; stronger word than thuri&quot;)<br /> mus: to corrupt, to curdle (replaces &quot;viruhthim&quot;, which now refers to acts [especially those of Bale Hounds] of turning places into Wounds and Shoals)<br /> <b>halhala: </b>sacred ground (lit. &quot;divine secret&quot; or &quot;divine inheritance&quot;; replaces &quot;unurifanda&quot;, which now refers to extremely powerful locuses or other wellsprings of sacred power only; such places are polar opposites of wounds)<br /> <b>sum: </b>to give, to present (replaces &quot;sagrik&quot;, which now means to offer, to sacrifice and/or to give up something for a greater good)<br /> <b>humur: </b>a surrender (lit. &quot;honour-fodder&quot;; replaces &quot;sar e habalthu&quot;, which means to flee or run from battle like a coward, or to give up in the face of a difficult situation without trying)<br /> <b>e'ne:</b> from<br /> <br /> <b>Lu'im Iduth: </b>The Deceiver Lune (lit. &quot;the Moon's defiling clay&quot;)<br /> <b>Urdam:</b> Believer Wolves, followers of the Deceiver Lune<br /> <b>Ili Sugin'dab: </b>The Penitent, first follower of the Deceiver Lune<br /> <b>Numun Sala: </b>The Lune of Mercy, the Lune Lu'im Iduth claimed to be when it appeared to Ili Sugin'dab<br /> <b>Sag'suga Isim:</b> The Empty Hunger (lit. &quot;the fat king who needs sustenance&quot;)<br /> <b>Lul'Aya:</b> The False Father (lit. &quot;liar father&quot;), short for <b>Ninglul Aya</b><br /> <b>Imadih Shedu:</b> A spirit dedicated to change and chaos, and the original form of Lul'Aya<br /> <b>Ghal'urfarah Aya:</b> &quot;Great Wolf-Father&quot;, the form of Lul'Aya that takes the shape of Urfarah<br /> <b>Inim-Galag:</b> The heralds (pack) that follows Lul'Aya<br /> <b>Mash'ng-Idud: </b>&quot;Eyes of the Moon&quot;, the twisted spirit-scouts of Lul'Aya<br /> <b>Gir'shedu: </b>&quot;Berserkers&quot;, twisted Gauru-esque werewolves that serve as the fighters of Lul'Aya<br /> <b>Ansar-zalag:</b> The Heavenly Fire (lit. &quot;the smoking brightness of heaven&quot;)<br /> <b>Lilia'izi:</b> The scouts and occasional shock troops of Ansar-zalag<br /> <b>Mulan Naminigir: </b>Star Herald, fanatical worshippers of Ansar-zalag that have been gifted with his power<br /> <b>Gagh-Azur: </b>The Mouth of the Depths (lit. &quot;mouth of the roiling figure&quot;)<br /> <br /> And these are the ones I speculate are canon, but I'm not entirely sure:<br /> <br /> <b>shedu: </b>a being, an elemental, a physical representation of something; another name for a spirit<br /> <b>ghal: </b>great, mighty, all-powerful<br /> <b>nigir:</b> a herald, a representative<br /> <b>id-: </b>a suffix denoting things associated with Luna, usually in the form of <b>idu</b><br /> <b>Idud: </b>an alternative spelling for <b>Iduth</b> \u2014 considering it comes from the name of an idigam's servants, I'd use &quot;Idud&quot; to refer to things that are supposed to be moon-like or represent the moon, but are mockeries of or not quite right<br /> <b>mulan:</b> a star; I'd treat my existing <b>malan </b>interpretation of it as an alternative spelling<br /> <br /> And finally, the term replacing childbirth (and the act of it) is <b>harsum </b><b>dur</b>, which means &quot;to present a child to the world&quot;. <b>Dursagrik </b>means to sacrifice a child, or give up a child for the greater good, and afterbirth is now known as <b>ipu</b>.<br /> <br /> I linked to the new spirit terms earlier in the thread, and Wasu-Im and Basu-Im are on the previous page. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 03-29-2015, 10:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T11:13:49-07:00","id":461247,"title":"","content":"Not sure whether it's necessary for me to point out that <b>hithimu</b> and <b>hithisu</b> are from the 1e lexicon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T11:15:19-07:00","id":461249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=461247#post461247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure whether it's necessary for me to point out that <b>hithimu</b> and <b>hithisu</b> are from the 1e lexicon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally necessary. Thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T14:25:55-07:00","id":461467,"title":"","content":"You're missing an Oath there, Sikla, namely <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Italic\"><b><i>Su A </i></b><i><b>Sar-Hith Sa.</b> </i><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">\u201cPay each spirit in kind.\u201d</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T14:41:34-07:00","id":461502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=461467#post461467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're missing an Oath there, Sikla, namely <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Italic\"><b><i>Su A </i></b><i><b>Sar-Hith Sa.</b> </i><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">\u201cPay each spirit in kind.\u201d</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=371423#post371423\">We covered that one earlier.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T14:45:11-07:00","id":461505,"title":"","content":"I still appreciate people pointing these things out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Satchel, I have your quote: <b>Igimdu-E'ne-Zagsgul</b>, lit. &quot;Shoulder-Seeing-One&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T15:46:22-07:00","id":461606,"title":"","content":"With gifts like Luna's Embrace now in 2e, I've decided to translate a few words that refer to gender and sexuality. If anyone thinks any of the connotations here are offensive, let me know IMMEDIATELY so I can change it to something more suitable, and also let me know if I missed anything. Translations for male and female can be found in the dictionaries already on the front page.<br /> <br /> <b>ala'ma:</b> a helpful spirit with intersexual characteristics<br /> <b>sethu:</b> a helpful spirit with no gender-defining characteristics, or a sexless/gender spirit<br /> <b>munidim:</b> a spirit of intersexuality<br /> <b>nidiim:</b> a spirit of femininity<br /> <b>muniim:</b> a spirit of masculinity<br /> <b>munidh:</b> intersex<br /> <b>nuhasilah:</b> sexless or having no sex<br /> <b>falahasilah:</b> transsexual (lit. &quot;changed parts&quot;)<br /> <b>kuhasilah:</b> biological sex (lit. &quot;one's own body parts&quot;)<br /> <b>kuhae:</b> gender identity (lit. &quot;one's own sense of self&quot;)<br /> <b>nidae:</b> identifying as the female gender<br /> <b>munidhae:</b> identifying as the intersex gender<br /> <b>munae:</b> identifying as the male gender<br /> <b>nuhae:</b> identifying as no gender or genderless<br /> <b>futhae:</b> identifying as a gender that is not female, male, genderless or intergender<br /> <b>za'hae:</b> genderfluid (lit. &quot;moving gender&quot;)<br /> <b>falahae:</b> transgender (lit. &quot;changed genders&quot;)<br /> <b>ene'ae:</b> one's preferred gender identity<br /> <b>ashae:</b> to have one gender<br /> <b>minhae:</b> to have two genders<br /> <b>peshae:</b> to have three genders<br /> <b>limmuhae:</b> to have four genders<br /> <b>yahae:</b> to have five genders<br /> <b>sharhae:</b> to have many or multiple genders<br /> <b>hae'im:</b> spirits of gender concepts; add <b>'im</b> to the end of any of the previous gender listings to get the name for a spirit of that gender<br /> <br /> <b>gima-kiliteg:</b> homoromantic (lit. &quot;loves the same&quot;)<br /> <b>minsur-kiliteg:</b> biromantic (lit. &quot;loves both&quot;)<br /> <b>fu'i-kiliteg:</b> heteroromantic (lit. &quot;loves the opposite&quot;)<br /> <b>thu-kiliteg:</b> panromantic (lit. &quot;loves all&quot;)<br /> <b>netehnar:</b> aromantic (lit. &quot;not attracted romantically&quot;, &quot;doesn't have romantic feelings&quot;)<br /> <b>gima-ene:</b> homosexual (lit. &quot;finds pleasure in the same&quot;)<br /> <b>minsur-ene:</b> bisexual (lit. &quot;finds pleasure in both&quot;)<br /> <b>fu'i-ene:</b> heterosexual (lit. &quot;finds pleasure in the opposite&quot;)<br /> <b>thu-ene:</b> pansexual (lit. &quot;finds pleasure in all&quot;)<br /> <b>neteg:</b> asexual (lit. &quot;not attracted sexually&quot;, &quot;doesn't have feelings of attraction&quot;)<br /> <b>fu'i:</b> the opposite, the other side<br /> <i>(suffix -im to any of these to get the names of the spirits that represent these concepts)</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 03-30-2015, 10:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T18:54:49-07:00","id":461743,"title":"","content":"Decided to add translations for all the new wolf-blood tells, and some related vocab.<br /> <br /> <b>urzif:</b> &quot;mark of the wolf&quot;, First Tongue name for a tell<br /> <b>Urfaramuth:</b> &quot;Father-blooded&quot;, wolfblooded said to be descended from Father Wolf<br /> <b>Idumuth:</b> &quot;Moon-blooded&quot;, wolf-blooded said to be descended from Mother Moon<br /> <b>kuk'u:</b> &quot;blessed of bite&quot;, the Bite tell<br /> <b>igim-nukuth:</b> &quot;seeing-scar&quot;, the Bitten tell<br /> <b>uralasuh:</b> &quot;ritual hands&quot;, the Clever Fingers tell<br /> <b>halfra:</b> &quot;somewhat-man&quot;, the Devil Inside tell<br /> <b>azihigi:</b> &quot;cursed eye&quot;, the Evil Eye tell<br /> <b>irsim:</b> &quot;fragrant&quot;, the Exciting tell<br /> <b>hithim gihia:</b> &quot;spirit messenger&quot;, the Horse tell<br /> <b>shartha hiri'us:</b> &quot;Host compass&quot;, the Host-Ache tell<br /> <b>luluzu:</b> &quot;false-fleshed&quot;, the Liar's Skin tell<br /> <b>kizuur:</b> &quot;boundary marker&quot;, the Marker tell<br /> <b>iduzif:</b> &quot;moon-mark&quot;, the Moon-Marked tell<br /> <b>nusu:</b> &quot;never-alone&quot;, the Phantom Pack tell; a phantom pack is known as a <b>Hisdum</b><br /> <b>Shuriligim:</b> &quot;Twilight eyes&quot;, the Piercing Eyes tell<br /> <b>gizbaz:</b> &quot;hidden garment&quot;, the Second Skin tell<br /> <b>Idurhan:</b> &quot;Moon's wolf&quot;, the Shape-Shifted tell<br /> <b>Hisisur:</b> &quot;Shadow-half&quot;, the Shadow Twin tell<br /> <b>gus-luzuk:</b> &quot;skin-thief&quot;, the Skinned tell<br /> <b>dar hissu:</b> &quot;loose spirit&quot;, the Spirit Double tell<br /> <b>giri-sulu:</b> &quot;nose-lure&quot;, the Strong Scent tell<br /> <b>ulal ubiur:</b> &quot;essence teat&quot;, the Third Nipple tell<br /> <b>nahdazi:</b> &quot;locus-soulled&quot;, the Waystone tell<br /> <b>lul'urdum:</b> &quot;pack-false&quot;, the Wolf Sign tell<br /> <b>Fenris-nuzi:</b> &quot;soul full of Fenris's fire&quot;, the Fenris-Ur's Blood merit<br /> <b>Kamduis-nighzu:</b> &quot;Kamduis's knowing&quot;, the Kamduis-Ur's Blood merit<br /> <b>Hikaon-igim:</b> &quot;Hikaon's sight&quot;, the Hikaon-Ur's Blood merit<br /> <b>Sagrim-dakh:</b> &quot;Sagrim-touched&quot;, the Sagrim-Ur's Blood merit<br /> <b>Skolis-annunhia:</b> &quot;Skolis's strength&quot;, the Skolis-Ur's blood merit<br /> <b>usu'dur:</b> &quot;alone-child&quot;, the Ghost Child merit<br /> <b>Ithadur:</b> &quot;Crescent phase child&quot;, the Crescent Moon-Born merit<br /> <b>Radur:</b> &quot;Full phase child&quot;, the Full Moon-Born merit<br /> <b>Cahadur:</b> &quot;Gibbous phase child&quot;, the Gibbous Moon-Born merit<br /> <b>Elodur:</b> &quot;Half phase child&quot;, the Elodoth Moon-Born merit<br /> <b>Irradur:</b> &quot;No phase child&quot;, the No Moon-Born merit<br /> <b>urdum-sehe:</b> &quot;pack-honoured&quot;, the Pack Bound merit<br /> <b>ur-kahrih:</b> &quot;wolf-suckled&quot;, the Raised by Wolves merit","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 03-30-2015, 08:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T05:06:47-07:00","id":462113,"title":"","content":"With all of the hard work you do, it's strange to me that the devs haven't just put you to work at least on a volunteer basis. &gt;.&gt; If it were me, your dictionaries would be canon just 'cuz who else is gonna do all this with this much passion?<br /> <br /> I, for one, thank you immensely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T05:34:07-07:00","id":462119,"title":"","content":"I second that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T05:44:17-07:00","id":462134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gebbethine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=462113#post462113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With all of the hard work you do, it's strange to me that the devs haven't just put you to work at least on a volunteer basis. &gt;.&gt; If it were me, your dictionaries would be canon just 'cuz who else is gonna do all this with this much passion?<br /> <br /> I, for one, thank you immensely.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's enough for me that <b>urdur</b> is canon, and that the playerbase is so grateful for all this work. You guys are my muse \u2014 you present me with challenges, ideas and requests that make me think. Half of the grammar and vocabulary wouldn't have been hashed out if people didn't have me translating spirit-names and larger pieces of text. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: a few things I missed putting up before.<br /> <br /> <b>namtar:</b> consequences; fate, destiny, a decreed fate; that which has befallen another<br /> <b>ihdar:</b> seer, soothsayer, fortune-teller<br /> <b>bakkuk:</b> a specific trigger for Kuruth (lit. &quot;fly-bite&quot;)<br /> <b>balalim:</b> a passive trigger for Kuruth (lit. &quot;storm-brewer&quot;)<br /> <b>bazur:</b> a common trigger for Kuruth (lit. &quot;undoing-call&quot;)<br /> <b>sulu:</b> bait, lure<br /> <b>Hiskabhlu:</b> a spiritual touchstone (lit. &quot;Shadow-link&quot;)<br /> <b>Gurkabhlu:</b> a physical touchstone (lit. &quot;Flesh-link&quot;)<br /> <b>Aya-su:</b> &quot;Father-fleshed&quot; \u2014 to take the Father's Form when not in rage<br /> <b>namtar-ni:</b> &quot;fated prey&quot; or &quot;chosen prey&quot;, the preferred prey of each tribe's <i>Siskur-Dah</i><br /> <b>daha:</b> to hunt fairly, to hunt respectfully; to hunt with <i>daha</i> is to hunt like you should, and to end it like you should, instead of perverting and drawing out the process<br /> <b>dahskir-uguf:</b> &quot;heedless to the hunting howls&quot; \u2014 to ignore or deny the <i>Siskur-Dah</i> and the urge towards it<br /> <b>neha-im:</b> &quot;calmed storm&quot; or &quot;calmed Rage&quot; \u2014 said of a werewolf or other shapeshifter with the Controlled Burn merit","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 03-30-2015, 09:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T06:22:46-07:00","id":462174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=461042#post461042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>isibh:</b> a spiritual warrior like a paladin, a warrior-priest or a warrior-monk; not to be confused with a <b>hafal-isib</b>, which is a military chaplain, though a chaplain could also be an isibh</div> </div> </div> </div>This actually hits closer to what I-personally meant when I asked for a translation of chaplain, but that was my fault for not describing the character quite right. Also, thank you for the solar translations. Have a cookie!<br /> <br /> EDIT: Got to this page, saw your post on sexualities and romantic orientations, misted up IRL. Thank you, friend. THOUGH: you have an implication that asexuals don't 'find pleasure', conflating asexuality and celibacy in a way that's inaccurate (it doesn't offend me so much as irk me). A lot of ace folk do have sex and find pleasure; it's 