ate":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T11:22:56-07:00","id":486547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=486490#post486490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, I like that &quot;woven&quot; things could easily refer to Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hallows and Loci are the same thing. I'm not sure, however, if Essence is just Mana in a form spirits can process, or if Mana and Essence are the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T11:32:52-07:00","id":486566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=486547#post486547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hallows and Loci are the same thing. I'm not sure, however, if Essence is just Mana in a form spirits can process, or if Mana and Essence are the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>They aren't. One is otherworldly, the other isn't, despite their resonances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T22:07:55-07:00","id":487046,"title":"","content":"Well, now that the Hungers are out....<br /> <br /> <b>Ralzhaf:</b> A Beast's Hunger.<br /> <b>barsak:</b> A Beast's Satiety.<br /> <b>mas:</b> Dreams, dreaming; has a more mystical connotation than <b>visktha</b><br /> <b>Cahamas:</b> Another name for a <b>Cahavisktha</b>, a Cahalith's prophetic dreams, but with a more religious or spiritual meaning<br /> <b>Affamas:</b> &quot;Eldest of Dreams&quot;, the Primordial Dream.<br /> <b>Sau'ak:</b> A Tyrant. The Hunger For Power is known as the <b>S</b><b>au'ak-Ralzhaf</b>.<br /> <b>Surof:</b> A Collector. The Hunger For the Hoard is known as the <b>Su</b><b>rof-Ralzhaf</b>.<br /> <b>Anghu:</b> A Nemesis. The Hunger For Punishment is known as the <b>A</b><b>nghu-Ralzhaf</b>.<br /> <b>Kakan:</b> A Predator. The Hunger For Prey is known as the <b>K</b><b>akan-Ralzhaf</b>.<br /> <b>Zikzag:</b> A Ravager. The Hunger For Ruin is known as the <b>Z</b><b>ikzag-Ralzhaf</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 04-21-2015, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T07:51:34-07:00","id":487264,"title":"","content":"<b>sag:</b> Front, forward, forward-facing<br /> <b>sag thakkan:</b> Front door, front gate<br /> <b>u'asgu:</b> stairs, staircase<br /> <b>sag-u'asgu:</b> front stoop<br /> <b>afad:</b> a small shelter such as an open tent; a porch or gazebo<br /> <b>hirmak:</b> a furnace or kiln; an oven<br /> <b>umak:</b> to blow, to puff<br /> <b>saganumak:</b> a furnace for heating; a heater (lit. &quot;blows heat&quot;)<br /> <b>assudunfath:</b> a breaker or fuse (lit. &quot;power-breaker&quot;)<br /> <b>guzluh:</b> a box, a container<br /> <b>assudunfath guzluh:</b> fuse box<br /> <b>zummurigsu:</b> a gable; a joining part of a roof<br /> <b>maar garum:</b> a place where wagons or other vehicles are kept (more broad than <b>ramamaar garum</b>)<br /> <b>maar thakkan:</b> the garage door (lit. &quot;gate to the wagons&quot;); a more car-oriented term is <b>ramamaar thakkan</b><br /> <b>luzukeshla:</b> a skeleton key; an automatic door opener such as a garage door opener<br /> <b>zurum:</b> waste, litter; pee, poop, droppings<br /> <b>zurukurum:</b> a garbage can, a dustbin<br /> <b>unuhzar lalarak:</b> a shed in a garden or yard, usually used to keep tools and yard equipment in<br /> <b>anfahirfathra:</b> a girder; steel beams (lit. &quot;skeleton of iron/metal&quot;)<br /> <b>nisigarum:</b> greenhouse<br /> <b>zummur ahlalu:</b> the gutters, the raincatchers, the piping around the sides of a roof<br /> <b>gindu:</b> hallway, corridor<br /> <b>eshla:</b> a key<br /> <b>bakar:</b> a hall or public place like one; a gathering place<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Anna'u&quot;:</b> The spirit version of &quot;guth ni&quot;, which means &quot;cool&quot;, &quot;rad&quot;, or &quot;awesome&quot;. It literally means &quot;I gift you with my approval&quot;. &quot;Guth ni&quot; is more werewolf/predatory shapeshifter phrasing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 04-21-2015, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T17:52:53-07:00","id":487819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=487264#post487264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>&quot;Anna'u&quot;:</b> The spirit version of &quot;guth ni&quot;, which means &quot;cool&quot;, &quot;rad&quot;, or &quot;sweetness and rye&quot;. It literally means &quot;I gift you with my approval&quot;. &quot;Guth ni&quot; is more werewolf/predatory shapeshifter phrasing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really should mention, Sikla.... literally NO one other than me ever says &quot;sweetness and rye&quot;. It's a Litheon-ism that I accidentally use instead of saying something sensible (other phrases include yelling &quot;fruit by the foot&quot; instead of cursing, &quot;oh my tits&quot; instead of &quot;oh my god&quot;. My personal vernacular is a bit off regular english). People are going to be confused if you use it as an example. ;P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All Things Strive.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4708-litheon","name":"Litheon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T17:57:09-07:00","id":487821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Litheon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=487819#post487819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really should mention, Sikla.... literally NO one other than me ever says &quot;sweetness and rye&quot;. It's a Litheon-ism that I accidentally use instead of saying something sensible (other phrases include yelling &quot;fruit by the foot&quot; instead of cursing, &quot;oh my tits&quot; instead of &quot;oh my god&quot;. My personal vernacular is a bit off regular english). People are going to be confused if you use it as an example. ;P</div> </div> </div> </div>Noted! (And that's actually kind of cool.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T18:49:27-07:00","id":487835,"title":"","content":"I don't think I've translated the names of all the derangements from 1e oWoD. I think I'll do that now; please let me know, guys, if any of these give the wrong message or seem politically incorrect.<br /> <br /> <b>tabh:</b> a repetitive behaviour; a compulsion; a tic<br /> <b>isu:</b> to be urged, to be compelled; to be obsessed, an obsession<br /> <b>Yagekentabh:</b> The Abyssal Compulsion derangement, in which one is compelled into learning more about the Abyss and its secrets<br /> <b>hirihdin-estha:</b> The Animalistic Dependency derangement from Vampire, in which one is dependent on Animalism or seeing animals nearby to use it on (lit. &quot;animal-bound&quot;)<br /> <i>(Anxiety has already been translated)</i><br /> <b>skir-izu:</b> Aphasia, the loss of the ability to speak or understand speech (lit. &quot;stolen of speech&quot;)<br /> <b>negargar:</b> to circle around; to avoid; the Avoidance Derangement, in which one avoids a place, person or thing due to a past trauma or something similar<br /> <b>sa'ath:</b> to trap or cage an animal; to snare an animal or one's prey; the Banish the Beast Derangement from <i>Changing Breeds</i>, in which a shapeshifter represses their bestial nature so thoroughly, it is <i>very</i> difficult to shapeshift into it<br /> <b>hirihdinirih:</b> zoophobia; the Beast Fears derangement<br /> <b>muthtabh:</b> the Blood Fascination Derangement, in which one is compelled or drawn towards images of blood or blood itself<br /> <b>sa'ath-nirih:</b> the Cage Shock Derangement, in which a shapeshifter begins losing control if indoors or otherwise confined (lit. &quot;trap fear&quot;)<br /> <b>sakhskir:</b> an emotion, feeling (lit. &quot;heart-speech&quot;)<br /> <b>sakhskir-tuf:</b> the Cataplexy Derangement, in which one collapses (though remains conscious) after laughter or a strong emotion (lit. &quot;struck by emotion&quot;)<br /> <b>agzu:</b> to be dangerous, to be a threat; a danger, a threat<br /> <b>agzigitabh:</b> the Compulsive-Aggressive Disorder Derangement, in which everyone is seen as a threat<br /> <b>garrmal:</b> the Decadence Derangement, in which a character loses their sense of excess when it comes to extreme decorum, triggered by a victory in the social arena or a humiliating defeat<br /> <b>thimasafru:</b> Delusional, hallucinating; delusions, hallucinations; to delude oneself (lit. &quot;lying [to the sufferer] thoughts or visions because of tricked senses&quot;)<br /> <b>isuthimasafru:</b> a delusional obsession, such as those found in certain mental health disorders; the Delusional Obsession derangement<br /> <b>luldudam:</b> the Delusional Witness derangement, in which one justifies (or sometimes hallucinates) something when witnessing/having witnessed supernatural phenomena in order to fit it into their belief system (lit. &quot;lying to believe&quot;)<br /> <b>gidumm:</b> to bury, to roll up, to put away<br /> <b>thima-gidumm:</b> The Repression Derangement; to repress, to compartmentalize<br /> <br /> More to come.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 04-25-2015, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T10:41:17-07:00","id":488468,"title":"","content":"<b>waru:</b> to deny, to refuse; to refute<br /> <b>waruthima:</b> denial; the Denial Derangement (lit. &quot;denying thoughts&quot;)<br /> <b>namri:</b> dependent, dependence; the Dependent Personality derangement<br /> <b>muththim:</b> the Dependent-Personality Derangement for bloodbound, when a blood-bound cannot use their resolve to fighting against a Dominator's Domination of them (lit. &quot;blood-weakened&quot;)<br /> <b>a'rah:</b> to drown; drowning (also spelt as <b>a rah</b>)<br /> <b>zurum-a'rah:</b> Diogenes Syndrome; the Diogenes Syndrome Derangement (lit. &quot;drown in waste&quot;)<br /> <b>uzakazi:</b> depersonalization; the Depersonalization derangement (lit. &quot;faded soul&quot;)<br /> <b>ihid:</b> divination, fortune-telling<br /> <b>ihidisu:</b> the Divination Compulsion derangement, in which one is obsessed with telling fortunes<br /> <b>safru:</b> sensory input that is flawed or incorrect, such as audio hallucinations caused by mental illness, or tastebuds that taste everything as sweet instead of sour because of miracle berries","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 04-25-2015, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T12:20:51-07:00","id":491852,"title":"","content":"More Derangements, and a few other words that are not Derangements, but things I forgot to add earlier.<br /> <br /> <b>afu:</b> old age; elderly; an old thing<br /> <b>afutabh:</b> the Degenerative Fixation Derangement, in one fixates negatively on signs of aging; for Ghouls, it's a fear of aging once the blood bond wears off, which can lead to begging and harassing one's master for more<br /> <b>maran:</b> Depression; the Depression Derangement (lit. &quot;of greatest sadness&quot;)<br /> <b>dafa:</b> Erythema, a redness or rash caused by infection, disease, etc. such as the &quot;bullseye mark&quot; of Lyme's disease; for vampires spending blood to look alive around others, it's <b>zisu</b> (lit. &quot;life-skin&quot;)<br /> <b>aselulu:</b> a habitat; an ecosystem<br /> <b>estha-kiliteg:</b> Demiromantic<br /> <b>estha-ene:</b> Demisexual (lit. &quot;finds pleasure in those they feel a bond to&quot;)<br /> <b>farsekhae:</b> Of undecided or &quot;curious&quot; gender orientation<br /> <b>farsekh-ene:</b> Of undecided or &quot;curious&quot; romantic orientation<br /> <b>farsekh-kiliteg:</b> Of undecided or &quot;curious&quot; sexual orientation<br /> <b>garin:</b> a temple; a church; a place of worship<br /> <b>agmamu:</b> the Feral Antics Derangement, in which a shapeshifter acts like a wild animal with little human behaviour or speech (lit. &quot;beast-acting&quot;)<br /> <b>sa'ath-uth:</b> the Feral Frenzy Derangement, in which one goes feral or into a rage-like state if they feel confined and until they &quot;escape&quot; (lit. &quot;rage of the trap&quot;)<br /> <b>guzbhu:</b> a fetish of the sexual kind<br /> <b>namguzbhu:</b> the Fetishism Derangement<br /> <b>emmu:</b> to abuse; abuse<br /> <b>emmul:</b> an abuser; one who abuses<br /> <b>hirihdin emmu:</b> animal abuse<br /> <b>zatharzemmul:</b> the Filthy Brutes! Derangement, in a shapechanger abuses animals as a way of lashing out at themselves or their shapeshifter side<br /> <b>ta'af:</b> a fixation; to fixate; to focus on<br /> <b>mata'af:</b> to focus greatly; hyperfocus<br /> <b>lilta'af:</b> to focus weakly; underfocus<br /> <b>ta'haf:</b> the Fixation Derangement (lit. &quot;fixates badly&quot;); an unhealthy fixation<br /> <b>farsesu:</b> a psychological fugue; the Fugue Derangement (lit. &quot;fog of the self/body-fog&quot;)<br /> <b>shaeme:</b> glossolalia; the Glossolalia Derangement<br /> <b>dunfathaf:</b> the Goetic Fracture Derangement, in which your personal demon becomes personified and tries to manipulate you into succumbing to it (lit. &quot;broken bad piece&quot;)<br /> <b>nirthima:</b> delusions of grandeur; the Grandiose Delusion Derangement<br /> <b>kulu'ugigurr:</b> to be speciesist towards humankind; the Hate of Man Derangement","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 04-25-2015, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T16:08:17-07:00","id":492062,"title":"","content":"Correcting some stuff already translated, and more Derangements.<br /> <br /> - <b>Ameni</b> now means &quot;a reason; an answer; an answered question&quot;<br /> - <b>Mannu</b> now means &quot;a qualified person; those who are fit for a certain job; those who know what to do in a certain situation&quot;<br /> - <b>Mu</b> (to pilot, to ride, etc.) is now <b>mu'u</b>, as it turns out just plain <b>mu</b> means &quot;to name, to address; a name or address&quot;.<br /> - <b>Mas</b> (goat, sacrifical animal) is now <b>ma'as</b>, due to it being a homonym with the word for dreams, <b>mas</b><br /> <br /> And now, words.<br /> <br /> <b>mag:</b> to be sick, to be ill; a more neutral word than <b>gurim</b>, and used by the Pure and spirits in general to refer to illness or madness<br /> <b>tag-sahaz:</b> A serial killing spree; the act of serial killing<br /> <b>umamutag-sahaz:</b> The Hunter King Derangement, in which a shapeshifter hates their animal side so much, it manifests as the serial killing and/or abuse of animals<br /> <b>zeh:</b> to leak; to spill<br /> <b>zehvisktha:</b> The Hypnagogic Hallucination Derangement; hypnagogic hallucination, in which one hallucinates while coming out of or going into the sleep phase. Also known as <b>zehmas</b>. (Lit. &quot;leaking dreams&quot;)<br /> <b>affah:</b> the past; past times<br /> <b>affah kusku:</b> The Identity Erasure Derangement, in which a ghoul or vampire is compelled to destroy all evidence of their past, human life<br /> <b>haflal-sakhskir:</b> An inferiority complex; the Inferiority Complex Derangement (lit. &quot;feelings about being little-bad [inferior]&quot;)<br /> <b>haflal:</b> weak; inferior<br /> <b>thalabu:</b> to be sleepless; to have recurring trouble getting to sleep; insomnia; the Insomnia Derangement<br /> <b>ihlif:</b> to be awake; to wake up; to awaken<br /> <b>zarru:</b> a state of being in which a supernatural that has hibernated for a long time (such as a vampire) wakes up and mistakes people, places or events for things from the past; the Intermetamorphosis Derangement<br /> <b>dhuthmu:</b> to argue against; to defy; to disobey<br /> <b>nirdhuthmu:</b> the Irrational Defiance Derangement, in which one is compelled to disobey their superiors<br /> <b>nufulum:</b> irrationality, irrational, without logic; the Irrational Derangement<br /> <b>naafutusakh:</b> to lose compassion, to lose care for someone, to lose empathy; the Loss of Compassion Derangement<br /> <b>liltabh:</b> the Magical Ideation Derangement, in which a vampire is compelled to seek some sort of greater intelligence or power in the surrounding environment","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 04-25-2015, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T19:40:00-07:00","id":493162,"title":"","content":"So I decided to write up some lyrics to the song &quot;Sacrifice&quot; from <i>Vikings</i>. There are no official lyrics for this song, the singer (Sharon Lyons) said that she picked random Celtic-sounding/Latin-sounding syllables. Especially with Norse Werewolves on the near horizon, I thought it would be appropriate to create an Uratha version of this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Mx96NA7ak5s\" data-code=\"Mx96NA7ak5s\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Mx96NA7ak5s/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Uremehir:</b><br /> <br /> Magh da su-ah eh;<br /> Si bun-gala,<br /> Eh Matires.<br /> Si-ah, si-la;<br /> Si bun-kala,<br /> Muh de.<br /> Su-sulea,<br /> Ase-endesh,<br /> Matu eh, mati ya<br /> Ezem de.<br /> <br /> Magh da du-ah eh;<br /> Si bun-ghala,<br /> Eh Matires.<br /> Si-lal, si-la;<br /> Si bun-kala,<br /> Si mus-tala,<br /> Muh de.<br /> Ase-endesh,<br /> Matu eh, mati ya<br /> Ezem de.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>English:</b><br /> <br /> It is now time to watch as the body is burnt;<br /> Remember the labour of the bellows,<br /> And keep watch for the Burning Ship of Our Lady.<br /> It is now time to remember, and to remember to keep vigilant;<br /> Remember the bellows as they must be,<br /> And pour out [an offering or libation] from the cups.<br /> Body of tar,<br /> The priests make you a shrine now;<br /> Watch over this land, [for] five burning ships<br /> Carry you through this celebration [in your honour].<br /> <br /> It is now a time to watch and act;<br /> Remember to protect the bellows,<br /> And keep watch for the Burning Ship of Our Lady.<br /> Remember the little [things], and remember to keep vigilant;<br /> Remember the bellows as they must be,<br /> Remember the holy cry to battle,<br /> And pour out [an offering or libation] from the cups.<br /> Body of tar,<br /> The priests make you a shrine now;<br /> Watch over this land, [for] five burning ships<br /> Carry you through this celebration [in your honour].","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T16:38:47-07:00","id":495382,"title":"","content":"(note to self, stop taking breaks, or else Sikla will fill half a page + of translations.)<br /> Also, there's apparently a new, extended version of Edge of Night for the Hobbit movies, if you wanted to tack that one on to the end of your previous translation. And as an aside, what is the Words of Red moon, again? I have no idea.<br /> <br /> (1794 words, 129 Phrases/Zodiacs, and 7 Songs. 1930, I suppose. where are you gonna count 2000? ;P)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All Things Strive.","edited":{"userid":4708,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4708-litheon","user":"Litheon","date":".  Editing to stop myself from double posting. 04-28-2015, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4708-litheon","name":"Litheon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T07:49:57-07:00","id":496279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Litheon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=495382#post495382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(note to self, stop taking breaks, or else Sikla will fill half a page + of translations.)<br /> Also, there's apparently a new, extended version of Edge of Night for the Hobbit movies, if you wanted to tack that one on to the end of your previous translation. And as an aside, what is the Words of Red moon, again? I have no idea.<br /> <br /> (1794 words, 129 Phrases/Zodiacs, and 7 Songs. 1930, I suppose. where are you gonna count 2000? ;P)</div> </div> </div> </div>In about 60 more words. I will find the extended translation and see what I can whip up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Now then, for some random things I didn't think about until now, some of which were going to be used for something or other.<br /> <br /> <b>gimak:</b> a grave, a tomb<br /> <b>ghirbadrasu:</b> a skeleton<br /> <b>tala:</b> a battle cry, a war cry<br /> <b>hazi:</b> mint<br /> <b>sasaha:</b> a spice; a condiment; flavouring<br /> <b>azu:</b> myrtle<br /> <b>suhunkhu:</b> angelica (lit. &quot;watchful against pain&quot;)<br /> <b>shasaha:</b> allspice (lit. &quot;spice of many flavours&quot;)<br /> <b>mudunu'uf:</b> anise (lit. &quot;good friend of the belly&quot;)<br /> <b>munn:</b> salt<br /> <b>simhaziz:</b> coriander (lit. &quot;smells like stink and insects&quot;, referring to the bad smell of the unripe fruit)<br /> <b>gutrina:</b> licorice/liquorice (lit. &quot;sweet root&quot;)<br /> <b>uzurum:</b> a canopic jar (lit. &quot;organ jar&quot;)<br /> <b>zilul:</b> a zombie, the walking dead (lit. &quot;false-dead&quot;)<br /> <br /> Edit: the Words of Red Moon is a prophecy about wolves creating a new world, from the somewhat-obscure anime by Bones (creators of things like <i>Cowboy Bebop</i>), <i>Wolf's Rain</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 04-29-2015, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T11:35:26-07:00","id":496520,"title":"","content":"I actually forgot to add the names &amp; kennings to that number.<br /> Sooo. 1930 + 14 (these) + 78 (kennings) + 99 (Unique names) = 2121. And with a fanfare not unlike the anticlimatic splut of a cupcake hitting the floor you passed 2000 translations a little while ago. ;P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All Things Strive.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4708-litheon","name":"Litheon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-29T12:02:29-07:00","id":496568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Litheon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=496520#post496520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually forgot to add the names &amp; kennings to that number.<br /> Sooo. 1930 + 14 (these) + 78 (kennings) + 99 (Unique names) = 2121. And with a fanfare not unlike the anticlimatic splut of a cupcake hitting the floor you passed 2000 translations a little while ago. ;P</div> </div> </div> </div>...Five second rule. *picks up cupcake, eats it*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T21:46:49-07:00","id":498279,"title":"","content":"<b>lif'ne:</b> Atavism (lit. &quot;inner power&quot;)<br /> <b>zud:</b> Inherent ability; a dread power<br /> <b>besthima:</b> a psychic power (lit. &quot;blessed thought&quot;)<br /> <b>aylum:</b> a stag, a buck<br /> <b>argu:</b> a doe<br /> <b>dhusu:</b> a donkey<br /> <b>dhur:</b> a male equine; a stallion<br /> <b>em'e:</b> a female equine; a mare<br /> <b>kamun:</b> a female bird; a hen<br /> <b>bulsen:</b> a male bird; a rooster, a cockerel","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T02:48:21-07:00","id":498577,"title":"","content":"Really like what you're doing here, good stuff! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Is there any link or place where I can see English to First Tongue in alphabetical order? I'd like to look up certain words and write them as First Tongue or perhaps straight Sumer in forum-play posts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T07:48:44-07:00","id":498831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=498577#post498577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really like what you're doing here, good stuff! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Is there any link or place where I can see English to First Tongue in alphabetical order? I'd like to look up certain words and write them as First Tongue or perhaps straight Sumer in forum-play posts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Check the original post, first page. All the dictionary links and FT-to-English links I use are there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T22:48:43-07:00","id":499840,"title":"","content":"*nods* Yeah, I was looking more for English to First Tongue for ease of reference... ^__^ I've seen the amazing work done in the spreadsheets and links, though they list First Tongue in alphabetical order, which I find hard when I'm after a what a specific English word might be in First Tongue...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T23:11:36-07:00","id":499882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=499840#post499840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*nods* Yeah, I was looking more for English to First Tongue for ease of reference... ^__^ I've seen the amazing work done in the spreadsheets and links, though they list First Tongue in alphabetical order, which I find hard when I'm after a what a specific English word might be in First Tongue...</div> </div> </div> </div>There's an English-to-FT dictionary currently being worked on by Litheon, I believe, but it's a bit of a work in progress. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> When it's ready, I'll put a link up on the original post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T23:44:37-07:00","id":499910,"title":"","content":"Ah, awesome! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+x