ew-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=500863#post500863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, it's ready to be used, but all the word categories (noun, verb, adjective) is all off. Plus I haven't finished the sorting by like terms row. Feel free to put it up, since even the other link goes there anyway. ;P<br /> <br /> It'll be WIP for a long while (since I've been working on other projects, like cards, GM screens, actual work, moving etc etc.) so may as well post it.<br /> <br /> And even if it isn't posted, you can find it on around page 26 of this forum thread.<br /> Or right here!<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1TSgzm7rkkXyobz7wHfIGhGHT34zItHorGJnxsIvsisU/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Oh, also, misread something, but you CAN sort by English to FT on this. There are filters. you can also sort by canon word and related terms. just click the martini looking thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are a saint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T22:58:02-07:00","id":501395,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much! I'm totally going to go to town on adding First Tongue words into my Pbp dialogue now! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T17:55:43-07:00","id":513525,"title":"","content":"I was just curious about some things, and figured I could ask for help. For ease, I'll just split the request into two parts. The first is some help doing translation to english. More specifically, I was hoping you could figure out the meaning of some Idigam names thrown out in the 2e core. I also listed what the book says about them in case it helps.<br /> <br /> \u2022Sul-Kushiri: Born of a hot, rusting junkyard. Influences are Heat, Metal, Rust.<br /> <br /> \u2022Guhinim Thirih\u2019Lulul: Born of a business conference. Influences are Money, Influence, Deception.<br /> <br /> \u2022Sehendenna Gaskalla: Born of the arctic waters around a research vessel. Ban is that it must flee from that hotter than blood, Bane is metal from the ship.<br /> <br /> \u2022Lulusumhul: Earthbound, Born around a goat herd. Ban prevents it from harming animal herders, bane is hand-spun goat wool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T10:39:11-07:00","id":517164,"title":"","content":"So, out of curiosity (and a love for Con-Langs) do you think that the First Tongue is grammatically functional enough to be spoken as an actual language, similar to Quenya from LoTR? Because that would be pretty awesome if people started speaking First Tongue. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5700-nuwisha-nutjob","name":"Nuwisha Nutjob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T11:58:46-07:00","id":517223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nuwisha Nutjob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=517164#post517164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, out of curiosity (and a love for Con-Langs) do you think that the First Tongue is grammatically functional enough to be spoken as an actual language, similar to Quenya from LoTR? Because that would be pretty awesome if people started speaking First Tongue. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's getting there. I still have a LOT of ground to cover, and I read somewhere that a language needs 2000 words (I have about 1,400+ actual words ready) to at LEAST be workable. My goal is that, like Quenya, Klingon or Valyrian, that people can start speaking Uremehir at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T11:26:18-07:00","id":518325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=517223#post517223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's getting there. I still have a LOT of ground to cover, and I read somewhere that a language needs 2000 words (I have about 1,400+ actual words ready) to at LEAST be workable. My goal is that, like Quenya, Klingon or Valyrian, that people can start speaking Uremehir at some point.</div> </div> </div> </div>EPIC! Keep up the good work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5700-nuwisha-nutjob","name":"Nuwisha Nutjob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T20:05:57-07:00","id":523884,"title":"","content":"I may have missed something, but do you have any thoughts on First Tongue grammar? I have a little experience with constructed languages, and I'd be willing to take a crack at working out some basic syntax and morphology, if you like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T21:19:00-07:00","id":528487,"title":"","content":"Two requests:<br /> <br /> &quot;Star-crossed Wolf&quot; and &quot;Unraveling Night-Sky&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T22:15:55-07:00","id":529599,"title":"","content":"@CatDoom: I do have some rough notes written down on how I do things, so if you'd like to take a look and offer input, that would be cool. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Translations:<br /> <br /> dawu: to ravel; to wind; to twist; to wind up<br /> kudawu: to unwind; to undo; to be undone, like a ball of yarn or string<br /> Kulkaggabhu-Ur: Star-Crossed Wolf (totem)<br /> Ur Kulumulan/Ur-Kulumalan/Urkulumalan: Star-Crossed Wolf (non-totem)<br /> Kudawu Khil-Ulke: Unravelling Night-Sky<br /> sengh: to cook, to prepare food<br /> tuth: to slap, to smack, to swat<br /> sketuth: lit. meaning &quot;cook-slap&quot;, it refers to the act in Baltic myths of a werewolf cooking their meat by slapping someone in the face with it<br /> Sunluhal: The crippled boys of Baltic myth who lead werewolves/The Hounds of God to their Christmas parties (lit. &quot;the humble masters&quot;)<br /> gindu lalarak: hall closet<br /> gaz'gal: a basket, sturdier than decorative ones, used for carrying loads such as food or clothing; a hamper<br /> assi: a hinge, a strap<br /> ubbu: a hose; tubing<br /> sakanafur: an inglenook<br /> sigi: fleece, fur, fluff; padding, insulation; to be fluffy or furry<br /> gugh: a ladder<br /> isihar: a lamp, a lantern; a torch<br /> mudhur: to be dirty; filthy, dirty, unclean<br /> mudhur susk: dirty laundry, dirty clothes<br /> suskthus: laundry, laundry room (lit. &quot;a bathing area for clothes&quot;)<br /> zas: grass, turf<br /> zaskur: lawnmower (lit. &quot;grass-reaper&quot;)<br /> garum umfisah: library (lit. &quot;home of scholars&quot;)<br /> dubhur: light switch (lit. &quot;makes light&quot;)<br /> fantha: any sort of building support or supporting device, such as a support beam or lintel<br /> cahha: a story, a tale<br /> <br /> &quot;Cahha kal nihhina&quot;: &quot;This story is true&quot;, a common beginning to most werewolf stories. It's roughly equivalent to &quot;once upon a time&quot;, &quot;once...&quot; or &quot;long ago&quot;, but with more historical and important connotations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 05-27-2015, 10:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T23:10:47-07:00","id":529622,"title":"","content":"Dude, that's awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T09:38:42-07:00","id":530061,"title":"","content":"<b>inu: </b>duty; an obligation; responsibility, accountability; to be responsible or accountable for something (Litheon, if you could change the existing inu entry to this, that would be great)<br /> <b>men'u: </b>affection, caring, fondness<br /> <b>namzeh</b><b>:</b> agreeableness; to be diplomatic or agreeable<br /> <b>zeh: </b>diplomacy<br /> <b>nihthuh: </b>amicability, geniality; to be pleasant or good to be around<br /> <b>zi'il: </b>benevolence; to be of a benevolent nature<br /> <b>namsum: </b>charity, giving<br /> <b>namluk: </b>cleanliness; to be clean<br /> <b>hugidam: </b>confidence; to be confident<br /> <b>ummus: </b>forethought, planning, consideration; to be considerate<br /> <b>shusuf: </b>to gather together, to pull together; teamwork, working together<br /> <b>kal astagdu: </b>the Uratha version of &quot;shusuf&quot;, referring to teamwork and meaning &quot;to become one hunter&quot;<br /> <b>nihdhi: </b>courtesy, politeness; good manners or behaviour<br /> <b>mudhhal:</b> creativity; to be creative <br /> <b>u'se: </b>to be curious, to wonder; wondering, curiosity, pondering<br /> <b>aru: </b>to be dedicated to; devotion, dedication<br /> <b>basdu: </b>dignity, self-respect<br /> <b>takus: </b>a werewolf-oriented word that means to hunt persistently, to be diligent, or to persevere in one's duties; the werewolf version of <b>agus</b><br /> <b>agus: </b>to work, to toil; to persevere, to be diligent<br /> <b>skirin: </b>discretion, caution, guardedness<br /> <br /> To be continued later. This makes three or four different word lists I'm working on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T21:50:29-07:00","id":532759,"title":"","content":"Hi everybody!<br /> <br /> I'm the storyteller for a nWoD crossover game, prominently featuring Changing Breeds - which I'm casting in a similar role to what they had in cWoD, as the dispersed, former peers of the Uratha themselves. The chronicle is Mirrors, Monsters, and Misfits. I'll try to post about it in a more proper context later!<br /> <br /> First Tongue is showing up prominently as I build up my reveals. In fact, seeing this thread is why I signed up here. (I had an account at White Wolf long ago. I'm sure it's somewhere safe)<br /> <br /> I'd like to help with this project, as much as I'm certain I'll be getting out of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Here's the general way that I'm handling language in my game:<br /> <br /> Anything in nWoD takes precedence over cWoD if there's an overlap, but as with any language there will be reuses of terms.<br /> <br /> cWoD Common Parlance and Vulgar Argot and Old Form and such things are still used. They would only appear as First Tongue if there's a specific proper noun or import word.<br /> <br /> cWoD &quot;First Tongue&quot; terms replaced by nWoD ones become the general terms as used by the Fera or all Therians ( * ) while nWoD ones are specific to the Uratha. For example, a Nuwisha might speak of his crinos form, which is called manabozho, and compare it to the crinos form of the Garou (who call themselves Uratha) which is called gaurau. The same Nuwisha might speak of a Simba Heart-Ripper, and compare her Ahroun auspice to the Ahroun auspice of the Garou, which they call Rahu.<br /> <br /> Some of this is deliberate. I'm casting the Uratha as having the greatest, most-dominant culture of the Therians, but who have lost quite a lot of knowledge in the process. They'll be discovering that some Fera have ideas and terms of which they aren't aware.<br /> <br /> Some of it is also deliberately mismatched. There just isn't a one-to-one matchup of all the concepts involved, and that's just fine. <br /> <br /> Terms from Changing Breeds are included into First Tongue. If they don't match the Sumerian Grimming, that's fine. Languages do funny things. For example, even though the Uratha would scoff at the notion, our Nuwisha and Simba might ask one about their wolf Nahual, or point out when their Aietha is being displayed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Here's the first major reveal I was able to drop, using an incarnation of First Tongue. It was delivered by a spirit ally to a character who was briefly separated from her body and starting a spirit quest. She happened to be near a cenotaph, which she couldn't approach because of the Minjur ban (adopted from cWoD Ratkin as a fun surprise they're still cogitating on). I'm sure that a version of it would be greatly improved by the development in this thread, but presented as-written!<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Annitu kashurra,<br /> Annitu sibum!<br /> (behold greatness, behold o witness.)<br /> <br /> Abzu imbaru lapan, Tammabukku matum.<br /> (primeval mists before, in the land of dragons --<br /> that being lost to time in the land of dragons)<br /> Rakbu Minjur, suqammumu Minjur, Rakbu im Autochthon.<br /> (messenger mice, silent mice, messengers beside god-machine)<br /> Abzu kimah lapan, la'atzu lapan<br /> (primevalland of mist, land of spirits)<br /> Ikkibu mitutu lapan, Minjur-zu. Ikkibu Erset la tari, Minjur-zu.<br /> (Forbidden from the land land of the dead, you Minjur. <br /> Forbidden from the land of no return, you Minjur)<br /> Ilat Kishpu Kashurra.<br /> (Sorcery Supreme and awesome)<br /> Cacama, cacama, cacama!<br /> (amen amen amen)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ( * ) In the context of my game, all of the breeds are Therians. The survivors of the wolves' dominance are the Fera. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T21:56:06-07:00","id":532763,"title":"","content":"So just so I understand what you're asking: you'd like me to create a &quot;true&quot; First Tongue of this for your players to compare it to to rebuild the old language?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T07:38:26-07:00","id":533174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=532763#post532763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So just so I understand what you're asking: you'd like me to create a &quot;true&quot; First Tongue of this for your players to compare it to to rebuild the old language?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, no. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm jumping in the thread to help out! What I posted was some that I'd already done and is official in terms of my chronicle. I posted it because I thought it might be interesting to share some First Tongue &quot;in the field&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T09:51:56-07:00","id":533315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=533174#post533174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, no. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm jumping in the thread to help out! What I posted was some that I'd already done and is official in terms of my chronicle. I posted it because I thought it might be interesting to share some First Tongue &quot;in the field&quot;.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sweet! More translators, helpers, etc. are always appreciated! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Do you have a wordlist of stuff you've translated so far, other than that lovely snippet you posted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T14:54:46-07:00","id":533661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=533315#post533315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sweet! More translators, helpers, etc. are always appreciated! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Do you have a wordlist of stuff you've translated so far, other than that lovely snippet you posted?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aha, now we come around full circle! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> My snippet was the first thing I wrote out for my current chronicle. I was creating my own First Tongue glossary, which was rather laborious and incomplete.<br /> <br /> As a part of that I was searching the web for more First Tongue that had been already done. In the course of doing that I found the thread on White Wolf's forums, and shortly after that found this thread. <br /> <br /> And so here I am!<br /> <br /> I'll be going through the glossaries and linked spreadsheets asap to catch up.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T15:14:19-07:00","id":533676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=533661#post533661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aha, now we come around full circle! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> My snippet was the first thing I wrote out for my current chronicle. I was creating my own First Tongue glossary, which was rather laborious and incomplete.<br /> <br /> As a part of that I was searching the web for more First Tongue that had been already done. In the course of doing that I found the thread on White Wolf's forums, and shortly after that found this thread.<br /> <br /> And so here I am!<br /> <br /> I'll be going through the glossaries and linked spreadsheets asap to catch up.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If it also helps, I'm thinking of putting out how I come up with the grammar beyond Grimming, and a couple other peeps have offered to work on that with me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T18:38:14-07:00","id":533867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=533676#post533676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it also helps, I'm thinking of putting out how I come up with the grammar beyond Grimming, and a couple other peeps have offered to work on that with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be very helpful, yes!<br /> <br /> I had a few thoughts on that. Nothing too concrete yet, but that spirits and simpler minded entities would be very straightforward. &quot;Noun verb.&quot; &quot;Noun verb object.&quot; &quot;Noun adjective.&quot; Since the language never had a Noah Webster to clean it up and organize it, people using First Tongue would tend to follow their native structure and grammar. &quot;Adjective noun verb adverb indirect-object direct-object.&quot;<br /> <br /> I didn't have much thought about conjugation and the like.<br /> <br /> I'm the cliath here, and you're the elder. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> [edited to add: Is there any part of this project to gather Common Parlance, Old Form, or Vulgar Argot like concepts? ]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":6192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","user":"Simon Darkstep","date":". 05-30-2015, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T19:00:38-07:00","id":533884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=533867#post533867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would be very helpful, yes!<br /> <br /> I had a few thoughts on that. Nothing too concrete yet, but that spirits and simpler minded entities would be very straightforward. &quot;Noun verb.&quot; &quot;Noun verb object.&quot; &quot;Noun adjective.&quot; Since the language never had a Noah Webster to clean it up and organize it, people using First Tongue would tend to follow their native structure and grammar. &quot;Adjective noun verb adverb indirect-object direct-object.&quot;<br /> <br /> I didn't have much thought about conjugation and the like.<br /> <br /> I'm the cliath here, and you're the elder. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> [edited to add: Is there any part of this project to gather Common Parlance, Old Form, or Vulgar Argot like concepts? ]</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, funny you bring this up: werewolves have their own dialect of First Tongue (stated in canon somewhere), but with what appears to be more wolf/animal/lunar-oriented concepts in lieu of more common spirit parlance (personal thoughts/observation?). Idigam appear to borrow more from modern Sumerian in their First Tongue, and also more frequently use glottal stops. &quot;Old Form&quot; is the Spirit Tongue as the spirits speak it, the purest form of the language out there. I have marked down where I can, in definitions, what is Werewolf-oriented and what isn't.<br /> <br /> I'll try and see if I can find my grammar notes to share with you all. They're around here somewhere....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T19:53:43-07:00","id":533936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=533884#post533884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, funny you bring this up: werewolves have their own dialect of First Tongue (stated in canon somewhere)</div> </div> </div> </div>Both the 1e and 2e corebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T19:54:55-07:00","id":533938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=533936#post533936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both the 1e and 2e corebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T12:24:29-07:00","id":534706,"title":"","content":"<u>Tommy Shoveljaw and the Heart of Ages</u><br /> <br /> (This is from the perspective I\u2019m presenting in my chronicle. It may vary from yours. Specifically, I\u2019m making a point of using cWoD terms and concepts to round out what\u2019s present in nWoD, and wrapping it all up in a crossover chronicle.)<br /> <br /> Tommy Shoveljaw was used to being big. Even among the Uratha of his Pack and Tribe, he had few rivals for size or strength.<br /> <br /> Looking up, and up, and up, all he could do was whistle through his teeth at the enormous size of the tree that loomed before him. The trunk was as large around as a building. The top was not at all visible.<br /> <br /> He was, perhaps, the smallest thing around.<br /> <br /> He was no stranger to visiting the Umbra \u2013 the Shadow as some called it. This, however, was the deepest he had ventured into the <i>hisil</i>. The forest seemed to enclose him fully, paths forward and back appearing and vanishing like dappled sunlight filtered through leaves.<br /> <br /> Tommy had been told that he would know the Heart of Ages when he found it. He was quite sure this was it. His pack\u2019s last several battles had become tougher and tougher. He knew that he needed more understanding, to deal with the spirits and other night folk. The Heart of Ages was supposed to be the wisest entity around.<br /> <br /> Just in front of the trunk of the Heart of Ages stood a totem pole. Seven segments composed the pole, each as high as the span of a forearm, and each covered in carved leering faces and strange glyphs. The segments sometimes rotated creakily.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh great tree, Heart of Ages, teach me wisdom!\u201d Tommy called out. The words sounded lame, even to the big Rahu. Communication was never his strong point.<br /> <br /> Two of the segments of the totem pole spun, slowly, the creaking carrying words in a soft spoken baritone. \u201c<i>Sangezin namsu duaf. Uremehir.</i>\u201d (Wisdom begins with attention. (use)First Tongue.)<br /> <br /> Tommy sighed. \u201cCome on, tree. I barely got a \u2018D\u2019 in Spanish. Dos tacos de chupacabras, por favor. Donde es el telefono?\u201d<br /> <br /> The Heart of Ages responded not at all, nor did the totem pole speak. Trees were humorless; who would have guessed?<br /> <br /> \u201c<i>Uremehir</i>\u2026 uhhh. Uremeh-dug\u2026. Uhh\u2026 <i>Uremehir</i> no-dug-oh.\u201d (I don\u2019t speak First Tongue, in broken First Tongue. Maybe if Tommy said it louder.)<br /> <br /> Tommy waited for a response. It was a long way here and a long way back, just to be foiled by a language barrier. He spared himself a rare moment of self pity. If only there were some sort of glossary or phrase book, he could use to get by.<br /> <br /> The situation seemed hopeless. So much for this show. He bowed from the waist. \u201cThank you, oh great Heart of Ages. I will learn <i>Uremehir</i> and return.\u201d He turned and took a step the way he had come.<br /> <br /> The totem pole creaked. \u201c<i>Zu</i>.\u201d (Learn.) The word was shockingly blunt. Tommy turned in his tracks, staring.<br /> <br /> The segments of the pole spun, sometimes one or two, never more than three. They would stop, alternate, change directions. Each time it creaked the words of simple <i>Uremehir</i>, one of the faces would be leering at him, watching him. The spoken words were accompanied by images of light and shadow dancing in the depths of the forest, showing him ideas, objects, and concepts.<br /> <br /> It was going to be a long Seeking\u2026. The Heart of Ages was going to start at a beginning, and allow no shortcuts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> While Tommy and the Heart of Ages are having lessons in First Tongue, here are a few terms he might have in his phrasebook.<br /> <br /> <br /> Night Folk: (Common Parlance) People of the night. Any person who has supernatural power, such as a mage, werewolf, vampire, changeling, etc. Sometimes used as well for those without supernatural power, or with a limited form of power, but who are aware.<br /> <br /> <i>Khilerin</i>: (First Tongue) lit. \u201cNight Folk.\u201d Some speakers slur the pronunciation like \u201cKhlern.\u201d There is some debate whether the term was adopted from <i>Uremehir</i> or adopted by <i>Uremehir</i>.<br /> <br /> Backstage: (Vulgar Argot) A rough synonym for Night Folk. Some supernaturals couch their discussions in show terms. To be backstage, or to be a backstage person, is to be one of the ones in the know. To have a backstage pass is to be a normal mortal who is intentionally or accidentally involved with the supernatural enough to become aware of some truths. To preserve secrecy, backstage passes should be dealt with quickly, otherwise the band will acquire roadies or a fan club.<br /> <br /> Band, the: (Vulgar Argot) To be in the band is to be part of a group of supernaturals. Sometimes called an Act, a Troupe, etc.<br /> <br /> Audience, the: (Vulgar Argot) Those at or near a Show, but not Backstage. Most backstage folk are careful not to reveal too much to the audience. Some clever Bands will make use of Roadies to help keep the Audience where they belong and limit the growth of the Fan Club.<br /> <br /> Show, the: (Vulgar Argot) A whole scene where supernaturals encounter each other. To get ready for the show is to prepare for the encounter, gearing up for battle, intrigue, or diplomacy.<br /> <br /> Roadies: (Vulgar Argot) Normal mortals who have become aware of the supernatural intentionally or accidentally. This usually implies that they stay close to a Band for protection. Roadies may also be good mortal allies.<br /> <br /> Fan Club: (Vulgar Argot) Normal mortals who have become aware of the supernatural intentionally or accidentally. This usually implies that they have been able to return, more or less, to their normal lives, still aware of the supernatural.<br /> <br /> <i>Ansala</i>: (First Tongue) A performer or performance. Used as a First Tongue equivalent to Backstage or Band. Also used generically to refer to the whole scene of a supernatural encounter, and the people and entities therein, as a First Tongue equivalent to Show. Some spirits who interact with people may pick up this term. They probably would not understand the concept of a show, but would use the term to describe an encounter of some interest.<br /> <br /> <i>Ansalag</i>: (First Tongue) lit. \u201cAlpha Performer\u201d All of those directly involved in an <i>Ansala</i>, in the sense of a supernatural encounter. A spirit using the term probably means itself, along with others who can directly perceive or affect it.<br /> <br /> <i>Ansalatra</i>: (First Tongue) lit. \u201cBeta Performer\u201d All of those indirectly involved in an <i>Ansala</i>. This may include bystanders, victims, or investigators. A spirit using the term probably means others who cannot perceive or affect it, and may use the term to describe mortals under the effects of it\u2019s Influences.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> [Edit to correct formatting]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":6192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","user":"Simon Darkstep","date":". 05-31-2015, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T23:30:37-07:00","id":536602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=529599#post529599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@CatDoom: I do have some rough notes written down on how I do things, so if you'd like to take a look and offer input, that would be cool. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sure! Can you kick them over to me in a PM or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-02T07:59:28-07:00","id":537010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=536602#post536602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure! Can you kick them over to me in a PM or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>You bet! When I get a moment, they'll head your way. Conlangers unite!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874