 one of my Uratha's deed names: 'Drums-Fall-Silent'. As in 'that dude is so impressive that when he starts doing stuff, even fundamental things like the beat in the background stop and take notice 'cause daaaamn.'<br /> <br /> Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I love what your work has brought to the game - I have used your thread more than once to blend in some first tongue flavor!</div> </div> </div> </div>It's my pleasure to help! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> When I have a moment, I'll get that done as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T02:09:36-07:00","id":542398,"title":"","content":"Does ancient pseudo-Sumerian have a word for shark? I want to call a fetish something like &quot;Shark-tooth Blade&quot; but can't find through my own research anything like Shark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T07:26:25-07:00","id":542573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gullinbursti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=542398#post542398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does ancient pseudo-Sumerian have a word for shark? I want to call a fetish something like &quot;Shark-tooth Blade&quot; but can't find through my own research anything like Shark.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be <b>Rogeakuk Uhur</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <b>Rogea</b> means &quot;shark&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T09:24:06-07:00","id":542682,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T09:58:06-07:00","id":542716,"title":"","content":"Apocalypse was really on the ball with some of these terms, though I guess they took a lot from existing languages and myths, which in turn descended from the 'First Tongue.' I've always avoided the study of languages but this thread is very interesting and educational.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T10:22:11-07:00","id":542734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=542716#post542716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apocalypse was really on the ball with some of these terms, though I guess they took a lot from existing languages and myths, which in turn descended from the 'First Tongue.' I've always avoided the study of languages but this thread is very interesting and educational.</div> </div> </div> </div>Intentional part on the writers' end. They said that some Apocalypse terms have been Grimmified and added to the language as an &quot;in-joke&quot;. When in doubt, yank something from the old lines and give it an Uremehir spin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T09:58:58-07:00","id":548840,"title":"","content":"<b>Barbrarilen:</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Bhalakh-Nethul-Mekhar:</b> Drums-Fall-Silent (lit. &quot;drums respectfully lower and become silent [in his presence]&quot;)<br /> <br /> <b>bhalakh:</b> Drum, drumbeats<br /> <b>ne:</b> To be respectful; to show respect; respect, respectfulness</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T21:17:37-07:00","id":549744,"title":"","content":"Awesome. Thanks, Sikla! One heck of a mouthful, but that is exactly what I was looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3070,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","user":"Barbrarilen","date":". 06-11-2015, 12:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T09:00:58-07:00","id":550233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=549744#post549744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awesome. Thanks, Sikla! One heck of a mouthful, but that is exactly what I was looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not the worst one I've come up with. One word: <b>Shariminbharduthdur</b>.<br /> <br /> It was at that moment I realized I needed to pay better attention to grammatical rules in a language with agglutinative properties that remind me of German's extremely long constructions. Seriously, in canon, some of the Idigam's servants have names that are <i>seven syllables long</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T11:11:53-07:00","id":550366,"title":"","content":"<b>abrekh:</b> earnestness, seriousness, solemness, graveness; to be serious, to be intense, to be earnest<br /> <b>zihul:</b> enthusiasm, liveliness, verve, vigour; to be enthusiastic, to be manic, to be extremely happy<br /> <b>zisahfa:</b> ethics, morals, code of behaviour<br /> <b>sehene:</b> to be ethical, to be honourable, to be lawful<br /> <b>dhi'ri:</b> excellence, high quality, of the highest standard; to be excellent, to be supreme<br /> <b>wardhu:</b> faithfulness, devotion, servitude; to be faithful or devoted (non-werewolf phrasing)<br /> <b>amadu:</b> a Forsaken-exclusive word for faithfulness, devotion, servitude or the qualities thereof; it roughly means &quot;Mother's doings&quot; or &quot;the doings of Mother [as we perform them]&quot;<br /> <b>lultagus:</b> a Pure-exclusive word for faithfulness, devotion, servitude or the qualities thereof; it's more popular with Fire-Touched, but it's spread among the cause, and it roughly means &quot;to hunt down and kill lies&quot;<br /> <b>ghurrum:</b> flexing, bending or the capability to do so; to be flexible, figuratively and/or literally speaking<br /> <b>skaglasum:</b> forgiveness, to forgive; a pardon, to pardon, to excuse or let off the hook","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 06-21-2015, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T18:20:49-07:00","id":550940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=550366#post550366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>abhrekh:</b> earnestness, seriousness, solemness, graveness; to be serious, to be intense, to be earnest<br /> <b>ghurrum:</b> flexing, bending or the capability to do so; to be flexible, figuratively and/or literally speaking</div> </div> </div> </div>How are you handling words that could be verbs or could be adjectives, like &quot;ghurrum&quot;? It could mean a that a person is flexible, or that a person is flexing. Is there implied conjugation in First Tongue?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T18:36:38-07:00","id":550958,"title":"","content":"&quot;Simon is not allowed to take a selfie with a Lune.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Simon nu kal du kuku-mede abha Lunim.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <i><b>ku</b>: Oneself, I, self<br /> <b>kuku</b>: Word-doubled usage indicating something of or by or to oneself.<br /> <b>mede</b>: picture or image<br /> <b>du</b>: to make or act<br /> <b>abha</b>: with</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> [edited for better grammaring]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":6192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","user":"Simon Darkstep","date":". 06-12-2015, 10:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T19:04:14-07:00","id":550978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=550940#post550940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How are you handling words that could be verbs or could be adjectives, like &quot;ghurrum&quot;? It could mean a that a person is flexible, or that a person is flexing. Is there implied conjugation in First Tongue?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>First Tongue is...funny, that way. It all depends on how you phrase it that helps infer meaning. For example, <b>ghurrum kadul</b> is &quot;a flexible stick&quot;, but &quot;a stick's flexibility&quot; could be either <b>kadul ghurrum</b> or <b>kadul namghurrum</b> (the latter meaning &quot;a stick's flexible-ness&quot; thanks to the nam- prefix). The strange language that is this poetic, proto-Sumerian creation relies a lot on context in several cases, kind of like how the number of homonyms in Sumerian suggests there was a different way to infer meanings, such as using tone. It's a tricky language that way.<br /> <br /> Edit: Missed your earlier post. According to my translations, <b>du</b> means to do or act, <b>abha</b> means &quot;with&quot;, and <b>ku</b> means &quot;I, me, mine&quot;. I can't remember the other translations off the bat, but I will say this: <b>my translations do not have to be your translations</b>. If you come up with words different to the ones I've put up, that is totally okay and cool, because nWoD is a sandbox and it's awesome if everyone has their own version of FT. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 06-11-2015, 10:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T21:33:46-07:00","id":551076,"title":"","content":"Indeed!<br /> <br /> I'm trying to be as faithful to the lexicon as I can be. A language must be able to communicate. A conlang may be somewhat relaxed, being window dressing for the vast majority of the fans. <br /> <br /> I'm still chugging through all the as-posteds trying to get them together into my own notes, to pull back out from. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T21:53:36-07:00","id":551098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=551076#post551076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed!<br /> <br /> I'm trying to be as faithful to the lexicon as I can be. A language must be able to communicate. A conlang may be somewhat relaxed, being window dressing for the vast majority of the fans.<br /> <br /> I'm still chugging through all the as-posteds trying to get them together into my own notes, to pull back out from. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>We have wiggle room, believe me. I've had to come up with certain grammatical constructions not talked about already by the seat of my pants. One does not realize how hard it is to find a way to express the word &quot;but&quot; until they have to translate a block of text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T07:52:08-07:00","id":551467,"title":"","content":"Updated my post! <br /> <br /> I agree entirely on having wiggle room. In fact, that sounds like something I was imagining in-setting characters having to deal with as well. <br /> <br /> Simple spirits might very well only manage words or short phrases as their thoughts. &quot;Greedy!&quot; &quot;Delicious!&quot; &quot;Hate!&quot; &quot;Fear werewolf!&quot; and the like. That's what I had in mind with the word-doubling for emphasis.<br /> <br /> Others might combine the language with a metered and lyrical delivery, which is a little like the verse I posted earlier. Or they might be demonstrative (showing their meaning by flexing their Influences) or empathic.<br /> <br /> People coming from the contemporary world would have a lot of more complicated things to say. &quot;Next Tuesday we need to step sideways and hide until the eclipse, then launch a coordinated strike along with our Kitsune allies, on the haunted Verge and burn all the Fetters, then we can regroup and face the entity hiding in the attic.&quot; They'd also probably be much more literal than lyrical. <br /> <br /> I like where you're going with the modifier-object pairs. That makes a lot of sense. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Inspired by examples:<br /> <br /> <i>Hanzer Ga'a. Hanzer Ga'a. Hanzer hanzer Ga'a.</i><br /> (Red fox. Red fox. Red Red fox.)<br /> <br /> <i>Hadar Garum, Hanzer Ga'a. Dar Garum, Hanzer hanzer Ga'a.</i><br /> (Burn down the house, red fox. Destroy the house, red red fox.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T07:56:52-07:00","id":553038,"title":"","content":"Simon, I'll get to your stuff in a moment, when I have more time. For now, have some translations I've been meaning to post:<br /> <br /> <b>ku'otok:</b> a whip, especially one used as a weapon or as an object of discipline or torture (animal whips and the like are usually referred to as <b>usan</b>)<br /> <b>kabrah:</b> zest, energy, spitfire, liveliness; a fiery personality or temperament; to be full of &quot;piss and vinegar&quot;, as it were; to be spicy (like a food) or a hot-blooded individual<br /> <b>apan:</b> common sense, shrewdness, sensibleness, canniness; a voice of reason<br /> <b>naukh:</b> an advisor or advisory service, a councillor; to advise, to rede, to give council<br /> <b>barogh:</b> usurper; to usurp, to overthrow; an uprising or coup<br /> <b>yanas:</b> order, zen, peace; the proper way of things<br /> <br /> And Litheon, I have a correction: <b>daa</b> should be <b>da'a</b>, and <b>haa</b> should be <b>ha'a</b>, since I don't believe that double-vowels can exist in words without a word-final consonant. <b>Hu'</b> should also be <b>hu</b>, because I haven't seen a construction where a glottal stop is word-final.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 06-21-2015, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T17:19:02-07:00","id":553568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=553038#post553038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Litheon, I have a correction: <b>daa</b> should be <b>da'a</b>, and <b>haa</b> should be <b>ha'a</b>, since I don't believe that double-vowels can exist in words without a word-final consonant.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fairly odd restriction, though come to think of it, it would appear to tell us something about First Tongue pronunciation. Double vowels are most likely written to indicate long vowels, and it would be strange for long vowels to occur only before a consonant. On the other hand, it's possible that all vowels in open syllables are long, while vowels in closed syllables may be either long or short. Thus, doubling the vowel in writing would only be necessary in closed syllables, since we don't need to be told that open syllable vowels are long.<br /> <br /> This appears to have been how vowel length worked in ancient Egyptian (though the Egyptian vowel system as a whole isn't that well understood, since the Egyptian writing system didn't explicitly indicate vowels until they switched to the Greek-derived Coptic alphabet). Sumerian, on the other hand, probably didn't distinguish vowels based on length, but there's evidently some debate on that topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T17:53:06-07:00","id":553586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=553568#post553568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a fairly odd restriction, though come to think of it, it would appear to tell us something about First Tongue pronunciation. Double vowels are most likely written to indicate long vowels, and it would be strange for long vowels to occur only before a consonant. On the other hand, it's possible that all vowels in open syllables are long, while vowels in closed syllables may be either long or short. Thus, doubling the vowel in writing would only be necessary in closed syllables, since we don't need to be told that open syllable vowels are long.<br /> <br /> This appears to have been how vowel length worked in ancient Egyptian (though the Egyptian vowel system as a whole isn't that well understood, since the Egyptian writing system didn't explicitly indicate vowels until they switched to the Greek-derived Coptic alphabet). Sumerian, on the other hand, probably didn't distinguish vowels based on length, but there's evidently some debate on that topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the double-vowels are totally justified to avoid too many homonyms? One of the rules the writers put down is &quot;avoid homonyms as much as possible&quot;.<br /> <br /> Edit: I've also sent you a message on my notes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 06-13-2015, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T00:29:47-07:00","id":554010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=553586#post553586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the double-vowels are totally justified to avoid too many homonyms? One of the rules the writers put down is &quot;avoid homonyms as much as possible&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could look at it that way. In languages like Latin and Classical Arabic, long vowels are treated as separate sounds from short vowels. So, using the convention of writing double vowels for long vowels in closed syllables, &quot;bat&quot; could be a totally different word from &quot;baat,&quot; and you could hear the difference in how long the vowel sound was held relative to other speech sounds. In this case, however, &quot;ba&quot; would always be pronounced as &quot;baa&quot;, because it's an open syllable, though adding the second &quot;a&quot; is unnecessary since the vowel length is completely predictable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T08:15:26-07:00","id":554319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=554010#post554010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could look at it that way. In languages like Latin and Classical Arabic, long vowels are treated as separate sounds from short vowels. So, using the convention of writing double vowels for long vowels in closed syllables, &quot;bat&quot; could be a totally different word from &quot;baat,&quot; and you could hear the difference in how long the vowel sound was held relative to other speech sounds. In this case, however, &quot;ba&quot; would always be pronounced as &quot;baa&quot;, because it's an open syllable, though adding the second &quot;a&quot; is unnecessary since the vowel length is completely predictable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen a word-final h tacked on to some words after open vowels like &quot;a&quot;. Perhaps that could solve the issue of having no consonant at the end, so a word like &quot;daa&quot; is properly written as &quot;daah&quot;. I don't see this kind of issue with &quot;ii&quot; or &quot;uu&quot;, though, it appears to be the exception. MAYBE &quot;ee&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T08:46:20-07:00","id":554347,"title":"","content":"Well, some languages <i>do</i> allow an actual &quot;h&quot; sound at the end of a word; Arabic would be one example of that. It's also worth noting that the &quot;h&quot; produced by Grimm's law was a velar fricative, like the &quot;ch&quot; at the end of <i>Bach</i> or the &quot;x&quot; in the Mexican Spanish pronunciation if <i>M\u00e9xico</i> (well, in most dialects, anyway). American English speakers don't usually pronounce the velar fricative as such, but it's a somewhat &quot;stronger&quot; sound than the English &quot;h&quot;, and is less likely to be dropped at the end of a word.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 06-14-2015, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T08:53:10-07:00","id":554351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=554347#post554347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, some languages <i>do</i> allow an actual &quot;h&quot; sound at the end of a word; Arabic would be one example of that. It's also worth noting that the &quot;h&quot; produced by Grimm's law was a velar fricative, like the &quot;ch&quot; at the end of <i>Bach</i> or the &quot;x&quot; in the Mexican Spanish pronunciation if <i>M\u00e9xico</i> (well, in most dialects, anyway). American English speakers don't usually pronounce the velar fricative as such, but it's a somewhat &quot;stronger&quot; sound than the English &quot;h&quot;, and is less likely to be dropped at the end of a word.</div> </div> </div> </div>Duly noted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T08:04:00-07:00","id":555668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=550958#post550958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Simon is not allowed to take a selfie with a Lune.&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Simon nu kal du kuku-mede abha Lunim.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <i><b>ku</b>: Oneself, I, self<br /> <b>kuku</b>: Word-doubled usage indicating something of or by or to oneself.<br /> <b>mede</b>: picture or image<br /> <b>du</b>: to make or act<br /> <b>abha</b>: with</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> [edited for better grammaring]</div> </div> </div> </div>In my translations, this would be, <b>&quot;Simon nukal du kumede gada Lunim,&quot;</b> with the only differences being how some words are adjoined and a few translations. <b>Gada</b> means &quot;with&quot;, not <b>abha</b> (my mistake), and <b>kumede</b> means &quot;selfie&quot; (lit. &quot;me-picture&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T08:28:18-07:00","id":563047,"title":"","content":"With the new Neolithic teaser out, it's time to crank out a few terms based on what we've been given. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Pangaea has already been translated as <b>Gurihisil</b>, but as for the others....<br /> <br /> <b>Luzuk-Sakh'na:</b> &quot;Stolen heart-stones&quot;, the omphalos stones that the Wise use to protect their settlements<br /> <b>-zi'im:</b> Meaning &quot;living spirits&quot;, it's a suffix used to refer to creatures in the Border Marches that are hybrids of flesh and spirit, the Pangaens<br /> <b>Kadhruzi'im:</b> Any of the major God-Pangaens such as Rat, Wolf or Spider<br /> <b>Dhumamu-Kisura:</b> &quot;Territory/Pllace of the Wild Beasts&quot;, a name for the Border Marches<br /> <b>Sarusagh:</b> &quot;The First to Write&quot;, the Vinca culture of Europe<br /> <b>Tag-Estha:</b> &quot;Hunting-Bound&quot;, those who still live a hunter-gatherer lifestyle in the face of the Agricultural Revolution","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 06-21-2015, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T08:45:59-07:00","id":563053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=563047#post563047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the new Neolithic teaser out, it's time to crank out a few terms based on what we've been given. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Pangaea has already been translated as <b>Gurihisil</b>, but as for the others....<br /> <br /> <b>Dhumamzi'im:</b> Any of the major God-Pangaens such as Rat, Wolf or Spider</div> </div> </div> </div>If I'm translating this correctly, then that term is a bit off as it refers to beasts specifically.<br /> <br /> One of the Pangaeans slain by <i>Urfarah </i>is Mountain <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T09:13:46-07:00","id":563069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=563053#post563053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I'm translating this correctly, then that term is a bit off as it refers to beasts specifically.<br /> <br /> One of the Pangaeans slain by <i>Urfarah </i>is Mountain <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Duly noted! I will look up a term better suited to natural phenomenon in general. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: Fixed with a term that means &quot;wild, untamed&quot; in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 06-21-2015, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T11:44:02-07:00","id":563186,"title":"","content":"A few more terms:<br /> <br /> <b>Al'al-Lukunka:</b> &quot;Those Who Labour in the Fields&quot;, or those who have adopted a farming/sedentary lifestyle in the wake of the Agricultural Revolution<br /> <b>Nam'gal'al-Shaghu:</b> &quot;The Rise of Abundant Fields&quot;, or the Agricultural Revolution<br /> <b>Naafutuzi:</b> &quot;The Lost Souls&quot;, those who were lost or wandering in the wilderness and became Claimed, or succumbed to the whims of the Pangaeans<br /> <b>Kadhrumdur:</b> &quot;The Wild Children&quot;, another name for Pangaeans<br /> <b>Shulasa:</b> &quot;The Defilers&quot;, a name the Pangaens have for the Wise<br /> <b>Namzu-Luhal:</b> &quot;The Wise Masters&quot;, another name for the Wise<br /> <br /> And cleaning up a few terms that are homonyms in Sumerian, so if translated, they don't mash together:<br /> <br /> <b>adal:</b> To engulf, to surround; to spread the arms, to hug, to embrace, or the act(s) thereof<br /> <b>a'il:</b> To raise one's arms or legs up; to carry something over the head, to hold something up off the ground; a worker or labourer; a gofer, or someone whose job is carrying and/or retrieving things<br /> <b>anhal:</b> Defeat, conquering, vaniquishing; to be defeated<br /> <b>a'ash:</b> supplies, goods; to supply<br /> <b>a'az:</b> Wish; to wish, to hope for<br /> <b>ahur:</b> armpit, leg-pit, or any other folds in the limbs or body; bodily orifices<br /> <b>ab:</b> saltwater; the sea<br /> <b>abgu:</b> sea-fish, sea creatures<br /> <b>a'ab:</b> a female cow, a heifer<br /> <b>adh:</b> a log, a plank, or a series or construction made out of; a raft made out of logs or planks<br /> <b>athdha:</b> a car wreck; a shipwreck; an accident involving vehicles; to wreck a vehicle<br /> <b>aham:</b> an artificial pond; a tailings pond; a pond used for irrigation waters or storing water from a dam<br /> <b>agham:</b> a profession; a job; employment<br /> <b>uk:</b> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">a paste; phlegm, mucus, sputum; foam, scum; saliva, spittle</span><br /> <b>ak:</b> to dry out or make dry, such as drying meat, fruit or leather<br /> <b>akan:</b> vomit, effuvia<br /> <b>ahan:</b> a fish with great symbolic importance; a fish seen as divine; a fish-like symbol or effigy<br /> <b>hial:</b> primitive or crude fencing; reed fencing<br /> <b>a'al:</b> hoe, pickaxe; to hoe, to dig with such a tool<br /> <b>alu:</b> demon, evil spirit<br /> <b>al'a:</b> a wooden drum<br /> <b>a'la:</b> irrigation gates; devices used for managing the flow of irrigation waters<br /> <b>ala'a:</b> manacles, chains; metal objects or devices used to bind or hold things down<br /> <b>a'ala:</b> silt, sendiment<br /> <b>a'lal:</b> wood or stone figurines or effigies used for divine purposes, such as a sacred statue; the part of a temple where said effigies are located<br /> <b>aldar:</b> mighty, powerful, awe-inspiring, awesome<br /> <b>al'dar:</b> to assign work; to divide up bigger work or jobs into smaller jobs or activities<br /> <b>a'an:</b> spadix, or the conical-shaped organ parts of flowers and animals<br /> <b>anda:</b> To be physically high up or in a high place<br /> <br /> I'll work on more of the homonyms later. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 06-21-2015, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T12:20:37-07:00","id":563271,"title":"","content":"Hey, Sikla.<br /> <br /> I was hoping I could get you to give me the word for &quot;farm&quot;. I believe your transaltion of 'farmer' is 'matha', so something 'math'-derived would be best (since I've been using something similar until now).<br /> <br /> I am running a pretty big game, I think I will have a cool list soon.<br /> <br /> Is there an up-to-date dictionary? And do you have any interest in making a PDF?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T12:46:06-07:00","id":563303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gebbethine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=563271#post563271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, Sikla.<br /> <br /> I was hoping I could get you to give me the word for &quot;farm&quot;. I believe your transaltion of 'farmer' is 'matha', so something 'math'-derived would be best (since I've been using something similar until now).<br /> <br /> I am running a pretty big game, I think I will have a cool list soon.<br /> <br /> Is there an up-to-date dictionary? And do you have any interest in making a PDF?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's set in a Neolithic period, I've got one already: <b>Al'al-Lukunka</b> was a term for a farmer, or someone from the farming community. If you want a more specialized term, go for <b>ensik</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for dictionaries, try the original post. Two people have compiled a dictionary and phrase-guide. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 06-21-2015, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T15:17:23-07:00","id":563439,"title":"","content":"What's the grammar like for stringing words together? Conjugation? Conjunctions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T15:41:39-07:00","id":563453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=563439#post563439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the grammar like for stringing words together? Conjugation? Conjunctions?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have some notes I can send you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T01:03:06-07:00","id":563801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=563047#post563047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Sarusagh:</b> &quot;The First to Write&quot;, the Vinca culture of Europe</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems a bit odd, as if the Uratha somehow anticipated the invention of writing and had a word for it already when they first encountered it. While it might make sense as a term used in hindsight, when the concept of writing had become more familiar and widespread, I'd recommend giving them a name that's more descriptive of the act of writing, without using a word explicitly meaning &quot;to write.&quot; Maybe something like &quot;They Who Make Scratches in Clay.&quot;<br /> <br /> I would also like to see your notes on morphology and syntax, if you don't mind. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T12:23:54-07:00","id":564435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=563801#post563801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This seems a bit odd, as if the Uratha somehow anticipated the invention of writing and had a word for it already when they first encountered it. While it might make sense as a term used in hindsight, when the concept of writing had become more familiar and widespread, I'd recommend giving them a name that's more descriptive of the act of writing, without using a word explicitly meaning &quot;to write.&quot; Maybe something like &quot;They Who Make Scratches in Clay.&quot;<br /> <br /> I would also like to see your notes on morphology and syntax, if you don't mind. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Noted. I'll come up with a name more appropriate for the time-period. In the meantime, I've sent you and Simon Darkstep the first bits of my syntax notes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T13:32:53-07:00","id":564498,"title":"","content":"Some further homonyms clarified. I had all of the a-homonyms finished, but I messed up on the file. I'll be returning to them when I'm not tempted to throw my computer across the room. &gt;.&lt;<br /> <br /> <b>bha:</b> half; to divide into shares, share, halve; to allot<br /> <b>salasa:</b> thirty<br /> <b>ba:</b> a catch-all term for marine creatures whether supernatural or mundane<br /> <b>nalfazu:</b> any long, flowing garments such as coats, coverings or cloaks that also act as protective clothing \u2014 aprons and ponchos would count as such<br /> <b>bhah:</b> non-combative cutting tools, such as a builder's knife<br /> <b>gabhlu:</b> legs or supporting posts on a piece of furniture<br /> <b>bhadh:</b> remote, distant, faraway; open ground or lack of cover in the distance<br /> <b>fe:</b> one who threshes grain; a threshing edge; the act of threshing grain<br /> <b>fal:</b> digging, excavation; to dig or investigate, as if to find or recover; to recover goods or property<br /> <b>bhala:</b> food waste left over from processing; wasted food, food unfit for consumption<br /> <b>bhantha:</b> child-like, youthful; to be sagacious, energetic, wild<br /> <b>banthu:</b> a quotient<br /> <b>ban'dha:</b> a stanchion or support<br /> <b>banhi:</b> a response or answer to a call or summons<br /> <b>fanhi:</b> taper, bevel, slant, incline<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T14:02:58-07:00","id":564522,"title":"","content":"Just for the sake of clarity, I've worked up a phonemic inventory/pronunciation guide; let me know if I got anything wrong:<br /> <br /> <b>Nasal Consonants</b><br /> <br /> m - pronunciation is roughly the same as English, as in &quot;map&quot;<br /> n - pronunciation is roughly the same as English, as in &quot;nap&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Stop Consonants</b><br /> <br /> p - pronunciation is roughly the same as English, as in &quot;pit&quot;<br /> b - pronunciation is roughly the same as English, as in &quot;bit&quot;<br /> bh (IPA /b\u02b1/) - a &quot;murmured b&quot;; no direct English comparison, but like the initial sound in &quot;Bh\u0101rat,&quot; a Hindi term for India<br /> <br /> t - an un-aspirated t sound, as in the English &quot;stone&quot;<br /> th (IPA /t\u02b0/) - an aspirated t, as in the English &quot;tin&quot;; may also be pronounced as a fricative, as in the English &quot;thin&quot;<br /> d - pronunciation is roughly the same as English, as in &quot;din&quot;<br /> dh (IPA /d\u02b1/) - a &quot;murmured d&quot;; no direct English comparison, but like the initial sound in &quot;dh\u00e1rma,&quot; a Sanskrit religious term<br /> <br /> k (sometimes written &quot;c&quot;) - an un-aspirated k or hard c sound, as in the English &quot;scone&quot;<br /> kh (IPA /k\u02b0/) - an aspirated k or hard c, as in the English &quot;cut&quot;<br /> g - pronunciation is roughly the same as English, as in &quot;gut&quot;<br /> gh (IPA /g\u02b1/) - a &quot;murmured g&quot;; no direct English comparison, but like the initial sound in the &quot;gh\u0101s,&quot; a Hindi word meaning &quot;grass.&quot;<br /> <br /> ' (IPA /\u0294/) - a glottal stop, like the &quot;catch&quot; between the two syllables of the exclamation &quot;uh-oh!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fricative Consonants</b><br /> <br /> f - pronunciation is roughly the same as English, as in &quot;fat&quot;<br /> <br /> s - pronunciation is roughly the same as English, as in &quot;sap&quot;<br /> z - pronunciation is roughly the same as English, as in &quot;zap&quot;<br /> sh (IPA /\u0283/) - pronunciation is roughly the same as English, as in &quot;shine&quot;<br /> <br /> h (probably IPA /x/) - If we're going by how Sumerian was probably pronounced and the sounds Grimm's Law actually produced, this is <i>not</i> pronounced like the English &quot;h,&quot; but rather like the &quot;ch&quot; at the end of the German pronunciation of &quot;Bach&quot; or the &quot;x&quot; in most Mexican Spanish pronunciations of &quot;Mexico.&quot; The difference can be hard for English speakers to detect, but this sound is made with the tongue in roughly the same position it would be if one were making a &quot;k&quot; sound, and produces a more audible hiss of air than is typical for the English &quot;h.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Approximant Consonants</b><br /> <br /> y (IPA /j/) - pronunciation is roughly the same as English, as in &quot;yes&quot; (I've seen y appear as a vowel in at least one First Tongue word, but that my be a fluke and its probably safe to pronounce it the same as &quot;i&quot;)<br /> <br /> w - pronunciation is roughly the same as English, as in &quot;we&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Liquids</b><br /> <br /> l - pronunciation is roughly the same as English, as in &quot;left&quot;<br /> r - probably pronounced as either a flap or a trill; in other words, in more or less the same manner as a single &quot;r&quot; in Spanish. I think one of the special powers English-speaking werewolves get is the ability to roll their r's. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Vowels</b><br /> <br /> Pronouncing the plain vowels in more or less the same way that they're pronounced in Spanish is probably a safe bet, at least for the long vowels:<br /> <br /> a - like the vowel in &quot;palm&quot;; probably never like the vowel in &quot;hat&quot;<br /> e - roughly like the vowel in &quot;face&quot;; possibly like the vowel in &quot;dress&quot; when short<br /> i - like the vowel in &quot;feed&quot;; possibly like the vowel in &quot;bit&quot; when short<br /> o - roughly like the vowel in &quot;goat&quot;; possibly like the vowel in &quot;thought&quot; when short<br /> u - like the vowel in &quot;goose&quot;; possibly like the vowel in &quot;foot&quot; when short<br /> <br /> Each of these vowels may be short or long. Based on the occurrence of doubled vowels in written First Tongue, vowels are probably always pronounced long in open syllables (syllables <i>not</i> ending in a consonant) and may be either short (written as a single vowel) or long (written as a double vowel) in syllables ending with a consonant. The difference between short and long vowels is mostly in how long the sound is &quot;held,&quot; but they may be a qualitative difference in how they're pronounced as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> There may be some distinction, particularly in terms of vowel length or quality, between stressed and unstressed syllables, but as stress is not indicated in written First Tongue it's probably safest to assume that syllable stress is not a major feature of the way the language is pronounced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 06-22-2015, 11:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T14:16:44-07:00","id":564542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=564522#post564522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">just for the sake of clarity, I've worked up a phonemic inventory/pronunciation guide; let me know if I got anything wrong:<br /> <br /> <b>Nasal Consonants</b><br /> <br /> m - pronunciation is roughly the same as English, as in &quot;map&quot;<br /> n - pronunciation is roughly the same as English, as in &quot;nap&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Stop Consonants</b><br /> <br /> p - pronunciation is roughly the same as English, as in &quot;pit&quot;<br /> b - pronunciation is roughly the same as English, as in &quot;bit&quot;<br /> bh (IPA /b\u02b1/) - a &quot;murmured b&quot;; no direct English comparison, but like the initial sound in &quot;Bh\u0101rat,&quot; a Hindi term for India<br /> <br /> t - pronunciation is roughly the same as English, as in &quot;tin&quot;<br /> d - pronunciation is roughly the same as English, as in &quot;din&quot;<br /> dh (IPA /d\u02b1/) - a &quot;murmured d&quot;; no direct English comparison, but like the initial sound in &quot;dh\u00e1rma,&quot; a Sanskrit religious term<br /> <br /> k (sometimes written &quot;c&quot;) - an un-aspirated k or hard c sound, as in the English &quot;scone&quot;<br /> kh (IPA /k\u02b0/) - an aspirated k or hard c, as in the English &quot;cut&quot;<br /> g - pronunciation is roughly the same as English, as in &quot;gut&quot;<br /> gh (IPA /g\u02b1/) - a &quot;murmured g&quot;; no direct English comparison, but like the initial sound in the &quot;gh\u0101s,&quot; a Hindi word meaning &quot;grass.&quot;<br /> <br /> ' (IPA /\u0294/) - a glottal stop, like the &quot;catch&quot; between the two syllables of the exclamation &quot;uh-oh!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fricative Consonants</b><br /> <br /> f - pronunciation is roughly the same as English, as in &quot;fat&quot;<br /> th (IPA /\u03b8/) - always pronounced as in &quot;thin,&quot; <i>not</i> as in &quot;then&quot;<br /> <br /> s - pronunciation is roughly the same as English, as in &quot;sap&quot;<br /> z - pronunciation is roughly the same as English, as in &quot;zap&quot;<br /> sh (IPA /\u0283/) - pronunciation is roughly the same as English, as in &quot;shine&quot;<br /> <br /> h (probably IPA /x/) - If we're going by how Sumerian was probably pronounced and the sounds Grimm's Law actually produced, this is <i>not</i> pronounced like the English &quot;h,&quot; but rather like the &quot;ch&quot; at the end of the German pronunciation of &quot;Bach&quot; or the &quot;x&quot; in most Mexican Spanish pronunciations of &quot;Mexico.&quot; The difference can be hard for English speakers to detect, but this sound produced with the tongue in roughly the same position it would be if one were making a &quot;k&quot; sound, and produces a more audible hiss of air than is typical for the English &quot;h.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Approximant Consonants</b><br /> <br /> y (IPA /j/) - pronunciation is roughly the same as English, as in &quot;yes&quot; (I've seen y appear as a vowel in at least one First Tongue word, but that my be a fluke and its probably safe to pronounce it the same as &quot;i&quot;)<br /> <br /> w - pronunciation is roughly the same as English, as in &quot;we&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Liquids</b><br /> <br /> l - pronunciation is roughly the same as English, as in &quot;left&quot;<br /> r - probably pronounced as either a flap or a trill; in other words, in more or less the same manner as a single &quot;r&quot; in Spanish. I think one of the special powers English-speaking werewolves get is the ability to roll their r's. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Vowels</b><br /> <br /> Pronouncing the plain vowels in more or less the same way that they're pronounced in Spanish is probably a safe bet, at least for the long vowels:<br /> <br /> a - like the vowel in &quot;palm&quot;; probably never like the vowel in &quot;hat&quot;<br /> e - roughly like the vowel in &quot;face&quot;; possibly like the vowel in &quot;dress&quot; when short<br /> i - like the vowel in &quot;feed&quot;; possibly like the vowel in &quot;bit&quot; when short<br /> o - roughly like the vowel in &quot;goat&quot;; possibly like the vowel in &quot;thought&quot; when short<br /> <br /> Each of these vowels may be short or long. Based on the occurrence of doubled vowels in written First Tongue, vowels are probably always pronounced long in open syllables (syllables <i>not</i> ending in a consonant) and may be either short (written as a single vowel) or long (written as a double vowel) in syllables ending with a consonant. The difference between short and long vowels is mostly in how long the sound is &quot;held,&quot; but they may be a qualitative difference in how they're pronounced as well.<br /> <br /> First Tongue also has at least two diphthongs:<br /> <br /> ai - like the vowel in &quot;price&quot;<br /> au - like the vowel in &quot;mouth&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> There may be some distinction, particularly in terms of vowel length or quality, between stressed and unstressed syllables, but as stress is not indicated in written First Tongue it's probably safest to assume that syllable stress is not a major feature of the way the language is pronounced.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well if this isn't the most awesome thing I've seen all day. o_o You, sir, are brilliant.<br /> <br /> Just a couple of quick clarifications:<br /> <br /> &quot;Th&quot; is actually a &quot;murmured t&quot;, if that makes sense. It can, however, be pronounced as a &quot;th&quot;; in 1e, the latter pronunciation was used in &quot;Cahalith&quot;, and in 2e, the former was used for &quot;Cahalith&quot;. So...free variation?<br /> <br /> As for diphthongs, I'm kind of on the fence about those. Diphthongs existed in PIE, but in Sumerian, vowels beside vowels are pronounced as separate vowels. The exception I make in my rough draft of FT is that, if two vowel are beside each and are the same vowel, the vowel is lengthened rather than the second vowel be made its own separate syllable. So <b>nuun</b> (prince) is pronounced with a long &quot;u&quot;, but the diphthong &quot;ai&quot; is pronounced &quot;a-i&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T19:03:48-07:00","id":564835,"title":"","content":"And I've finished translating all the B-homonyms without messing up my file! YESSSSSSSSSS!<br /> <br /> <b>fa'ra:</b> outside, outer edge, on the fringe; to be set outside or aside; strange, different, outlandish; to split from the norm, to lead an alternative lifestyle; to be separated, willingly or unwillingly, from normal society<br /> <b>bharra:</b> to mix a colour or dyes; mixed colours, colours such as secondary or tertiary colours<br /> <b>bara:</b> a fish with multicoloured or colourful scales<br /> <b>farakh:</b> a place or position of lordship or kingliness; a throne or dais; a title of prestige or royalty<br /> <b>faragh:</b> the testicles or ballsack of a male animal<br /> <b>barah:</b> something that spreads out open and/or widely, like a wide, flat plain or steppe<br /> <b>bharbhar:</b> reeds, papyrus, water plants<br /> <b>uku'u:</b> a sewing or weaving shuttle<br /> <b>bharim:</b> mainland, a continent; dry land seen from sea; an ocean shoreline<br /> <b>farsudh:</b> a notational line in music<br /> <b>bharzud:</b> A pot specifically used for keeping plants in<br /> <b>farshuhal:</b> One's livestock or owned animals<br /> <b>faza:</b> dwarf, dimunitive; one who is underdeveloped or undernourished; to be stunted in growth<br /> <b>fasa:</b> small fish such as minnows, usually used for bait or preyed on by bigger, more aggressive fish<br /> <b>be'e:</b> to deduct, remove; to diminish, reduce; to withdraw, receive (as an allotment)<br /> <b>fil:</b> to have a burning or souring taste or sensation<br /> <b>bhilam:</b> any member of the elephant family such as a mammoth, mastodon or modern elephant; unlike <b>tila'ghaleram</b>, which refers mostly to Asian or African elephants, this also refers to their ancestors<br /> <b>fir:</b> insects of a locust- or grasshopper-type; to scatter, disperse or shred apart, like how a swarm of locusts breaks apart<br /> <b>pisah:</b> A name for starfish, brittle stars or sometimes coral formations resembling such<br /> <b>bhis:</b> a trickle, a drip; to trickle, drip or making a trickling/dripping noise<br /> <b>wu:</b> to flit around; to move about irregularly; to chase about like a bird chasing an insect<br /> <b>bhu'u:</b> translating roughly as &quot;perfect knowledge&quot;, it refers to concepts, ideas and knowledge that is only passed around the upper tiers of secret orders, respected fellowships and society in general \u2014 the most guarded secrets of the Ordo Dracul count as <b>bhu'u</b><br /> <b>fufui:</b> the wild date palm<br /> <b>ibru:</b> rations, allocated food<br /> <b>bhul:</b> to blow out, to remove something or filter out something by blowing on it; to shake out; the use of air to sift out things, such as tossing grain into the air and letting the weak kernels go with the wind<br /> <b>fu'ul:</b> fish that travel along by jet propulsion, such as squids or jellyfish; an action or manner of travel resembling aquatic jet propulsion<br /> <b>fuluh:</b> a needle or pin; a stake; a needle-shaped object; to sew<br /> <b>bhuluh:</b> sharp, spiny plants; plants or plant-parts that stick up like needles or are needle-like<br /> <b>buluk:</b> to be sick and/or trembling with anxiety or fear; vomiting or having gastrointestinal problems because of fear or anxiety<br /> <b>falakum:</b> the resin of an aromatic tree, or the tree itself<br /> <b>bhun:</b> anything that inflates with liquid or air, such as bellows or even a human bladder<br /> <b>bhur'bur:</b> a sacred authority; a catch-all term for those recognized as spiritual leaders in an official capacity, such as a bishop<br /> <b>abhru:</b> a meal or food sacrificed as chiminage or an offering to a spirit or deity<br /> <b>niku:</b> a bowl or container used to hold sacrificed/offered food<br /> <b>bur:</b> the cutting or ripping out of something to sacrifice; the act of performing a sacrifice by tearing something out or cutting out something, such as tearing a heart from your foe<br /> <b>bu'er:</b> a place or location where sacrifices of food, or beings intended as food, takes place<br /> <b>bur'u:</b> a unit of area or volume, such as a cubic meter or square meter<br /> <b>bursah:</b> a building where servants are kept, or the servants that live in a servant building (as opposed to living off their master's property)<br /> <b>fu'ru:</b> a catch-all term for any carrion-eating bird, such as a vulture, crow, rook or condor<br /> <b>bhurru:</b> a sparrow; small, songbird-type birds","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 06-22-2015, 11:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T19:23:43-07:00","id":564845,"title":"","content":"How about first tongue terms for the various generations under <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strauss%E2%80%93Howe_generational_theory\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Strauss\u2013Howe generational theory</b></a> (fun fact, I once wrote an English paper on the similarity of Hemingway's work and the pop culture of gen X (including pop culture both aimed at and written by gen X, including VtM) and how those similarities reflect the common traits of the lost generation and Gen X.)<br /> <br /> I especially want terms for the GI generation through the homeland generation (aka the living mortal generations) but I also want FT terms for the generations that are now only represented by the vampires and such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T19:26:00-07:00","id":564846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=564845#post564845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about first tongue terms for the various generations under <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strauss%E2%80%93Howe_generational_theory\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Strauss\u2013Howe generational theory</b></a> (fun fact, I once wrote an English paper on the similarity of Hemingway's work and the pop culture of gen X (including pop culture both aimed at and written by gen X, including VtM) and how those similarities reflect the common traits of the lost generation and Gen X.)<br /> <br /> I especially want terms for the GI generation through the homeland generation (aka the living mortal generations) but I also want FT terms for the generations that are now only represented by the vampires and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh-ho-ho-ho, I likey me a challenge! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'll see what I can do with these. What are you planning on using the terms for, if I may ask?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T19:27:38-07:00","id":564871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=564542#post564542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well if this isn't the most awesome thing I've seen all day. o_o You, sir, are brilliant.<br /> <br /> Just a couple of quick clarifications:<br /> <br /> &quot;Th&quot; is actually a &quot;murmured t&quot;, if that makes sense. It can, however, be pronounced as a &quot;th&quot;; in 1e, the latter pronunciation was used in &quot;Cahalith&quot;, and in 2e, the former was used for &quot;Cahalith&quot;. So...free variation?<br /> <br /> As for diphthongs, I'm kind of on the fence about those. Diphthongs existed in PIE, but in Sumerian, vowels beside vowels are pronounced as separate vowels. The exception I make in my rough draft of FT is that, if two vowel are beside each and are the same vowel, the vowel is lengthened rather than the second vowel be made its own separate syllable. So <b>nuun</b> (prince) is pronounced with a long &quot;u&quot;, but the diphthong &quot;ai&quot; is pronounced &quot;a-i&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So th is an aspirated stop, like kh? I had assumed that it was the result of &quot;Grimming forward,&quot; like f (which Sumerian doesn't have). Having the two pronunciations be in free variation wouldn't necessarily be too implausible, since really ancient Greek had a series of aspirated stops that turned into fricatives in later dialects of Greek (interestingly, these stops came from the Proto-Indo-European voiced-aspirated stop series, so the Greek theta often corresponds to a d sound in related Germanic language words, for instance). It's a little odd for k to be the only stop that distinguishes between aspirated and un-aspirated forms, anyway, though there are some odd sound systems out there and this would hardly be the most unusual either way.<br /> <br /> As for getting rid of Diphthongs, that's surely an option, but it would be slightly unusual if, say, &quot;a'i&quot; (with a glottal stop) was distinguished from &quot;ai&quot; (where the vowels are in separate syllables but not separated by a glottal stop. I think Hawaiian makes that distinction, but the glottal stop in Hawaiian is treated as a perfectly normal stop (since it came from earlier instances of /k/). That said, the glottal stop has a kind of odd distribution in First Tongue anyway (a little bit reminiscent of the &quot;laryngeals&quot; posited for Proto-Indo-European, actually), so it could fit with the overall structure of the language.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T19:30:24-07:00","id":564874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=564846#post564846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh-ho-ho-ho, I likey me a challenge! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'll see what I can do with these. What are you planning on using the terms for, if I may ask?</div> </div> </div> </div>Been thinking of how the differences between generations might be manifested in werewolf culture ever since the Dark Eras kick starter (things like which tribes and lodges are most popular with werewolves of different generations, how the popular culture of those generations influenced the shadow and what kinds of totems werewolves of different generations would have, etc). I figure a quick write up of those differences might be a good character creation reference.<br /> <br /> Oh and keep in mind, I consider Millennials who were kids in the 80s to be a somewhat different generation than Millennials who were kids in the 90s, due to the political differences between 80s and 90s pop culture aimed at kids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 06-22-2015, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T19:51:18-07:00","id":564882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=564871#post564871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So th is an aspirated stop, like kh? I had assumed that it was the result of &quot;Grimming forward,&quot; like f (which Sumerian doesn't have). Having the two pronunciations be in free variation wouldn't necessarily be too implausible, since really ancient Greek had a series of aspirated stops that turned into fricatives in later dialects of Greek (interestingly, these stops came from the Proto-Indo-European voiced-aspirated stop series, so the Greek theta often corresponds to a d sound in related Germanic language words, for instance). It's a little odd for k to be the only stop that distinguishes between aspirated and un-aspirated forms, anyway, though there are some odd sound systems out there and this would hardly be the most unusual either way.<br /> <br /> As for getting rid of Diphthongs, that's surely an option, but it would be slightly unusual if, say, &quot;a'i&quot; (with a glottal stop) was distinguished from &quot;ai&quot; (where the vowels are in separate syllables but not separated by a glottal stop. I think Hawaiian makes that distinction, but the glottal stop in Hawaiian is treated as a perfectly normal stop (since it came from earlier instances of /k/). That said, the glottal stop has a kind of odd distribution in First Tongue anyway (a little bit reminiscent of the &quot;laryngeals&quot; posited for Proto-Indo-European, actually), so it could fit with the overall structure of the language.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would axe the glottal stop between vowels, then. The poor glottal stop is abused in conlangs to a ludicrous degree; I feel the presence it already has in First Tongue is enough.<br /> <br /> T is supposed to be an aspirated/murmured t, yeah, and I think the free variation between the &quot;th&quot; sound and the &quot;murmured t&quot; sound should stay, to show a relation to the PIE-descended languages. As for the k having aspirated/non-aspirated variances, I like the fact it's the odd sound out. These idiosyncrasies (I think that's the term) help make the language feel more natural, in my opinion. I'm wondering if diphthongs and the separate vowel-syllables should be something else in free variation, or maybe have the Werewolf dialect not have diphthongs, to show that the Uratha are younger and closer to humans in the grand scheme of things.<br /> <br /> Young Man, that is an absolutely awesome idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T20:45:07-07:00","id":564943,"title":"","content":"Alright, I went ahead and edited the guide to remove the diphthongs and describe th as an aspirated t. The term &quot;murmur,&quot; FYI is usually used to describe a quality known as breathy voice, in which the vocal chords are allowed to vibrate as they do when producing a voiced consonant like d, but are held farther apart to allow more air to escape between them. Aspirated stops are also characterized by spread vocal chords, but in their case the chords are kept from vibrating, as in a voiceless consonant like t. So it doesn't make much sense to talk about a &quot;murmured&quot; t, unless you mean something other than breathy voice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T20:50:09-07:00","id":564947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=564882#post564882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Young Man, that is an absolutely awesome idea.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks. I am about to post some differences between generations in a new thread.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T21:31:57-07:00","id":564983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=564943#post564943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, I went ahead and edited the guide to remove the diphthongs and describe th as an aspirated t. The term &quot;murmur,&quot; FYI is usually used to describe a quality known as breathy voice, in which the vocal chords are allowed to vibrate as they do when producing a voiced consonant like d, but are held farther apart to allow more air to escape between them. Aspirated stops are also characterized by spread vocal chords, but in their case the chords are kept from vibrating, as in a voiceless consonant like t. So it doesn't make much sense to talk about a &quot;murmured&quot; t, unless you mean something other than breathy voice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Noted. I forgot about the distinction and got it mixed up, my mistake. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T21:49:51-07:00","id":564993,"title":"","content":"No worries; linguistics is complicated. :P<br /> <br /> And now, here's some First Tongue written with Devanagari, because I can:<br /> <br /> Amahan Iduth: \u0906\u092e\u093e\u0939\u0928\u094d \u0908\u0926\u0941\u0925\u094d<br /> <br /> Idigam: \u0908\u0926\u0940\u0917\u092e\u094d<br /> <br /> Uratha: \u090a\u0930\u093e\u0925\u093e<br /> <br /> Urfarah: \u0909\u0930\u094d\u092b\u093c\u093e\u0930\u0939\u094d<br /> <br /> Fenris-Ur: \u095e\u0947\u0928\u094d\u0930\u093f\u0938\u0941\u0930\u094d<br /> <br /> Hikaon-Ur: \u0939\u0940\u0915\u093e\u0913\u0928\u0941\u0930\u094d<br /> <br /> Kamduis-Ur: \u0915\u092e\u094d\u0926\u0942\u0907\u0938\u0941\u0930\u094d<br /> <br /> Sagrim-Ur: \u0938\u0917\u094d\u0930\u093f\u092e\u0941\u0930\u094d<br /> <br /> <br /> Indic scripts work pretty well, since the Indo-Aryan languages typically have four stop series. There doesn't seem to be any equivalent to the hyphen, however...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 06-23-2015, 12:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T22:23:25-07:00","id":565004,"title":"","content":"I was presenting First Tongue as having no actual written language, but expressed by literate people in whatever script they're comfortable with. Perhaps with a mix of claw scratches and scents and pictures for some things that are difficult to translate exactly or need emphasis.<br /> <br /> An actual written form (in my chronicle's context) would be a lost marvel worth questing to find. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T22:35:00-07:00","id":565009,"title":"","content":"And here are the D-homonyms. I have a few left to go, but for now, I hit a blank.<br /> <br /> <b>tha'a:</b> decorated side-boards on a chariot or other animal-pulled cart or vehicle; an advertisement or sign posted on a vehicle<br /> <b>thaf:</b> to hold, to seize, to take; to accept, take charge of or take over; to envelop, bind or overwhelm suddenly<br /> <b>dhagh:</b> damage or destruction from a military attack; a hostile takeover; a military takeover<br /> <b>da'ag:</b> vicinity, near side; a nearby house or dwelling<br /> <b>dhaghan:</b> a place where a spirit or deity is said to be in slumber; a pit or place in the ground ritually used to bind down a spirit or deity into slumber<br /> <b>thal:</b> the ability of flight<br /> <b>dal:</b> lines that divide up units of measurement, such as the dividing lines on a ruler; a vessel with dividing lines on it for measuring purposes, such as a measuring cup<br /> <b>thalla:</b> to shine brightly or fiercely, like a sun or star; incredibly valuable jewellery, such as the Queen of England's royal jewels<br /> <b>thar:</b> birds of the francolin family; the black francolin in particular<br /> <b>da'ar:</b> an onomotopoeia meant to depict a dripping rhythm<br /> <b>dhara:</b> dried blood \u2014 werewolves also used this term to refer to the smell of old blood or old kills<br /> <b>dara:</b> dead fish, usually the kind on the shore that have dried out and are beginning to smell disgusting<br /> <b>tharanshuf:</b> negligent or lazy workers or servants<br /> <b>tha'ri:</b> a universal constant; something which the world is made up of, or which supports the world it exists in<br /> <b>dhe:</b> to shape or create by pouring or sifting, such as pouring metal into a mould to shape it<br /> <b>di'i:</b> to have to go to the bathroom really bad; to have an affliction or disorder of the bowels; bowel or lower gastrointestinal distress<br /> <b>thibh:</b> the wooden board of a door; a simple wooden entrance, such as a trapdoor raised by rope instead of having a complex lock<br /> <b>thi'if:</b> frustration, irritation; pent-up or smouldering anger; a slow-burning anger instead of a sudden blowout<br /> <b>thifida:</b> colic or bloat, as found in animals such as horses or dogs<br /> <b>thithli:</b> a group of different types of fish, such as a menagerie of fish in a private aquarium; an aquarium or aquatic exhibit, like the ones at a marine park<br /> <b>thih:</b> numb or floppy limbs or parts of the body; unresponsive parts of the body that have lost feeling<br /> <b>dhik:</b> thorny weeds or invasive plants; an infestation of poisonous, dangerous or invasive plants<br /> <b>thilim:</b> an oven used for cooking food<br /> <b>dhilim:</b> a spoon; a balance pan or shallow bowl<br /> <b>dhi'im:</b> to check; to approach; to come forward or bring forth cautiously<br /> <b>thi'im:</b> corpse-scent, or the smell of cadavers whether fresh or old<br /> <b>dimm:</b> a dead plant<br /> <b>di'im:</b> the poles that hold up fencing<br /> <b>dhimhu:</b> the actual plant that legumes are harvested from, not the edible legumes themselves<br /> <b>di'nih:</b> stubbornness, obstinateness; to have the stubbornness of a mule or billygoat; to be unshakeable or unswaying in one's beliefs<br /> <b>dinigh:</b> potash<br /> <b>thirig:</b> to be great or exceeding; lofty, high-up; excess, surplus, abundance or bounty<br /> <b>thi'rih:</b> to tear or cleave out a feature in the landscape, often said of the feats of certain mythological features; a gorge or canyon<br /> <b>dirri:</b> a raft made out of reeds","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 06-25-2015, 10:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T22:39:21-07:00","id":565012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=564993#post564993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No worries; linguistics is complicated. :P<br /> <br /> And now, here's some First Tongue written with Devanagari, because I can:<br /> <br /> Amahan Iduth: \u0906\u092e\u093e\u0939\u0928\u094d \u0908\u0926\u0941\u0925\u094d<br /> <br /> Idigam: \u0908\u0926\u0940\u0917\u092e\u094d<br /> <br /> Uratha: \u090a\u0930\u093e\u0925\u093e<br /> <br /> Urfarah: \u0909\u0930\u094d\u092b\u093c\u093e\u0930\u0939\u094d<br /> <br /> Fenris-Ur: \u095e\u0947\u0928\u094d\u0930\u093f\u0938\u0941\u0930\u094d<br /> <br /> Hikaon-Ur: \u0939\u0940\u0915\u093e\u0913\u0928\u0941\u0930\u094d<br /> <br /> Kamduis-Ur: \u0915\u092e\u094d\u0926\u0942\u0907\u0938\u0941\u0930\u094d<br /> <br /> Sagrim-Ur: \u0938\u0917\u094d\u0930\u093f\u092e\u0941\u0930\u094d<br /> <br /> <br /> Indic scripts work pretty well, since the Indo-Aryan languages typically have four stop series. There doesn't seem to be any equivalent to the hyphen, however...</div> </div> </div> </div>*babbles at the epicness* DEVS! GET AN EXCUSE FOR MORE INDIAN WEREWOLF SETTINGS, STAT!<br /> <br /> Simon Darkstep, the 1e Rage book's cover seemed to have a werewolf with FT writing on his fetish-hand wraps. It looked a lot like the glyphs used in W:tA for the Garou language, and in my personal game-canon, that's what's used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T00:32:03-07:00","id":565074,"title":"","content":"I love linguist geeks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T07:58:18-07:00","id":565412,"title":"","content":"More of those A-homonyms. Almost finished this particular list....<br /> <br /> <b>a:</b> water; bodily fluids<br /> <b>ghesha:</b> a leather sheath, scabbard, harness or other method of storage for a weapon<br /> <b>ah'ah:</b> the cry of a bird<br /> <b>andibhal:</b> a sign of authority; a badge or other symbol marking one has having authority<br /> <b>ara:</b> to grind by hand; a hand-powered grindstone or mill; a tool used for grinding things in general<br /> <b>a'ra:</b> divination through mathematical means, such as astrology or numerology<br /> <b>arra:</b> a civil servant; a functionary<br /> <b>hesara:</b> the rudder of a boat<br /> <b>araf:</b> to pin back; a pin for a broch or to hold cloth back<br /> <b>arraf:</b> a still<br /> <b>araki:</b> to calculate the distance between places using stars on a map; an astronomical unit (AU)<br /> <b>araghi:</b> an improvised performance or musical composition<br /> <b>ariah:</b> steppe, desert; abandoned land; a deserted place<br /> <b>arina:</b> a pervasive or stubborn weed; roots that are difficult to remove and/or well-embedded in the dirt<br /> <b>erina:</b> fish that hide in rocks, and who can be difficult to catch or bait out<br /> <b>azig:</b> ammunition for slings; a slingstone<br /> <b>asih:</b> a waterskin; a watering can<br /> <b>aslum:</b> a rod or stick used for measuring, such as a yardstick; the measurement depicted on such a tool","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T19:47:06-07:00","id":568677,"title":"","content":"It's time to finish up some of these word lists. First up, the kennings; all should be translated by now.<br /> <br /> <b>thir-tenu:</b> &quot;forest-cheeked&quot; = cheek forest = a beard<br /> <b>ithakusgidassum:</b> &quot;that which empowers the bow&quot; = force of the bow = an arm<br /> <b>uhur-esi:</b> &quot;sword tree&quot; = a man<br /> <b>thalla-esi:</b> &quot;brightly-jewelled tree&quot; = jewelry tree = a woman<br /> <b>zagsgu'na:</b> &quot;shoulder-rock&quot; = rock of the shoulders = the head<br /> <b>mirska umfin:</b> &quot;dragon's claws&quot; = lindworm claws = ice skates<br /> <b>ummamu:</b> &quot;witch-beast&quot; = a wolf<br /> <b>gaghul:</b> &quot;one of great hunger/one of hungry jaws&quot; = hungry one = a bear<br /> <b>illag izi:</b> &quot;the waters' fire&quot; = gold<br /> <b>amahaskekh:</b> &quot;mother's ice&quot; = ice = silver<br /> <b>haful:</b> &quot;war-one&quot; = man of war = a brave person<br /> <b>hiirga'ar:</b> &quot;slip-escape&quot; = scamp = a weak person<br /> <b>nuzahudu:</b> &quot;slow-gifting&quot; = gift tardy = a greedy person<br /> <b>zagga-su:</b> &quot;glitter-bodied&quot; = glittering = a fashionable person<br /> <b>rogea-su:</b> &quot;shark-bodied&quot; = sharkskin = a noisy or loud person<br /> <b>gulukikul:</b> &quot;hateful one&quot; = hater = an enemy<br /> <b>kukdu-mirska:</b> &quot;biting harmful snake&quot; = biting snake = a sword or piercing weapon<br /> <b>Uthah-Nin:</b> &quot;Sister of Daytime&quot; = &quot;Day-Sister&quot; = the Earth<br /> <b>Mathanim:</b> &quot;Lands Above&quot; = &quot;World Above&quot; = the sky<br /> <b>Illag-Saragarag Garum:</b> &quot;House of Water's/Watery Sand&quot; = House of Sand = the sea<br /> <b>Thuah-Zalag:</b> &quot;Always Bright&quot; = Everglow = the Sun<br /> <b>Sufalul:</b> &quot;The Growing/Turning/Changing One&quot; = Waxer = the Moon<br /> <br /> <b>hiir:</b> slippery, wiggly; to slip through or out of<br /> <b>ga'ar:</b> to escape; to flee; to get away","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T05:41:24-07:00","id":569093,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry to bother you if these have been done already but I'd like some names for animals, if possible:<br /> Raven, Magpie, Deer (and if separate; Moose). Bear, Eagle, Falcon, Wolverine, Lynx, Ox, Wild Boar.<br /> <br /> If you could write them up as kenning-style names as well, I'd be extremely thankful. Those names are mostly for Scandinavian settings. (Which might be inferred from the animals chosen. :P)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T07:15:10-07:00","id":569166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=569093#post569093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry to bother you if these have been done already but I'd like some names for animals, if possible:<br /> Raven, Magpie, Deer (and if separate; Moose). Bear, Eagle, Falcon, Wolverine, Lynx, Ox, Wild Boar.<br /> <br /> If you could write them up as kenning-style names as well, I'd be extremely thankful. Those names are mostly for Scandinavian settings. (Which might be inferred from the animals chosen. :P)</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you like me to look up actual kennings for these, or would you like me to make up some original ones?<br /> <br /> Next word list to finish: the a-homonyms.<br /> <br /> <b>ahzh:</b> magically-created boils, sores, or legions; a curse, gift or magic that causes skin disease such as an outbreak of boils<br /> <b>as:</b> one<br /> <b>ahs:</b> a small loaf of traveller's bread; rations or food fit for travelling with<br /> <b>a'ask:</b> six<br /> <b>azah:</b> a butterfly<br /> <b>asagh:</b> a surface area in mathematics; a marked-out allotment of field, such as on a survey<br /> <b>askudh:</b> extremities, limbs; horns, spikes or spines on something<br /> <b>asgudh:</b> a lock or locking bar on a door<br /> <b>asnan:</b> grains or cereals<br /> <b>asnen:</b> a mole; a beauty mark; freckles<br /> <b>assa:</b> to be the perfect candidate; to be one's first choice in a situation; a desirable or very eligible mate<br /> <b>isthe:</b> a shrine or chapel<br /> <b>aste:</b> a chair, throne or seat that a divine figure or effigy is seated upon<br /> <b>adhuya:</b> rites meant to purify, ritually cleanse and/or consecrate an area or thing<br /> <b>adua:</b> someone who purifies or ritually cleanses things (usually said of priests or priestesses)<br /> <b>au:</b> someone who tows wrecked or disabled vehicles, like boats or cars<br /> <b>a'u:</b> high water; raging water; high tides<br /> <b>aur:</b> the underarm or under-legs on a body; concealed or covered-up parts of the body<br /> <b>a'ur:</b> the limbs of something (a tree, an animal, a machine, etc.)<br /> <b>ay'a:</b> to groan; to moan; to make sounds of woe<br /> <b>ahyah:</b> marshland, swampland; the swamp or marsh surrounding certain river deltas, such as the nile; to turn something swampy or marsh-like<br /> <b>azadh:</b> the head or tips of reedy plants, such as the leafy tips of papyrus<br /> <b>asath:</b> a reed shelter; a nest made by waterfowl, especially one made out of water-plants<br /> <br /> And with that finished, more of the d-homonyms:<br /> <br /> <b>dhu:</b> to hold, to keep in custody; to heap or pile up; to accumulate<br /> <b>dhuku:</b> a pet fish<br /> <b>thudu:</b> woe, lament<br /> <b>du'u:</b> to fix upright, to drive in, to erect; to impregnate, to make someone pregnant<br /> <b>thi'u:</b> the platform on which a deity or a deity-effigy's throne or seat is affixed<br /> <b>dhuthu:</b> to play a musical instrumental<br /> <b>thu'u:</b> to push, to thrust; to gore<br /> <b>dhu'u:</b> to caulk; caulking; to fit something on or together<br /> <b>thuthu:</b> to spin or whirl<br /> <b>lawu:</b> to circle or go around; to search around somewhere; to take one's time searching","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 06-26-2015, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T08:59:19-07:00","id":569292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=569166#post569166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would you like me to look up actual kennings for these, or would you like me to make up some original ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>Whichever you'd enjoy the most. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Also, is it just me who think this, or does kennings make really good names for spirits? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T10:41:18-07:00","id":569386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=569292#post569292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, is it just me who think this, or does kennings make really good names for spirits?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not wrong. One of the exact things a dev was going for in First Tongue was &quot;this weird, poetic language&quot;. Certain words actually translate out as kennings, and my intent with my kenning translation idea was to help inspire deed names, pack names, totem names, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T11:08:38-07:00","id":569420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=569386#post569386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certain words actually translate out as kennings</div> </div> </div> </div>I will never not find the actual name of the Little Road Tyrants completely hilarious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T11:11:08-07:00","id":569421,"title":"","content":"<b>Seidrmadr:<br /> <br /> haf-sa'asugagh:</b> &quot;stinking gluttonous jaws&quot; = wolverine<br /> <b>ulke-asnen:</b> a starling (lit. &quot;sky freckle&quot; because of their huge flocks that dot the heavens)<br /> <b>hafalagulke-asnen:</b> &quot;freckle of the warring skies&quot; = &quot;war-starling&quot; = raven<br /> <b>mezhum:</b> black and white-spotted; piebald; pied-coloured<br /> <b>mezhum-luzuk:</b> &quot;piebald thief&quot; = a magpie<br /> <b>filsagardur:</b> heather (lit. &quot;children of sour [acidic] soul&quot;)<br /> <b>filsagardur-gi'endu:</b> &quot;those who step through the children of acidic soils&quot; = &quot;heather stepper&quot; = a deer<br /> <b>fuful-kurul:</b> &quot;twig-rending one&quot; = a moose<br /> <b>habarrath:</b> &quot;plow-slave&quot; = an ox<br /> <b>skekhesir-umfin:</b> &quot;snowshoe-claws&quot; = a lynx<br /> <b>usan-ninna:</b> &quot;whip-striking predator&quot; = a falcon<br /> <b>imin-kuthdu:</b> &quot;storm-cleaver&quot; = &quot;storm-shearer&quot; = an eagle<br /> <b>kur-al'al:</b> &quot;rends-the-fields&quot; = a wild boar or pig","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T11:53:15-07:00","id":569466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=569421#post569421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Seidrmadr:<br /> <br /> haf-sa'asugagh:</b> &quot;stinking gluttonous jaws&quot; = wolverine<br /> <b>ulke-asnen:</b> a starling (lit. &quot;sky freckle&quot; because of their huge flocks that dot the heavens)<br /> <b>hafalagulke-asnen:</b> &quot;freckle of the warring skies&quot; = &quot;war-starling&quot; = raven<br /> <b>mezhum:</b> black and white-spotted; piebald; pied-coloured<br /> <b>mezhum-luzuk:</b> &quot;piebald thief&quot; = a magpie<br /> <b>filsagardur:</b> heather (lit. &quot;children of sour [acidic] soul&quot;)<br /> <b>filsagardur-gi'endu:</b> &quot;those who step through the children of acidic soils&quot; = &quot;heather stepper&quot; = a deer<br /> <b>fuful-kurul:</b> &quot;twig-rending one&quot; = a moose<br /> <b>habarrath:</b> &quot;plow-slave&quot; = an ox<br /> <b>skekhesir-umfin:</b> &quot;snowshoe-claws&quot; = a lynx<br /> <b>usan-ninna:</b> &quot;whip-striking predator&quot; = a falcon<br /> <b>imin-kuthdu:</b> &quot;storm-cleaver&quot; = &quot;storm-shearer&quot; = an eagle<br /> <b>kur-al'al:</b> &quot;rends-the-fields&quot; = a wild boar or pig</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is great. Thanks!<br /> Just a small problem with the starlings; the huge flocks doesn't happen in Scandinavia (at least I've never seen that, and I've lived here all my life...). That said, War-starling is a great name. Kinda feels like another raven-kenning; Blood Swan. Which is beautiful. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thanks again. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T13:57:19-07:00","id":569563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=569466#post569466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is great. Thanks!<br /> Just a small problem with the starlings; the huge flocks doesn't happen in Scandinavia (at least I've never seen that, and I've lived here all my life...). That said, War-starling is a great name. Kinda feels like another raven-kenning; Blood Swan. Which is beautiful. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thanks again. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's a defining feature of the species, according to Wikipedia, so that's what I was going with; the spirit world has their names for things, and we have ours. That being said, if you can link to the species that's found in Scandinavia, then I can come up with a much more fitting name for that particular species! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It gives me an excuse to expand the vocab.<br /> <br /> Still, I'm so glad you liked it! Some of these were hard. xD<br /> <br /> Edit: More d-homonyms. They should now all be done! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>zef:</b> knee<br /> <b>duf:</b> to strew around; to smash up; to heap up or pile up, like a tornado leaving a heap of mangled cars in its wake; to pour onto the ground from a great height; to whirl around (said of a tornado, dust storm, or other wind-dominant weather event)<br /> <b>thuffu:</b> a tablet, whether used for writing or otherwise (not the modern kind)<br /> <b>du'ubh:</b> a pole-pin<br /> <b>thufban:</b> a fence, natural or artificial, made out of stone<br /> <b>thufbana:</b> the stones that make up a stone fence (also may refer to the singular)<br /> <b>thufhal:</b> a runner, courier or messenger; a scribe's assistant; a scribe who writes down things as they are being spoken; a secretary; one who records cases in a court room<br /> <b>dubhla:</b> birds that like to nest on top of tall towers or other tall, urban structures, like pigeons or the odd falcon<br /> <b>dhubhla:</b> a gate tower<br /> <b>Dhubzargu:</b> The piscine sages and scribes of Sumeria, who may or may not have been Bith Balag<br /> <b>dhubzar:</b> a scribe in a high position, such as a king's personal scribe; a secretary or assistant to someone of high status<br /> <b>thubhul:</b> to draw a liquid, such as water or wine; to cause a quantity of liquid to grow<br /> <b>thubul:</b> to paralyse through parasitic means, such as how the Cordyceps fungus plants into a host, and grows throughout their nervous system<br /> <b>thu'uh:</b> a beautiful bird; a songbird kept as a pet, for its song or to decorate/add ambiance, such as a canary; a valuable and beautiful bird<br /> <b>thuh:</b> a clay pot for holding liquid; a capacity of measurement as described by potfuls (for example, an order of ten potfuls of wine for a party)<br /> <b>duha:</b> to command, to rule; rulership or command<br /> <b>thuhha:</b> a situation when any power goes to one's head, and they become brash or tyrannical because of it; to be tyrant-minded or tyrannical in rule<br /> <b>thahu:</b> to loosen or release from; to open up; grain bran, consisting of the outer layers of the grain shells after they've been separated from the grains inside<br /> <b>dul:</b> to cover with fabric or a garment of some kind; a cloth cover, such as canvas roof; to gather, place or bring things or people under such cover<br /> <b>thun:</b> to dig; to rock, to churn around<br /> <b>thepu:</b> a thrusting weapon, such as a polearm<br /> <b>dhun:</b> to lay out a warp on a warping board<br /> <b>dhur:</b> pest birds; birds that come and pick at fields to eat the seeds or crops<br /> <b>du'ur:</b> a ledger board<br /> <b>durr:</b> to fart; to break wind","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 06-26-2015, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T19:52:44-07:00","id":569853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=569563#post569563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a defining feature of the species, according to Wikipedia, so that's what I was going with; the spirit world has their names for things, and we have ours. That being said, if you can link to the species that's found in Scandinavia, then I can come up with a much more fitting name for that particular species! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It gives me an excuse to expand the vocab.<br /> <br /> Still, I'm so glad you liked it! Some of these were hard. xD</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I can figure out.. it's the same species, I suppose winters are just too harsh for them up here, or some such. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> The only birds I ever see in huge flocks are jackdaws.<br /> <br /> And I get that this was hard. I am terrible at everything that has to do with naming things. I'm continually impressed by your skill at this. All this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> How would you translate this; Sword-field harvester; i.e. scavenger, someone who harvest the fields which have been sown by the sword? (Gods, it took some slight effort not to write hath been sown by the sword...) ...Or possibly spear. We've seen a lot of swords in these kennings. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T20:06:32-07:00","id":569857,"title":"","content":"I got another request. After watching some nature documentaries, I learned about wolf 302m from Yellowstone AKA Mr. Cassanova. This wolf had a different reproductive strategy from most wovles, which mate for life. Instead, he snuck through other pack's territory and mated with their younger non alpha females, then ran away to avoid the pissed off alphas/parents.<br /> <br /> So what would the first tongue phrase be for a werewolf that had illicit affairs with lower ranking/younger members of other packs behind the backs of the other pack's leaders, and snuck through the other packs terrority to do it? I can't help but think that this behavior would be common with a certain breed of irraka.<br /> <br /> I want something along the lines of &quot;idiot who cleaves outside the pack&quot; or something like that, but indicating that it is typically irraka that do this, and that it is a very bad idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T20:21:43-07:00","id":569863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=569857#post569857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got another request. After watching some nature documentaries, I learned about wolf 302m from Yellowstone AKA Mr. Cassanova. This wolf had a different reproductive strategy from most wovles, which mate for life. Instead, he snuck through other pack's territory and mated with their younger non alpha females, then ran away to avoid the pissed off alphas/parents.<br /> <br /> So what would the first tongue phrase be for a werewolf that had illicit affairs with lower ranking/younger members of other packs behind the backs of the other pack's leaders, and snuck through the other packs terrority to do it? I can't help but think that this behavior would be common with a certain breed of irraka.<br /> <br /> I want something along the lines of &quot;idiot who cleaves outside the pack&quot; or something like that, but indicating that it is typically irraka that do this, and that it is a very bad idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be a <b>zahduluzuk</b> or &quot;womb thief&quot; (<b>zahdur</b> = womb). That's the polite term, though; if you wanted something equivalent to &quot;man-whore&quot;, that would be <b>kliatemul</b> (&quot;lowly-tasting one&quot;...either because they taste bad to their new mates because of the stink of their old ones, they have bad taste in mates, or they like the taste of pack members who'll roll on their backs for a night).<br /> <br /> Seidrmadr, I'll see what I can do about your translation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 06-26-2015, 11:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T00:07:05-07:00","id":570014,"title":"","content":"I could use words for coyote, hummingbird, mockingbird, and maybe fog, if you think it would be appropriate to have a word separate from mist. If you don't mind. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 06-27-2015, 03:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T11:25:02-07:00","id":570374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=570014#post570014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could use words for coyote, hummingbird, mockingbird, and maybe fog, if you think it would be appropriate to have a word separate from mist. If you don't mind. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Collectively, coyotes, jackals and other, smaller-sized members of the dog family are known as <b>sehker-nu'ur</b>, &quot;little not-dogs&quot;. That being said, they all have proper names in the First Tongue vernacular:<br /> <br /> <b>urwasa:</b> coyote<br /> <b>urur:</b> jackal<br /> <b>ursir:</b> New Guinea singing dogs<br /> <b>urindabin:</b> dingo<br /> <b>urzif:</b> African painted wild dogs<br /> <b>iurhir:</b> domesticated dogs (this one is canon)<br /> <b>urithim:</b> feral dogs or pariah dogs<br /> <b>urthilibi:</b> Indian dhole<br /> <b>urkanisik:</b> short-eared dog<br /> <b>kaurpak:</b> maned wolf (neither wolf nor fox, but still a canid)<br /> <b>kaurnuteh:</b> Falklands wolf (actually a close relative of the maned wolf)<br /> <b>kaurat:</b> bush dog<br /> <br /> As for the others....<br /> <br /> <b>barzegh:</b> fog, thick mist; has a connotation of heavier or worse fog than <b>farsekh</b><br /> <b>wupa:</b> hummingbird (lit. &quot;flitting-wings&quot;)<br /> <b>thuskirlul:</b> mockingbird (lit. &quot;many-song liar&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 06-27-2015, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T11:51:36-07:00","id":570403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=565012#post565012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *babbles at the epicness* DEVS! GET AN EXCUSE FOR MORE INDIAN WEREWOLF SETTINGS, STAT!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd love an excuse to write Indian werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T12:01:59-07:00","id":570409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=570403#post570403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love an excuse to write Indian werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Devangari can be used to write out First Tongue. All it's missing is a symbol to stand for the hyphen. If that isn't a plot hook, combined with links between Proto-Indo-European and FT, I don't know what is.<br /> <br /> Also, because I forgot Seidrmadr's other kenning &gt;.&lt;:<br /> <br /> <b>uhural'al-ghuurdu:</b> &quot;harvester of the sword field&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T12:29:54-07:00","id":570428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=570409#post570409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Devangari can be used to write out First Tongue. All it's missing is a symbol to stand for the hyphen. If that isn't a plot hook, combined with links between Proto-Indo-European and FT, I don't know what is.<br /> <br /> Also, because I forgot Seidrmadr's other kenning &gt;.&lt;:<br /> <br /> <b>uhural'al-ghuurdu:</b> &quot;harvester of the sword field&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks! Just want to remind you that you rock!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T13:49:19-07:00","id":570558,"title":"","content":"Since I think I got all the d-homonyms, it's time to move onto the e-homonyms. If you don't see all of the e-homonyms here, it's because their translations were covered in other words.<br /> <br /> <b>e'e:</b> barley<br /> <b>kammu:</b> chaff, fodder<br /> <b>e:</b> a vocative interjection, equivalent to, the &quot;oh&quot; in, &quot;Oh God!&quot;<br /> <b>asku:</b> to leave, to go out; to remove, to take away, to bring out<br /> <b>a'e:</b> to raise or bring up something; to rear something; to raise a child<br /> <b>maku:</b> raving; to rave<br /> <b>eth:</b> to pierce or scratch; to rip apart or demolish using claws<br /> <b>ed:</b> strong emotions; to have angry mood swings; to be angry because of a mood swing<br /> <b>etha:</b> a space between shelves that has things in it<br /> <b>ethadi:</b> a prebend or prebendary<br /> <b>edhadhi:</b> an offering of flour, whether as a gift, in trade, or as a sacrifice to the gods<br /> <b>edendha:</b> birds that live on flat plains or open ground<br /> <b>ethen:</b> plain, open country; a wide, open desert; hot steppe<br /> <b>ehal:</b> a palace, temple or other important building that has a spirit sealed inside of it; a building of great importance that has a slumbering building-spirit<br /> <b>ehar:</b> a wall or something repurposed as a wall, such as the side of a cliff that was built around<br /> <b>ehirr:</b> a bakery","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 06-28-2015, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T15:10:54-07:00","id":570625,"title":"","content":"I'm back with another odd request. For a game I'm developing I need a phrase which is basically a new oath tenant: &quot;The Wolf Must Ride.&quot; This is in reference to a pack of werewolf street racers using Car Wars/Mad Max style auto duelling through the shadow as ritual combat in lieu of actual warfare with the Pure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/15.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div><br /> That guy you've never heard of.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3069-runeknight3","name":"RuneKnight3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3069_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T15:14:00-07:00","id":570632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RuneKnight3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=570625#post570625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm back with another odd request. For a game I'm developing I need a phrase which is basically a new oath tenant: &quot;The Wolf Must Ride.&quot; This is in reference to a pack of werewolf street racers using Car Wars/Mad Max style auto duelling through the shadow as ritual combat in lieu of actual warfare with the Pure.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Urum da mu'u.</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Enjoy!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T16:17:37-07:00","id":570668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=570409#post570409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Devangari can be used to write out First Tongue. All it's missing is a symbol to stand for the hyphen. If that isn't a plot hook, combined with links between Proto-Indo-European and FT, I don't know what is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... strictly speaking, there are other potential problems. There's no character for a glottal stop in Devanagari, and there are no characters for a long &quot;e&quot;, though the character romanized as &quot;ai&quot; should be an acceptable substitute. Devanagari short &quot;a&quot; is usually pronounced as a schwa (like the &quot;uh&quot; in the first syllable of the word &quot;number&quot;), but that's not really a huge deal. Also, the Indo-Aryan languages don't generally have an alveolar &quot;t&quot;, but rather two different, similar consonants that are pronounced more or less in front of (dental stops) and behind (retroflex stops) the English &quot;t.&quot; I would recommend using Devanagari's dental consonant characters for th, t, d, and dh, rather than the retroflex ones.<br /> <br /> I would advise using the character for &quot;ph&quot; instead of &quot;f&quot;; Sanskrit and Hindi don't have f except in loanwords, and the character used in Devanagari is the character for &quot;ph&quot; with a diacritic. However, since there's no aspirated p in first tongue, you can just use the character with no diacritic. It's a bit more of a stretch, but you can probably use the character for &quot;j&quot; to represent First Tongue z, for similar reasons. Finally, you have to use the &quot;v&quot; character for First Tongue &quot;w&quot;, but Hindi /v/ can be pronounced as [w], so it's not a big deal.<br /> <br /> Also worth noting, I've been using the virama, a diacritic that looks like this: \u094d , in first tongue words that end in a consonant. All consonant chracters in Devanagari have an implied short a following the vowel unless a different vowel or no vowel is indicated by a diacritic. However, the default vowel isn't generally pronounced at the end of modern Hindi words, so the virama may not be strictly necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 06-27-2015, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T21:13:34-07:00","id":570876,"title":"","content":"Decided to translate the names of some W:tA totems. Feel free to use these in your games of both old lines and new. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Nanfarthir-Sua:</b> Alley Cat (lit. &quot;city-cat&quot;)<br /> <b>Dhabhariri:</b> Coyote (lit. &quot;the great trickster&quot;)<br /> <b>Ku'udh-Luzuk:</b> Cuckoo (lit. &quot;nest-thief&quot;)<br /> <b>Kaga'a:</b> Fox (lit. &quot;the great fox&quot;)<br /> <b>Imkikik-Zagga:</b> Magpie (lit. &quot;chases-the-shining&quot;)<br /> <b>Nammguth-Hirim:</b> Lady Luck (lit. &quot;the flower of luck&quot;/&quot;the luck maiden&quot;)<br /> <b>Namus-Lulul:</b> Opossum (lit. &quot;the one who fakes their own death&quot;)<br /> <b>Ghalam-Suh:</b> Raccoon (lit. &quot;clever paws&quot;)<br /> <b>I'iltha'u:</b> Whitewater (lit. &quot;wild high waters&quot;)<br /> <b>Silamza:</b> Bison (lit. &quot;wild cow that brings men close&quot;)<br /> <b>Lirum-Abisharu:</b> Buffalo (lit. &quot;mighty and strong bull&quot;)<br /> <b>Anirpa:</b> Eagle (lit. &quot;lordly wings of heaven&quot;)<br /> <b>Aradeninima:</b> Falcon (lit. &quot;most honourable of the hunting birds&quot;)<br /> <b>Ammahi-Ur:</b> Ice Wolf (lit. &quot;glacial wolf&quot;)<br /> <b>Zurubbu-Ur:</b> Winter Wolf (lit. &quot;cold weather wolf&quot;; could also use <b>Skolis-Ur</b>, but this is if you want a completely different wolf totem with a wintry theme)<br /> <b>I'ilth-Nir:</b> Lion (lit. &quot;wild lord&quot;)<br /> <b>Wuwa-Ninnah:</b> Merlin (lit. &quot;swift bird that whooshes by&quot;)<br /> <b>Parihgu:</b> Osprey (lit. &quot;winged fish-eater&quot;)<br /> <b>Nenneshdu:</b> Sphinx (lit. &quot;the lion-mistress&quot;)<br /> <b>Zimul:</b> Stag (lit. &quot;branches out with life&quot;)<br /> <b>Asharedhul:</b> Stallion (lit. &quot;the virile one&quot;)<br /> <b>Hirim-Pa:</b> Swan (lit. &quot;the flower with wings&quot;)<br /> <b>Kar-Agadhuna:</b> Bear (lit. &quot;the great and hoary one&quot;)<br /> <b>Kuunag-Babhusisu:</b> Black Unicorn (lit. &quot;the shadow of Unicorn&quot;)<br /> <b>Ghudam-Rimu:</b> Bull (lit. &quot;the wildest of bulls&quot;)<br /> <b>Lu'u-U'uf:</b> Dog (lit. &quot;man's best friend&quot;)<br /> <b>Tanidtu-Ur:</b> Fenris (lit. &quot;fame-wolf&quot;; could also use <b>Fenris-Ur</b>, but this is if you want a completely different totem that's tied to the Norse wolf)<br /> <b>Hu'udh-Zubh:</b> Flea (lit. &quot;jumps-and-sucks&quot;)<br /> <b>Ansudh-Kaninna:</b> Griffin (lit. &quot;the great hunting lion-eagle&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 06-28-2015, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T23:47:29-07:00","id":571040,"title":"","content":"I figured I'd share some names I came up with for a couple San Francisco Bay Area-based spirit courts:<br /> <br /> <b>Anzaghar-De-Ulke</b> (&quot;Tower Piercing Heaven&quot;): The spirit of the Transamerica pyramid (&quot;de&quot; is my own, intended as a verb meaning &quot;to pierce&quot;)<br /> <br /> <b>Fela-Nuun</b> (&quot;The Defiled Prince&quot;): Originally the spirit of a minor stream that was obliterated by the growing city, now the bitter and hateful lord of the city's sewer system (&quot;fel&quot; is meant to be a word meaning &quot;to defile&quot;; &quot;fela&quot; is a past-participle)<br /> <br /> <b>Hanzer Affathir</b> (&quot;Flame-colored Forest Elder&quot;): General term for the spirits of redwoods, particularly old-growth redwoods<br /> <br /> <b>Kath Dhuruthfara</b> (&quot;Weaver of Golden Bonds/Ropes&quot;): The spider-like, deranged spirit of the Golden Gate Bridge; possibly a Magath (The &quot;dhur&quot; part of &quot;dhuruthfara&quot; is mine, meant to mean &quot;rope&quot; or &quot;bond&quot;)<br /> <br /> <b>Nir Hanzersakh</b> (&quot;Lord Blazingheart&quot;): A particularly potent and hostile redwood spirit, who still holds a grudge for the logging of the Santa Cruz Mountains<br /> <br /> <b>Nir Zaghuldhim</b> (&quot;Lord of the Carnelian Pillar&quot;): The spirit of 555 California Street, the second tallest building in the city, which is clad in carnelian granite (&quot;zaghul&quot; is mine, intended to mean &quot;carnelian&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 06-28-2015, 03:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T00:11:32-07:00","id":571063,"title":"","content":"Hey that's pretty cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T00:18:04-07:00","id":571065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=571040#post571040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I figured I'd share some names I came up with for a couple San Francisco Bay Area-based spirit courts:<br /> <br /> <b>Anzaghar-De-Ulke</b> (&quot;Tower Piercing Heaven&quot;): The spirit of the Transamerica pyramid (&quot;de&quot; is my own, intended as a verb meaning &quot;to pierce&quot;)<br /> <br /> <b>Fela-Nuun</b> (&quot;The Defiled Prince&quot;): Originally the spirit of a minor stream that was obliterated by the growing city, now the bitter and hateful lord of the city's sewer system (&quot;fel&quot; is meant to be a word meaning &quot;to defile&quot;; &quot;fela&quot; is a past-participle)<br /> <br /> <b>Hanzer Affathir</b> (&quot;Flame-colored Forest Elder&quot;): General term for the spirits of redwoods, particularly old-growth redwoods<br /> <br /> <b>Kath Dhuruthfara</b> (&quot;Weaver of Golden Bonds/Ropes&quot;): The spider-like, deranged spirit of the Golden Gate Bridge; possibly a Magath (The &quot;dhur&quot; part of &quot;dhuruthfara&quot; is mine, meant to mean &quot;rope&quot; or &quot;bond&quot;)<br /> <br /> <b>Nir Hanzersakh</b> (&quot;Lord Blazingheart&quot;): A particularly potent and hostile redwood spirit, who still holds a grudge for the logging of the Santa Cruz Mountains<br /> <br /> <b>Nir Zaghuldhim</b> (&quot;Lord of the Carnelian Pillar&quot;): The spirit of 555 California Street, the second tallest building in the city, which is clad in carnelian granite (&quot;zaghul&quot; is mine, intended to mean &quot;carnelian&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mind if a swipe a few things from your game-dialect for my dictionary? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T00:32:05-07:00","id":571068,"title":"","content":"I'd be honored; they're all degrimmed or grimmed (in the case of &quot;fel&quot;) Sumerian. Another one I was playing around with was <b>faaf</b>, &quot;first and foremost; pre-eminent,&quot; for <b>Faaf Na</b>, &quot;the First Stone,&quot; the spirit of Mount Diablo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 06-28-2015, 03:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T08:29:54-07:00","id":571414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=571068#post571068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be honored; they're all degrimmed or grimmed (in the case of &quot;fel&quot;) Sumerian. Another one I was playing around with was <b>faaf</b>, &quot;first and foremost; pre-eminent,&quot; for <b>Faaf Na</b>, &quot;the First Stone,&quot; the spirit of Mount Diablo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can I also just mention HOW PRETTY your translations are? This is a seriously linguistically-nerdy moment of mine, but it's just the way you've arranged and figured out everything that looks so lovely! *nerdout*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T09:41:40-07:00","id":571565,"title":"","content":"Some translations for the mundane versions of above-listed totems:<br /> <br /> <b>pagukak:</b> osprey (lit. &quot;winged fish carrier&quot;)<br /> <b>ahdha-im'fa:</b> sphinx (lit. &quot;lion of the riddle&quot;)<br /> <b>hutham:</b> North American bison (lit. &quot;wild bovine&quot;)<br /> <b>wuninna:</b> merlin (lit. &quot;flitting hunter&quot;)<br /> <b>zurthu:</b> falcon (lit. &quot;flashing whirl&quot;)<br /> <b>ek:</b> a louse or flea<br /> <b>uhu-ikhi:</b> opossum (lit. &quot;skull-face&quot;)<br /> <b>ku'udhlul:</b> cuckoo (lit. &quot;nest-liar&quot;)<br /> <br /> And derived words:<br /> <br /> <b>ahdha:</b> a difficult question; a riddle; a word problem<br /> <b>uhu:</b> the skull bone<br /> <b>ku'udh:</b> a nest for birds or insects<br /> <br /> And now, more e-homonyms.<br /> <br /> <b>edhuru:</b> an heir<br /> <b>ethuru:</b> a camp; a temporary settlement<br /> <b>egur:</b> a labour camp; a prison camp<br /> <b>elamagum:</b> a landmark consisting of stones or trees that form a canopy or cover that provides ample shade<br /> <b>eli:</b> young, female sheep or lambs; ewes not old enough for breeding<br /> <b>ehli:</b> fluffy or downy birds of white or pale colouring, whether young or old<br /> <b>ellagh:</b> wild bean plants, or wild plants with bean-like fruit or flowers<br /> <b>ellah:</b> a kidney or the kidneys<br /> <b>elangh:</b> beads made out of dried beans or plant pods<br /> <b>em'u:</b> the point of a plow; the point of a battering ram, hammer or any other object that is meant to deliver concussive force<br /> <b>em'e:</b> a female equine such as a jenny donkey, a mare, a molly mule, etc.<br /> <b>emmeh:</b> a wet nurse; an animal brought in to nurse other orphan animals or animals that have been taken from their mothers<br /> <b>emes:</b> a position, whether religious or mundane, of one who monitors the seasons and patterns of the weather; a weather forecaster<br /> <b>bhelu:</b> the highest of the high priests; a religious figure analogous to a Pope or prophet; the religious rulers of a theocracy<br /> <b>en:</b> a priestess with a high-ranking position<br /> <b>endu:</b> a male priest with a high-ranking position<br /> <b>sibtu:</b> an incantation; a spell, especially one spoken aloud<br /> <b>enzi:</b> a mayor; the ruler of a city<br /> <b>ensik:</b> a farmer<br /> <b>enzidh:</b> a lead animal; the animal that leads a pack of hunting predators, such as the lead wolf; an alpha-ranked or dominant animal<br /> <b>Enzith:</b> the highest-ranking ritemaster or religious figure in a pack or alliance of Pure, usually a Fire-Touched<br /> <b>era:</b> the leader of an assembly or meeting<br /> <b>erengu:</b> literally meaning &quot;herd-fish&quot;, this is an unflattering term the enemies and haters of the Bith Balag have for the fish-shifters' mortal relations<br /> <b>erenu:</b> a cedar tree<br /> <b>eresh:</b> a queen or queen-figure; a term for a high-ranking female leader<br /> <b>eres:</b> knowing, wise; an inventor, someone who spearheads revoluntionary new ideas; a name for the first humans that mastered agriculture and domesticated livestock and wolves<br /> <b>erif:</b> a sister-in-law<br /> <b>emum:</b> a father-in-law<br /> <b>errin:</b> a yoke; to yoke to a plow; a team of animals or humans yoked to a plow<br /> <b>esakh:</b> an inheritance of crops or arable land<br /> <b>esagh:</b> a place to store grain in; a granary<br /> <b>ezi:</b> diorite or dolerite<br /> <b>ezir:</b> a street<br /> <b>itdu:</b> bitumen or pitch<br /> <b>guesir:</b> fishing sandals","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 06-29-2015, 12:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T11:53:58-07:00","id":571722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=571414#post571414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can I also just mention HOW PRETTY your translations are? This is a seriously linguistically-nerdy moment of mine, but it's just the way you've arranged and figured out everything that looks so lovely! *nerdout*</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks man! You should see the actual conlangs I've worked on. :P<br /> <br /> <i>Na yeth t\u012b kbau Rom w\u00ed Mhakh Thandim ryang na n\u00e1 de ganggen rom w\u00ed na, o dandai w\u014dm mro ba &quot;Mhakh Rom,&quot; au! </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T11:59:55-07:00","id":571724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=571722#post571722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thanks man! You should see the actual conlangs I've worked on. :P<br /> <br /> <i>Na yeth t\u012b kbau Rom w\u00ed Mhakh Thandim ryang na n\u00e1 de ganggen rom w\u00ed na, o dandai w\u014dm mro ba &quot;Mhakh Rom,&quot; au! </i></div> </div> </div> </div>Link.<br /> <br /> Link now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T13:08:15-07:00","id":571800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=571724#post571724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Link.<br /> <br /> Link now.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That one's part of a (theoretically) ongoing game where two teams create proto-languages, each player derives one or more daughter languages from the proto-lang, and then the other team tries to reconstruct the proto-language from the daughter languages. Thus, I can't take complete credit for the grammar, though the changes made from the parent language are my own.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the language is part of a shared setting called Akana, which has a wiki. The page for Mhakh Thandim is <a href=\"http://akana.conlang.org/wiki/Mhakh_Thandim\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>; you can see its &quot;sister&quot; languages by clicking on the &quot;Ronquian Languages&quot; category link at the bottom of the page, and there's lots of other good stuff elsewhere on the wiki. Also, if you're interested in conlangs, I would recommend checking out <a href=\"http://www.incatena.org/viewforum.php?f=13&amp;sid=a5e618f20244b16b5b08199d38ba9f04\" target=\"_blank\">ZBB</a>. I've been pretty active there in the past, though lately my interests have wandered somewhat. I'll probably come back to it some time soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T22:02:15-07:00","id":572202,"title":"","content":"<b>palgan:</b> a Place-That-Isn't, or a place in the Shadow with no Earthly equivalent<br /> <b>eskdar:</b> A special type of Place-That-Isn't that is a relic of long-lost Pangaea<br /> <b>durokh:</b> a planet that cannot hold or sustain mortal life; a planet that has lost all its life after some great apocalyptic event<br /> <b>thanah:</b> a planet able to sustain life, such as Earth<br /> <b>muludh:</b> the suns of other worlds<br /> <b>Nusigruyim:</b> The Nameless, nameless and formless spirits of the Wyld from W:tA<br /> <b>Kathrarim:</b> the various spider-like or spider-spirits that serve the Weaver from W:tA; a catch-all term for regular Pattern Spider-spirits<br /> <b>Gulukik-Kathrarim:</b> Channel-Spiders, hatred- and intolerance-spreading Weaver-spirits from W:tA<br /> <b>Futhukh-Kathrarim:</b> Covenant Spiders, conformity-based Weaver-spirits from W:tA<br /> <b>Sehag-Nir:</b> The Patriarch (lit. &quot;The Lord of Obedience&quot;), a Wyrm-tainted obedience spirit of the Weaver's from W:tA<br /> <b>Ninhummun:</b> The Incarna of Science, controlled by the Weaver","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 09-03-2016, 10:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T17:49:49-07:00","id":574533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you call a 'point' of essence? In character I usually say 'an ounce'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would use <b>bhisa</b>. It literally means &quot;droplet, ounce, or point&quot; in the sense you're using, and more literally, &quot;drip-bead&quot; or &quot;droplet (of liquid)&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T13:50:26-07:00","id":575577,"title":"","content":"And now the e-homonyms are finished!<br /> <br /> <b>es:</b> to be cold or of a low temperature<br /> <b>esh:</b> flour that needs further refining; coarse flour meant to be ground down more<br /> <b>esshu:</b> a small shrine or area devoted to a religious figure inside a household; a household shrine or altar, such as that used for Wicca<br /> <b>kushesh:</b> a tent or pavilion where religious services are performed, or where a makeshift shrine is kept; tents made into churches by travelling preachers or religious figures<br /> <b>ez:</b> three; the number three; triplets; to be in triplicate<br /> <b>esklam:</b> an almond tree<br /> <b>esk:</b> an almond nut<br /> <b>nesesh:</b> a turpentine tree, or any tree of the terebinth family<br /> <b>ezmu:</b> groundwater; water from a well<br /> <b>eshdha:</b> a sacred goblet or cup; a grail<br /> <b>ezda:</b> one thing in particular; one thing that stands out; a chosen or prophesied thing; lit. &quot;the one&quot;<br /> <b>estham:</b> a tavern or inn<br /> <b>esdham:</b> a discussion or consultation<br /> <b>ese:</b> a unit of length or volume measured on a string, such as a yard of string<br /> <b>esla:</b> a band, belt or tie of some sort; bonds or ropes that hold something<br /> <b>ezla:</b> a drumstick or hoop stick<br /> <b>meggu:</b> a reed sieve, or any sort of sieve<br /> <b>eslah:</b> a trap for animals; a hunting trap<br /> <b>izimusen:</b> a firebird or phoenix<br /> <b>musen:</b> a catch-all term for birds","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 07-01-2015, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/