heonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T20:07:33-07:00","id":575959,"title":"","content":"And now we begin with the g-homonyms.<br /> <br /> <b>hafa:</b> the chest, breast or breastbone<br /> <b>irdu:</b> a frontier<br /> <b>habhanal:</b> to strike with a great amount of force; to run over, to plough over; to be struck by a vehicle<br /> <b>ghabanhal:</b> the front guard or bumper of a vehicle, such as a chariot's front guard or the front bumper of a car<br /> <b>gafil:</b> the main beam/body (or &quot;basket&quot;) of a chariot<br /> <b>hafshum:</b> a tablet of sale; a receipt<br /> <b>ghabsum:</b> a catch-all term for sellers or merchants<br /> <b>hadha:</b> flax or linen<br /> <b>hadhala:</b> sacred clothing or vestments, such as a priest's robes<br /> <b>gathala:</b> one who is newly-ordained to a priesthood or religious order<br /> <b>hakh:</b> a small, sharp object such as a nail, a peg or an arrowhead<br /> <b>haghul:</b> an eyeball<br /> <b>khaggul:</b> a mash tun for brewing<br /> <b>haghulgu:</b> the eyeball of a fish; a fish-eyed lens or visual phenomenon<br /> <b>khakghul:</b> the heart of a plant<br /> <b>halah:</b> a singer of sad songs or lamentations<br /> <b>ghala:</b> the female genitals; a vulva<br /> <b>hallam:</b> to be skilled or clever; to be of a tasteful or masterful make<br /> <b>gham:</b> a crooked or bent stick; a shepherd's crook<br /> <b>shigru:</b> the haft or hilt of something<br /> <b>gam:</b> the mathematical concept of depth<br /> <b>khamgham:</b> a diving water bird<br /> <b>gamghamgu:</b> fish that live deep in ponds, rivers or lakes; bottom-feeder fish<br /> <b>khana:</b> shackles<br /> <b>gha'ana:</b> roughly, an order to request to come over; to beckon or call someone over \u2014 it's an FT word that embodies the concept of waving at someone and telling them, &quot;Come on!&quot;<br /> <b>kha'ne:</b> the total area of a non-quadrilateral figure<br /> <b>abhuna:</b> moreover; in addition to; besides; a further matter<br /> <b>khanam:</b> a female sheep or goat<br /> <b>khanzer:</b> when capitalized, an Avernian Gate, or a portal to the underworld or an underground realm; an entrance to a tunnel, mine or other subterranean structure<br /> <b>khar:</b> a cake; baked goods<br /> <b>gharanu:</b> to heap up; to pile up; to stack up<br /> <b>kha'ar:</b> to be heroic; a heroic feat, action or event<br /> <b>garru:</b> a knob<br /> <b>hargar:</b> hairstyles associated with the upper class, such as nobility or royalty<br /> <b>ha'ar:</b> retirement; to be retired<br /> <b>heskhar:</b> an implement<br /> <b>khara:</b> cream<br /> <b>ghar:</b> to be deserted; to be abandoned or empty<br /> <b>kharas:</b> a disaster or catastrophe<br /> <b>gharas:</b> a leek<br /> <b>haras:</b> a military encampment; a military base<br /> <b>harkhar:</b> an accumulation of something; a great amount<br /> <b>garhar:</b> pastries or a pastry","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 07-02-2015, 03:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T00:40:54-07:00","id":576161,"title":"","content":"More g-homonyms.<br /> <br /> <b>ghazam:</b> reeds; water grasses<br /> <b>hazham:</b> a specialist in a certain area of craftsmanship, such as a master bricklayer or pottery-maker<br /> <b>khe:</b> an arch or curve in architecture; a curving geometric shape on a building, such as a rosette<br /> <b>ghe:</b> a stroke; a mark; handwriting<br /> <b>ghi:</b> an essence or extraction of something<br /> <b>hi:</b> a judgement or verdict<br /> <b>khi:</b> a dried and/or stiff reed; a cane; a staff<br /> <b>niskhi:</b> a reedbed or reed thicket<br /> <b>gi'i:</b> to go back on an agreement; to return goods as part of a cancelled agreement; to announce the end of a cancelled partnership or contract<br /> <b>ghifil:</b> firewood or kindling<br /> <b>piru:</b> a sprout or offshoot<br /> <b>hibhil:</b> new or newborn; fresh, green; a greenhorn or green person in a place or line of work; a newbie<br /> <b>khidh:</b> to drag or tow; to pull a boat or car onto another surface or area, such as dragging a boat out of the water<br /> <b>hid:</b> to be long and tight, like a stretched rope<br /> <b>khith:</b> to survey or measure something like a property or field","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 07-02-2015, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T03:16:00-07:00","id":576254,"title":"","content":"Hi there, Sikla! I've been 