":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4708-litheon","name":"Litheon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T22:20:25-07:00","id":577084,"title":"","content":"For your Deed-Name, Sikla Alkis; I think <i>Author-of-Tongues</i> suits you well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T05:39:03-07:00","id":577275,"title":"","content":"Sikla--<br /> <br /> For &quot;The Agreement of Wolves&quot;, I'm taking from the dictionary that it would be something like,<br /> <br /> Ur Seh.<br /> <br /> Seh-Ur would be &quot;Agreement Wolf&quot;, which is a name.<br /> <br /> Would Ur Seh be something like &quot;wolves in agreement&quot;?<br /> <br /> In the game I am running there is a truce between the Pure and the Forsaken (for the moment, very shaky!) and I need name for it, and would prefer First Tongue.<br /> <br /> Further, it would be neat if I could have a term for those who have agreed to this truce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3855,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","user":"gebbethine","date":". 07-03-2015, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T08:12:21-07:00","id":577376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gebbethine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=577275#post577275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sikla--<br /> <br /> For &quot;The Agreement of Wolves&quot;, I'm taking from the dictionary that it would be something like,<br /> <br /> Ur Seh.<br /> <br /> Seh-Ur would be &quot;Agreement Wolf&quot;, which is a name.<br /> <br /> Would Ur Seh be something like &quot;wolves in agreement&quot;?<br /> <br /> In the game I am running there is a truce between the Pure and the Forsaken (for the moment, very shaky!) and I need name for it, and would prefer First Tongue.<br /> <br /> Further, it would be neat if I could have a term for those who have agreed to this truce.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're looking for <b>Urag-Seh</b>, which means &quot;the agreement of [the] wolves&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> As for a name <b>Sehul</b>, or &quot;the Agreed&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T08:47:26-07:00","id":577387,"title":"","content":"Thanks, duder!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T12:14:22-07:00","id":579067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=576762#post576762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was going over my generational werewolf notes and I thought of something.<br /> <br /> What would be a good name for spirits of post-modernism that serve formless idigam (and sometimes hang out with magi, as a M:tAs reference)? I am thinking that Post-modernism, what with it's belief in the non-existence of objective truth, would be a perfect fit with the undefined nature of the formless and that the team up would have been a big threat in the 90s.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still have to translate the Werewolf generations, but to get this little challenge done now: <b>Nu-Huginihhinim</b>, which means &quot;spirits not of a whole truth&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T06:21:28-07:00","id":579745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=576346#post576346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> These shouldn't take long. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Question, though: are these totems, greater spirits, PCs, etc?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=576627#post576627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They will be PCs... but Beast ones. So i think they will not be Totems (though maybe in the End they could), but they could qualify as Spirits, maybe, at some point. I trust your intuition, as always.<br /> <br /> And by the way, i'm totally behind FallenEco and ElvesofZion. You have crafted names for me EVERY single time i came bothering. So, i am very, very grateful to you, mate. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> These are all Deed Names i'd suggest for you: <i>Name-Crafter. Father-of-Names. Thousand-Words. First Tongue-Weaver.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Just in case you overlooked it, that's the answer to your quesiton <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T22:48:30-07:00","id":580559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=576254#post576254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi there, Sikla! I've been thinking about some names soon to be used and i wanted to ask for you translations one more time,if you feel like it:<br /> <br /> Dark Star Lord<br /> <br /> Quiet Lord of the Starred Sky<br /> <br /> The Whisper in the Emptyness between the Stars<br /> <br /> Thank you for your time! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><b>Sumukh-Mulan-Nir:</b> Dark Star Lord (implying the PC is a lord of the starts that is meant to be <i>feared</i>)<br /> <b>Mulanulke-Mekhar-Nir:</b> Quiet Lord of the Starred Sky (lit. &quot;starry skies' silent lord&quot;)<br /> <b>Dumuskir-Ina-Mulunag-Thi'rih:</b> The Whisper In the Emptiness Between the Stars (lit. &quot;the whisper in the canyons of the stars&quot;)<br /> <br /> Young Man, other than the Non-Objective Truth Spirits, I'm still trying to figure out a translation for you. I have a bit of a block. &gt;.&lt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T23:38:43-07:00","id":580577,"title":"","content":"Skipping ahead to the \u011d section of homonyms because, as I recently found out, this decorated g actually stands for the <b>ng</b> sound, such as one you might find in certain pronunciations of the word &quot;finger&quot;. It can be recognized as <b>n</b>, <b>ng</b>, <b>nh</b> or any of the Grimmified g-settings, so I'm taking this chance to add a little diversity to the dictionary.<br /> <br /> <b>ga:</b> a house<br /> <b>nal:</b> to watch over; to guard; to protect; to have something as a ward; to defend a position<br /> <b>ghal:</b> to open something<br /> <b>nes:</b> a penis; the male genitalia<br /> <b>khesla:</b> to be quiet for the purposes of listening or overhearing; to be eavesdropping; to be listening for a certain sound<br /> <b>nhesur:</b> to abandon a claim or property<br /> <b>neshur:</b> to harrow; harrow<br /> <b>khesfir:</b> to be dried out, as in dried food; to be dried, dehydrated or shriveled up<br /> <b>khesfigu:</b> dried fish<br /> <b>nesfur:</b> an architectural ornament<br /> <b>khesbur:</b> a ceremonial or symbolic crook, such as the Crook of Osiris<br /> <b>neshbur:</b> a wasp<br /> <b>niskhana:</b> a birch tree<br /> <b>neshana:</b> a wooden pestle<br /> <b>neskur:</b> a plan<br /> <b>hesgur:</b> a strategist; a planner<br /> <b>heshgihti:</b> a workshop; a collection or union of workers<br /> <b>gheskihdi:</b> a craftsman<br /> <b>hisla:</b> a downhill or badly-going battle; a time of great strife<br /> <b>nezla:</b> a secret or spare key; a passcode, password or other such secret method to get into somewhere<br /> <b>hessuthumak:</b> a tally stick<br /> <b>gezudhumag:</b> notes to oneself; casual hand-written records, such as phone numbers written down on a napkin; Post-It Notes<br /> <b>nesdugh:</b> to have understanding or great wisdom/experience in a matter; to have good sense of reason; one who is prepared or of a prepared nature<br /> <b>Nesdughgu:</b> Bith Balag who served as teachers and advisors to ancient priests, as well as to the nobility and their children<br /> <b>himusen:</b> a nocturnal bird<br /> <b>hi:</b> to be nocturnal; night-related<br /> <b>nibar:</b> a cloister; a place where priests or other religious personnel live<br /> <b>hipar:</b> a tree full of edible fruit<br /> <b>nhir:</b> a native or local<br /> <b>nhirgu:</b> fish local to an area<br /> <b>ni'ir:</b> to flash; a flash or flashy sight<br /> <b>ghir:</b> a scorpion; a stinging insect, or an animal or creature with a sting<br /> <b>niri:</b> a razor; a dagger; a short blade<br /> <b>gi'ri:</b> via, by means of, under the authority of someone<br /> <b>ghiri:</b> path; way; a distance to be walked<br /> <b>ghusur:</b> a tree trunk<br /> <b>nhuzhur:</b> the stocks or stockades<br /> <br /> And some corrections to the dictionary, since there are more duplicates:<br /> <br /> <b>abha:</b> The abha entry standing for the word &quot;who&quot; was an accident, and should be removed.<br /> <b>bur:</b> The &quot;bur&quot; entry that mentions sacrifice and tearing out a foe's heart should instead be <b>bhu'uhr</b>.<br /> <b>du:</b> The two &quot;du&quot; entries should be merged as one.<br /> <b>si:</b> The &quot;si&quot; entry that refers to filling or loading up should now be <b>si'i</b>.<br /> <b>thun:</b> The entry that refers to churning things around should instead be <b>thu'un</b>.<br /> <b>urzif:</b> The entry that refers to African wild dogs should instead be <b>ursharzif</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 07-07-2015, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T07:15:43-07:00","id":580919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=580559#post580559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Young Man, other than the Non-Objective Truth Spirits, I'm still trying to figure out a translation for you. I have a bit of a block. &gt;.&lt;</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not refer to the generations using &quot;Deed names&quot; of a sort referring to what those generations were associated with? The GI generation would be &quot;Those who came of age in the war against the fascists&quot; and similar translations would exist for the other generations? That's my suggestion, but you're the linguist here, so it's ultimately up to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T07:44:50-07:00","id":580942,"title":"","content":"I was wondering about a previous translation and a reverse translation.<br /> <br /> Previously, in the Slasher name breakdown, we found that Thima-Li'inamsu means 'thoughts of a thousand deaths.' Could that also be used to say 'thousand thoughts of death' as a sort of maliciously named spirit being? If not, what would be a better translation of that? Also, what would just 'Thousand Thoughts' be, as in a genius or a very active mind.<br /> <br /> And in another thread, we got a clue possibly maybe for the upcoming Pack book and I was wondering if it could be translated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/537852-the-pack?p=576770#post576770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for what I'm writing about, here's a First Tongue phrase that might feature in part of it (might, not certain yet, depends on a few things): <i>Uma Suguthkuth</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only part I think I recognize is kuth, for cut.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T08:20:19-07:00","id":580969,"title":"","content":"I actually have all the words for this translation memorized. xD<br /> <br /> <b>li'imthima:</b> a highly intelligent person; a mundane genius (lit. &quot;thousand thoughts&quot;)<br /> <b>Li'imusthima:</b> A Thousand Thoughts of Death (lit. &quot;A Thousand Killing Thoughts&quot;), for a malicious spirit-being<br /> <br /> As for that word, it appears to translate to &quot;victory-cut crown&quot;, or &quot;victory cut from a sweet body&quot;. <b>Suguth</b> means &quot;headdress&quot; or &quot;crown&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why not refer to the generations using &quot;Deed names&quot; of a sort referring to what those generations were associated with? The GI generation would be &quot;Those who came of age in the war against the fascists&quot; and similar translations would exist for the other generations? That's my suggestion, but you're the linguist here, so it's ultimately up to you. </div> </div> </div>That could work, but I have to find something universal. Depending on your culture, what one generation from one place is remembered as could be entirely different in another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 07-07-2015, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T08:28:19-07:00","id":580974,"title":"","content":"Thanks! I found your slasher translations very 'pretty' like CatDoom's San Fran ones. Which is fun, considering their morbid source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T08:35:50-07:00","id":580975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=580974#post580974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks! I found your slasher translations very 'pretty' like CatDoom's San Fran ones. Which is fun, considering their morbid source.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel they're some of my best attempts thus far. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And hey, there are some very pretty words out there that are incredibly morbid, like <i>thanatos</i>.<br /> <br /> Edit: Fixed the genius translation, accidentally used the word for face instead of thousand. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 07-06-2015, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T08:41:39-07:00","id":580981,"title":"","content":"And lethiferous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T08:59:29-07:00","id":580989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=580969#post580969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for that word, it appears to translate to &quot;victory-cut crown&quot;, or &quot;victory cut from a sweet body&quot;. <b>Suguth</b> means &quot;headdress&quot; or &quot;crown&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite close!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T09:02:25-07:00","id":580993,"title":"","content":"<b>hin:</b> permanent; to be permanent<br /> <b>khen:</b> to verify as true; to establish or verify in a legal context<br /> <b>ghin:</b> to be of moderate, medium or average quality<br /> <b>gir:</b> anger, rage; to be berserk or berserking; a berserker<br /> <b>girgu:</b> long, aggressive fish such as a barracuda; fish-like monsters such as the leviathan<br /> <b>khir:</b> a dowry<br /> <b>ghir:</b> a large jar; jars meant to store large objects or quantities<br /> <b>ghi'ir:</b> a runner; an athlete that runs or does track; a jogger<br /> <b>khi'ir:</b> to harness; to tie up; yoke; hitch up; bind up<br /> <b>anshe:</b> invasive trees or large bushes that are choking out other plants in a garden or farming plot; trees and large plants whose roots are growing into the foundations of a building or buildings<br /> <b>hirah:</b> raw materials<br /> <b>ghirak:</b> tools used for building things<br /> <b>khirkhid:</b> a fish-eating bird<br /> <b>khirkhigu:</b> fish stolen or caught by fish-eating birds<br /> <b>hirhir:</b> rodents that stow away on ships, such as rats<br /> <b>hirgirgu:</b> supplies of fish destroyed by rodents or other animals like birds<br /> <b>khiri:</b> a cry or crying sound<br /> <b>hiri:</b> a chair or seat<br /> <b>khiri'ilu:</b> lament; a wailing cry; to verbally express angst<br /> <b>hirilu:</b> a bird with a sad song, such as a whippoorwill<br /> <b>hizi:</b> a fish that lives in the reeds or weedy places of a river or water body<br /> <br /> More g-homonyms picked away at. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Progress is slow, but good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T09:04:22-07:00","id":580995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=580989#post580989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Quite close!</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it &quot;victory cut from a great height&quot;? Is it a &quot;sweet, high victory&quot;? Is it &quot;victory cut from fish&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T09:10:05-07:00","id":581003,"title":"","content":"'Victory through cutting off the head'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T09:13:52-07:00","id":581032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=581003#post581003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'Victory through cutting off the head'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooooooh, I was so close! &gt;.&lt; That sounds bad-*** as crap, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T14:40:15-07:00","id":581554,"title":"","content":"And now, for various terms in <i>War Against the Pure</i>'s shapeshifter section that don't have an FT translations, starting with the werebulls. And some other stuff.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Werebulls (Baal-Hadad, Gudthabak)</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>ghudam:</b> the &quot;blade&quot; or leader of a werebull herd<br /> <b>uthzif:</b> a &quot;sun-mark&quot;, or the solar spirit brands the werebulls have carved/burnt/etc. into their flesh<br /> <b>Ghulthu'u:</b> the hybrid form of the Baal-Hadad<br /> <b>Abisu:</b> the animal form of the Baal-Hadad<br /> <b>Mabhos:</b> the near-beast form of the Baal-Hadad<br /> <b>Ahaskudh:</b> the near-human form of the Baal-Hadad<br /> <b>Dhigir-Mir:</b> &quot;Rage of the Gods&quot;, the werebulls' name for Death Rage<br /> <b>anbis:</b> a bull-changer who becomes a white cow, and considered more sacred or lucky than others (lit. &quot;heavenly cow&quot;)<br /> <b>Nihhina-Sagrik Alal:</b> The Rite of Molech, or the Rite of True Sacrifice<br /> <b>Malgu:</b> An alternate name for Helios used by the Baal-Hadad<br /> <b>Zahigi-Dhigir:</b> &quot;Unawakened Gods&quot;, the bull-blooded that have the potential to become Baal-Hadad<br /> <b>Anizi:</b> &quot;holy fires&quot;, or the Helions of Helios that visit the Baal-Hadad (and are believed to actually be Helios's avatars)<br /> <b>subhur:</b> the mortal &quot;herd&quot; that a werebull or werebulls rule over<br /> <b>ammar:</b> &quot;calves&quot; or &quot;calf&quot;, children or descendants of a werebull, who usually act as liaisons or have some sort of important position when it comes to the werebull herd<br /> <b>subhurhia:</b> the offerings a werebull's herd are supposed to make to their bull-headed overlords<br /> <b>absasa:</b> personal idols the Baal-Hadad make themselves that grant them special boons and bonuses<br /> <b>Anizalath:</b> a &quot;holy fire&quot; that a Baal-Hadad has taken as a totem<br /> <b>Malgubes-igi:</b> said of a werebull that has the Sun-Flecked Eyes aspect, it literally means &quot;sun-blessed eyes&quot; and refers to how the sun grants them better sight<br /> <b>zulalumag-zif:</b> &quot;the punishment's mark&quot;, a Castigating Brand put upon one by a werebull<br /> <b>halzugenak:</b> the title or deed name of a werebull<br /> <br /> <b><u>Other Stuff:</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>yaan:</b> perfect knowledge or heavenly wisdom; knowledge that is inherently true about the fundamental reality of the universe<br /> <b>dhigir:</b> a catch-all term for deities, gods or goddesses<br /> <b>abhos:</b> like <b>abis</b>, this refers to cows and cattle, but can also refer to more ancient members of the cow family, and extinct cow breeds<br /> <b>burhia:</b> a catch-all term for sacrifices or offerings<br /> <b>zulalum:</b> a punishment; a sentence","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 07-07-2015, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T20:06:44-07:00","id":581864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=580969#post580969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That could work, but I have to find something universal. Depending on your culture, what one generation from one place is remembered as could be entirely different in another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the strauss Howe theory is spefically for the generations of the western world in general and America specifically. so I was thinking that naming generations is something western and american werewolves do. Still if universalness is desired, why not work the range of birth dates for each generation into the name, and then have a more culturally specific label before the date range?<br /> <br /> Something like &quot;The GI generation, whelped from 1901 to 1924&quot;<br /> <br /> Some Cahalith telling epic stories of these generations would use an even longer, poetic version that worked the turnings that formed the generations into the name. Most use the shorter version above<br /> <br /> Like &quot;The GI generation, whelped from 1901 to 1924, during the unraveling that was the (insert poetic name for world war one here) and the (insert poetic name for Proibition here) and came of age in the time of Crisis that was the (insert poetic name for the great depression here) and the (insert poetic name for the 2nd world war).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T20:15:51-07:00","id":581893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=581864#post581864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well the strauss Howe theory is spefically for the generations of the western world in general and America specifically. so I was thinking that naming generations is something western and american werewolves do. Still if universalness is desired, why not work the range of birth dates for each generation into the name, and then have a more culturally specific label before the date range?<br /> <br /> Something like &quot;The GI generation, whelped from 1901 to 1924&quot;<br /> <br /> Some Cahalith telling epic stories of these generations would use an even longer, poetic version that worked the turnings that formed the generations into the name. Most use the shorter version above<br /> <br /> Like &quot;The GI generation, whelped from 1901 to 1924, during the unraveling that was the (insert poetic name for world war one here) and the (insert poetic name for Proibition here) and came of age in the time of Crisis that was the (insert poetic name for the great depression here) and the (insert poetic name for the 2nd world war).</div> </div> </div> </div>With this in mind, I'll start with a Westernized translation of the generational names, and if anyone else has suggestions for other spheres of the world, hit me up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T20:30:13-07:00","id":581901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=581893#post581893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With this in mind, I'll start with a Westernized translation of the generational names, and if anyone else has suggestions for other spheres of the world, hit me up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strauss%E2%80%93Howe_generational_theory#Timing_of_generations_and_turnings\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>'s a list of the western generations and the turnings they were born in.<br /> <br /> If you really wanted to get fancy, you could work the generation type into the Cahalith version. the generation types are Prophets (such as the boomers) who are born in a high (such as the period between WW2 and the assassination of Kennedy) and come of age in an awakening, Nomads (such as generation X) who are born in an awakening (such as the counter culture era of the 60s and 70s) and come of age in an unraveling, Heroes (such as the millainals) who are born in an unraveling (such as the culture wars/post modernsim of the 80s and 90s) and come of age in a crisis (which may either be the war on terror or the global economic crisis for this particular cylce).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T00:01:09-07:00","id":581999,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the traductions, Sikla! ^^<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T09:25:21-07:00","id":582426,"title":"","content":"Added a few more Baal-Hadad terms, and now, time for the werecats to get a mini-lexicon. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b><u>Werecats (The Colony, Suthanu-sua)</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Zuarri:</b> the goddess Bast/Bastet, patroness and &quot;mother&quot; of all werecat kind<br /> <b>Maeresh Zuarri:</b> &quot;Great Lady Bastet&quot;, a respectful title for Bastet<br /> <b>Amahan Zuarri:</b> Another name for Bastet, meaning &quot;Mother Bastet&quot;<br /> <b>Zi'irulag-Kadah:</b> &quot;The Great Hunt of the Sinful&quot;, the driving mission and entire purpose for the Colony's existence<br /> <b>Zi'irani:</b> the prey of the Suthanu-sua, sinful and inharmonious individuals<br /> <b>Nuserdha:</b> &quot;The Guiltless&quot;, or those who are mistakenly slain by the werecats in their missions<br /> <b>Kuth-Kurah:</b> &quot;The Call&quot;, in which a werecat gains a nagging urge to convert another into one of the Colony; coloquially known as &quot;going into heat&quot;<br /> <b>Suammethu:</b> &quot;The Fever&quot;, or the spiritual disease that is meant to turn one into one of the Colony; this is fatal if a werecat doesn't intervene and bring the victim into the fold, and is coloquially known as &quot;Cat Scratch Fever&quot;<br /> <b>umfi'ira:</b> the foul, pungent oil extruded from a werecat's claws that is used to &quot;infect&quot; another with the Colony curse<br /> <b>Suaigi:</b> the near-human form of the Suthanu-sua<br /> <b>Usiira:</b> the hybrid form of the Suthanu-sua<br /> <b>Tagaraah:</b> the near-beast form of the Suthanu-sua<br /> <b>Ehsua:</b> the animal form of the Suthanu-sua<br /> <b>Zifara:</b> &quot;soul-colour&quot;, or the &quot;auspice&quot; of a werecat as determined by their eyes<br /> <b>Suthzibigi:</b> a Bloodeyes werecat<br /> <b>Afuahigi:</b> a Goldeyes werecat<br /> <b>Thiranigi:</b> a Leafeyes werecat<br /> <b>Thuhhima:</b> The megalomaniac Madness Rage of the werecats<br /> <b>Namserdha:</b> &quot;The Guilt&quot; \u2014 when capitalized, it refers to the madness werecats suffer if they do not kill a sinful person within a certain time period<br /> <b>Karana:</b> &quot;The Burden&quot; \u2014 the trials and tribulations of the werecat curse, and the heavy burden it lays on the chosen werecat, sometimes driving the werecat completely insane; a word used to sum up a werecat's existence<br /> <b>Zulalumul:</b> &quot;Punishers&quot;, werecats who turn others into one of the Colony because they were sinful offenders as mortals<br /> <b>Numalasul:</b> &quot;The Careless&quot;, werecats who choose a new Colony curse victim completely at random<br /> <b>Suaziha:</b> &quot;Cat-Cursed&quot;, those who were picked to become werecats because of a vengeful werecat, or completely at random<br /> <b>Sua-Namtar:</b> &quot;Cat-Chosen&quot;, those who were deliberately picked to become werecats after a period of long observation and thought<br /> <b>yamak:</b> the various beliefs and superstitions of the Suthanu-sua<br /> <b>ziramak:</b> things believed to be sinful or taboo, and thus fodder for punishment or retribution, by the werecats<br /> <b>suamu:</b> the deed name of a werecat<br /> <b>dumizu:</b> the act of a werecat stealing a child's life force to gain essence; considered the <b>ziramak</b> of all <b>ziramak</b> by the Colony<br /> <b>kuk-keli:</b> a &quot;neck-biter&quot;; said of werecats who have the Spinebite aspect<br /> <b>murudu:</b> a &quot;sprayer&quot;; said of werecats who have the Malodor aspect<br /> <b>thulmalas:</b> a &quot;graceful faller&quot;; said of werecats who have the Righting Reflex aspect<br /> <br /> <br /> And derived terms:<br /> <b>ummethu:</b> fever, sickness, illness<br /> <b>i'ira:</b> a scented oil or residue<br /> <b>serdha:</b> crime, offense; to be guilty of something<br /> <b>namserdha:</b> guilt, guiltful feelings<br /> <b>muru:</b> mist; drizzle; spray","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 07-09-2015, 08:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T04:09:27-07:00","id":584501,"title":"","content":"More g-homonyms! (And a couple of derived terms.)<br /> <br /> <b>hu'u:</b> a corded net<br /> <b>ghu:</b> the entirety, sum or total of a deal, a lot, or some other legal, financial or business-related thing<br /> <b>kuu:</b> fibrous plants that have not yet been retted (soaked) for use<br /> <b>khu:</b> the bank of something, like a river or gully<br /> <b>khu'u:</b> the pulse in the neck; the arterial pulse<br /> <b>khumusen:</b> birds that nest on the sides of hills or riverbanks, like certain types of swallows<br /> <b>huu:</b> the voice or cry of a certain animal; an animal call or the mimicry of one<br /> <b>ghu'u:</b> to square something in mathematics<br /> <b>kalabu:</b> to cover with; to slip into; to slip through<br /> <b>hu'e:</b> to roar; to call out in invocation; to call out or challenge a god or spirit; used as an interjection in the vein of, &quot;I call to you, O ____!&quot;<br /> <b>khuf:</b> to purify oneself through means of a ritual bath; rites that involve bathing or dunking someone in water, such as baptism<br /> <b>hubh:</b> to stand up when one is called for; to stand at attention<br /> <b>ghubh:</b> to be assigned to a task; an assignment<br /> <b>zeru:</b> dislike; to have a dislike or distaste for something or someone; to have disgust for<br /> <b>skir dhe:</b> to address someone; to call out to someone<br /> <b>zerru:</b> to ignore; to neglect<br /> <b>kuluhuu-skir:</b> to bray; to bawl; to bellow or shout in some sort of distress, such as pain, sadness or fear<br /> <b>haranu:</b> to pile up something, like throwing sacks of flour into a pile; to sort into piles<br /> <b>shurru:</b> to lean; to bend forwards; to bow<br /> <b>ghith:</b> to drag; dragging; to pull along<br /> <b>keli ghith:</b> a werewolf phrasing meaning &quot;to rob&quot; or &quot;to take unlawfully&quot; (it literally means &quot;drag by the neck&quot;, referring to a scavenger dragging away stolen prey)<br /> <b>ganazu:</b> to bow down; to submit; to bend the knee; to become a vassal<br /> <b>bukhuru:</b> a gathering; an assembly<br /> <b>la'a:</b> hanging; to hang<br /> <b>keli la'a:</b> to embrace; to hug tightly; to crash into someone in a tackle-hug; to glomp<br /> <b>shaghu-skir:</b> to lift the head to howl; a howling session carried out by a wolf pack or werewolf pack<br /> <b>hufar:</b> enemy, foe<br /> <b>ghubar:</b> a metal ingot<br /> <b>hubhar:</b> the nape of the neck; neck hairs; hackles<br /> <b>ghubhi:</b> an eel<br /> <b>gubhi:</b> a marsh bird, like an egret<br /> <b>khud:</b> to pounce on; to jump on to attack<br /> <b>gud:</b> an ox; a bull<br /> <b>hudu:</b> the buttocks, hindquarters or flank of an animal<br /> <b>huthu:</b> a tight and sturdy rope meant to restrain or control something, such as a lead rope or tight bonds","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 07-09-2015, 07:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T12:42:57-07:00","id":586360,"title":"","content":"I had a bunch of homonyms written up...but I lost them. So I'm skipping ahead to some shorter homonym-sections because they're quick and easy to do, and because I am tempted to throw something across the room. @_@ So have some i-homonyms for now.<br /> <br /> <b>i:</b> a vocative exclamation in the vein of, &quot;Hey!&quot;<br /> <b>i'i:</b> oil; grease; butter or lard; a fatty substance<br /> <b>ih:</b> the clothing you are wearing<br /> <b>if:</b> to be furious; to curse at someone in anger; an angry insult<br /> <b>ibh:</b> the hips<br /> <b>ib:</b> a job listing; available work<br /> <b>ifsi:</b> the square root of something<br /> <b>ibhzi:</b> to have enough; enough of something; used as an imperative exclamation equivalent to, &quot;Enough!&quot; or, &quot;Stop it!&quot;<br /> <b>ithim:</b> a wild or feral animal<br /> <b>idhim:</b> a serious or important matter<br /> <b>idim:</b> to be slow-witted; to be of low intelligence; simpleton; idiot<br /> <b>itim:</b> a water table<br /> <b>ithu:</b> a gatekeeper; a porter; a doorman<br /> <b>idhu:</b> a room used for ritualistic or cultic purposes<br /> <b>ighi:</b> to be readable; legibility in writing or pictures<br /> <b>ighihal:</b> a wooden sign<br /> <b>ikhingal:</b> a siege weapon<br /> <b>ihihal:</b> an act of wisdom; a decision considered wise<br /> <b>ihisigsikh:</b> jaundice<br /> <b>igidaf:</b> blinkers for an animal<br /> <b>ikhiten:</b> a fraction or portion in mathematics<br /> <b>ihiden:</b> mesh, netting<br /> <b>i'is:</b> seeds; a package or bundle of seeds<br /> <b>il:</b> to raise or carry; a basket being carried<br /> <b>i'il:</b> tax, taxes; a taxman<br /> <b>Ilgu:</b> a Bith Balag who oversees religious rites and sacrifices to Mother Ocean<br /> <b>ilu:</b> a joyful song<br /> <b>i'illu:</b> the religious songs and hymns of the Bith Balag<br /> <b>im:</b> a rain or rainstorm; to run down something in droplets or rivulets","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 08-24-2015, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T14:52:12-07:00","id":587449,"title":"","content":"Hey, Sikla, can I get &quot;dragon&quot; and &quot;opium&quot; (and &quot;Opium Dragons&quot;)? (And maybe this will inspire a new list of words.)<br /> <br /> In this case, by the way, dragon is more in the Eastern context, where they are heavenly beings, not necesarily just big fire-breathing lizards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3855,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","user":"gebbethine","date":". 07-11-2015, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T15:25:25-07:00","id":587464,"title":"","content":"I'd love to have some of my homebrewed tribal names translated, and one of my favorite 40k references as well, as it'd make a good Blood Talon battle cry.<br /> <br /> World-Bearer, Mother Ox, and the phrase: The Crimson Road Before the Iron Fetter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T20:42:15-07:00","id":588804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gebbethine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=587449#post587449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, Sikla, can I get &quot;dragon&quot; and &quot;opium&quot; (and &quot;Opium Dragons&quot;)? (And maybe this will inspire a new list of words.)<br /> <br /> In this case, by the way, dragon is more in the Eastern context, where they are heavenly beings, not necesarily just big fire-breathing lizards.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not Sikla, but I might be able to help out<br /> <br /> For Opium, a reasonably well sourced Wikipedia article claims that the Sumerians used the term &quot;hul gil,&quot; translating it as &quot;joy plant.&quot; Cross-referencing this with the online Sumerian dictionary, &quot;hul&quot; does indeed mean joy, but &quot;gil&quot; seems to mean something more like &quot;treasure.&quot; Regardless, I would go with <b>hul-ghil</b> or <b>hulghil</b> for that one.<br /> <br /> For Dragon, Sikla's dictionary already has a term: <b>mirska</b>, which can also refer to serpents, so it seems appropriate to your needs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T21:38:17-07:00","id":588851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=588804#post588804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Dragon, Sikla's dictionary already has a term: <b>mirska</b>, which can also refer to serpents, so it seems appropriate to your needs.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes sense. Up until relatively recently serpent was the standard name for dragons. Or, if nothing else, variant words for serpent, such as wyrm/worm/wurm. (That was funnier to write out than it had any right to be...)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T00:00:18-07:00","id":588925,"title":"","content":"In point of fact, the Ancient Greek \u03b4\u03c1\u03ac\u03ba\u03c9\u03bd (dr\u00e1k\u014dn), source of the Latin draco, which in turn became the Old French dragon and from there entered English, could mean &quot;serpent&quot; as well as Dragon. It may have originally been an epithet of the mythological Python, as it seems to be related to \u03b4\u03c1\u03b1\u03ba\u03b5\u1fd6\u03bd (<i>drake\u00een</i>), meaning roughly &quot;to see clearly.&quot; Python was associated with the power of prophecy, hence the associated with sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T00:06:36-07:00","id":588928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=588925#post588925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In point of fact, the Ancient Greek \u03b4\u03c1\u03ac\u03ba\u03c9\u03bd (dr\u00e1k\u014dn), source of the Latin draco, which in turn became the Old French dragon and from there entered English, could mean &quot;serpent&quot; as well as Dragon. It may have originally been an epithet of the mythological Python, as it seems to be related to \u03b4\u03c1\u03b1\u03ba\u03b5\u1fd6\u03bd (<i>drake\u00een</i>), meaning roughly &quot;to see clearly.&quot; Python was associated with the power of prophecy, hence the associated with sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, suspected as much, but I'm not at all knowledgable when it comes to ancient Greek.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T11:48:51-07:00","id":602049,"title":"","content":"Hey there Alkis, how have you been?<br /> I have a few name requests for alternative forsaken tribes for you, if you so choose to translate.<br /> <br /> Hell-Eaters<br /> Glass Breakers<br /> Red Kings<br /> Mist Walkers<br /> Border Hunters","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T14:48:06-07:00","id":602277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=602049#post602049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey there Alkis, how have you been?<br /> I have a few name requests for alternative forsaken tribes for you, if you so choose to translate.<br /> <br /> Hell-Eaters<br /> Glass Breakers<br /> Red Kings<br /> Mist Walkers<br /> Border Hunters</div> </div> </div> </div>What are these?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T14:53:00-07:00","id":602283,"title":"","content":"Seemed interesting to me, too. Maybe alternative tribes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T17:09:51-07:00","id":602372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=602277#post602277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What are these?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm glad you asked bud! These are several alternate tribes for the Forsaken that I have been writing, and I am hoping to get the first up here for you guys, the Hell-Eaters ( a tribe dedicated to cleansing Wounds and hunting down Wound-born spirits)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T17:10:40-07:00","id":602374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=602283#post602283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seemed interesting to me, too. Maybe alternative tribes?</div> </div> </div> </div>You are quite correct, good sir.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T18:24:54-07:00","id":602406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=602372#post602372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm glad you asked bud! These are several alternate tribes for the Forsaken that I have been writing, and I am hoping to get the first up here for you guys, the Hell-Eaters ( a tribe dedicated to cleansing Wounds and hunting down Wound-born spirits)</div> </div> </div> </div> Forgive me if this is presumptive, but would you care to give maybe a sentence or two explaining who each of them are? It might help Mr. Alkis with translating them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T22:28:58-07:00","id":602595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=602406#post602406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Forgive me if this is presumptive, but would you care to give maybe a sentence or two explaining who each of them are? It might help Mr. Alkis with translating them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well okay, though I do not believe he actually needs them, but here we go.<br /> <br /> Glass Breakers- hunters who tear down the false belief that technology makes human kind invincible, Shepards of artificial spirits.<br /> Red Kings- Killers of the Pure who seek to create a Forsaken led Uratha Nation.<br /> Mist Walkers- Lore seekers who study the past and the shades of the unquiet dead in order to understand the consequences of the Sundering.<br /> Border Hunters- fanatical worshippers of Urfarah's teachings who mercilessly hunt spirits, Ridden, and Hosts in equal measure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T19:01:07-07:00","id":604388,"title":"","content":"Glass Breakers = Anzahzur<br /> Red Kings = Su Lughal<br /> Mist Walkers = Barsheng Raghabha<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-26T21:20:35-07:00","id":604463,"title":"","content":"And perhaps &quot;Mashninna&quot; for Border Hunters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T19:52:00-07:00","id":605246,"title":"","content":"Thanks kinkster, I like all of them! I wonder if sikla will give his versions too, it would definitely be good for reference. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T18:37:38-07:00","id":607332,"title":"","content":"Young Man, if you see this, I am still working on your generational names. They're proving exceptionally challenging, and I have a bit of writer's block. I promise to get them up as soon as possible, and if I've missed anyone else's translations, please let me know.<br /> <br /> R- and P-homonyms have been finished in this list, as well as a number of other things. I've been working on this for a while.<br /> <br /> <b>amahula: </b>a grandmother (informal term is ama\u2019a)<br /> <b>anusum: </b>Meaning &quot;heavenly serpent&quot;, it is a less specific and more catch-all term for positive serpent-spirits, such as the aforementoned <b>sangrun</b><br /> <b>asa: </b>a child or young individual (informal term, equivalent to &quot;kid&quot;)<br /> <b>asa-er: </b>&quot;kid's tears&quot; \u2014 the act of a werewolf pup killing or lashing out at their parents, siblings, etc. in a fit of Rage<br /> <b>athatha: </b>a grandfather (informal term is ath\u2019a)<br /> <b>awan:</b> inspiration; to inspire; to have a stroke of genius; to have a revelation or a eureka moment; when used as a vocative expression, it is equivalent to the cry of, \u201cEureka!\u201d<br /> <b>aya-er: </b>\u201cfather\u2019s tears\u201d \u2014 the act of a werewolf father killing or lashing out at their children, mate, etc. in a fit of Rage<br /> <b>bahar: </b>a projectile weapon, such as a gun or bow<br /> <b>bakh:</b> breath; to breathe<br /> <b>basazu:</b> disappearance; to disappear; to become invisible, or invisibility itself<br /> <b>be'es:</b> to slice into; to cut into; to carve up meat in preparation for a meal, such as carving a turkey<br /> <b>be'esghi:</b> a marsh rat; a sewer rat<br /> <b>be'esh:</b> a large mouse<br /> <b>besdurzi:</b> descendants, offspring; an offshoot of something<br /> <b>besgi: </b>to line a container or item of storage with something, such as a small chest lined with felt<br /> <b>besh:</b> a fig tree or its fruit<br /> <b>Buremehir: </b>First Tongue as spoken by those unable to express its nuances and inhuman quirks, such as mortal humans<br /> <b>busru:</b> natural protection or shelter; shadow or shade from the sun that is cast by a natural feature, such as a tree or a large rock<br /> <b>bu'u:</b> a fish pond; an aquarium<br /> <b>buzur:</b> a cave; a cavity or nook; a hole in ground or rock<br /> <b>da\u2019esar:</b> the afterlife; to be heavenly or angelic; an afterlife or spiritual paradise<br /> <b>dalan:</b> temporary; to be temporary or passing; of limited use or usefulness<br /> <b>damara: </b>mortal; to be mortal; one\u2019s mortality<br /> <b>fawu: </b>a patrol; to patrol<br /> <b>gabhula:</b> one who is considered unmatched, unopposable, and/or complete and total in their authority over something; the name literally means &quot;to blow out [weaklings like chaff], flood and filter through something&quot;<br /> <b>ginan: </b>an empathic bond, such as that expressed between those of a Bith Balag pod, or the pack bond shared by werewolves thanks to certain gifts, abilities or rites<br /> <b>gorah:</b> hearsay, rumour, gossip; to gossip or spread rumours<br /> <b>Gurihemehir:</b> The mortal languages found in the Flesh.<br /> <b>Hisuremehir: </b>The dialect of First Tongue spoken in the Shadow, and both the first and oldest dialect of First Tongue spoken<br /> <b>Irifamehir: </b>The High Speech language used by Mages.<br /> <b>kharakh:</b> a woman or man of ill repute; one who sleeps around; used among werewolves as a female equivalent to the term <b>zahduluzuk</b><br /> <b>Kharyesh:</b> First Tongue name for the Kerberoi (both singular and plural)<br /> <b>lan:</b> a path or patrol route; directions<br /> <b>marra:</b> extermination; a genocide; to exterminate something<br /> <b>nenyah:</b> babysitting; a babysitter; a nurse or matron; to rear or watch over children<br /> <b>nesu:</b> to be distant; distance; the horizon<br /> <b>nhosas:</b> a catch-all term for energy and its forms, such as kinetic energy, supernatural energy, chemical energy, etc.<br /> <b>pa:</b> a wing or patagia; a branch or frond that resembles a wing<br /> paa: a catch-all term for specialized projectile weapon ammo, such as arrows specifically made to pierce the hide of a nigh-invulnerable Shadow-creature<br /> pa'a: a pouch<br /> padh: to find or discover something; a find, a discovery<br /> pagh: an enclosure for birds or fowl; to cage or capture birds<br /> pakh: to leave something behind; to abandon something<br /> pe'esh: to anoint something; a substance used for anointing<br /> pes: the signs of pregnancy; to show the signs of pregnancy; a pregnant woman's stomach<br /> pesh: a tuft; a crest<br /> pu: the mouth of an inanimate object (like a gargoyle), a manmade feature (such as a well), or a natural feature (such as a cave)<br /> pusur: a call or summons to a place or event; a summoning ritual<br /> pu'u: a cistern or well; a watering hole<br /> ra: to be pure or clear; purity, clarity; clearness<br /> ra'ah: a disease or symptom consisting of fluid in the lungs or respiratory system, such as fluid in the lungs from pneumonia<br /> rah: to flood; to drown or be drowing in some sort of liquid; a death caused by drowning<br /> rak: to kill by strangulation, crushing or beating something to death; to beat or hit something until it breaks<br /> ranan: banishment; exile; to be banished or exiled (<b>galer</b> refers to banishing or exiling a spirit or entity, or banishment in ritualistic terms \u2014 this is more physical banishment)<br /> rig: an animal stall<br /> righ: to donate; a donation<br /> ri'ih: a complaint; to cry, wail or complain about something<br /> rikh: an infusion; to boil something down to liquid<br /> sama'i: Western-style dragons and similar such beings \u2014 more specific than <b>mirska</b>, it refers more to the winged, four legged-dragon or two-legged wyvern Westerners are familiar with<br /> sangrun: Chinese-style dragons and similar such beings<br /> sublu: a water source; the source of a river; the water table or groundwater of a place<br /> tadhesar: the act of finding redemption; to try and reach a heavenly state; to ascend to heaven, or to reach or be accepted into the afterlife; concepts such as Golconda for vampires<br /> tul: architectural features designed after animals, such as statuettes or carvings of fish or wolves<br /> tulgu: effigies or fish or fish-like deities, such as statues dedicated to the Sumerian god Dagon<br /> Urathemehir: The dialect of First Tongue spoken by the Uratha<br /> ururu: comforting words; to comfort someone verbally; a lullaby; to sing a lullaby<br /> var: canine behaviours and body language \u2014 when capitalized as &quot;Var&quot;, it refers to the subtle, canid nuances present in the Uratha dialect of Uremehir, such as posture and the baring of teeth<br /> yabh: equal; equality; to be equal to something or someone<br /> yakor: the smell or scent of someone in the process of dying, described with such terms such as the smell of organs shutting down, fluids stagnating and bowels being released<br /> yaruru: soothing; to soothe; to calm or comfort","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 08-02-2015, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T09:10:09-07:00","id":607975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=607332#post607332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Young Man, if you see this, I am still working on your generational names. They're proving exceptionally challenging, and I have a bit of writer's block. I promise to get them up as soon as possible, and if I've missed anyone else's translations, please let me know.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's okay, take your time. I don't need them right away, still need to get a group together before I can use the translations.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T15:08:51-07:00","id":610015,"title":"","content":"With the Neolithic Eras book coming up on Onyx Path's schedule, I've decided to translate the names of various Proto-Indo-European gods that came about in the early days of man. (They were &quot;born&quot; about a millennium or so after Urfarah, but eh. xD) These gods are the &quot;ancestors&quot;, so to speak, of various Indo-European religions such as the Greek, Celtic and Slavic pantheons. More info on them can be found here: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proto-Indo-European_religion\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proto-...opean_religion</a><br /> <br /> <b>Ulke-Nirfarah:</b> Dy\u0113us Ph't\u0113r, the Sky Father. God of the daytime sky, and lord of the PIE Pantheon. His &quot;descendants&quot; include the Greek Zeus and Roman Jupiter.<br /> <br /> <b>Skurbarag-Ul:</b> Plth'wih', the Broad One. Patroness of wide, flat spaces and the meandering rivers that cross them. Her &quot;descendants&quot; include the Sanskrit Prithvi and Hittite Lelwani.<br /> <br /> <b>Tufuful-Hursakhnir:</b> Perkwunos, the Striker. God of war, thunder and oaken forests. His &quot;descendants&quot; include the slavic Perun and the Norse Fj\u00f6rgyn.<br /> <br /> <b>Setsethah-Egiir:</b> H'eusos, the Dawn. Goddess of the rising sun. Her &quot;descendants&quot; include the Roman Aurora and Greek Eos.<br /> <br /> <b>Duhahu-Shathusa:</b> PriHeh', the Beloved Friend. Goddess of love. Her &quot;descendants&quot; include the Norse Freyja and Frigg.<br /> <br /> <b>Dagukurum-Eresh:</b> Deh'nu, the River. Goddess of the rivers. Her &quot;descendants&quot; include the Welsh D\u00f4n and Irish Danu.<br /> <br /> <b>Abisag-Nazarul:</b> Welnos, the Guardian of Cattle. God of cows. His &quot;descendants&quot; include the Slavic Veles and Latvian Velns.<br /> <br /> <b>Makaf-Adur:</b> H'epom Nepots, Grandson of the Waters. God of water and the sea. His &quot;descendants&quot; include the Roman Neptune and Celtic Nechtan.<br /> <br /> <b>Anmin:</b> the Divine Twins, who take many forms in the Proto-Indo-European myths. Sometimes, they are recognized as the <b>Sisumin</b> (or &quot;Horse Twins&quot;), sons of the Sky Father and brothers of H'eusos \u2014 one is a horse, the other is a boy, or perhaps they can shift back and forth. (Sound familiar?) One is sometimes known as <b>Dhurlu'u</b> (&quot;Mann&quot;, whose descendants are the Germanic Mannus and Norse Mann), and the other is <b>Dhurmin</b> (&quot;Yemi&quot;, whose descendants are the Indic Yama and Norse Ymir). They are also sometimes represented by the Morning and Evening Stars, and in some traditions, accompany their sister as she brings forth the sun.<br /> <br /> <b>Ninuth:</b> Seh'ul, the Sun. While H'eusos is the goddess of the dawn, Sehul is the sun itself, and often recognized as female to the Indo-Europeans. Her descendants include the Roman Sol and Sanskrit Surya.<br /> <br /> <b>Sesiduth:</b> Meh'not, the Moon. While seen as female by many (including the werewolves themselves), the Moon is often seen as a masculine god to the PIE people. His descendants include the Latvian Meness and Norse Mani.<br /> <br /> <b>Su'ba-Ul:</b> Peh'uson, the Shepherd. God of pastoral duties. His descendants include the Greek Pan and Roman Faunus.<br /> <br /> <b>Nammez:</b> the Fates, Triplets of Destiny (singular <b>Nammul</b>). Triple goddesses who oversaw the fates of all in existence. Their &quot;descendants&quot; include the Norse Norns and the Greek Moirai.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 07-31-2015, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T15:25:34-07:00","id":610028,"title":"","content":"Interestingly, the linked wiki page doesn't indicate time periods for the origination of these gods.<br /> <br /> I think they all post date when the Neolithic chapter is set.<br /> <br /> Edit: indeed, a little digging indicates these PIE gods are probably a millennia away still in the time of the chapter <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","user":"Acrozatarim","date":". 07-31-2015, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T16:02:28-07:00","id":610058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=610028#post610028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interestingly, the linked wiki page doesn't indicate time periods for the origination of these gods.<br /> <br /> I think they all post date when the Neolithic chapter is set.<br /> <br /> Edit: indeed, a little digging indicates these PIE gods are probably a millennia away still in the time of the chapter <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>My bad. &gt;.&lt; I'll fix that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T11:15:43-07:00","id":616686,"title":"","content":"The question came up in another thread of what the First Tongue term for Lunacy would be, so I figured I'd qeue up a request for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T01:57:52-07:00","id":617388,"title":"","content":"For Lunacy, I'd go with a simple &quot;Shu-e&quot; or 'Shu-dhum' depending on context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T23:28:53-07:00","id":627302,"title":"","content":"There is a canon translation in 1e: <b>Idigathim</b>. <b>Shu-e</b> or <b>Shu-dhum</b>, however, could be used as a term for Lunacy by other shifters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T23:43:31-07:00","id":627304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=627302#post627302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a canon translation in 1e: <b>Idigathim</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the literal translation for it?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T20:38:07-07:00","id":628189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=627304#post627304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's the literal translation for it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Very roughly, it works out as &quot;the great weakness from the Moon&quot; or &quot;weakness in sight of the Moon&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T17:17:22-07:00","id":629255,"title":"","content":"Random Geist words.<br /> <br /> Yadabhan: The Lower Depths of M:tA<br /> Erihalamku: The Underworld<br /> Irabhu: The Autochthonous Depths of the Underworld (a.k.a. The Upper Reaches)<br /> Ardaru: The Lower Mysteries of the Underworld (a.k.a. Tartarus)<br /> Namushar: A Dead Dominion<br /> Namus-Nir: A Deathlord<br /> Abhigalu: A Psychopomp<br /> Lemnul: A Chthonian<br /> Enhur: A River of the Underworld \u2014 all river names are Enhur (name) in First Tongue<br /> <br /> And the Rivers are:<br /> Hakaran: Acheron, the River of Woe<br /> Gagalal: Qiq-ol-mal, the River of Blood<br /> Khuthuu: Styx, the River of Hate<br /> Khunabu: Hun Hunahpu, the River of Bone Dust<br /> Uzamal: Eriadnos, the River of Amber<br /> Adhgura: Id-Kura, the River of Consumption<br /> Namuzia: Eresh-ki-gala, the River of Dead Seed<br /> Yulmaz: Sinaan, the River of Scorpions<br /> Gu'udhgi: Pishon, the River of Gold<br /> Luhuth: Kohan-Il, the River of Pus<br /> Ghiriluu: Cocytus, the River of Lamentation<br /> Ugu'uk: Phlegethon, the River of Fire<br /> Amyakhi: Hvergelmir, the River of Ice<br /> Ukmazu: Lethe, the River of Memory<br /> Urdhafar: Urdabrunnr, the River of Fate<br /> Ma'uranzi: Anahita, the River of Life","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 08-21-2015, 12:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-16T18:00:13-07:00","id":629336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=627302#post627302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a canon translation in 1e: <b>Idigathim</b>. <b>Shu-e</b> or <b>Shu-dhum</b>, however, could be used as a term for Lunacy by other shifters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah ha! I *knew* there must have been a canon word. I just couldn't find it in the dictionary. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> #failednikinkhim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T11:53:26-07:00","id":631360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=629336#post629336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah ha! I *knew* there must have been a canon word. I just couldn't find it in the dictionary. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> #failednikinkhim.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's okay! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I've had to go back and redo a lot of my own stuff, especially with 2e out. Major props to whomever made <b>urdur</b> canon, though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>irkathi:</b> A politician, leader or other high-ranking figure who illegally or falsely gained their position; a corrupt or illegally-appointed politician<br /> <b>absa:</b> Spirits or beings that are born of or rule over rivers, lakes and other natural water bodies, such as undines or the mythological nixies and mermaids<br /> <b>himar:</b> Spirits or beings that rule over or born of dreams, the imagination and concepts of creativity and divination; the chimera of <i>Changeling: the Dreaming</i><br /> <b>thagani:</b> Spirits that are born of or rule over disease, decay, and other such concepts of sickness<br /> <b>erali:</b> A spirit or totem who will only work with or respond to someone of a certain sex, gender and/or sexual orientation, whether due to preference or due to ban<br /> <b>galisi:</b> Spirits that are born of or rule over purification, healing, and spiritual or physical cleansing or curing, such as the removal of pollution from water<br /> <b>lugiba:</b> A whistleblower; one who exposes corruption or wrongdoing, such as investigative journalist; one who has dedicated their life or job to exposing truth, bringing justice and making people accountable","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 08-18-2015, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T22:33:19-07:00","id":633116,"title":"","content":"<b>zibh:</b> A talen<br /> <b>ilulath:</b> A shapeshifter or werewolf totem (replaces <b>uralath</b>, which now refers, per 2e canon, to wolf-spirits related to werewolf totem broods)<br /> <b>Urihudu:</b> Wolf-bloods that are said to be strongly related to Father/Mother Moon<br /> <b>Idunbhu:</b> Wolf-bloods that are aid to be strongly related to Mother/Father Wolf<br /> <b>Idulathru:</b> Moon Gifts<br /> <b>Urfalathru:</b> Wolf Gifts<br /> <b>Hisilathru:</b> Shadow Gifts<br /> <b>sa'ak:</b> A Facet<br /> <b>Uragalal:</b> Wolf Rites<br /> <b>Duragalal:</b> Pack Rites","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T17:49:00-07:00","id":634074,"title":"","content":"<b>namlugas:</b> the Alarming Alacrity aspect, in which a shifter gains extra speed by the force of their will (lit. &quot;will-speed)<br /> <b>sakhrih:</b> the Carnivore's Puissance aspect, in which a shifter gains Essence by eating the heart of another (lit. &quot;heart-eating&quot;)<br /> <b>adhkhakizal:</b> the Echolocation aspect, in which a shifter is able to navigate or travel by echolocation; echolocation in general (lit. &quot;to track by echoes&quot;)<br /> <b>basazif:</b> the Invisible Mark aspect, in which a shifter is able to leave some sort of unseen trace (such as a scent mark) for another to pick up (lit. &quot;invisible mark&quot;)<br /> <b>anunumamath:</b> the Spirit Animal aspect, in which a shifter calls on a spirit animal to assist one of its skills or abilities; an animal spirit that is not as powerful as a totem, but acts as an aide or guide to a being (such as the spirit companions of some werewolves, or the aforementioned spirit animals of some shifters)<br /> <b>yeh'renigi:</b> the Unsettling Eye aspect, in which a shifter's eyes have an eerie, unsettling cast (lit. &quot;eyes of a fearful aura&quot;)<br /> <b>kensefath:</b> the Cull the Weak Aspect, in which a shifter can instinctively discern who is the weakest in a certain group<br /> <b>uthkaskeer:</b> the Unsettling Cry aspect, in which a shifter creates an unnerving and horrifying cry to frighten others with (lit. &quot;intimidating shriek&quot;)<br /> <b>umaminan:</b> the Feral Collective aspect, in which a shifter can tap into the minds of every animal it shifts into within a certain radius (lit. &quot;beast-bond&quot;)<br /> <b>umagathusa:</b> the Hypnotic Allure aspect, in which the shifter radiates some sort of awe-inspiring or magnetic presence to draw others in (lit. &quot;draw of the beast&quot;)<br /> <b>hithahru:</b> the Parallel Numina aspect, in which a shifter can gain a power similar or like a spirit's Numen<br /> <b>gehannunhia:</b> the War Heart aspect, in which a shifter gains strength every time they are injured<br /> <b>adhkhar:</b> to resound; to echo; an echo or repeated sound<br /> <b>hithahu:</b> a Numen or Numina<br /> <b>wagsa:</b> sepsis, pus; an abscess, blood poisoning; an infection; things such as the bacteria in a komodo dragon's mouth, which cause extreme infection after the lizard bites its prey<br /> <b>mudu'na:</b> a bezoar; the Bezoar merit (lit. &quot;gut-stone&quot;)<br /> <b>geh:</b> A blow; an injury; a wound<br /> <b>namkili:</b> a charm; a talisman<br /> <b>ni-namkili:</b> a prey charm of the Prey Charm merit<br /> <br /> And now, canon breakdowns of each of the shapeshifter form names, plus some new ones I came up with:<br /> <br /> <b>Hishu:</b> The human form, literally meaning &quot;society-scraping shadow&quot;. I'd peg this name as a universal term for the shapeshifter human form.<br /> <b>Dalu:</b> The near-human form, literally meaning &quot;that which is broad&quot;. The name implies a broadening of the features (shoulders, face, frame, etc.) seen in werewolves, but I'd also apply this to other shifters, as they too gain some broad and gangly proportions.<br /> <b>Shatilu:</b> The war form, literally meaning &quot;that which a fight will end with&quot;. The werewolves call this form &quot;Gauru&quot; (lit. &quot;gift of the wolf's maw&quot;), but the term <b>Shatilu</b> is meant to be a universal term shifters use for this form.<br /> <b>Susmamu:</b> The near-beast form, literally meaning &quot;the renowned beast&quot;. The werewolves call this form &quot;Urshul&quot; (lit. &quot;the wolf of younger times&quot;), but the term <b>Susmamu</b> is meant to be a universal term like <b>Shatalu</b>.<br /> <b>Unamu:</b> The beast form, literally meaning &quot;the wild beast&quot;. The werewolves call this form &quot;Urhan&quot; (lit. &quot;the wolf at the door&quot;), but the term <b>Unamu</b> is meant to be another universal term.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 08-22-2015, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T18:20:39-07:00","id":634137,"title":"","content":"And now, various elements and alchemical metals, because why not?<br /> <br /> <b>guk:</b> The neutral, catch-all term for silver<br /> <b>zalaha:</b> Mercury (lit. &quot;silvery/shiny water&quot;)<br /> <b>zakar:</b> a powder or dust<br /> <b>izakar:</b> Sulphur/sulfur (lit. &quot;fire-dust&quot;)<br /> <b>athkal:</b> Copper<br /> <b>a'anna:</b> Tin<br /> <b>ahar:</b> Lead<br /> <b>eghu:</b> Antimony<br /> <b>ashihi:</b> Arsenic<br /> <b>lulana:</b> Bismuth<br /> <b>lukamalu:</b> Boron<br /> <b>mulan-ti:</b> Magnesium<br /> <b>kakbhur:</b> Phosphorus<br /> <b>nuinimki:</b> Platinum<br /> <b>duizia:</b> Potassium<br /> <b>ghi'i-fuluh:</b> Zinc<br /> <b>kithmunn:</b> Sal ammoniac<br /> <b>rihillu:</b> Aqua fortis<br /> <b>nirillu:</b> Aqua regia<br /> <b>zillu:</b> Aqua vitae<br /> <b>zalahadur:</b> Amalgam (mercury/other metal mix)<br /> <b>nuzela-usagh:</b> Sulfates or a sulfate<br /> <b>ghi'i:</b> an alloy<br /> <br /> The alchemical processes and related terms:<br /> <br /> <b>tinigh-shengh:</b> Calcination<br /> <b>tinigh:</b> A calciner<br /> <b>shengh:</b> To heat something in a kiln<br /> <b>takabh:</b> Congelation; to thicken; to congeal<br /> <b>suhiak-uskuf:</b> Fixation; to separate and reform as the same thing or something different<br /> <b>zigh:</b> Dissolution; to dissolve<br /> <b>za'al:</b> Digestion; to digest, to disintegrate, to melt down<br /> <b>sii:</b> Distillation; to distill, to brew<br /> <b>fala-dumu:</b> Sublimation; to sublimate, to become a gas directly from a solid state; to turn into something airy or air itself<br /> <b>me'e:</b> Separation; the chemical process of separation into fractions; to refine something, such as oil<br /> <b>dulalkar:</b> Ceration; to mollify or make wax-like a hard substance by using liquid throughout cooking<br /> <b>lalkar:</b> Wax<br /> <b>kuur:</b> Incineration; to incinerate, to burn wholly<br /> <b>gizim:</b> Fermentation; to ferment, to rot; to make something through the process of fermentation, such as beer or cheese<br /> <b>zaanu:</b> Multiplication; to refine or increase the potency of something by repeating the process that made it, or repeating something done to it<br /> <b>dhiri'ri:</b> Projection; the creation of a Philosopher's Stone; to turn a lesser substance into something greater via magic, alchemy, science, etc.; to turn lead into gold; to perform a miraculous transformation; to ascend or reach a higher state<br /> <br /> And random stuff:<br /> <br /> <b>enthur:</b> navel, belly-button<br /> <b>aranum:</b> a safe used for keeping money; a register; a cashbox<br /> <b>asuhna:</b> saffron<br /> <b>kalubha:</b> partridge or partridges<br /> <b>fithu:</b> a place where a totem, god or other powerful prefers to reside or manifest<br /> <b>thuzia:</b> turquoise or its colour/color<br /> <b>dhamsak:</b> hippopotamus<br /> <b>aba'al:</b> a substitute; to substitute or replace with<br /> <b>huuth:</b> application of something like powder to the skin; rubbing in something; to rub something in or on, such as applying lotion to the skin or a covering to meat<br /> <b>kammu:</b> a stroke; to be paralyzed by a stroke; the effects of a stroke<br /> <b>hasfum:</b> terracotta<br /> <b>huthush:</b> a bridegroom; a male fiance<br /> <b>ehia:</b> a bride; a female fiance<br /> <b>imzug:</b> a worksheet; schoolwork; homework<br /> <b>izku:</b> a fin or flipper<br /> <b>neznaruak:</b> a stela<br /> <b>idkuru:</b> a ladle<br /> <b>ahr:</b> remains of buildings or settlements; ruins; rubble<br /> <b>surr:</b> a plectrum<br /> <b>zakhmug:</b> the beginning of the year; the New Year<br /> <b>zarra:</b> a door pivot<br /> <b>zenzenbhal:</b> a quail","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 08-21-2015, 07:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T05:09:41-07:00","id":634463,"title":"","content":"<b>mug:</b> The catch-all term for a year. The term <b>u-iduth</b> (&quot;gift of the Moon&quot;) is now poetic werewolfy phrasing.<br /> <b>illar:</b> a pointing arrow; an arrow shape<br /> <b>iduu:</b> The non-poetic version of <b>u-iduth</b>, also meaning &quot;year&quot;, and exclusive to werewolves<br /> <b>zer:</b> sunburn; to be sunburnt<br /> <b>ahuhum:</b> a sash; a ribbon<br /> <b>bisirium:</b> a treasured or valuable object; an item of great worth; a treasure or piece of treasure<br /> <b>nushu:</b> leek<br /> <b>iksa:</b> cactus<br /> <b>ziragir:</b> cannibal; cannibalism; to engage in cannibalism<br /> <b>hebri:</b> redemption; to redeem<br /> <b>memedh:</b> to assist in battle; a person or thing that is helpful or helps in battle; a poetic term for reinforcements<br /> <b>nadash:</b> an obsession with defeating a particular individual in combat<br /> <b>basar:</b> a rookie; a greenhorn; fresh meat or new blood<br /> <b>fikh:</b> a state of being in which one is unable to shapeshift out of their current form; to lose the ability to shapeshift<br /> <b>sekedh:</b> to lose one's way in the Shadow; to be lost in the Shadow<br /> <b>be'enu:</b> to make first contact with; first contact with another land, people or being, or the first contact one has had with others in a while<br /> <b>firdan:</b> a discount; a price reduced; to cheapen or reduce the cost of<br /> <b>mebki:</b> to defy the odds; luck or luckiness<br /> <b>dara'i:</b> harshness; to be harsh<br /> <b>dih:</b> softness; to soften; to be soft<br /> <b>zaghul:</b> carnelian (thank CatDoom for coming up with this one <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T07:38:49-07:00","id":634585,"title":"","content":"Some flying terms and flight-related things!<br /> <br /> <b>anninna:</b> fighter plane (lit. &quot;metal hawks&quot;)<br /> <b>pannabis:</b> cargo plane (lit. &quot;ox with metal wings&quot;)<br /> <b>anafasfas:</b> seaplane (lit. &quot;metal duck&quot;)<br /> <b>thuthupa:</b> rotorcraft, such as helicopters (lit. &quot;spinning wings&quot;)<br /> <b>anamusen:</b> plane (lit. &quot;metal bird&quot;)<br /> <b>hirlu:</b> a glider (lit. &quot;that which glides&quot;)<br /> <b>farastuh:</b> a kite (lit. &quot;flying fabric&quot;)<br /> <b>askeer-musenus:</b> catch-all term for a jet, especially large ones like boeings (lit. &quot;screeching bird-killer&quot;)<br /> <b>ba'arask:</b> coleopter (lit. &quot;fan-flier&quot;)<br /> <b>etpa:</b> ornithopter (lit. &quot;flapping wings&quot;)<br /> <b>annaziz:</b> ultralight aircraft (lit. &quot;metal insects&quot;)<br /> <b>kaf-gus:</b> ground effect vehicle (lit. &quot;sea-skinner&quot;)<br /> <br /> And derived terms:<br /> <br /> <b>fasfas:</b> a duck<br /> <b>tuh:</b> a textile; fabric<br /> <b>et:</b> to move up or down; to flap; flapping<br /> <br /> And more random terms;<br /> <br /> <b>gharaan:</b> activism, advocacy; an activist or advocate<br /> <b>zidhuri:</b> moderation, self-control; to take things in moderation<br /> <b>zafidu:</b> a female barkeep; a woman who prepares or serves alcohol<br /> <b>asbir:</b> a host; to host something or be a host to someone<br /> <b>amanth:</b> to be subject to; to subject something or someone to<br /> <b>fanasil:</b> a guerrilla fighter<br /> <b>kandri:</b> a rival or opponent in a challenge or change or leadership, or a political race<br /> <b>elam:</b> the defender or proponent in a challenge or change of leadership, or a political race","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 08-21-2015, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T14:05:42-07:00","id":635053,"title":"","content":"Have some z-homonyms!<br /> <br /> <b>zaa:</b> a gemstone bead, or a bead inlaid with gemstones<br /> <b>za'a:</b> property, estate<br /> <b>zah:</b> a specific person; a person designated for something<br /> <b>zagha:</b> a lead rope; a nose rope, such as one used to lead an ox<br /> <b>za'ah:</b> of a sweet flavour; a sweet disposition or personality<br /> <b>zihku:</b> markings on the liver used by a haruspex to determine omens<br /> <b>za'ak:</b> a piece of jewellery/jewelry; an adornment or decoration to attach to a piece of jewellery/jewelry<br /> <b>zahl:</b> to get up early; to rise with the sun<br /> <b>zaal:</b> the light of the rising sun<br /> <b>zalzal:</b> a person of nobility or noble blood<br /> <b>zalakh:</b> a shiny or polished stone or gemstone<br /> <b>zamzam:</b> a type of instrument that appears to look like and/or mimics the sound of a bird<br /> <b>samsammu:</b> a bird with an exceptionally musical or complex song<br /> <b>zanna:</b> a larva or larvae; a caterpillar<br /> <b>za'ra:</b> to be overtly or excessively concerned; overprotectiveness; anxiousness, great worry<br /> <b>zarah:</b> a braid, plait or overlap of some kind<br /> <b>zaara:</b> overlapping, layered or braided fabric<br /> <b>zarak:</b> a stork or heron<br /> <b>zarakh:</b> grief, grieving; a show of grief, or a public display of grieving<br /> <b>zaza:</b> to bow down; to subjugate oneself<br /> <b>zahza:</b> weak or ill cattle livestock, usually caused by overexertion or lack of proper nourishment<br /> <b>ze:</b> bare dirt; featureless land; an area consisting mostly of dirt, with little to no foliage<br /> <b>zezi:</b> the gall bladder<br /> <b>ma'ardu:</b> bile, vomit, stomach acid<br /> <b>zedha:</b> a piglet<br /> <b>zetha:</b> a bad smell; a stench; a stink<br /> <b>zahek:</b> an unusually large or voracious piglet or baby animal \u2014 the opposite of a runt<br /> <b>zekzul:</b> farm birds, such as barn swallows<br /> <b>zenna:</b> a siege weapon<br /> <b>zena:</b> the rid or midrib of a plant<br /> <b>zii:</b> the chirping of birds<br /> <b>zi'i:</b> to cut, remove or erase something; an eraser or erasing agent such as White-Out<br /> <b>zib:</b> donkey bridle<br /> <b>zi'id:</b> loyalty; to be loyal<br /> <b>zikgu:</b> threshold<br /> <b>zih:</b> town centre<br /> <b>zinal:</b> living, thriving; vitality; to bring or be full of life<br /> <b>zigum:</b> a hostel<br /> <b>zikum:</b> a bright and clear sky<br /> <b>zil:</b> boiling; to boil<br /> <b>zir:</b> defective, broken; a defect<br /> <b>sirthum:</b> an olive or olives; the olive tree<br /> <b>zabhlu:</b> a work team<br /> <b>zis:</b> emmer wheat<br /> <b>zu'u:</b> flint<br /> <b>zuh:</b> shale used for building<br /> <b>zuu:</b> the point of a blade or something sharp, such as a sword, scythe, tool or hoe<br /> <b>subuth:</b> a battle mace<br /> <b>zufuth:</b> a spiny fish<br /> <b>zugasedh:</b> a group or concentration of something (such as forces) for rent<br /> <b>zugesra:</b> mercenary troops<br /> <b>zum:</b> revolution; to revolve<br /> <b>zuhr:</b> roiling, to roil; to break through and churn; to bubble up<br /> <br /> And more random words:<br /> <br /> <b>dhemesh:</b> a border in conflict or question; a gray line or boundary between ideologies, peoples, places, etc.<br /> <b>endam:</b> a widely-held or dominant belief or belief system<br /> <b>amin:</b> among shapeshifters, this refers to the unique, personal scent that surrounds something in existence \u2014 everything that exists has a scent, or a lack thereof, that makes it identifiable to the educated tracker or sniffer<br /> <b>ansa:</b> something used to trap, capture or tap into occult energies or sources<br /> <b>rahar:</b> sibling rivalry; competition among siblings or family members","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 08-21-2015, 11:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T03:05:06-07:00","id":635547,"title":"","content":"<b>Shatalu:</b> The war form, literally meaning &quot;that which a fight <i>starts out</i> with&quot;<br /> <br /> Weren't the Kill Form suposed to be used the last? Like to give the <i>coup d' grace</i>? Maybe it should be something like <i>The form that ends a fight</i>? Which also means that once is adopted, shit got too real.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T05:33:03-07:00","id":635682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=635547#post635547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Shatalu:</b> The war form, literally meaning &quot;that which a fight <i>starts out</i> with&quot;<br /> <br /> Weren't the Kill Form suposed to be used the last? Like to give the <i>coup d' grace</i>? Maybe it should be something like <i>The form that ends a fight</i>? Which also means that once is adopted, shit got too real.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, I'm thinking in Apocalypse terms. Replace that with <b>Shatilu</b>, which means &quot;that which a fight will end with&quot;.<br /> <br /> Edit: More stuff.<br /> <br /> <b>dhusia:</b> quartz<br /> <b>suthan:</b> amber<br /> <b>sagarna:</b> sandstone<br /> <b>zumasna:</b> limestone<br /> <b>hu'ena:</b> sediment, silt<br /> <b>anghalna:</b> marble<br /> <b>athfar:</b> basalt<br /> <b>mesna:</b> obsidian or onyx<br /> <b>galhaku:</b> poor planning; thoughtlessness; to ignore one's common sense in favour of something else, usually resulting in something ending badly<br /> <b>nalgha:</b> forethought, pre-planning; to expect something; preparation, or to be prepared<br /> <b>kuruk:</b> Roughly meaning &quot;to draw out the forgotten&quot;, it refers to those who attempt to bring justice to old crimes or find long-wanted fugitives \u2014 basically a catch-all term for bounty hunters, detectives, and others who pursue cold cases and the like<br /> <b>rennu:</b> the cessation of existence; to be completely forgotten and unknown to others; to be wiped or erased from reality; a retcon","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 08-22-2015, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T16:33:53-07:00","id":638443,"title":"","content":"More i-homonyms. These are now finished!<br /> <br /> <b>i'im:</b> mud; clay<br /> <b>im'ma:</b> the previous year, last year, the year before<br /> <b>immah:</b> the vulva<br /> <b>immal:</b> a wild cow; cows that have gone feral or have been abandoned; an undomesticated cow<br /> <b>im'mal:</b> to be ludicrously wealthy; to have a great deal of livestock or possessions; the 1%<br /> <b>imma:</b> one's facial features<br /> <b>imsu:</b> a small, clay tablet that fits in one's hands, kept for notes or usage; a notepad; one's notes<br /> <b>in:</b> to abuse one's power; abuse of one's position<br /> <b>ihn:</b> a sector<br /> <b>indubh:</b> to delimit; to fix a boundary<br /> <b>inthuf:</b> to insult; an insult, usually made in anger<br /> <b>inimgal:</b> a claim; an entitlement to claim<br /> <b>inimhal:</b> to be eloquent; eloquence<br /> <b>ir:</b> might, mightiness; to be very strong or powerful<br /> <b>irru:</b> a ring, a band; a washer; a peg<br /> <b>i'ir:</b> to plunder; plunder, looting<br /> <b>deldu:</b> a saying or proverb<br /> <b>ihr:</b> an attractive scent; the smell of someone or something in heat/in a breeding cycle<br /> <b>irmanu:</b> apricot; the apricot tree<br /> <b>iri:</b> an important or major city<br /> <b>ir'i:</b> osteoporosis<br /> <b>irri:</b> to be high up; to be elevated<br /> <b>i'ri:</b> the manifestation of a spirit, being or god into the physical world<br /> <b>isim:</b> an aromatic substance; something that causes a pleasing odour<br /> <b>issim:</b> animal fattener; animal feed; to fatten up something<br /> <b>idima:</b> a darkness or shadow considered sacred or mystical<br /> <b>itima:</b> a sanctuary<br /> <b>izigu:</b> a fish with fiery or brilliant scales, or a fish whose colour resembles fire","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T23:13:02-07:00","id":638844,"title":"","content":"<b>na'a:</b> a smoky or hazy silhouette of something; a poetic name for a ghost<br /> <b>na'u:</b> a pestle or pestle-shaped stone<br /> <b>nadheh:</b> incense<br /> <b>natheh:</b> advice; to advise<br /> <b>naghar:</b> a carpenter or joiner<br /> <b>nagharmusen:</b> a woodpecker<br /> <b>nahar:</b> garden plants; ornamental plants<br /> <b>nagha:</b> alkali-rich plants such as potash<br /> <b>naha:</b> mortar<br /> <b>na'am:</b> pre-planned instructions; a course of lessons; a syllabus<br /> <b>naam:</b> a minor title of lordship, equivalent to &quot;duke&quot; or &quot;duchess&quot;<br /> <b>namarum:</b> a reflective or shiny garment; a gaudy or well-decorated garment<br /> <b>namaru:</b> a reflective or glassy surface or