 etc.<br /> bakku: a small biting insect, such as a mosquito or fly<br /> nuh: sperm; masculity, manhood<br /> nuu: to spin thread; the art or act of spinning thread<br /> nugushu: a widow<br /> nukuzu: a door fitting<br /> sumu: alfalfa grass<br /> nummun: the larvae of insects; caterpillars, maggots<br /> nun: fighting, combat<br /> nunnu: a metal object<br /> sa: advice or counselling; gathered intelligence or knowledge<br /> gizzu: a reed-bundle<br /> sah\u2019a: a lexical entry<br /> ze: to equal or be equal to; to be comparable to; to rival or compete with; rivalry, competition<br /> zah\u2019a: adornments, jewellery; to adorn or decorate oneself<br /> ga\u2019lu: roasting, burning; to roast or parch, especially in a cooking sense<br /> sasa: to sting; a sting or stinging sensation<br /> mishlu: the middle or center; to reach the center<br /> thamu: gut, sinew, tendon<br /> ma\u2019adnu: the string of a musical instrument or a bow<br /> fithnu: a catgut string or gutstring<br /> zetu: to capture with a net<br /> sagh: goodness, a good thing; to be good, beautiful, precious<br /> zagh: precious, rare; of a high quality or standard<br /> zikh: to scatter or disperse; to destroy or kill something by throwing it against something else, like breaking a plate by smashing it against a wall<br /> saha: a press; to press something<br /> zakha: reaping; to reap, as in reaping crops or a bounty<br /> sagha: a skirt or kilt<br /> zan: the front or nearmost side of something<br /> sansagh: an important person or place, such as a VIP guest or a capital city<br /> sa\u2019agh: the leader of a foreign country; the leader of a type of government that is not one\u2019s own<br /> zanha: one who purifies the ground or people to be used in a rite or religious ceremony, such as a ritual bath attendant, or someone who smudges<br /> sahk kal: to be leading against, to be opposing; an opposing or attacking force<br /> sahk dhu: to measure out a heaping amount; to be measured in heaping amounts<br /> saghdu: a crown; the very top of one\u2019s head; the top of a hill or building<br /> sandhu: a warp beam on a loom<br /> sahthu: a stone carved into the shape of a head; a terminus or herm in architecture<br /> santhu: a smitten person; one who is in love or smitten<br /> sahhar: an upper millstone; a stone used as or a candidate to be an upper millstone<br /> sahgal: an important stone monument; a marker, mountain or other stone-/land-based landmark or feature of great importance or note<br /> sangeseth: fish on a string; a string or cord used to hang and/or dry fish on<br /> zahgi: cultic rites; rites specific to a certain cult or religious group<br /> sak: a mat<br /> za\u2019akh: playfulness; to be playful<br /> zakar: frosted, freezing; to freeze or chill, to frost over; something that is chilling, terror-inspiring; to strike fear into the hearts of others, to make others\u2019 blood run cold<br /> zakkar: a sponge or other absorbent surface/item that can carry liquid, or is specifically meant to carry/soak up liquid<br /> sakin: a peg<br /> zakin: yeast<br /> zakir: a net for carrying straw, barley, etc.; a haynet<br /> zahi\u2019ir: a mixture of herbs that is burnt or smoked for sacred effect or purposes, such as a form of incense or meditation<br /> sala: a bug-ridden or lousy animal; to be infested with fleas, ticks, lice, etc.; someone who is considered dirty, unclean and/or unhealthy</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 10-11-2015, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T14:01:42-07:00","id":695335,"title":"","content":"As always, amazing work on everything!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T23:37:21-07:00","id":695769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=692672#post692672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wyrdhamster: If you look at the dictionary link in the FT guide linked on the first page (my links aren't working), there are already a bunch of animal names translated. Unless you\u2019re looking for names for the Changing Breeds, as opposed to names for their animal forms?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I look for the First Tounge names for the Breeds itself, <b>not</b> their forms. Things like <b><i>Uratha</i></b>, not <i>Dalu</i> or <i>Gauru</i>.<br /> <br /> I would be glad if you translated basic Breeds from 1ED <b>Changing Breeds</b> book - so Bears, Cats ( best would be division between House Cats, Lions and Tigers ), Crows, Deers, Elks, Dogs, Elephants, Foxes, Horses. Hyenas, Monkeys, Rats, Snakes and Spiders.<br /> <br /> I know it's a lot, but it would much ease mine project to call them the way like <b><i>Uratha</i></b>. Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-10-2015, 02:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T14:03:15-07:00","id":697896,"title":"","content":"Here's the first set of translations, Wyrdhamster:<br /> <br /> <b>Maksuari:</b> Bastet (lit. \u201cgreat wildcats\u201d)<br /> - <b>La-Gulumu:</b> The Bahgrasha (\u201csteadily balanced\u201d)<br /> - <b>Ulkesakhag-Kuk:</b> The Balam (lit. \u201cfangs of the Sky-Heart [Huracan]\u201d)<br /> - <b>Sahsuhaziha:</b> The Bubasti (lit. \u201cthe starving-cursed\u201d)<br /> - <b>Guthemehir-Na\u2019iska:</b> The Cait Sith (lit. \u201cthe honey-tongued tricksters\u201d)<br /> - <b>Guzen-Agzu:</b> The Hatara (lit. \u201cthe golden dangers\u201d)<br /> - <b>Udhuf-Malu:</b> The Klinkerash (lit. \u201cthe charcoal-pelts\u201d)<br /> - <b>Dumag-Ahdha:</b> The Qualm\u2019a Ni (lit. \u201criddles of the wind\u201d)<br /> - <b>Anbes-Nir:</b> The Rajanya (lit. \u201cheaven-blessed rulers\u201d)<br /> <br /> <b>Saragmathag-Ghalkaka:</b> Land Titans (lit. \u201call-powerful giants of dry land\u201d)<br /> - <b>Nimurag-Annunhia:</b> Azubuike (lit. \u201cstrength of the embers\u201d)<br /> - <b>Mekhar-Gushasu:</b> Iravati (lit. \u201cthe quietly greedy\u201d)<br /> - <b>Gazh-Aha:</b> Jhaa (lit. \u201cghostly treasures\u201d)<br /> - <b>Gi\u2019endhu-Hursakh:</b> Mhol\u00e9-Rho (lit. \u201cwalking/moving mountains\u201d)<br /> <br /> <b>Isi\u2019esh-Lugurra:</b> Laughing Strangers (lit. \u201claughing strangers\u201d)<br /> - <b>Eth-Suh:</b> Archunem (lit. \u201cscratching hands\u201d)<br /> - <b>Mebki-Saghbadu:</b> Baitu (lit. \u201cthose who promise luck\u201d)<br /> - <b>Nuthif-Ina-Namushar:</b> Minjur (lit. \u201cthose who are never permitted into the world of the dead\u201d)<br /> - <b>Dhabhariridur:</b> Mistai (lit. \u201cchildren of the Great Trickster\u201d)<br /> - <b>Saghbestha-Husal:</b> Reynardi (lit. \u201coathbound scoundrels\u201d)<br /> - <b>Sissi-Umamu:</b> Wapathemwa (lit. \u201cpale beasts\u201d)<br /> <br /> <b>Elthum-Imria:</b> The Pack (lit. \u201cthe clan of the canines\u201d)<br /> - <b>Wardhu-Thusa:</b> Maerans (lit. \u201cthe faithful friends\u201d)<br /> - <b>Fa\u2019rag-Lisrih:</b> Riantes (lit. \u201cscrap-eaters of the fringe\u201d)<br /> - <b>Shurdaka:</b> Vargr (lit. \u201cthe many forgotten wolves\u201d)<br /> - <b>Kanmasag-Skirdu:</b> Warrigal (lit. \u201cDreamtime singers\u201d)<br /> <br /> <b>Lu\u2019ukhi-U\u2019nu:</b> the Royal Apes (lit. \u201clike man but not\u201d)<br /> - <b>Thim-Yul:</b> Abathakathi (lit. \u201cthose who create poisons\u201d or \u201cthose who weaken with poison\u201d)<br /> - <b>Thallizi-Malu:</b> Tothians (lit. \u201cmanes of brightest fire\u201d)<br /> - <b>Sahk-Lulafunana:</b> Babi-Ahsh (lit. \u201chooded stones\u201d)<br /> - <b>Garinazaru:</b> Hanumani Brahman (lit. \u201ctemple guardians\u201d)<br /> - <b>Kakuf:</b> the Hugranjah (lit. \u201cbig feet\u201d)<br /> - <b>Anluhalag-Kisurahud:</b> the Order of the Luminous Way of Sun Wukong (lit. \u201cthe Heavenly Master\u2019s border warriors\u201d)<br /> <br /> Derived terms:<br /> <b>sissezina:</b> corn (lit. \u201cpale grains\u201d \u2013 \u201ccorn\u201d originally referred to any grain-cereal in PIE)<br /> <b>udhuf:</b> charcoal, coal<br /> <b>Ulkesakh:</b> the Central American god Huracan, also known as the Heart of the Sky<br /> <b>kaka:</b> a giant, a titan; to be excessively huge or great in size<br /> <b>nimur:</b> ashes, embers, glowing coals<br /> <b>isi\u2019esh:</b> laughter, to laugh; joyful crying, or the act of<br /> <b>lugurra:</b> stranger, outsider; a foreign or unknown thing, person or place<br /> <b>husal:</b> a rogue, a ruffian, a scoundrel<br /> <b>sissi:</b> paleness; to be pale<br /> <b>elthum:</b> a vaguer term for a pack of canines or canine-like beings, whether it\u2019s a pack of hunting dogs, a pack of wolves, a group of African hunting dogs, etc.<br /> <b>imria:</b> a clan, a bloodline, a family<br /> <b>lis:</b> crumbs, scraps<br /> <b>Kanmas:</b> the Australian Dreamtime (lit. \u201cgreat holy dream\u201d)<br /> <br /> I apologize that they're not all here. I had to take a break because my eyes were getting fried from staring at the screen too long. @_@","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T20:13:32-07:00","id":700409,"title":"","content":"<b>Cahha-Khazumamu:</b> The Shadow Breeds (lit. \u201chidden beasts of legend\u201d)<br /> - <b>Uthrih-Nir:</b> Cold Kings (lit. \u201csun-drinking lords\u201d)<br /> - <b>Askudh-Aha:</b> Horned Folk (lit. \u201cthose crowned with horns\u201d)<br /> - <b>Sumukh-Bhuryaan:</b> Mendeans (lit. \u201cblack-shadowed teachers\u201d)<br /> - <b>Makaf-Bes:</b> Oceanborn (lit. \u201cocean-blessed\u201d)<br /> - <b>Udhnamga-Illuza:</b> Olutakami (lit. \u201cfuture-swimmers\u201d)<br /> - <b>Illutha-Thun:</b> Riverkin (lit. \u201ctravellers of watery trails\u201d)<br /> - <b>Hu\u2019udh-Ihdar:</b> Kinno\u2019balo (lit. \u201chopping prophets\u201d)<br /> - <b>Namzu-Nuzagsi:</b> Serpentines (lit. \u201cthe limbless wise\u201d)<br /> - <b>Daremehir-Igazalag:</b> M\u00e9lusinae (lit. \u201csplit-tongued charmer\u201d)<br /> - <b>Shar-Ina-Ulke:</b> the Swarm (lit. \u201cmany-in-the-sky\u201d)<br /> - <b>Gulukikhil-Sahsuha:</b> Mimma Lemnua (lit. \u201chunger of the seething night\u201d)<br /> - <b>Adugu-Hursathra:</b> Taurae (lit. \u201cthose of able backbone\u201d)<br /> - <b>Dufimin-Zif:</b> Yumni (lit. \u201cmarked by the whirling storm\u201d)<br /> - <b>Zalasagan-Sidukhazdu:</b> Whiskey Croc (lit. \u201cmoon-warmed cavern-hiders\u201d)<br /> <br /> Derived terms:<br /> <b>udhnamga:</b> the future<br /> <b>illuza:</b> swimming; to swim<br /> <b>hu\u2019udh:</b> jumping; to jump<br /> <br /> Other translations:<br /> <b>innakh:</b> complete and undying love; the concept of a love, whether familial, romantic or friendly, in which a pair or group is so bound that nothing can break such a bond, save maybe death<br /> <b>ha\u2019in:</b> a mark of shame, such as a castigation brand; a hex or jinx, especially one that leaves a visible mark on the sufferer, whether spiritually, mentally or physically; a curse upon one\u2019s bloodline or family; a flaw in one\u2019s aura that suggests some sort of heinous nature, such as a diablerist\u2019s contaminated aura<br /> <b>kaggam:</b> the act of driving an animal or a group of animals into a certain spot, or baiting or luring them, to make them easier to catch or kill<br /> <b>skulgi:</b> to return to a belief thought superior than the current belief system; a regression to an older belief from a newer one<br /> <b>manal:</b> to become or be uninvolved; a lack of involvement in a conflict, debate, disagreement, etc.<br /> <b>abketh:</b> to restore order, to keep the peace<br /> <b>unrah:</b> someone known for being loathsome or spiteful; an unpleasant person, place, being or situation<br /> <b>unrahama:</b> a rude, informal term equivalent to the Danish <i>kaelling</i>, translating as \u201cspiteful mother\u201d \u2013 it refers to a miserable mother who yells at her children, with equivalents being <b>unrahaya</b> (an angry father who keeps yelling at his family) and <b>unrahasa</b> (a bratty kid who doesn\u2019t stop screaming at their parents)<br /> <b>dufuk-thiguth:</b> equivalent to the English \u201cGrammar Nazi\u201d or Finnish \u201cpilkunnussija\u201d (but more scathing, and not nearly as rude), it refers to a person who checks for grammar and punctuation errors to an almost annoying and/or distracting degree<br /> <b>u\u2019segah:</b> a person who asks too many questions (lit. \u201cwondering mouth\u201d)<br /> <b>unrazinna:</b> a building or structure specifically put up to annoy or harass a neighbour, such as a \u201cspite fence\u201d<br /> <b>kilituf rih:</b> to eat past the point of being full because you love the food so much<br /> <b>aransagkkal:</b> weight gained from emotional overeating<br /> <b>a\u2019azameni:</b> an answer that is unrelated to the question that was asked","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T22:22:16-07:00","id":700490,"title":"","content":"Working on a project involving &quot;WereDolphins&quot; and possibly other Cetaceans.<br /> <br /> I would like an appropriate name for their &quot;race&quot; as well as a title for their &quot;progenitor&quot;, the ocean itself.<br /> <br /> I would also ask for Auspice replacements, however, I have yet to decide on an appropriate equivalent that comes in a multiple of five. Same for the Tribes. So I don't exactly need support for that right now.<br /> <br /> Thank you for your expertise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 10-14-2015, 01:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T04:18:54-07:00","id":700638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=700490#post700490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Working on a project involving &quot;WereDolphins&quot; and possibly other Cetaceans.<br /> <br /> I would like an appropriate name for their &quot;race&quot; as well as a title for their &quot;progenitor&quot;, the ocean itself.<br /> <br /> I would also ask for Auspice replacements, however, I have yet to decide on an appropriate equivalent that comes in a multiple of five. Same for the Tribes. So I don't exactly need support for that right now.<br /> <br /> Thank you for your expertise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any particular gender for the ocean-deity? As for the werecetaceans, first things that comes to mind is <b>Bhurudur</b>, or &quot;children of the deep&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14