e\"><br /> Haha, I wish! No, it's just a fan thing. I love the Mokol\u00e9 enough that I have an idea for how to bring them back in <b>Forsaken </b>terms, using the Neolithic as a basis.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you make this canon, I will squee so hard....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T20:52:09-07:00","id":709893,"title":"","content":"I have no ability to make it canon, but I do intend to write up a full document, if that helps?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T22:01:07-07:00","id":709957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=709893#post709893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no ability to make it canon, but I do intend to write up a full document, if that helps?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes Please! Thank You, thank you!<br /> <br /> That would be much appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T11:08:36-07:00","id":710963,"title":"","content":"Some M:tA terms!<br /> <br /> <b>Hurlul:</b> the Lie (lit. &quot;the collective lie&quot;)<br /> <b>mawaru:</b> Disbelief (lit. &quot;the great denial&quot;)<br /> <b>Yagekenag-Sertha:</b> Paradox (lit. &quot;Abyssal punishment&quot;)<br /> <b>suhusamm:</b> a Backlash form of Paradox (lit. &quot;pain-price&quot;)<br /> <b>thafala:</b> a Havoc form of Paradox (lit. &quot;a sudden, overwhelming change&quot;)<br /> <b>ummagurim:</b> a Bedlam form of Paradox (lit. &quot;witch's madness&quot;)<br /> <b>harmathabur:</b> an Anomaly form of Paradox (lit. &quot;reality break&quot;)<br /> <b>viruhk-zif:</b> a Branding form of Paradox (lit. &quot;mark of corruption&quot;)<br /> <b>Khamkur:</b> a Manifestation form of Paradox (lit. &quot;intruder&quot;)<br /> <b>gul'umu:</b> the Effect of a Mage's power<br /> <b>Ananshah:</b> the theoretical Empyrean<br /> <b>Namusizi-Ah:</b> the Exile (lit. &quot;time of the dying fires&quot;)<br /> <b>Ehanubhda-Eresh:</b> the Exarch known as the Eye (lit. &quot;the queen who watches the four corners of the world<br /> <b>Thirik-Harmatha:</b> the Fallen World<br /> <b>Lulthahu-Zahigi:</b> a False Awakening<br /> <b>Thuguth-Nir:</b> the Exarch known as the Father (lit. &quot;the all-judging king&quot;)<br /> <b>zus:</b> to sink; sinking<br /> <b>khugh:</b> a seal; to seal away<br /> <b>anubtha:</b> a crossroads<br /> <b>anubhda:</b> the four cardinal directions; the four corners of a geometric figure such as a square, a rectangle, etc.<br /> <b>Irifadhag-Zus Hafal:</b> the First Wizards' War (lit. &quot;the war that sunk Atlantis&quot;)<br /> <b>Anubtha-Khugh:</b> the Exarch known as the Gate (lit. &quot;the seal of the crossroads&quot;)<br /> <b>hissumma:</b> a Ghost Mage<br /> <b>me'de:</b> a Glyph","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 10-20-2015, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T13:27:10-07:00","id":711185,"title":"","content":"You're doing such a wonderful work ! I'm amazed ! (you're the main reason I decided to create an account here I must admit, haha xD)<br /> So... I have a request for a sentence. It might seem a bit &quot;harcore&quot;... But, what could be the translation for : &quot;Step aside or I will bite your balls off.&quot; ? :3<br /> Also, is there a word to talk about a werewolf that is fighting his/her true nature ? <br /> <br /> Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8681-bluehilde","name":"Bluehilde","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T13:56:11-07:00","id":711206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluehilde</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=711185#post711185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're doing such a wonderful work ! I'm amazed ! (you're the main reason I decided to create an account here I must admit, haha xD)<br /> So... I have a request for a sentence. It might seem a bit &quot;harcore&quot;... But, what could be the translation for : &quot;Step aside or I will bite your balls off.&quot; ? :3<br /> Also, is there a word to talk about a werewolf that is fighting his/her true nature ?<br /> <br /> Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hehe, thank you! ^.^<br /> <br /> Nah, that translation shouldn't be too hard, I just need to figure out the syntax. As for a werewolf fighting his or her true nature, I think I <i>did</i> have something for that...could you be more specific on the nature of the fight? For example, are they clinging to human beliefs and habits in an attempt to make their true nature &quot;go away&quot;?<br /> <br /> Edit: Fixed words in the list. <b>Medeh</b> should be spelt <b>me'de. Khug </b>was supposed to be <b>khugh</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 10-20-2015, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T13:59:07-07:00","id":711209,"title":"","content":"Awesome ! thanks !<br /> As for the &quot;fight&quot;, yes, it's about them clinging to human beliefs indeed. (However, the other option seems interresting too ! I'll check in case you've found something already for it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8681-bluehilde","name":"Bluehilde","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T14:09:57-07:00","id":711219,"title":"","content":"Here we are!<br /> <br /> First, we have <b>gitsur</b>: &quot;Anthropocentric wolf, anthropocentrism; the werewolf condition in which one is uncomfortable being a wolf, and prefers to work in their human forms&quot;. Then we have <b>sa'ath</b>, which a name for<span style=\"font-family:arial\"> Banish the Beast Derangement from Changing Breeds, in which a shapeshifter represses their bestial nature so thoroughly, it is very difficult to shapeshift into it. Then there's the disturbing condition known as </span><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\">umamutag-sahaz</span></b><span style=\"font-family:arial\">, or the </span><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The Hunter King Derangement, in which a shapeshifter hates their animal side so much, it manifests as the serial killing and/or abuse of animals. The milder form of this is </span><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\">zatharzemmul</span></b><span style=\"font-family:arial\">, or the </span><span style=\"font-family:arial\">the Filthy Brutes! Derangement, in a shapechanger abuses animals as a way of lashing out at themselves or their shapeshifter side. Then there is <b>Gurihal nirih</b>, which means &quot;</span><span style=\"font-family:arial\">one who hates, fears or avoids the Shadow; Shadow aversion&quot;.<br /> <br /> Do any of these sound like your guy? If not, I'll work on something. I just realized I haven't finished translating all the Derangements yet in WoD. &gt;.&gt;;</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T14:22:40-07:00","id":711235,"title":"","content":"I thought gurihal referred to the material world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T14:26:43-07:00","id":711241,"title":"","content":"The one about the Hunter King Derangement is totally my guy ! You nailed it, haha :')<br /> Also, the first one works for another character I know, so it's awesome \u00b0w\u00b0<br /> <br /> (Hope you manage to do all the Derangements then ! Sounds tiring \u00b0_\u00b0)<br /> <br /> EDIT : &quot;material&quot; as a shadow under our feet and not the &quot;Shadows&quot; with a capital S ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8681-bluehilde","user":"Bluehilde","date":". 10-20-2015, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8681-bluehilde","name":"Bluehilde","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T17:32:06-07:00","id":711476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=711235#post711235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought gurihal referred to the material world?</div> </div> </div> </div>Its literal translation is &quot;worries of the Flesh&quot;. The spirits first used it in a sort-of-derogative way to refer to spiritual beings who are &quot;too comfortable&quot; with the <b>Gurihal</b>, and its usage drifted from there. It's kind of like how &quot;nerd&quot; used to be a bit meaner than it is now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluehilde</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=711241#post711241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one about the Hunter King Derangement is totally my guy ! You nailed it, haha :')<br /> Also, the first one works for another character I know, so it's awesome \u00b0w\u00b0<br /> <br /> (Hope you manage to do all the Derangements then ! Sounds tiring \u00b0_\u00b0)<br /> <br /> EDIT : &quot;material&quot; as a shadow under our feet and not the &quot;Shadows&quot; with a capital S ?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Shadow&quot; as in the spirit world, the <b>Hisil</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T18:03:33-07:00","id":711513,"title":"","content":"Huh cool. They gotta use the term gurihal more, calling it the 'real world' doesn't seem accurate, and especially doesn't seem like something werewolves would do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T23:21:55-07:00","id":711889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=711513#post711513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh cool. They gotta use the term gurihal more, calling it the 'real world' doesn't seem accurate, and especially doesn't seem like something werewolves would do.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a <i>bunch</i> of canon terms that were never used, or mentioned only once. When was the last time you read things like <b>muhil kasha</b>, <b>lama</b>, and <b>ithagihi</b> in more than one book, or at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T09:59:22-07:00","id":712611,"title":"","content":"A bunch of random translations that piled up in my files. They include the start of the L-homonyms.<br /> <br /> <b>pataaku me'de:</b> Illumination-style Glyphs<br /> <b>zarah me'de:</b> Palimpsest-style Glyphs<br /> <b>sar'e me'de:</b> Vulgar-style glyphs<br /> <b>sar'e:</b> a mixture of something; to mix or combine something<br /> <b>luga:</b> sin; to sin<br /> <b>zilugath:</b> a Goetic demon (lit. &quot;living sin&quot;)<br /> <b>lugakana alal:</b> Goetia (lit. &quot;sin-summoning rites&quot;)<br /> <b>Antha:</b> Golden Road (lit. &quot;road to heaven&quot;)<br /> <b>Anthar:</b> a Wending, or Golden Road left by an archmage that has become unstable<br /> <b>la\u2019a:</b> flooding, floodwaters<br /> <b>laal:</b> stretching, hanging; suspension, a suspended state; to be hanging or suspended; to stretch out<br /> <b>lagha:</b> dry, scaly and/or diseased skin; conditions such as psoriasis or eczema<br /> <b>lakha:</b> a criminal; a tomb robber, plunderer or burglar<br /> <b>laggha:</b> a term considered more polite for the female genitals, such as how \u201clady bits\u201d or \u201clady parts\u201d may be used in euphemism to them<br /> <b>laghaf:</b> a tree stump<br /> <b>lahab:</b> a legal notice, such as a notice of debt or eviction<br /> <b>lahabh:</b> excess, excessiveness<br /> <b>lagaf:</b> railing, fencing<br /> <b>lahabh-musen:</b> an excessively noisy bird<br /> <b>lah: </b>rotting clothing or pelts; moth-eaten clothes; hair or skin on animals attacked by parasites or disease<br /> <b>la\u2019ak:</b> to bring a lot of; to bring many; used in reference to many beings bringing something, or many things being brought<br /> <b>lakh: </b>drying, dry; to dry out<br /> <b>lakan: </b>a bottle or flask<br /> <b>laak:</b> a male goat, a billy goat<br /> <b>la\u2019ag:</b> an animal raised and/or used for meat, or the flesh of such an animal<br /> <b>la\u2019al: </b>a minor or lesser priest<br /> <br /> <b>zi\u2019i:</b> drunkenness; to be drunk, intoxicated, under the influence<br /> <b>gissar-ibru:</b> compost, fertilizer (lit. \u201crations for the fields\u201d)<br /> <br /> <b>thu\u2019shia:</b> a crystal<br /> <b>ket ahana:</b> pearl (lit. &quot;shellfish treasure-stone&quot;)<br /> <b>aha suhum:</b> abalone (lit. &quot;treasure shell&quot;)<br /> <b>hikaon-uhurdur:</b> aegerine/acmite (lit. &quot;black daggers&quot;)<br /> <b>zufa:</b> agate<br /> <b>kafla'a-zufa:</b> blue lace agate (lit. &quot;sea-flooded agate&quot;)<br /> <b>izi-zufa:</b> fire agate (lit. &quot;fiery/burning agate&quot;)<br /> <b>fir nisik:</b> amazonite (lit. &quot;shattering green&quot;)<br /> <b>duksium-zi\u2019i:</b> amethyst (lit. \u201cprotector of the drunk\u201d)<br /> <b>abis-sulu:</b> ammolite (lit. \u201cbuffalo lure\u201d)<br /> <b>anna-thu\u2019shia:</b> metal-coated crystals such as rainbow quartz (lit. \u201cmetal-crystals\u201d)<br /> <b>hikaon anzah:</b> obsidian (lit. \u201cblack glass\u201d)<br /> <b>hikaon er:</b> Apache tears (lit. \u201cblack tears\u201d)<br /> <b>gissar-ibru\u2019shia:</b> apatite (lit. \u201cfertilizer crystal\u201d)<br /> <b>thirik-udhkasagan:</b> apophyllite (lit. \u201cdisintegrates [flakes off] when hot\u201d)<br /> <b>kafillu-na:</b> aquamarine (lit. \u201cseawater stone\u201d)<br /> <b>degirumsar-dunfath:</b> mica (lit. \u201cnearly-perfect pieces\u201d)<br /> <b>degirumsar-ansar:</b> biotite (lit. \u201cnearly perfect iron\u201d)<br /> <b>mutherna:</b> bloodstone (lit. \u201cbloody tears stone\u201d)<br /> <br /> This also includes a number system. As number systems spirits war for control across the world, the spirits that embody each number fight for their independence, and spirits of concepts like halves and thirds seem near-insane sometimes. The first 29 numbers have managed to hold onto their independence, but anything after 30 falls under the base ten number's influence...in some areas. Sometimes, it's in name only. As for why there are only sixty numbers translated, that's because the concept of sixty numbers (plus the numbers for 100 and 1000) are the only ones that survived an all-out spiritual war, having subdued the existence of other numbers to make them fall under their purview. In order to say anything past 60, you have to phrase it as a math problem \u2014 for example, &quot;60 plus 10&quot; instead of saying &quot;70&quot;.<br /> <br /> The exceptions to this are the numbers above 1000. The 1000+ spirits are capricious and powerful, known for tricks such as breaking themselves into tiny pieces to escape, reforming elsewhere as a series of swirling motes. Others flood their attackers with hundreds of mathematical equations at a time, shorting out their brains with strings of complex algebra. They refused to be named, as a name gives power and ties them down, and must be summoned or called for with a (poetic) math equation. Asking for a spirit of the number 2000 would be in kenning form, with lines such as, &quot;I beseech the help of the Glorious Thousand-Times-Twice, That Which Is Greater In Double than Thousand, the Hundreds-Mote Lord of Two-Oh-Oh-Oh.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then you get to the spirits that represent millions and more. As the brains of Earthly creatures can only conceptualize up to a certain amount of something, spirits that reach a million or more become increasingly bizarre and alien. The big numbers reach near-Celestine levels of power, and as numbers get bigger, it gets harder and harder to tell if some numbers <i>are</i> Celestines. The bigger numbers are also rarer in number of brood, as they absorb any number spirits nearby to retain their immense, numerical power. Asking for their help isn't wise, but if necessary, they will demand hefty sacrifices and the loss of much. They're the bigwigs, after all.<br /> <br /> Spirits are freaking <i>weird</i>.<br /> <br /> nas - 0<br /> as - 1<br /> min - 2<br /> pesk - 3<br /> limu - 4<br /> ya - 5<br /> a'ask - 6<br /> emin - 7<br /> ussu - 8<br /> ilimmu - 9<br /> uthuli - 10<br /> namu - 11<br /> iskden - 12<br /> sina - 13<br /> dagsu - 14<br /> lem'mu - 15<br /> ashk - 16<br /> imman - 17<br /> samaned - 18<br /> elem'u - 19<br /> nish - 20<br /> es'dha - 21<br /> shena - 22<br /> salas - 23<br /> lemuu - 24<br /> hansad - 25<br /> sa - 26<br /> immin - 27<br /> shamaeth - 28<br /> ilem - 29<br /> ba - 30<br /> baas - 31<br /> bamin - 32<br /> bapesk - 33<br /> balimu - 34<br /> baya - 35<br /> ba'ask - 36<br /> bemin - 37<br /> bussu - 38<br /> bailimmu - 39<br /> nishdur - 40<br /> nishdunamu - 41<br /> nishiskden - 42<br /> nisina - 43<br /> nishdagsu - 44<br /> nishlem'mu - 45<br /> nishashk - 46<br /> nishimenn - 47<br /> nisamaned - 48<br /> nishelem'u - 49<br /> me'adur - 50<br /> mesdha - 51<br /> me'shena - 52<br /> me'salas - 53<br /> me'lemuu - 54<br /> me'hansad - 55<br /> mesa - 56<br /> me'immin - 57<br /> me'shamaeth - 58<br /> me'ilem - 59<br /> badur - 60<br /> meyadu - 100<br /> ikhi - 1000","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 11-09-2015, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T10:56:57-07:00","id":712712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=711889#post711889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a <i>bunch</i> of canon terms that were never used, or mentioned only once. When was the last time you read things like <b>muhil kasha</b>, <b>lama</b>, and <b>ithagihi</b> in more than one book, or at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I had to look those up. But still, using gurihal would save a lot of trouble explaining the direction.<br /> <br /> Is lama just for 'female' spirits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T12:58:22-07:00","id":712920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=712712#post712712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I had to look those up. But still, using gurihal would save a lot of trouble explaining the direction.<br /> <br /> Is lama just for 'female' spirits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Any spirit that identifies itself as female is a <b>lama</b>, though I believe that heavily female-oriented concepts (such as a spirit of female fertility or menustration) would also count as <b>lama</b>. Like IRL, if a spirit responds to a certain pronoun, you use that identity for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T14:04:37-07:00","id":712996,"title":"","content":"Hey, Sikla. I don't know how updated the spreadsheet dictionary is. Is everything up to day with all the latest stuff you've posted here?<br /> <br /> In any case, can I get a translation for &quot;Iceberg&quot;? Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T14:24:53-07:00","id":713017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gebbethine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=712996#post712996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, Sikla. I don't know how updated the spreadsheet dictionary is. Is everything up to day with all the latest stuff you've posted here?<br /> <br /> In any case, can I get a translation for &quot;Iceberg&quot;? Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's somewhat out of date. It hasn't been updated since July.<br /> <br /> As for an iceberg, that would be <b>skekhmatha-ina-makaf</b>, &quot;ice-land in the sea&quot;. An ice sheet is <b>skekhmatha</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T16:59:32-07:00","id":713201,"title":"","content":"Hrm. Interesting. Any shorter version of iceberg? I'm thinking of a deed name and don't really want a long one. I guess 'Skekhmatha' would be okay, if it's 'ice-land'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T17:40:52-07:00","id":713312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gebbethine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=713201#post713201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hrm. Interesting. Any shorter version of iceberg? I'm thinking of a deed name and don't really want a long one. I guess 'Skekhmatha' would be okay, if it's 'ice-land'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, here's a better one: <b>thun skekh</b>, &quot;travelling ice&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T22:11:27-07:00","id":713699,"title":"","content":"Because I was bored, the old, pre-fall battle cry for the World Eaters:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Ningsufaghiringu namfarsilarathra </b>\u2013 &quot;The Crimson Road before the Iron Fetter,&quot; lit: &quot;my bloody path before I serve in iron.&quot; I like the rhythm to it. You can hear the contempt. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":". 10-22-2015, 01:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T22:28:21-07:00","id":713733,"title":"","content":"Nice job! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Great to see other people trying a hand at translation!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T13:34:21-07:00","id":715331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=713312#post713312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, here's a better one: <b>thun skekh</b>, &quot;travelling ice&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hrm. I'm more going for the &quot;iceberg theory&quot; reference; what's the word for 'hidden' or 'secret'? 'Hidden/secret ice' would be great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3855,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","user":"gebbethine","date":". 10-22-2015, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T23:18:06-07:00","id":721990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gebbethine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=715331#post715331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hrm. I'm more going for the &quot;iceberg theory&quot; reference; what's the word for 'hidden' or 'secret'? 'Hidden/secret ice' would be great.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be <b>khaz-skekh.</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T09:45:27-07:00","id":723411,"title":"","content":"Thanks! Much appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T10:06:40-07:00","id":738719,"title":"","content":"Okay, guys, quick question: do you guys like the look of the translations so far? Does everything seem like it still fits with the Proto-Sumerian theme, but also has enough of an Indo-European vibe that it fits being an offshoot of Proto-Indo-European?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T20:15:05-07:00","id":740706,"title":"","content":"I do. I'm not a linguist or nothin, I don't parlez vous non francais or habla espanol, well, un poco nada mas. Reading it, it seems like Klingon, to me. Not knowing what Klingon actually looks like, I'm just referring to a more guttural tone, with a lot of hard syllables but actually saying the words seems more like a regular language and not 'made up fantasy beast language,' which is really cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T09:40:57-07:00","id":744628,"title":"","content":"Minor correction:<br /> <br /> - <b>Mus</b> has been mis-translated. It's current definition actually is the definition of <b>halhala</b>. <b>Mus</b> instead means &quot;holy or sacred; a sacred place&quot;.<br /> - <b>Ahr</b> (meanng rubble, ruin) should instead be <b>ar</b>.<br /> - <b>Lal</b> is now one of the very rare homonyms in First Tongue; in addition to meaning &quot;small, tiny, minuscule&quot;, it also means &quot;show, reveal, display; to show, to display, to reveal&quot;. It differs from <b>la</b> in that <b>la</b> refers to more showing off something to be checked, measured or kept an eye on, while <b>lal</b> means to reveal something or show something off. It has a bit of a, &quot;Ta-da!&quot; quality to it in some contexts.<br /> - <b>K'kir</b> no longer means to be proud of something, or take pride of something in a good way, like being confident. <b>Sarae</b> does (see following post).<br /> <br /> And stuff I need to finish on:<br /> <br /> - The building part wordlist<br /> - All the derangements<br /> - Some more Mage vocab<br /> - The L-homonyms<br /> - The S-homonyms<br /> - The individual wordlists for WAtP shapeshifter cultures<br /> - The spices wordlist<br /> - The gemstone wordlist I had picked out (which I now need to find again) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> - Compling canon words<br /> - The names of the Changing Breeds in First Tongue","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 11-01-2015, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T08:45:26-08:00","id":746699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=744628#post744628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Minor correction:<br /> - The building part wordlist<br /> - All the derangements<br /> - Some more Mage vocab<br /> - The L-homonyms<br /> - The S-homonyms<br /> - The individual wordlists for WAtP shapeshifter cultures<br /> - The spices wordlist<br /> - The gemstone wordlist I had picked out (which I now need to find again) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> - Compling canon words<br /> - The names of the Changing Breeds in First Tongue</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget my generation names, if you're still working on them. It's okay if you couldn't come up with names for them, I get that concepts as broad as everyone born in a certain time period and the characteristics they share might be hard to translate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T09:14:01-08:00","id":746755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=746699#post746699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't forget my generation names, if you're still working on them. It's okay if you couldn't come up with names for them, I get that concepts as broad as everyone born in a certain time period and the characteristics they share might be hard to translate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honest to god forgot. o__o Can you link back to the Wiki page where the generation names were listed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T09:42:45-08:00","id":746853,"title":"","content":"Some s-homonyms, particularly of the word <b>sar</b> \u2013 that word\u2019s got multiple homonyms in-canon, so let\u2019s see if we can\u2019t make a few variations to make it less homonym-prone:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>sa\u2019ar:</b> garden plot; an area used or set aside for gardening or growing plants<br /> <b>sarra:</b> to shave; the act of shaving or the shavings that are remnant<br /> <b>sare:</b> smoking; to smoke something<br /> <b>sarae:</b> to gussy up, to make splendid, to decorate or make something lavish; to be proud of something, to take pride in something; confidence, high self-esteem, the good form of pride<br /> <b>shara:</b> slaughter, slaughtering; to slaughter something, like slaughtering an animal<br /> <b>sharah:</b> leather, bovine hide<br /> <b>zar\u2019e:</b> to mix something up; to confuse something for something else<br /> <b>sharu:</b> slander; to slander </div> </div> </div>Gemstones (and derived terms):<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>suhum-thu\u2019shia:</b> calcite (lit. \u201cshell-crystal\u201d)<br /> <b>ulke\u2019na:</b> celestine/celestite (lit. \u201csky-stone\u201d)<br /> <b>lalkar amahana:</b> chalcedony (lit. \u201cwaxy mother-stone\u201d)<br /> <b>athkal-duhu:</b> chalcopyrite (lit. \u201ccopper-carrier\u201d)<br /> <b>dagukurumu:</b> charoite (lit. \u201cgift of the river\u201d)<br /> <b>sehin:</b> glue<br /> <b>guzenag-ulkefarsehin:</b> chrysocolla (lit. \u201cgold\u2019s blue glue\u201d)<br /> <b>dufath\u2019na:</b> diamond (lit. \u201cthe enduring stone\u201d)<br /> <b>suhumdur\u2019na:</b> dolomite (lit. \u201cthe shell-born stone\u201d)<br /> <b>nisik\u2019na:</b> emerald (lit. \u201cthe green stone\u201d) </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T09:52:43-08:00","id":761560,"title":"","content":"<b>thispu:</b> syrup, honey; jello, pudding; a viscous or sweet substance that is edible<br /> <b>lal'gar:</b> catch-all term for underground water or water sources; used as a slang term for the Rivers in the Underworld<br /> <b>lam:</b> cutting, slicing; the action of cutting or slicing, such as using a scythe to cut crops<br /> <b>lamm:</b> flourishing, plentiful, abundant; to be full of life<br /> <b>la'am:</b> a sapling<br /> <b>larak:</b> childbirth difficulties; a stillbirth, a miscarriage; to die from childbirth<br /> <b>larag:</b> a yoke or harness<br /> <b>li:</b> a branch or twig<br /> <b>furasu:</b> a juniper<br /> <b>rukku:</b> to press or extract something, such as oil or wine<br /> <b>libh:</b> to be absent; to be dazed<br /> <b>iudhu:</b> fat or lard; a fattened-up animal<br /> <b>lif:</b> the heart, the circulatory system; the innermost vital organs<br /> <b>libli:</b> rich, well-off; high quality; to be happy with one's finances<br /> <b>lilu:</b> a fool; an idiot<br /> <b>lila:</b> a ghostly wind or breeze; a ghostly chill; the presence of spirit<br /> <b>li'il:</b> hypothermia, low body temperature<br /> <b>lup:</b> a turnip<br /> <b>luf:</b> a bag used for storage<br /> <b>lubh:</b> catch-all term for saltwater-living fish<br /> <b>lupi:</b> an axe made out of metal, such as a metal hatchet","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T11:18:40-08:00","id":761620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=746755#post746755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I honest to god forgot. o__o Can you link back to the Wiki page where the generation names were listed?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strauss%E2%80%93Howe_generational_theory\" target=\"_blank\">Here you go.</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 11-09-2015, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T10:34:35-08:00","id":769386,"title":"","content":"All the L-homonyms are done. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>nahdazum:</b> a Hallow<br /> <b>Shaghuhiak-Irifadh:</b> Hieraconis, the fabled new Atlantis (lit. &quot;The High City that Will Rise Again&quot;)<br /> <b>Anbesumma:</b> the Hieromagus, the prophecized most perfect of mages<br /> <b>Lul-Anumma:</b> a false Hieromagus<br /> <b>Sidukzi:</b> a Hollow One<br /> <b>Zaanyathi-Kuthim:</b> Imps, the Demons of Pandemonium<br /> <b>nihumlul:</b> to cheat; cheating<br /> <b>Namus-Nihumluldu:</b> a Lich<br /> <b>Sun-Sahfala:</b> The Locust-Eaters (lit. &quot;those who humbly disagree&quot;)<br /> <b>sahfala:</b> to disagree; to argue against; to rebel; to shake one's head no<br /> <b>Yagekemehir:</b> Low Tongue, the language of the Abyss<br /> <b>Ustegurim:</b> the Mad, walking vortexes of magical destruction as a result of a broken soul<br /> <b>Arath-Dam:</b> a Methodology<br /> <b>Difala-Namtar:</b> the Moirae (singular Moira), manifest beings of Fate from Arcadia (and possibly the True Fae)<br /> <b>fathah:</b> the future; future times<br /> <b>askah:</b> the present; present times<br /> <b>Fathah-I'ar:</b> The Nameless that became the Free Council<br /> <b>Fath-I'arag Hafal:</b> the Nameless War<br /> <b>Heshe-Hithim:</b> The Exarch known as the Nemesis (lit. &quot;that which holds back the spirits&quot;)<br /> <b>zukumma:</b> an Occulted Mage (a mage with the Occulation merit)<br /> <b>erpetu-zuk:</b> the power of Occultation itself<br /> <b>su'us dunfath:</b> an Ochemata<br /> <b>Sumukhmuth-Makaf:</b> the Ocean of Oroboros<br /> <b>Nazaru-Bhelu'du:</b> the dragon that dissolved into the Ocean of Oroboros<br /> <b>Namzutha:</b> a Path<br /> <b>Atag-Namuztha:</b> Path of Thistle, the way to the Watchtower of the Lunargent Thorn<br /> <b>Athi Kuthag-Namzutha:</b> Path of Scourging, the way to the Watchtower of the Iron Gauntlet<br /> <b>Zalnamtarag-Namzutha:</b> Path of Doom, the way to the Watchtower of the Lead Coin","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 11-19-2015, 08:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T11:34:36-08:00","id":769433,"title":"","content":"Can you translate <i>guhuh-gasgal?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T16:30:46-08:00","id":769621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=769433#post769433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you translate <i>guhuh-gasgal?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I can, but you'll have to provide some context. There's about half a dozen synonyms I'm looking at in the original Sumerian that could mean something.