rewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T10:07:15-07:00","id":972582,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the black Friday fad translation. I also asked for a FT word for a parental moral panic in the same post, it's okay if you forgot, I just think it might be useful for something I am working on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T13:33:26-07:00","id":972688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nikink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=972293#post972293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And fixed now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Enjoy!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks!<br /> <br /> Ahem, to the task at hand....<br /> _________________________________<br /> <br /> There are others out there. Some are ancient, perhaps even predating Pangaea, monsters that hunted when the moonlight had yet to fill all the overgrown crevasses of the primordial world. Some came after the <i>Uratha</i>, or perhaps came into being alongside them. A few shared in the great hunt. Others simply fought for their own reasons. They all vanished long ago, many hunted to extinction by the ancestors of the Forsaken in some forgotten conflict.<br /> <br /> Or did they?<br /> <br /> <b>Abhzu:</b> In an impossibly ancient time there was no divide between Land and Sea. Great predators ruled the deeps, hunting those abominations that would later walk the dirt. They disappeared into the inky depths long ago.<br /> <b>Barasu: </b>Once, it was said, that mortal men and women could walk as bears and speak to the earth as the bears do. Their kind has long since vanished from this world, wiped out by the Pure Tribes.<br /> <b>Saurilu: </b>They hold the Sun as sacred as the Uratha hold the Moon. Thunder follows in their steps. Their only remnants lie entombed in rock.<br /> <br /> Fearful rumors and heretical tales speak of even more skin-changers now lost to time. Some stories say they were contemporaries of the Uratha, and perhaps had their own patron gods in the lost age of Pangaea. What mysteries might they have taken into oblivion with them? What strange powers did they wield? If one were to part the veil of time and look back into the primeval world, what terrible beasts would they see hunting the wilds?<br /> <br /> If such creatures ever truly existed, most werewolves have never even heard of them. Certainly no living werewolf had ever met one, and the knowledge of spirits is couched in riddles filtered through inhuman perspectives. Yes, other monsters existed, the oldest spirits will say, and some could take the shapes of men and women and beasts. Yet even the oldest spirits cannot remember the day when these changing beasts went extinct....<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T15:14:48-07:00","id":972760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=972582#post972582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the black Friday fad translation. I also asked for a FT word for a parental moral panic in the same post, it's okay if you forgot, I just think it might be useful for something I am working on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh man, I totally missed that! Thanks for reminding me, I'll put it in a bunch of stuff I'm working on. I was finishing up Mage translations, but I'll be darned if I can find the document I had them in. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Does anyone also have any of the First Tongue words from The Pack and Dark Eras? I'm unable to get either at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T15:22:47-07:00","id":972770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=972760#post972760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh man, I totally missed that! Thanks for reminding me, I'll put it in a bunch of stuff I'm working on. I was finishing up Mage translations, but I'll be darned if I can find the document I had them in. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Does anyone also have any of the First Tongue words from The Pack and Dark Eras? I'm unable to get either at the moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Zakmur-dah refers to the first hunt of a pack.<br /> <br /> I also found the pharse &quot;Urum Da Takus&quot; which I think means the &quot;wolf must hunt&quot;<br /> <br /> Szigblal is a bird totem known as the wary nest<br /> <br /> egur sahendar,are spirits enslaved by the Warden in Dubai, which may be connected to the God Machine.<br /> <br /> Ukusguaku are leech hosts.<br /> <br /> and there are a bunch of other FT names for totems and lodges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 09-19-2016, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T16:24:30-07:00","id":972810,"title":"","content":"(70s new york FT words)<br /> <br /> The Kuspu Dinu are the Court of a Fair Wage that used to rule the Hisil of New york City<br /> <br /> The Ikkusunu are the Court of Indulgence is a destructive vice focused court that is one of the major power looking to replace the Kuspu Dinu.<br /> <br /> (neolithic stuff below)<br /> <br /> the Umfinthimma (the Loyal) are a sect of Uratha in the neolithic era that refuse to belive that father wolf may die and seek to preserve Pangaea<br /> <br /> the Kazithaga (The Cull) want to hunt mankind and reduce them to prey to save father wolf<br /> <br /> The Gathua (the Maw) believe that saving father wolf requires killing uratha to send the shards of his soul they possess back to him to replenish his strength<br /> <br /> The Sahenhar (The shepards) seek to guide humanity to produce more wolf blooded and get them to worship father wolf to save him<br /> <br /> The Ifila (the inheiritors) wish to kill father wolf to prevent him from dishonoring the hunt and entreat the first born for their help<br /> <br /> The Tesfurfarrahu (The Devourers) are a radical branch of the inheiritors that wish to consume father wolf's soul and take his place as a god.<br /> <br /> The Athdursa (The Mourners) think father wolf's death is inevitable and relive that sealing off Pangaea will be necessary to save the world when that happens.<br /> <br /> The only viking era terms are couple of spirits, there are also FT names for various spirits associated with the court of indulgence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T16:49:53-07:00","id":983597,"title":"","content":"Could you translate a few things for me? These are names of some of Hikaon-Ur's children in a game I run, was wanting them in the First Tongue:<br /> <br /> Blackened Wolf<br /> Ebony Wolf<br /> Darkest Wolf<br /> Shadowed Wolf<br /> Midnight Wolf<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12050-ursedrah-tahru","name":"Ursedrah-Tahru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12050_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T19:16:18-07:00","id":983681,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12050-ursedrah-tahru\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12050_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12050\" data-vbnamecard=\"12050\">Ursedrah-Tahru</a>:<br /> <br /> Ghihi-Ur: Blackened Wolf<br /> Shulmes-Ur: Ebony Wolf<br /> Masulmu-Ur: Darkest Wolf<br /> Ghiyedhen-Ur: Shadowed Wolf<br /> Ghifaa-Ur: Midnight Wolf<br /> <br /> These names are all cognates to words already in or not yet in the dictionary. I thought, since totems like these are unique and powerful spirits, that they deserved more unique names. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T15:38:21-07:00","id":985727,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1874_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1874\" data-vbnamecard=\"1874\">Sikla Alkis</a> <br /> <br /> These are really great, thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12050-ursedrah-tahru","name":"Ursedrah-Tahru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12050_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T12:44:17-07:00","id":990566,"title":"","content":"I have a request, I need a titles of werewolves in one of my dark ages games.<br /> first is for a Blood Talon viking who converted to Christianity his name is Bernhard Alexander but his original name was Flesh-Render. He got rid of it when he converted and uses a Norman name now. So I need one for Flesh-Render<br /> Also I have a Norman Werewolf who already has a title but the Pure gave him a derogatory one. He who lays with the blood demons, this is in reference to the vampires he travels with and because of the spartan relationship he has with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","name":"The Anubi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T15:14:08-07:00","id":990659,"title":"","content":"Oh one more request, I recently have been using Forsaken in old world of darkness as a replacement for Apocalypse. I was wondering if you could also come up with names for the clans. I already can use a few from the requiem list but I just need a few more.<br /> Assamites<br /> Brujah<br /> Cappadocian<br /> Giovanni<br /> Setites<br /> Lasombra<br /> Malkavians<br /> Ravnos<br /> Salubri (warriors, healers, watchers)<br /> Toreador<br /> Tremere<br /> Tzimisce<br /> <br /> I would be very appreciative if you help out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","name":"The Anubi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T08:09:47-07:00","id":990964,"title":"","content":"I can definitely do all of these. The old Vampire clans were something I was thinking of doing, and this gives me an excuse to do them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T10:17:59-07:00","id":991011,"title":"","content":"Was curious if you would be willing to do a couple of translations when you have the free time? I've been working on a few little projects and would love some aid in doing First Tongue translations. <br /> <br /> Singing Wolf - A homebrewed Firstborn. <br /> Dreaming Wolf, Gazing Wolf, Painted Wolf, and Screaming Wolf - Some of said Firstborn's brood.<br /> Silent Howlers - A tribe dedicated to staying out of politics and recording the passing of ages in hopes of keeping an undiluted and unwarped history. <br /> <br /> Thank you so much for your help if you choose to give this a shot. I really appreciate it. <br /> <br /> Also, is the collection of words on your first post a complete collection of all your translations so far? Or is there another compendium?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7621-threadwrought","name":"Threadwrought","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T07:26:16-07:00","id":992935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Threadwrought</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=991011#post991011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was curious if you would be willing to do a couple of translations when you have the free time? I've been working on a few little projects and would love some aid in doing First Tongue translations.<br /> <br /> Singing Wolf - A homebrewed Firstborn.<br /> Dreaming Wolf, Gazing Wolf, Painted Wolf, and Screaming Wolf - Some of said Firstborn's brood.<br /> Silent Howlers - A tribe dedicated to staying out of politics and recording the passing of ages in hopes of keeping an undiluted and unwarped history.<br /> <br /> Thank you so much for your help if you choose to give this a shot. I really appreciate it.<br /> <br /> Also, is the collection of words on your first post a complete collection of all your translations so far? Or is there another compendium?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's another compendium, but it's not been updated since last July by the current updater. I've been meaning to go back and remove the list you mentioned from the first post.<br /> <br /> I'll try and get these done as soon as I can. I don't have a lot of energy right now, but when I do, I'll get these done. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 11-07-2016, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T14:29:24-07:00","id":995348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=990964#post990964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can definitely do all of these. The old Vampire clans were something I was thinking of doing, and this gives me an excuse to do them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I really like using the Forsaken within Classic World Of Darkness and having them come up with names for the Clans is an interesting concept. Right now I have a plan to use the Forsaken in a dark ages game set during the Northern Crusade where the Slavic Forsaken have an odd belief that the vampires are actually the result of a Werewolf who was raised from the dead by Veles the Slavic god of the underworld to guard over the humans. But the children of the first vampire grew envious and formed tribes of their own and began to war. I did this to harken back to an old Slavic belief that a vampire comes into existence after the death of a werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","name":"The Anubi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T21:57:31-07:00","id":997007,"title":"","content":"What would be a good name for Prometheans made from werewolves resulting in abominations that cannot control their form or essence properly resulting in them needing to consume essence that fits their current refinements or they fall into being a centimanti, and instead of death rage making them wolf-men it turns them into idigam-like monsters that cannot stay in one true shape for more than a second. They are trying to become werewolves, but until then they are sort of uratha/magath/idigam abominations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T07:44:28-08:00","id":999212,"title":"","content":"I have a request. What would the first tongue phrase be for a spirit called Blood Flowing as Water?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T09:38:15-08:00","id":1013804,"title":"","content":"Lottery-Cheaters-Never-Prosper<br /> <br /> This is a strange type of justice spirit. It started out as a small gaffling of ill-will towards cheaters that eventual grew large and powerful enough to devour those cheat at major lotteries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T17:38:19-08:00","id":1019515,"title":"","content":"I apologize for my inactivity and lack of response. I've been busy with attending to things elsewhere. That being said, the current compendium of First Tongue words on the first page is a year out of date, so I'm trying to organize everything into an Excel file to upload somewhere. I'll try and translate as soon as I can, but there will be delays.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T22:56:11-08:00","id":1019625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=992935#post992935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's another compendium, but it's not been updated since last July by the current updater. I've been meaning to go back and remove the list you mentioned from the first post.<br /> <br /> I'll try and get these done as soon as I can. I don't have a lot of energy right now, but when I do, I'll get these done. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that guy is a jerk, who ever he is.<br /> (Or maybe he may have gotten busy then forgot about it...)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All Things Strive.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4708-litheon","name":"Litheon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T23:00:31-08:00","id":1019627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Litheon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=1019625#post1019625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that guy is a jerk, who ever he is.<br /> (Or maybe he may have gotten busy then forgot about it...)</div> </div> </div> </div>I blame you not one bit, dude. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> This is a massive project. Don't sweat it if some things are out of date. You're kind enough to organize my thoughts in the first place, and I super appreciate that. I wouldn't have come this far without your help and Nikink's help, among others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T23:16:26-08:00","id":1019631,"title":"","content":"Yeah. XP I organized a bit more. Got all your dumps into that dictionary from when I left off till now, in a rush job; but I think I'll officially stop updating it now, cause you prolly have your own solution. I never had patience for bookkeeping in the first place. ;D<br /> Have fun, dude! I'll be lurking.<br /> (And dang. missed lucky post number 777 by ONE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All Things Strive.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4708-litheon","name":"Litheon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T08:53:50-08:00","id":1019798,"title":"","content":"I appreciate it, dude. I can take it from here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You've been a big help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T08:57:54-08:00","id":1020906,"title":"","content":"Merciless-Firestorm-Awaiting-Its-Moment.<br /> <br /> The Rank 5 spirit responsible for the in the 1923 Berkeley fire, another conflagration on September 22, 1970, a smaller fire also started in Wildcat Canyon on December 10, 1980, Oakland firestorm of 1991, and 2016 Oakland warehouse fire. It is a very large and powerful fire spirit that gluts itself upon major fires, but waits patiently being tithed to by lesser flame spirits until given an opportunity to cause devastation, but never waiting more than half a century. .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 12-22-2016, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T13:08:17-08:00","id":1051117,"title":"","content":"Okay, so a bit of a progress report:<br /> <br /> - I'm going to have to redo my fanon grammar from the ground up. Canon grammar is closer to Sumerian grammar than I thought \u2014 one of the devs said that they had to learn Sumerian's basics for some translations in...<i>Signs of the Moon</i> from 1e, I think? Sentence translations and complex will have to be on hold for now, but I can still do simple Adjective-Noun translations.<br /> <br /> - I lost track of a bunch of word lists. Other than all the translations I need to get to on this page, as well as the ones listed in the OP, are there any others I need to get on that people requested? I know I'm still trying to figure out the eras of mankind for The Young Man In the Cafe.<br /> <br /> - I'm going to go back and clean up a bunch of words I think rely too heavy on apostrophes/stereotypical fantasy spellings (like &quot;ah&quot; for a long A vowel).<br /> <br /> - I'm going to find CatDoom's pronunciation guide and put it in the original post, for reference. I don't see anything in canon that gives a definitive contradiction to anything he came up with, and the 2e glossary entry of Cahalith actually has the final syllable pronounced as &quot;it&quot;, which lends to the idea that the th are aspirated (spoken with a noticeable puff of air) consonants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":1874,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","user":"Sikla Alkis","date":". 02-18-2017, 04:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T16:13:46-08:00","id":1051203,"title":"","content":"Awesome work. Simply awesome work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T11:32:04-08:00","id":1053342,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10343_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10343\" data-vbnamecard=\"10343\">The Anubi</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7621-threadwrought\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7621\" data-vbnamecard=\"7621\">Threadwrought</a>, @milo v3<br /> <br /> Uzu-Kur: Flesh-Ripper (lit. \u201crends flesh asunder\u201d)<br /> Muth Luzukag-Uzuh: He Who Lays With Blood Demons (lit. \u201cblood thief\u2019s whore\u201d, and that Uzuh is considered a very strong word, ESPECIALLY to the Forsaken; something not quite as bad [but would still curl the hairs off of polite company] is Muth Luzukag-Shiniduth)<br /> <br /> ghen: to move, to be in motion, to flow (as a liquid does)<br /> kum: the flow of a bodily liquid, such as urine, sweat or blood; to bleed, to secrete something<br /> hane: to blaze, to burn fiercely; a conflagration, a firestorm, a great and destructive fire; an out-of-control wildfire or bush fire<br /> <br /> Silighelum-Ur: Singing Wolf<br /> Mammudh-Ur: Dreaming Wolf<br /> Zibbu-Ur: Painted Wolf<br /> Talakgil-Ur: Screaming Wolf<br /> Mekhar-Skirthufhal: The Silent Howlers<br /> <br /> uzurih: a carnivore, a predator<br /> tag-uzurih: a hunting animal; a carnivore that obtains food by hunting<br /> gadh: an itch, a scratch; an irritation of some kind; to be agitated<br /> mirgadh: a sense of indignation, great anger or irritation; to be agitated, rowdy or riled up greatly; a fury that can move and change worlds (such as that of a political movement)<br /> ummia: an expert; a professional; one who is established in their field<br /> su-suhiak: a doctor, a medical professional (lit. \u201cbody-fixer\u201d)<br /> namarusu: a reflection; a mirrored image<br /> <br /> Namzutag-Uzurihag Zizu: The Assamites (&quot;life thieves of the Wise Hunter&quot;)<br /> Mirgadh-Skir: The Brujah (&quot;agitated voices&quot;)<br /> Namusag-Ummia: The Cappodocians (&quot;death's own experts&quot;)<br /> Namus-Nir Dum: The Giovanni (&quot;the family of dead lords&quot;)<br /> Sahfala-Mirska: The Setites (&quot;the rebellious snakes&quot;)<br /> Nu-Numarusu: The Lasombra (\u201cthe reflectionless\u201d)<br /> Mag-Ihdar: The Malkavians (\u201craving prophets\u201d)<br /> Thakh-Lakha: The Ravnos (\u201cwandering criminals\u201d)<br /> Suthar-Su-Suhiak: The Salubri (\u201cdoctors covered in the blood of the slaughtered\u201d/\u201cthose who mend mangled and bloody bodies\u201d)<br /> Sagh-Hespar: The Toreador (\u201cthose trapped by beauty\u201d)<br /> Muth-Ummaluzuk: The Tremere (\u201cblood witch-thieves\u201d)<br /> Uzu-Gheskihdi: Tzimisce (\u201cflesh crafters\u201d)<br /> <br /> Ventrue\u2019s already been translated. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> shargus\u2019urlul: \u201cMany-skinned liar-wolves\u201d, or Prometheans made out of wolves that need to feed on essence, or they lose control of themselves and their forms<br /> <br /> I\u2019m still getting the basics of the grammar. I need to come up with something that isn\u2019t a complete cut-and-paste of Sumerian itself, but still falls in line with what the devs had in mind. This is what I\u2019ve got so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T14:59:30-08:00","id":1053442,"title":"","content":"Thanks for remembering that request.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T15:21:55-08:00","id":1053462,"title":"","content":"This is so amazing! I will have to dig through this whole thread at some point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T11:53:04-08:00","id":1061299,"title":"","content":"I'm looking for a translated name for a curiosity spirit whose English name is &quot;Shiny Thing Found!&quot; He's magpie-shaped, if that helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T14:23:00-08:00","id":1061335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=1051117#post1051117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't see anything in canon that gives a definitive contradiction to anything he came up with, and the 2e glossary entry of Cahalith actually has the final syllable pronounced as &amp;quot;it&amp;quot;, which lends to the idea that the th are aspirated (spoken with a noticeable puff of air) consonants.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might have a pre-errata version of the PDF? That got corrected to represent a voiceless dental fricative in the glossary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T19:10:02-07:00","id":1062601,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar192_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"192\" data-vbnamecard=\"192\">Yossarian</a>: I do, thank you for pointing that out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> @Heu: Oh, this was a tough one. I'm still struggling to understand the verb chain in Sumerian, so I fell back on my old, homebrewed grammar for the name: Zalah-Bisirium-Kal-Fath. Because of a magpie's tendencies to pick up all the shiny things as their special treasures, the name literally means &quot;A Shiny Piece of Treasure Is Found!&quot;.<br /> <br /> And there are a huge chunk of translations I did, but I lost the file to them. Here are some translations from another list, mostly cobbled together from canon 1e words but with some other stuff thrown in. Now, most of this is pretty much guesswork, but this is what I managed to come up with:<br /> <br /> ethal: the ashes of the dead; ashes of a burned or cremated body<br /> huz: to have raised hackles; to be bristling with rage or fury; the state of a wolf or animal in an attacking or aggressively defensive position, i.e. claws out, teeth bared; a word to describe berserking attacks or a berserk individual<br /> inim: the words one has spoken and which are directly quoted from or attested to an individual<br /> udta: a position or point; in regards to the military, a line or place held or defended by something<br /> zith: loyalty or dedication, especially to a cause believed to be true and good (such as the cause of an archetypical paladin)<br /> zidh: formerly known as &quot;zith&quot;, this is now the spelling that refers to flour<br /> ahar: a metal lead, i.e. something like the ring put through a bull's nose to lead it along<br /> dul: to gather, to harvest; to reap<br /> ilthum: a band, a group; cohorts, reinforcements, aid; a term for a band of mercenaries or a group for hire in some way (such as a group of freelance artists)<br /> husa: the muscles of the neck<br /> de: the cheek<br /> shumm: garlic; an onion<br /> ba: allotments, halves, pieces; pieces cut out from something; a part sourced from something else<br /> bah: formerly &quot;ba&quot;, this is a catch-all term for marine creatures whether supernatural or mundane<br /> dagu: something or an action that destroys or kills by throwing or thrashing around<br /> kurum: curving, bending around, winding; something that is serpentine or river-like in how it winds<br /> dakabh: to ooze or drip; to be so soaked or saturated with something that you're dripping with it<br /> garga: the destruction associated with the destruction of kingdoms, the toppling of empires, the raiding of lands, etc.<br /> shula: to flood or overwhelm something to bring about a negative or destructive result, such as to spam e-mails or send a swarm of fighters against opponents to overwhelm them<br /> ghu: to devour, to consume, to ravenously eat (more vicious and savage connotations than rih)<br /> ghabha: the chest; the breast; a word used to refer to one's heart<br /> sughar: the fallen, the dead; a corpse<br /> hala: one who sings lamentations; one who delivers eulogies or speaks/sings in rememberance<br /> maaz: to be bursting with happiness or good feelings; to rejoice<br /> hon: to spawn heavily or reduce/replace in copious amounts, such as a population of rabbits that is breeding out of control<br /> endi: something that is appealing or valuable to children; something that provokes a childish response of &quot;I want it&quot; or &quot;oooh, shiny&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T07:19:36-07:00","id":1076954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=1053342#post1053342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, @milo v3<br /> <br /> Uzu-Kur: Flesh-Ripper (lit. \u201crends flesh asunder\u201d)<br /> Muth Luzukag-Uzuh: He Who Lays With Blood Demons (lit. \u201cblood thief\u2019s whore\u201d, and that Uzuh is considered a very strong word, ESPECIALLY to the Forsaken; something not quite as bad [but would still curl the hairs off of polite company] is Muth Luzukag-Shiniduth)<br /> <br /> ghen: to move, to be in motion, to flow (as a liquid does)<br /> kum: the flow of a bodily liquid, such as urine, sweat or blood; to bleed, to secrete something<br /> hane: to blaze, to burn fiercely; a conflagration, a firestorm, a great and destructive fire; an out-of-control wildfire or bush fire<br /> <br /> Silighelum-Ur: Singing Wolf<br /> Mammudh-Ur: Dreaming Wolf<br /> Zibbu-Ur: Painted Wolf<br /> Talakgil-Ur: Screaming Wolf<br /> Mekhar-Skirthufhal: The Silent Howlers<br /> <br /> uzurih: a carnivore, a predator<br /> tag-uzurih: a hunting animal; a carnivore that obtains food by hunting<br /> gadh: an itch, a scratch; an irritation of some kind; to be agitated<br /> mirgadh: a sense of indignation, great anger or irritation; to be agitated, rowdy or riled up greatly; a fury that can move and change worlds (such as that of a political movement)<br /> ummia: an expert; a professional; one who is established in their field<br /> su-suhiak: a doctor, a medical professional (lit. \u201cbody-fixer\u201d)<br /> namarusu: a reflection; a mirrored image<br /> <br /> Namzutag-Uzurihag Zizu: The Assamites (&amp;quot;life thieves of the Wise Hunter <br /> Mirgadh-Skir: The Brujah (&amp;quot;agitated voices&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Namusag-Ummia: The Cappodocians (&amp;quot;death's own experts&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Namus-Nir Dum: The Giovanni (&amp;quot;the family of dead lords&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Sahfala-Mirska: The Setites (&amp;quot;the rebellious snakes&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Nu-Numarusu: The Lasombra (\u201cthe reflectionless\u201d)<br /> Mag-Ihdar: The Malkavians (\u201craving prophets\u201d)<br /> Thakh-Lakha: The Ravnos (\u201cwandering criminals\u201d)<br /> Suthar-Su-Suhiak: The Salubri (\u201cdoctors covered in the blood of the slaughtered\u201d/\u201cthose who mend mangled and bloody bodies\u201d)<br /> Sagh-Hespar: The Toreador (\u201cthose trapped by beauty\u201d)<br /> Muth-Ummaluzuk: The Tremere (\u201cblood witch-thieves\u201d)<br /> Uzu-Gheskihdi: Tzimisce (\u201cflesh crafters\u201d)<br /> <br /> Ventrue\u2019s already been translated. <br /> <br /> shargus\u2019urlul: \u201cMany-skinned liar-wolves\u201d, or Prometheans made out of wolves that need to feed on essence, or they lose control of themselves and their forms<br /> <br /> I\u2019m still getting the basics of the grammar. I need to come up with something that isn\u2019t a complete cut-and-paste of Sumerian itself, but still falls in line with what the devs had in mind. This is what I\u2019ve got so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks man sorry i didn't get back to you sooner been very busy. Going to use these for a game soon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","name":"The Anubi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T16:10:05-07:00","id":1078003,"title":"","content":"There is one more request I would like to make it is for a friend who is creating a custom bloodline of vamps (Tons of vamps sorry bout that) The Harlequxi/Harlequxel. A bloodline we are doing a clanbook style pdf for. The concept is a bloodline is that they believe they know the secret of the universe that all life and creation is just a sick joke played by some unknown cosmic force and that there is no heaven or hell only the void of oblivion. They are heavily connected to the True Fae because their founder was kidnapped by one and escaped. But their main idealism is that everything is a joke so lets laugh along with it. Not mad per say but they know something few understand. They style themselves as renaissance jesters and Harlequins as well as stand up comedians and high class circus clowns. Pompous, insulting, yet jubilant and happy organizing themselves into high society whilst mocking it like a Jester would. <br /> <br /> Words:<br /> Harlequxi(singular)/Harlequxel(plural)<br /> The Divine Comedy: A giant flesh abomination that is used for the Divine Comedy which it is named after where other vampires are inducted into the bloodline and shown the grand joke the universe pulled on them. Covered in writhing laughing mouths it screams forever in joyous uproar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","name":"The Anubi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T08:08:28-07:00","id":1082618,"title":"","content":"Three Totems for my Swedish Packs to translate here:<ul><li>Watchdog</li> <li>Brunhilda ( yes, like famous Valkyrie )</li> <li>Moon Hound</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T16:35:05-07:00","id":1083218,"title":"","content":"I translated Watchdog as &quot;<span style=\"font-size:20px\">urginamid\u02b0u</span>&quot; for NateD.<br /> Moon Hound -&gt; Moon Dog -&gt; Iduth-ur<br /> <br /> Brunhilda is a personal name, I can't see it changing, except the b and d getting a bit breathier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">